an style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T21:09:17-07:00","id":1298484,"title":"","content":"I need this to live up to the hype, deep down in my core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">-Red</span></b> V5 Fan Content: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1259556-v5-the-masquerade\" target=\"_blank\">The Masquerade</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256114-v5-tzimisce-and-vicissitude\" target=\"_blank\">Tzimisce and Vicissitude</a> (non Program take), <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1253331-loresheets-chicago\" target=\"_blank\">Loresheet: Chicago</a> (pre CbN V5), <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1251576-v5-resonance-flavor\" target=\"_blank\">Resonance Flavor</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1291918-v5-morality\" target=\"_blank\">Morality System</a> Project Manager, Developer, Community Outreach at <a href=\"https://www.huntersentertainment.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Entertainment</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6164-red-eye","name":"Red Eye","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6164_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T21:14:08-07:00","id":1298487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1298481#post1298481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looks amazing!<br /> <br /> And I LOVE that Brian Mitsoda is on the dev team!!!<br /> <br /> YESSSSSSSSSSS!!!!<br /> <br /> VV is back, too!!!!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Eh? Where are you seeing VV?<br /> <br /> Also, it's confirmed to be based on V5's mechanics (Resonance was talked about heavily in the interview), set in Seattle, you're the victim of a Mass Embrace, you start out as a Thin Blood and you can manifest a clan later.<br /> <br /> Kotaku Article: <a href=\"https://www.kotaku.com.au/2019/03/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-is-getting-a-sequel-and-it-looks-pretty-good/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kotaku.com.au/2019/03/va...s-pretty-good/</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5704,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5704-thebiglarpnerd","user":"thebiglarpnerd","date":". 03-22-2019, 12:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5704-thebiglarpnerd","name":"thebiglarpnerd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T21:26:55-07:00","id":1298489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thebiglarpnerd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1298487#post1298487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Eh? Where are you seeing VV?<br /> <br /> Also, it's confirmed to be based on V5's mechanics (Resonance was talked about heavily in the interview), set in Seattle, you're the victim of a Mass Embrace, you start out as a Thin Blood and you can manifest a clan later.<br /> <br /> Kotaku Article: <a href=\"https://www.kotaku.com.au/2019/03/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-is-getting-a-sequel-and-it-looks-pretty-good/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kotaku.com.au/2019/03/va...s-pretty-good/</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I find it.. interesting....we're going to see werewolves in videogame before w5","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T21:37:14-07:00","id":1298492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1298489#post1298489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I find it.. interesting....we're going to see werewolves in videogame before w5</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Considering they stated that mechanics for both the video game and TT were developed simultaneously for Vampire, I'd expect there to be something similar going on for Werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5704-thebiglarpnerd","name":"thebiglarpnerd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T22:33:28-07:00","id":1298510,"title":"","content":"But must we be a wretched Thin Blood?<br /> <br /> Only pure Malkavian blood for me! <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T22:46:02-07:00","id":1298515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1298510#post1298510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But must we be a wretched Thin Blood?<br /> <br /> Only pure Malkavian blood for me!</div> </div> </div> </div>I got the very distinct impression in the interviews that we'll be picking up a Clan over the games plotline, which leads me to believe we'll engage in at least one very particular story at some point in the game (possibly a little bit about what the trailer was hinting at with the hunting down another Kindred). The website seems to imply 5 Clans (and a bonus Clan, whatever that means, for a total of 6).<br /> <br /> There were honestly a number of hinted implications over the course of the interviews, despite them being pretty tight lipped still.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">-Red</span></b> V5 Fan Content: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1259556-v5-the-masquerade\" target=\"_blank\">The Masquerade</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256114-v5-tzimisce-and-vicissitude\" target=\"_blank\">Tzimisce and Vicissitude</a> (non Program take), <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1253331-loresheets-chicago\" target=\"_blank\">Loresheet: Chicago</a> (pre CbN V5), <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1251576-v5-resonance-flavor\" target=\"_blank\">Resonance Flavor</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1291918-v5-morality\" target=\"_blank\">Morality System</a> Project Manager, Developer, Community Outreach at <a href=\"https://www.huntersentertainment.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Entertainment</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6164-red-eye","name":"Red Eye","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6164_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T22:56:38-07:00","id":1298519,"title":"","content":"I'm.... mixed on this preview.<br /> <br /> I like a lot of what I read, even some of the V5 inspired bits that I don't like in the V5 rules (blood Resonance for example). Who's working on it looks like a good team, I really like hearing that they're pretty open about the first game's flaws, etc.<br /> <br /> There's also a few red flags for me. I want a VtMB sequel to address that VtMB was overly reliant on combat and didn't really let you take non-combat routes because the end of the game was impossible if you did. Making a better combat system is awesome... but I want a better ability to play the game in different styles. I'm not sure at all about losing the VtM flavor of Disciplines for more generic vampire ability trees with different names. Starting as a thin-blood and getting a Clan in-game is really iffy for me. <br /> <br /> But it's early... and despite the excitement around the project, there's a lot of time between now and when all of these things are 100% final.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T23:01:53-07:00","id":1298520,"title":"","content":"My only issue right now is this seems very much like <i><b>Dishonored: The Masquerade</b></i>.<br /> <br /> Now, don't get me wrong, I like Dishonored.<br /> <br /> I LOVE <i>Dishonored</i>, in fact.<br /> <br /> <i>Dishonored</i> is also kind of based on V:TM:B.<br /> <br /> However, I should point out that we already have had an attempt to make this game and it was called <i><b>Dark</b></i>.<br /> <br /> And voice acting aside, <i>Dark </i>was a piece of shit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T23:21:45-07:00","id":1298528,"title":"","content":"I...actually wonder on just how much of V5's setting is being incorporated in Bloodlines 2. Especially when examining some of the other article previews, not just the trailer.<br /> <br /> The Blood Resonance stuff and it being this game's version of &quot;You Are What You Eat&quot; is so far the only indication of it. The Mass Embrace thing and there being a bunch of Caitiffs...doesn't really say much of V5 specifically since &quot;The Time of Thin Bloods&quot; has been a part of VtM's metaplot LONG before V5. No mention of Kindred society being under pressure due to the Second Inquisition being a thing. Or there being a power vacuum due to the Beckoning, etc. <br /> <br /> Of course, there may be more as some of the above is based on information that hasn't been shared yet. Or being the type of thing that enters spoiler territory that you have to play the game through...<br /> <br /> ...still, to not lead with any potential V5 goodness, makes the whole &quot;One World of Darkness&quot; transmedia initiative seem like a farce, yeah?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T23:27:59-07:00","id":1298531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1298528#post1298528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I...actually wonder on just how much of V5's setting is being incorporated in Bloodlines 2. Especially when examining some of the other article previews, not just the trailer.<br /> <br /> The Blood Resonance stuff and it being this game's version of &quot;You Are What You Eat&quot; is so far the only indication of it. The Mass Embrace thing and there being a bunch of Caitiffs...doesn't really say much of V5 specifically since &quot;The Time of Thin Bloods&quot; has been a part of VtM's metaplot LONG before V5. No mention of Kindred society being under pressure due to the Second Inquisition being a thing. Or there being a power vacuum due to the Beckoning, etc.<br /> <br /> Of course, there may be more as some of the above is based on information that hasn't been shared yet. Or being the type of thing that enters spoiler territory that you have to play the game through...<br /> <br /> ...still, to not lead with any potential V5 goodness, makes the whole &quot;One World of Darkness&quot; transmedia initiative seem like a farce, yeah?</div> </div> </div> </div>They've already said it's 5th Edition V:TM. It's more obvious in the Playthrough shown to news reporters.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I'm confused as to what gives you the idea it wouldn't be 5th Edition?<br /> <br /> The only difference is probably we'll have some Second Edition missions probably. It's not like the Beckoning would have a big effect on a Seattle Fledgling.<br /> <br /> Then again, I think it's in the minds of gamers that 5th Edition isn't just V:TM with a few minor tweaks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T00:12:02-07:00","id":1298538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1298531#post1298531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They've already said it's 5th Edition V:TM. It's more obvious in the Playthrough shown to news reporters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh have they? Where?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mind you, I'm confused as to what gives you the idea it wouldn't be 5th Edition? </div> </div> </div>My initial impression was that Bloodlines 2 was doing it's own thing separate from V5. That the guys at Hardsuit where doing mostly their own take on VtM, but not being beholden to what V5 was doing.<br /> <br /> There's also the impression that, given the usual development time of games, and the timing of where this game seems to be at now compared to V5, wonder at how reactive the development team could have been. In order to get to the point of pre-alpha for Bloodlines 2, the game had to have started development at least a year after Paradox acquired White Wolf. At the very least, a few years before V5 was released. Video game development has a LOT more moving parts to it that tabletop RPG development doesn't have to worry about. They're not just writing up text and playtesting a game to make sure things are balanced, it also includes other moving parts like make assets, build an engine, make sure the game even starts up when booting it up, all before figuring out if the game itself is even fun. That wouldn't leave a lot of room for Bloodlines 2 to react to any changes and developments in the V5 TRPG.<br /> <br /> Like, if they had to change or remove anything in response to all of the controversies that V5 has faced, either the changes were done in quick enough time to not impede with development, or there were no changes to be made.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, we've still seen nothing substantial of the Werewolf game aside from the word of its developer...in tandem with us knowing nothing new about Werewolf 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T01:37:12-07:00","id":1298549,"title":"","content":"Does it matter a lot which edition the game is based on? Video games based on RPG's tend to take huge liberties with implementing the rules of tabletop RPG's, to make for a good gaming experience. Which is as it should be, in my opinion.<br /> <br /> As long as the feeling of the game is right and the system works well.<br /> <br /> I really agree that it would be great if you could do mostly non-combat successfully as well. Given that stealth playthroughs is a pretty big thing in lots of games, I think I'll feel hopeful about stealth and/or social options throughout the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11756-razikale","name":"Razikale","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T01:51:34-07:00","id":1298551,"title":"","content":"We worked on the video game and V5 in tandem, so yes, it is based on V5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T03:02:30-07:00","id":1298557,"title":"","content":"It is not Beckett, is it?<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/1108028970564575233/1553223544/1500x500\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/1108028970564575233/1553223544/1500x500\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/1108028970564575233/1553223544/1500x500\" target=\"_blank\"> https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/1108028970564575233/1553223544/1500x500 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3792-trueann","name":"trueann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T03:18:33-07:00","id":1298558,"title":"","content":"I am officially pumped and pre-ordered as soon as it was humanly possible!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4259-eddie-fiori","name":"Eddie Fiori","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T04:57:04-07:00","id":1298561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1298538#post1298538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Meanwhile, we've still seen nothing substantial of the Werewolf game aside from the word of its developer...in tandem with us knowing nothing new about Werewolf 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>....except the season one content SEEMS to take inspiration from Under a Blood Red Moon and you know is called Season of the Wolf. So we're probably going to get some indepth on werewolves and not just &quot;Hey they kill vampires&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T05:10:02-07:00","id":1298562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>trueann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1298557#post1298557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is not Beckett, is it?<br /> <a href=\"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/1108028970564575233/1553223544/1500x500\" target=\"_blank\">https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banner...23544/1500x500</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Damn he's handsome!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T05:38:26-07:00","id":1298567,"title":"","content":"had to preorder it immediately.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This is me, just forgot my PW and changed my email<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25163-crytash2","name":"Crytash2","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25163_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T06:00:56-07:00","id":1298570,"title":"","content":"Sounds great but i wish they kept discliplines instead of using ability trees with different names and only 5 clans is a bit disappointing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T07:00:16-07:00","id":1298579,"title":"","content":"I don't want to be a thin blood. <br /> I want to be a properly Embraced Ventrue for once!<br /> I want my Agoge and I want to recite my lineage up to a 4th Generation Methuselah ancestor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T08:55:27-07:00","id":1298600,"title":"","content":"Also, I don't like this emphasis of &quot;Powers&quot; over Disciplines&quot;. Why can't we have Protean and then buy dots until we can use Mist Form?<br /> This game system seems &quot;vampiric&quot; yes, but not specifically Masquerade, do you understand?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T09:04:18-07:00","id":1298604,"title":"","content":"So, the game is set in Seattle?<br /> <br /> Well, clearly it is going to involve fights over coffee dominion - over who controls the WoD analog of Starbucks. And Magicians of the Bay (the WotC analog) will be very important to vampires as well. I fully expect a Ventrue to start cackling when he gets to make more changes to Forgotten Realms, while drinking from someone drinking some Starbuck's coffee.<br /> <br /> The game might also depict rain in Seattle. Maybe.<br /> <br /> And possibly some other bits of business like clans, generations, thin bloods, and the like.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T09:07:33-07:00","id":1298605,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I don't mind blood resonance in it. I'm not that stoked about how the hunger system will work, with the compulsions on top, but we'll see. Disciplines, I'm iffy aboutbeing replaced.<br /> <br /> V5 plot, I imagine it'll have as much of it as Bloodlines had the old VtM plot, so &quot;based on&quot; at best. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> However, one thing that will make, or break the game for me, is the aesthetics and mood (and music, of course). VtMB gave off the mood I associated with VtM over the years, right from the moment you took the first step into Asylum and &quot;<i>Isolation</i>&quot; started playing. It had the gothic-punk vibe all along. If this will follow in those footsteps and will have a similar feel to it, albeit with a more modern (but still gothic-punk) background, I'm good. If not, and it's going for V5's style and mood (whatever it is), I'll drop it.<br /> <br /> The concept arts are nice, though.<br /> <br /> PS: I can't convey how sad I am that this didn't get me stoked and hyped beyond all reason. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I never thought the best an announcement of VtMB 2 could bring out from me will be &quot;eh, wait and see, it has some chance to be good&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 03-22-2019, 12:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T09:09:31-07:00","id":1298606,"title":"","content":"Who owns Seattle in the game? Camarilla, Anarchs, Sabbat? It's close to Vancouver, I'd sacrifice to Belial for a cameo of Siegfried.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T09:10:54-07:00","id":1298609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1298605#post1298605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I don't mind blood resonance in it. I'm not that stoked about how the hunger system will work, with the compulsions on top, but we'll see.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where are people seeing this info about Blood Resonance and the five clans?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T09:20:03-07:00","id":1298613,"title":"","content":"I'll buy it when it releases. I'm excited but I'm not dropping money on skins.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ortam + Malkavia makes a Requiem fun.<br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Posts in this colour are Persuasion.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\">Posts in this colour are Seduction.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this colour are Intimidation.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/57-solomon-birch","name":"solomon birch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar57_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T09:27:47-07:00","id":1298617,"title":"","content":"Imma super excited!!!!!!<br /> <br /> Mass Embrace is an easy way to get away with the Sire stuff, much like in the first bloodlines. Too bad, but also different Sire plots for different clans would have been an hassle and so it's an understandable choice.<br /> <br /> And the Thin Blood thing is probably a way to get the average player through a long tutorial and then giving the choice of a clan not much later into the game. Like, one or two hours into it.<br /> Terrible for veteran players, but probably a good choice in favor of the newcomers.<br /> <br /> As for 5 clans only...<br /> I'm not completely against DLCs, as long as they add replayability and value to the experience and also if their price is fair.<br /> I can see the Nosferatu and Malkavian as very good expansions to the base game because they can alter the experience considerably.<br /> Yet they are two of the most popular clans so I don't know how good it would be to not sell them at day one.<br /> <br /> But really it would be nice if all Clan Banes could alter the experience more. In the original bloodlines malkavian and nosferatu felt different, the others not so much...<br /> <br /> And fingers crossed for all 13 clans eventually, especially the Ravnos and Giovanni (let me dream!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Ever since the Followers of Set rebranded themselves as The Ministry, I can barely keep a straight face around them.&quot; - Ramona","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","name":"Ravnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15944_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T09:30:17-07:00","id":1298619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1298617#post1298617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ravnos</div> </div> </div> </div>Tell me, what is this...&quot;Ravnos&quot; that you speak of?<br /> <br /> (Sorry but yeah, I seriously doubt Ravnos are going to be in it. Even Assamite is a long shot and they''re in the Cam now.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T09:57:42-07:00","id":1298625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardestadtTheEvenYounger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1298619#post1298619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tell me, what is this...&quot;Ravnos&quot; that you speak of?<br /> <br /> (Sorry but yeah, I seriously doubt Ravnos are going to be in it. Even Assamite is a long shot and they''re in the Cam now.)</div> </div> </div> </div>What part of &quot;let me dream!&quot; wasn't clear? :P<br /> <br /> Edit: I would be happy with Setites too, even if &quot;Ministry&quot; is a super-lame name for a clan :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Ever since the Followers of Set rebranded themselves as The Ministry, I can barely keep a straight face around them.&quot; - Ramona","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","name":"Ravnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15944_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T10:01:35-07:00","id":1298630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardestadtTheEvenYounger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1298609#post1298609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where are people seeing this info about Blood Resonance and the five clans?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The twitch stream last night talked about Blood Resonance. The Bloodlines 2 website has a clan section that has 5 plus a bonus, which have pictures if you click them that map to some of the clans. Tremere, Brujah and Ventrue are obvious; the others less so. The preview stuff that various reviewers got, and what the devs said, stated you start as a thin blood and choose a clan later. V5 explicitly allows Thin Bloods to diablerize a regular vampire to become a real vampire and join that clan, which is what most of us are guessing at. <br /> <br /> There was also a link and a citation of more clans being added via DLC, and all clan DLC would be free.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5704-thebiglarpnerd","name":"thebiglarpnerd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T10:02:51-07:00","id":1298632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardestadtTheEvenYounger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1298600#post1298600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I don't like this emphasis of &quot;Powers&quot; over Disciplines&quot;. Why can't we have Protean and then buy dots until we can use Mist Form?<br /> This game system seems &quot;vampiric&quot; yes, but not specifically Masquerade, do you understand?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Because you're playing a Thin Blood, and their powers work differently for V5. Plus, gamification and creation of custom mechanics to make ti work in a video game setting. Assumably when you get your full clan you'll get more traditional Disciplines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5704-thebiglarpnerd","name":"thebiglarpnerd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T10:06:16-07:00","id":1298635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardestadtTheEvenYounger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1298609#post1298609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where are people seeing this info about Blood Resonance and the five clans?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a Kotaku article where their reporter apparently got more access than the crowd at the announcement including getting to see a pre-alpha build of a level, and some of the features people are discussion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1298617#post1298617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mass Embrace is an easy way to get away with the Sire stuff, much like in the first bloodlines. Too bad, but also different Sire plots for different clans would have been an hassle and so it's an understandable choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh?<br /> <br /> Dragon Age: Origins came out over 8 years ago, with a multitude of different opening sections that varied on sex, race, and origin selection when you combined all of them, that has some impact on the game, but major impact on the ending.<br /> <br /> The idea that this is too hard now seems pretty questionable to me. It might not be worth it for the game, but none of us know enough about the game to know if it would add to it or not. The arguments against it in the later DA games is that as sequels the introduction aspect is less important, and DA 2 and DA I had tighter narratives without having to hedge as much to adapt to all the different origins.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And the Thin Blood thing is probably a way to get the average player through a long tutorial and then giving the choice of a clan not much later into the game. Like, one or two hours into it.<br /> Terrible for veteran players, but probably a good choice in favor of the newcomers. </div> </div> </div>It's terrible for veteran players (though really... it's 2019... making a tutorial that people don't hate to play or isn't just optional? Get out of AAA game design if you can't)... and it's not great for new players that Paradox wants to invest in the setting.<br /> <br /> Bloodlines 1 did a good job of balancing videogame concerns, with making something that was in-line enough, and familiar enough, to the TT RPG that people that got into VtM through it generally knew what they were looking at. Bloodlines 2 seems to be ignoring that concern and I'm not sure it's going to be a good thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T10:15:54-07:00","id":1298639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thebiglarpnerd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1298630#post1298630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Bloodlines 2 website has a clan section that has 5 plus a bonus, which have pictures if you click them that map to some of the clans. Tremere, Brujah and Ventrue are obvious; the others less so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you but where? I just see &quot;stay tuned for more details.&quot;<br /> <br /> Edit: Wait, never you mind, I see it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23725,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","user":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","date":". 03-22-2019, 01:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T10:16:44-07:00","id":1298640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1298635#post1298635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh?<br /> <br /> Dragon Age: Origins came out over 8 years ago, with a multitude of different opening sections that varied on sex, race, and origin selection when you combined all of them, that has some impact on the game, but major impact on the ending.<br /> <br /> The idea that this is too hard now seems pretty questionable to me. It might not be worth it for the game, but none of us know enough about the game to know if it would add to it or not. The arguments against it in the later DA games is that as sequels the introduction aspect is less important, and DA 2 and DA I had tighter narratives without having to hedge as much to adapt to all the different origins.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't say it's too hard. But it's more work. That can be avoided. I don't know their budget, but more cinematics, more voice acting, more character design require more budget. So I understand why such content could be avoided.<br /> Honestly my first thought went to Dragon Age Origins too.<br /> But instead of using that kind of feature for the Clans I would use it for the mortal background of your character.<br /> At the third or fourth playthrough it kinda bothered me that the Bloodlines protagonist was basically without a past. It would be cool if you could decide who your character was before the embrace and that it could have some impact to the storyline.<br /> (yes I remember the girl that you meet in Hollywood. I'm not talking about such minutiae. Although they were nice minutiae)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Ever since the Followers of Set rebranded themselves as The Ministry, I can barely keep a straight face around them.&quot; - Ramona","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","name":"Ravnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15944_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T10:24:38-07:00","id":1298645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1298635#post1298635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's terrible for veteran players (though really... it's 2019... making a tutorial that people don't hate to play or isn't just optional? Get out of AAA game design if you can't)... and it's not great for new players that Paradox wants to invest in the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay... why is it &quot;terrible for veteran players&quot; again? I mean, was it terrible that Redemption set the main character's clan outright because the story it wanted to tell worked with exactly those NPCs?<br /> Just like in tabletop gaming, both branching narratives and railroading have their place. One allows greater player freedom, the other makes it far easier to spend all your time on stuff the player will actually get to experience.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1298635#post1298635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bloodlines 1 did a good job of balancing videogame concerns, with making something that was in-line enough, and familiar enough, to the TT RPG that people that got into VtM through it generally knew what they were looking at. Bloodlines 2 seems to be ignoring that concern and I'm not sure it's going to be a good thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which part so far implies that they're ignoring tabletop familiarity? I mean, they did go through the trouble to set up an ARG, using references from the V5 core book. Matthew Dawkins already mentioned on the V5 Discord that V5 and Bloodlines 2 were created side by side actually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T10:31:59-07:00","id":1298646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1298645#post1298645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which part so far implies that they're ignoring tabletop familiarity? I mean, they did go through the trouble to set up an ARG, using references from the V5 core book. Matthew Dawkins already mentioned on the V5 Discord that V5 and Bloodlines 2 were created side by side actually.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Powers&quot; instead of &quot;Disciplines&quot; does have me a bit concerned.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T10:33:05-07:00","id":1298649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1298645#post1298645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay... why is it &quot;terrible for veteran players&quot; again? I mean, was it terrible that Redemption set the main character's clan outright because the story it wanted to tell worked with exactly those NPCs?<br /> Just like in tabletop gaming, both branching narratives and railroading have their place. One allows greater player freedom, the other makes it far easier to spend all your time on stuff the player will actually get to experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's &quot;terrible&quot; because it's not a full character creation toolbox from minute one. Hence why a veteran would prefer otherwise imho.<br /> And hey, I liked Redemption storyline as much as... well, everyone really.<br /> But it wouldn't be Bloodlines 2 if the game would go that route, it would be... Redemption 2 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (which I'd play too by the way (but Tremere centered!))","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Ever since the Followers of Set rebranded themselves as The Ministry, I can barely keep a straight face around them.&quot; - Ramona","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","name":"Ravnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15944_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T10:40:41-07:00","id":1298652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1298645#post1298645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay... why is it &quot;terrible for veteran players&quot; again? I mean, was it terrible that Redemption set the main character's clan outright because the story it wanted to tell worked with exactly those NPCs?</div> </div> </div> </div>But it's not Redemption's approach either. You get to pick your Clan... later in game. It's not Thin-blood all the way from what we know so far. It you were just playing a Thin-blood the whole time and never got to be a member of a Clan it would be... an interesting choice for the game, but it would have more merit than trying to compromise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which part so far implies that they're ignoring tabletop familiarity? </div> </div> </div>All the gameplay previews so far?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T11:17:55-07:00","id":1298675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1298649#post1298649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's &quot;terrible&quot; because it's not a full character creation toolbox from minute one. Hence why a veteran would prefer otherwise imho.<br /> And hey, I liked Redemption storyline as much as... well, everyone really.<br /> But it wouldn't be Bloodlines 2 if the game would go that route, it would be... Redemption 2 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (which I'd play too by the way (but Tremere centered!))</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you think that the possible choice of a clan was what made Bloodlines Bloodlines? I would see it as at best a part of the whole package. And if we're actually diablerising our way into one of the clans, the choice becomes a lot more meaningful than that of Bloodlines 1 where your Sire was... not a part of the story at all, beyond &quot;he got dusted on the Prince's orders. Oops.&quot; Other than that, if you didn't choose Malkavian or Nosferatu, your Clan only influenced maybe a handful of conversation options, most of them cosmetic at best.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardestadtTheEvenYounger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1298646#post1298646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Powers&quot; instead of &quot;Disciplines&quot; does have me a bit concerned.</div> </div> </div> </div>You do know that both terms exist in VtM terminology, right? Dominate is the Discipline, Mesmerize is a Power.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1298652#post1298652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it's not Redemption's approach either. You get to pick your Clan... later in game. It's not Thin-blood all the way from what we know so far. It you were just playing a Thin-blood the whole time and never got to be a member of a Clan it would be... an interesting choice for the game, but it would have more merit than trying to compromise.</div> </div> </div> </div>How so? Diablerising your way into a Clan is exactly how a Thinblood story might go according to the V5 rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1298652#post1298652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All the gameplay previews so far?</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you like one or two?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3118,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","user":"Cifer","date":". 03-22-2019, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T11:23:59-07:00","id":1298677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1298652#post1298652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But it's not Redemption's approach either. You get to pick your Clan... later in game. It's not Thin-blood all the way from what we know so far. It you were just playing a Thin-blood the whole time and never got to be a member of a Clan it would be... an interesting choice for the game, but it would have more merit than trying to compromise.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> All the gameplay previews so far?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I deeply hope that's true about picking your clan. Not sure if the free running action from the trailer is actually in the game, but it would make playing a Nosferatu a lot more fun than just slinking around alleyways with Obfuscate turned on.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> Just checked the site and found this<br /> <br /> <b>Blood in the Streets: </b>As one of the few free agents in town, you will choose a side and play an important role in the factional war for control of the blood trade. But can your allies answer why you were made, who's pulling the strings, and who your real enemies are? Or will you be more concerned with what you can do to get ahead among the vampire elite? The choice is yours.<br /> <br /> <b>Does this mean I can join the Sabbat!?</b> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-22-2019, 02:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T11:48:36-07:00","id":1298691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thebiglarpnerd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1298630#post1298630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The Bloodlines 2 website has a clan section that has 5 plus a bonus, which have pictures if you click them that map to some of the clans. Tremere, Brujah and Ventrue are obvious; the others less so.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm seeing one picture that looks like an updated version of Strauss' room, and then another that looks like some kind of magic sigil has been painted on the ground in blood. One of these is obviously Tremere, but the other one could possibly be Toreador. Second clan from the right could either be Malkavian or Nosferatu, since it looks like both an insane aslyum, as well as a sewer system. I can't tell what the final one is, but I'm going to guess that it might be Assamites, if this is taking place during 5th edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T12:08:45-07:00","id":1298696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1298675#post1298675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do know that both terms exist in VtM terminology, right? Dominate is the Discipline, Mesmerize is a Power.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a matter of terminology. In Bloodlines, you selected a clan and received access to the signature Disciplines those clans possessed in VtM. Admittedly, they had to be a bit altered in order to be useful to the game (Unlike in Redemption) but if you were a Gangrel, for instance, you got Animalism, Protean and Fortitude, each with five levels of strength. That is faithfulness to the tabletop.<br /> Right now, what the interviews and the gameplay previews seem to imply, is that, as a Thin Blood, you'll have access to generic vampiric powers that you could find in &quot;Dark&quot; or &quot;Vampyr&quot; rather than the Disciplines we know from VtM.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T12:50:43-07:00","id":1298709,"title":"","content":"Not happy to hear that Cara Ellison is on the writing team, but I'm stoked about Mitsoda and Avellone's involvement, so I think it will be okay.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T12:58:02-07:00","id":1298712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1298675#post1298675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think that the possible choice of a clan was what made Bloodlines Bloodlines?</div> </div> </div> </div>Alone, no.<br /> <br /> But if you consider how much the VtMB fan community considers the unofficial patches and mods to turn the good story/bad play original game into the 'real' experience and how much work went into things like adding more character creation options at start, or designing playable versions of other Clans (even if not functional in the main game)? I think it matters. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And if we're actually diablerising our way into one of the clans, the choice becomes a lot more meaningful than that of Bloodlines 1 where your Sire was... not a part of the story at all, beyond &quot;he got dusted on the Prince's orders. Oops.&quot; Other than that, if you didn't choose Malkavian or Nosferatu, your Clan only influenced maybe a handful of conversation options, most of them cosmetic at best. </div> </div> </div>Shovelhead + Diab into a Clan doesn't exactly spell out a compelling arc. It seems like it would end up being, &quot;And then you spend the rest of your game running from hit squads.&quot;<br /> <br /> I think a lot of VtMB fans would like more depth to character creation and impact on the game, not less. Esp. if Clans are going to be DLC.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You do know that both terms exist in VtM terminology, right? Dominate is the Discipline, Mesmerize is a Power. </div> </div> </div>Please tell me where in VtM I invest in Chiropteran to glide/fly, or Mentalism to gain telekinesis, or Nebulism to turn into mist?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How so? </div> </div> </div>It's character creation via tutorial at that point though. You're basically not finished 'making' your character until you get past the opening part and join a full proper Clan. It's not a bad overall videogame design thing, but it's not going to feel like a thinblood gaining a Clan by force story from VtM.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Could you like one or two? </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what you're asking here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T13:03:27-07:00","id":1298714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1298709#post1298709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not happy to hear that Cara Ellison is on the writing team, but I'm stoked about Mitsoda and Avellone's involvement, so I think it will be okay.</div> </div> </div> </div>What has Cara Ellison written?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T13:08:50-07:00","id":1298718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=g8qsxNt3f0Y\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=g8qsxNt3f0Y\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=g8qsxNt3f0Y\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=g8qsxNt3f0Y </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Brian, the lead narrator sounds a lot like the voice of the news anchor in bloodlines","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1440-lordofash","name":"LordOfAsh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1440_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T13:09:13-07:00","id":1298719,"title":"","content":"Hurray! I hope I'll be able to play it on my computer as well. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But please, let us one day also have a new Dark Ages Vampire game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T13:09:17-07:00","id":1298720,"title":"","content":"Furthermore, I would like to add that this whole &quot;Thin Blood who Diablerizes his way into a clan&quot; was just avoidable.<br /> Unless there's a very good plot reason for it that we won't know until we actually play the game, I don't see how much would have been changed by giving us clans from the get go. It's not as if in Bloodlines you required a sire to teach you clan culture or Disciplines. The game just occasionally acknowledged you belonged to X clan and that was that.<br /> <br /> Presumably, the identity(ies) of our Sire becomes an important plot point later on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T13:10:20-07:00","id":1298721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardestadtTheEvenYounger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1298714#post1298714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What has Cara Ellison written?</div> </div> </div> </div>Search her up. Not going to get into it here.<br /> <br /> I've got too much respect for Randy to get into a shit show.<br /> <br /> Suffice to say, I'm still very much excited for Bloodlines 2. Just got a bit of caution, is all.<br /> <br /> <br /> I've always said that we would never see another game like Bloodlines ever again. I'm pretty sure I'm still right on that, but that doesn't mean I won't take a sequel, filled with some vampires and perhaps a good story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T13:12:37-07:00","id":1298722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1298675#post1298675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think that the possible choice of a clan was what made Bloodlines Bloodlines?</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said that. My statement is that it would feel odd if in the sequel of that specific game that specific feature would be absent<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1298721#post1298721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always said that we would never see another game like Bloodlines ever again. I'm pretty sure I'm still right on that, but that doesn't mean I won't take a sequel, filled with some vampires and perhaps a good story.</div> </div> </div> </div>When we all have become so pessimistic? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Ever since the Followers of Set rebranded themselves as The Ministry, I can barely keep a straight face around them.&quot; - Ramona","edited":{"userid":15944,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","user":"Ravnos","date":". 03-22-2019, 04:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","name":"Ravnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15944_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T13:15:24-07:00","id":1298724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1298721#post1298721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Search her up. Not going to get into it here.<br /> <br /> I've got too much respect for Randy to get into a shit show.<br /> <br /> Suffice to say, I'm still very much excited for Bloodlines 2. Just got a bit of caution, is all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you Pm me?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T13:35:56-07:00","id":1298731,"title":"","content":"From what I've seen so far, everyone working on the project is great. Really don't understand the negativity about certain peeps (although I'm sure I could guess a few reasons). Cautiously optimistic because of the association with V5, but a lot of V5's problems won't have a negative impact on a video game (video games can handle complexities that work really poorly in tabletop).<br /> <br /> As for &quot;choosing your clan&quot; later on I imagine it will be a case of your actions leading to you discovering who your sire was, BUT your in-game selection will essentially effect what the &quot;truth&quot; is. So at the beginning your sire is a total mystery, but if you want to be playing as a Brujah down the line you'll discover that your sire was a Brujah (with you possibly making some sort of selection via a dialogue choice before this revelation).<br /> <br /> I doubt it will be a case of you joining a clan via Diablerie or anything like that! Sounds kind of extreme to be honest.<br /> <br /> EDIT: <span style=\"color:#14171A\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">https://twitter.com/9_volt_/status/1109185307918979072 </span></span></span> when The Discourse (TM) is &lt;3&lt;3&lt;3<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 03-22-2019, 04:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T13:42:56-07:00","id":1298734,"title":"","content":"re: &quot;power&quot; vs. &quot;discipline&quot;?<br /> <br /> I'm taking a deep breath and moving on to other things.<br /> <br /> The terms are a classic distinction without a difference at this point. It could be as small a difference as that &quot;power&quot; has fewer letters and fits better in text boxes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T13:53:11-07:00","id":1298737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1298712#post1298712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alone, no.<br /> <br /> But if you consider how much the VtMB fan community considers the unofficial patches and mods to turn the good story/bad play original game into the 'real' experience and how much work went into things like adding more character creation options at start, or designing playable versions of other Clans (even if not functional in the main game)? I think it matters.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Shovelhead + Diab into a Clan doesn't exactly spell out a compelling arc. It seems like it would end up being, &quot;And then you spend the rest of your game running from hit squads.&quot;<br /> <br /> I think a lot of VtMB fans would like more depth to character creation and impact on the game, not less. Esp. if Clans are going to be DLC.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I've read, DLC clans will be free. Also, clans being DLC in my opinion massively points to being more than a set of stats and abilities. And finally, we don't know enough about the power structures <i>or</i> the plot to know how it will work out. We don't know about the Setting of Seattle. Perhaps you take part in a blood hunt and noone's going to miss your victim. Perhaps you'll mostly move among Anarchs, who, according to Anarchs Unbound tolerate Diablerie to a greater degree than the Cam does. In short: Why think of the ways it won't work instead of the ways it might make for a compelling story?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1298712#post1298712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please tell me where in VtM I invest in Chiropteran to glide/fly, or Mentalism to gain telekinesis, or Nebulism to turn into mist?</div> </div> </div> </div>Chiropteran would be Gargoyle Flight, Mentalism sounds like Movement of the Mind and Nebulism like Protean, though admittedly at a level unlikely to be seen for a fledgling. V5 established that lots of vampires call disciplines lots of different things - that an uneducated mass embrace victim would make up their own cool names for it, well, why not?<br /> I must say I'm more than willing to discard the exact order of powers (&quot;You can't have Mesmerize if you don't have either Compel or Clouded Mind!&quot;) as long as the end result carries the feel of VtM.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1298712#post1298712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure what you're asking here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Typo - I meant &quot;link&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardestadtTheEvenYounger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1298720#post1298720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Furthermore, I would like to add that this whole &quot;Thin Blood who Diablerizes his way into a clan&quot; was just avoidable.<br /> Unless there's a very good plot reason for it that we won't know until we actually play the game, I don't see how much would have been changed by giving us clans from the get go. It's not as if in Bloodlines you required a sire to teach you clan culture or Disciplines. The game just occasionally acknowledged you belonged to X clan and that was that.<br /> <br /> Presumably, the identity(ies) of our Sire becomes an important plot point later on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, that's already been hinted at. The background of the Mass Embrace seems like it will be more important than the Embrace of the BL1 protagonist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T14:09:51-07:00","id":1298739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1298731#post1298731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I've seen so far, everyone working on the project is great. Really don't understand the negativity about certain peeps (although I'm sure I could guess a few reasons). Cautiously optimistic because of the association with V5, but a lot of V5's problems won't have a negative impact on a video game (video games can handle complexities that work really poorly in tabletop).<br /> <br /> As for &quot;choosing your clan&quot; later on I imagine it will be a case of your actions leading to you discovering who your sire was, BUT your in-game selection will essentially effect what the &quot;truth&quot; is. So at the beginning your sire is a total mystery, but if you want to be playing as a Brujah down the line you'll discover that your sire was a Brujah (with you possibly making some sort of selection via a dialogue choice before this revelation).<br /> <br /> I doubt it will be a case of you joining a clan via Diablerie or anything like that! Sounds kind of extreme to be honest.<br /> <br /> EDIT: <span style=\"color:#14171A\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">https://twitter.com/9_volt_/status/1109185307918979072 </span></span></span> when The Discourse (TM) is &lt;3&lt;3&lt;3</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's a more desirable choice but that only work if the PC is a Caitiff not a thin-blood.<br /> <br /> Or at least a 14th generation or higher thin-blood since as far as pre-V5 canon is concerned as Caitiff and thin-blood were different flaws that could be combined or not however 14th generation were always both with no hope to escape their weakness without diablerie.<br /> <br /> Honestly I think the premise work better if the PC is a Caitiff and is not thin blooded. It's far simpler and create less problems altough there are still some issues with going the &quot;discovery&quot; route.<br /> <br /> Altough there are still some possibilities of playing a thin-blood and not having to resort to diablerie:<br /> - Some Assamite use &quot;that&quot; ritual to lower your generation. Not the most exciting thing that could happen but it works I guess ?<br /> - You are simply of lower generation than 14th altough still a thin-blood. So you can have a clan. Problem: You remain a thin-blood with all it entails.<br /> - You are of 14th generation and your blood &quot;thickens&quot;. I think that happened in Becket's diary when a 14th generation became a Lasombra like this. You probably remain a thin-blood tough.<br /> <br /> Of course those solutions only really work in pre-V5 as being a thin-blood in V5 is to be a different beast than a normal vampire. For exemple you cannot learn any discipline if you are a V5 thin-blood (except if you picked a merit for it) wherehas in pre-V5 you just have level restrictions.<br /> And of courst &quot;that&quot; ritual does not exist in V5 as far as I know.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","name":"Morbus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T14:25:02-07:00","id":1298745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1298731#post1298731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for &quot;choosing your clan&quot; later on I imagine it will be a case of your actions leading to you discovering who your sire was, BUT your in-game selection will essentially effect what the &quot;truth&quot; is. So at the beginning your sire is a total mystery, but if you want to be playing as a Brujah down the line you'll discover that your sire was a Brujah (with you possibly making some sort of selection via a dialogue choice before this revelation).<br /> <br /> I doubt it will be a case of you joining a clan via Diablerie or anything like that! Sounds kind of extreme to be honest.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd prefer that but it doesn't really work for those poor Nosferats tough, does it?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T14:26:36-07:00","id":1298746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardestadtTheEvenYounger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1298745#post1298745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd prefer that but it doesn't really work for those poor Nosferats tough, does it?</div> </div> </div> </div>That... is a very good point. Hmm.<br /> <br /> If the Nosferatu are DLC, then maybe they'll be a New Game + thing? Honestly I think Nosferatu would be PERFECT for a New Game +.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T14:44:07-07:00","id":1298751,"title":"","content":"Slightly off topic but I've always wondered why folks see VTM:B as so integral to VtM that they want tabletop tie ins and all the rest? I mean I was playing VtM for over a decade before VtM:B came out so it had literally no effect on me except ' a neat tie in CRPG that my computer would die if it tried to run.....also so buggy as to be almost unplayable'.<br /> <br /> Just curious as it seems to be somewhat integral to some of the louder voices heres idea of what VtM is whereas for me it was the equivalent of a VtM keychain in regards to the actual game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T15:18:54-07:00","id":1298758,"title":"","content":"I would actually love to see the cutscene that plays out when your Thin Blood becomes a member of clan Malkavian.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Welcome to the clan, brother! You'll want to strap yourself in, because this ride's break lines have been cut!&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T15:24:29-07:00","id":1298759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1298751#post1298751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Slightly off topic but I've always wondered why folks see VTM:B as so integral to VtM that they want tabletop tie ins and all the rest? I mean I was playing VtM for over a decade before VtM:B came out so it had literally no effect on me except ' a neat tie in CRPG that my computer would die if it tried to run.....also so buggy as to be almost unplayable'.<br /> <br /> Just curious as it seems to be somewhat integral to some of the louder voices heres idea of what VtM is whereas for me it was the equivalent of a VtM keychain in regards to the actual game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably not the right person to talk about this, since I personally haven't even played the first Bloodlines game, but: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Bloodlines was many people's first exposure to VtM. That it was what initially hooked people into the setting, and prompted them to look further by picking up the TRPG.</li> <li>Bloodlines being the only VtM content that had people going. Game was released the same year that the WoD ended. And since this was a time where no one knew that a V20 was ever going to be a thing, and the initial controversies and backlash against Vampire the Requiem, Bloodlines was all people had.</li> <li>The simple merit that, in the time period it was released (and by extension now) video games received more coverage then TRPGs in the geek-sphere. That to the mainstream geek crowd, this was the most they were ever going to know about it. Same with Shadowrun, how many not immediately in the TRPG community only know it for the SNES game, or more recently, the Shadowrun Returns trilogy of games.</li> </ol><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T15:25:42-07:00","id":1298760,"title":"","content":"I am pretty sure in v5 you can just spend xp to increase blood potency, that is represented by the blood thickening over time at different degrees. Generation and potency are separate things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T15:29:18-07:00","id":1298762,"title":"","content":"So, probably zero chance of an ST mode like in Redemption, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T15:31:00-07:00","id":1298766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardestadtTheEvenYounger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1298762#post1298762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, probably zero chance of an ST mode like in Redemption, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>What's an st mode?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T15:33:19-07:00","id":1298768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1298766#post1298766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What's an st mode?</div> </div> </div> </div>It allows for a Storyteller to host games. My friends and I have been using it for years.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=B-gAsd-cDag\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=B-gAsd-cDag\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=B-gAsd-cDag\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=B-gAsd-cDag </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T15:34:42-07:00","id":1298770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardestadtTheEvenYounger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1298768#post1298768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It allows for a Storyteller to host games. My friends and I have been using it for years.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=B-gAsd-cDag\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=B-gAsd-cDag</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Cool. Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T17:28:36-07:00","id":1298795,"title":"","content":"Personally on the whole Thin-blood into clan thing. I would play it as your character, after going through the mass embrace and waking up thin-blooded, your character is given a run-down of the members of the Sabbat pack responsible for the embrace, (each of whom are conveniently Antribu of the available clans) and depending on who you pick to &quot;recognize&quot; you get a flash-back remembering that particular one jumping and embracing you. Later on, you focus down on dealing with that vampire in particular, which culminates in you diablerizing them in revenge. Ideally this would be largely a prolonged tutorial before the game properly begins, with your character having to rise up in kindred society despite the dubious circumstances of their embrace and rise. (The sixth bonus clan option is essentially hard mode of choosing not to diablerize your sire and sticking as thin-blood for the rest of the game.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24666,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24666-ravian","user":"Ravian","date":". 03-22-2019, 08:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24666-ravian","name":"Ravian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T18:08:57-07:00","id":1298806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardestadtTheEvenYounger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1298696#post1298696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not a matter of terminology. In Bloodlines, you selected a clan and received access to the signature Disciplines those clans possessed in VtM. Admittedly, they had to be a bit altered in order to be useful to the game (Unlike in Redemption) but if you were a Gangrel, for instance, you got Animalism, Protean and Fortitude, each with five levels of strength. That is faithfulness to the tabletop.<br /> Right now, what the interviews and the gameplay previews seem to imply, is that, as a Thin Blood, you'll have access to generic vampiric powers that you could find in &quot;Dark&quot; or &quot;Vampyr&quot; rather than the Disciplines we know from VtM.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> From what I've seen in videos so far, the player attacked somebody with bats (typical Animalism technique), and used telekinesis to retrieve a sledge hammer (which can be a form of Thaumaturgy). Would hardly call those generic, since they actually exist in the table top.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1298795#post1298795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally on the whole Thin-blood into clan thing. I would play it as your character, after going through the mass embrace and waking up thin-blooded, your character is given a run-down of the members of the Sabbat pack responsible for the embrace, (each of whom are conveniently Antribu of the available clans) and depending on who you pick to &quot;recognize&quot; you get a flash-back remembering that particular one jumping and embracing you. Later on, you focus down on dealing with that vampire in particular, which culminates in you diablerizing them in revenge. Ideally this would be largely a prolonged tutorial before the game properly begins, with your character having to rise up in kindred society despite the dubious circumstances of their embrace and rise. (The sixth bonus clan option is essentially hard mode of choosing not to diablerize your sire and sticking as thin-blood for the rest of the game.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That might have made sense, if they didn't promise future clans as free DLC. My personal take on it is that your heritage are going to be left a mystery for most of the early section of the game. Then, after a story driven Diablerie attempt, your character increases their generation to a point where your clan features begin to manifest, which is where you finally pick which clan you are.<br /> <br /> You'll probably never even meet your sire, as that would require rewriting the game's story every time a new clan comes out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-22-2019, 09:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T19:03:35-07:00","id":1298817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1298806#post1298806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> From what I've seen in videos so far, the player attacked somebody with bats (typical Animalism technique), and used telekinesis to retrieve a sledge hammer (which can be a form of Thaumaturgy). Would hardly call those generic, since they actually exist in the table top.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of VtM's Disciplines come from generic vampire powers as popularized by books and movies. Control of animals, invisibility, strength of 10 men, telekinesis.<br /> If turning into mist is part of a line abilities that include growing claws, turning into animals and seeing in the dark, well that's Protean. If not, it's a generic vampire power.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T22:58:09-07:00","id":1298855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1298806#post1298806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That might have made sense, if they didn't promise future clans as free DLC. My personal take on it is that your heritage are going to be left a mystery for most of the early section of the game. Then, after a story driven Diablerie attempt, your character increases their generation to a point where your clan features begin to manifest, which is where you finally pick which clan you are.<br /> <br /> You'll probably never even meet your sire, as that would require rewriting the game's story every time a new clan comes out.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fair, but considering they are likely going to be changes made to the story itself to incorporate the new clans (since they seem to imply a branching path where clan choice will have story implications aside from mechanics, it might not be inconceivable to alter the introduction to include additional members. Really it all depends entirely on how much the sire specifically featured in the game compared to the gang themselves. Have recognizing be something like a set of photographs put together by an ally who's been working to piece together the gang's identity, and add a new one whenever a new clan is introduced. Have a new mission for each as a sort of &quot;introduction to the clan&quot; that gives you a feel for their place in kindred society and abilities while you're tracking down and fighting them.<br /> <br /> Granted I don't know nearly enough about video games to say how reasonably conceivable all that is for DLC content of course, but that's just what I would do if I ran the zoo.<br /> <br /> <br /> Side note on generic thin-blood powers: We probably shouldn't forget that Thin-bloods have alchemy. I can't imagine they'd ignore all of that for a game that's so thin-blood focused. (Actually I'd bet some good money that the dude squeezing that bag of blood into a cup that we saw in the trailer is going to be our resident NPC alchemist, that we can bring ingredients to for new formulae.) Heck I'm pretty sure that telekinesis with the hammer was actually a textbook example of the alchemy formulae Far Reach.<br /> <br /> I imagine that thin blood alchemy will be your avenue to do a little experimentation with the lower levels of the disciplines before you settle on a clan to focus in on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24666-ravian","name":"Ravian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T03:02:46-07:00","id":1298890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1298855#post1298855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Side note on generic thin-blood powers: We probably shouldn't forget that Thin-bloods have alchemy. I can't imagine they'd ignore all of that for a game that's so thin-blood focused. (Actually I'd bet some good money that the dude squeezing that bag of blood into a cup that we saw in the trailer is going to be our resident NPC alchemist, that we can bring ingredients to for new formulae.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure about that - one of the press releases says we have a rather pathetic vampiric neighbour who tries as hard as possible to stay out of the whole politics business and survives by blood bags. It looks like that might be him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T15:17:50-07:00","id":1299045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1298709#post1298709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not happy to hear that Cara Ellison is on the writing team, but I'm stoked about Mitsoda and Avellone's involvement, so I think it will be okay.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Honestly looking at the worrying things we might expect from this game, Cara Ellison isn't on the list at all.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">&quot;I'm a gamer. I'm conservative. We exist.&quot;<br /> <br /> Oh I see now. Good day to you sir. Good day.</span> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> <br /> </span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T15:26:09-07:00","id":1299048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardestadtTheEvenYounger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1298817#post1298817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Most of VtM's Disciplines come from generic vampire powers as popularized by books and movies. Control of animals, invisibility, strength of 10 men, telekinesis.<br /> If turning into mist is part of a line abilities that include growing claws, turning into animals and seeing in the dark, well that's Protean. If not, it's a generic vampire power.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah but at least call them by their iconic signature names, call them &quot;Disciplines&quot; not &quot;Powers&quot;. Language is important, especially when you try to separate your IP from the flood of generic vampire movies and video games out there. Vampire has more than enough to stand out and be unique, why do they need to make it generic, especially when they're trying to pander to the fans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T15:28:50-07:00","id":1299049,"title":"","content":"Here's how it's going to go: the game will be another generic video game power trip. It will ignore the personal drama and politics that made the Pen and Paper so compelling in favor of what the &quot;gamer crowd&quot; want, because that shit sells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T16:13:54-07:00","id":1299068,"title":"","content":"Six clans rather than seven? The V5 core included the full Camarilla seven, so why cut one out, I wonder?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/100-jezmiller","name":"JezMiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T16:27:37-07:00","id":1299072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JezMiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299068#post1299068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Six clans rather than seven? The V5 core included the full Camarilla seven, so why cut one out, I wonder?</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume since they're adding more later on, they're going to focus on the ones that are relatively similar in playstyle first and save the clans that really change the game (like Nosferatu and Malkavian) for later. (Also I think that the sixth &quot;bonus&quot; clan may be remaining as a thin-blood or possibly caitiff.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24666-ravian","name":"Ravian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T17:41:53-07:00","id":1299083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299072#post1299072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I assume since they're adding more later on, they're going to focus on the ones that are relatively similar in playstyle first and save the clans that really change the game (like Nosferatu and Malkavian) for later. (Also I think that the sixth &quot;bonus&quot; clan may be remaining as a thin-blood or possibly caitiff.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They said they want to handle mental illness with sensitivity, so likely Malkavian won't be initially playable, and it won't be an over the top fishmalk ala Bloodlines 1 when/if it becomes playable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5704-thebiglarpnerd","name":"thebiglarpnerd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T19:48:01-07:00","id":1299111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299045#post1299045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Honestly looking at the worrying things we might expect from this game, Cara Ellison isn't on the list at all.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">&quot;I'm a gamer. I'm conservative. We exist.&quot;<br /> <br /> Oh I see now. Good day to you sir. Good day.</span> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>lol Uh...okay?<br /> <br /> I'm sure you'll be fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":95,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","user":"Fat Larry","date":". 03-23-2019, 10:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T19:51:57-07:00","id":1299113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299049#post1299049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's how it's going to go: the game will be another generic video game power trip. It will ignore the personal drama and politics that made the Pen and Paper so compelling in favor of what the <b>&quot;gamer crowd&quot; want, because that shit sells.</b></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hell yeah! Bloodlines sold millions so i'm sure they're going right for the same jugular!<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> <br /> Well, at least you waited a full 24 hours before completely shitting on a game about a year away from release. lol <br /> <br /> <br /> Unlike your judgment of me(which you're basing on my sig, because hooray?), I have honest to goodness reasons why I'm not a giant fan of hers. Regardless, I still think the game is going to be fantastic.<br /> <br /> <br /> In other news, Mitsoda went on Twitter today to confirm that the game WILL be about personal drama; <span style=\"color:#14171A\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">with reactive story/dialogue, a branching narrative, and tons of characters.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":95,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","user":"Fat Larry","date":". 03-23-2019, 10:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T20:37:06-07:00","id":1299123,"title":"","content":"They've said the plot will be over who controls Seattle's Blood Trade. Interesting as that might mean the Circulatory System rather than Second Inquisition and Beckoning will be THE major 5E element.<br /> <br /> Surprising.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T20:40:37-07:00","id":1299125,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.vg247.com/2019/03/21/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2-political-character-creator/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.vg247.com/2019/03/21/vam...acter-creator/</a><br /> <br /> I like the descriptions here.<br /> <br /> As for Cara Ellison, I really liked<b> Dishonored 2 </b>so I don't see anything wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-23-2019, 11:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T21:01:32-07:00","id":1299127,"title":"","content":"I keep wanting to read &quot;Hardsuit Labs&quot; as &quot;Hardestadt Labs.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299123#post1299123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They've said the plot will be over who controls Seattle's Blood Trade. Interesting as that might mean the Circulatory System rather than Second Inquisition and Beckoning will be THE major 5E element.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is probably easier to explain the Blood Trade, and to keep the relevant violent melodrama contained to Seattle, than it would be for the Beckoning or the SI. I mean, why should the PC care if a bunch of pissy elders shuffle off to the Middle East? And if the SI is coming to town, a reasonable PC would want to leave town - which means it stops being in Seattle.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":". 03-24-2019, 12:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T22:30:59-07:00","id":1299139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299049#post1299049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's how it's going to go: the game will be another generic video game power trip. It will ignore the personal drama and politics that made the Pen and Paper so compelling in favor of what the &quot;gamer crowd&quot; want, because that shit sells.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Steam forums are a cluster fuck of threads begging the developers to not fill the game with 5th Edition's modern political crap, and just give us a traditional World of Darkness story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T22:38:50-07:00","id":1299140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thebiglarpnerd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299083#post1299083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> They said they want to handle mental illness with sensitivity, so likely Malkavian won't be initially playable, and it won't be an over the top fishmalk ala Bloodlines 1 when/if it becomes playable.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> According to their website, the 6 clans are Toreador, Ventrue, Brujah, Tremere, Malkavian, and either Nosferatu, or Assamite.<br /> <br /> The Malkavian picture shows up in the trailer, and is clearly some kind of prison / asylum type area. As for the final picture, there's a lot of reading material stacked around the room, and it looks to be some kind of basement dwelling. Which is why I can't figure out which clan it represents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T01:56:01-07:00","id":1299148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299139#post1299139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Steam forums are a cluster fuck of threads begging the developers to not fill the game with 5th Edition's modern political crap, and just give us a traditional World of Darkness story.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is a &quot;traditional World of Darkness story&quot;? World of Darkness has been unabashedly political from the start. We even have a whole clan of radical political activists, look at the Brujah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T01:59:18-07:00","id":1299149,"title":"","content":"I can't even understand people who want a Vampire: The Masquerade game that is politics free, like what? Have any of you ever played any edition of the tabletop?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T02:02:13-07:00","id":1299150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299113#post1299113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Hell yeah! Bloodlines sold millions so i'm sure they're going right for the same jugular!<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> <br /> Well, at least you waited a full 24 hours before completely shitting on a game about a year away from release. lol <br /> <br /> <br /> Unlike your judgment of me(which you're basing on my sig, because hooray?), I have honest to goodness reasons why I'm not a giant fan of hers. Regardless, I still think the game is going to be fantastic.<br /> <br /> <br /> In other news, Mitsoda went on Twitter today to confirm that the game WILL be about personal drama; <span style=\"color:#14171A\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">with reactive story/dialogue, a branching narrative, and tons of characters.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Your optimism is making me optimistic. Let's just hope the game isn't a generic vampire game in the vein of Vampyr or Dark.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T02:28:54-07:00","id":1299154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299148#post1299148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What is a &quot;traditional World of Darkness story&quot;? World of Darkness has been unabashedly political from the start. We even have a whole clan of radical political activists, look at the Brujah.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, <b>vampire politics.</b> As in Machiavellian schemes for control over the city's territory and resources. Trying to usurp the power of those above you, and making pawns of those beneath you.<br /> <br /> Not politics about what gender pronouns you wish to go by, or about the current social climate happening in the middle east. We use role playing games to escape from reality, not be reminded of it.<br /> <br /> Plus, one of the people working on this game is spewing some bull crap about &quot;toxic masculinity&quot; being present in Bloodlines 1. No idea where she got that idea from, since I'm pretty sure the first game was equal opportunity for both genders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-24-2019, 05:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T02:39:54-07:00","id":1299156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299154#post1299154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yes, <b>vampire politics.</b> As in Machiavellian schemes for control over the city's territory and resources. Trying to usurp the power of those above you, and making pawns of those beneath you.<br /> <br /> Not politics about what gender pronouns you wish to go by, or about the current social climate happening in the middle east. We use role playing games to escape from reality, not be reminded of it.<br /> <br /> Plus, one of the people working on this game is spewing some bull crap about &amp;quot;toxic masculinity&amp;quot; being present in Bloodlines 1. No idea where she got that idea from, since I'm pretty sure the first game was equal opportunity for both genders.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampire politics and human politics go hand in hand too often for comfort. Vampires infiltrate high society to influence policies and protect the Masquerade, they involve themselves into civil rights groups and activism either to further their own ends or because they genuinely believe in the causes (see my Brujah argument).<br /> <br /> Also I don't understand the fuss about the gender pronoun customization. It's a cosmetic choice you choose for your character, just like their hair color or clothing style, you can just have your character be cis at character creation and forget you ever seen the slider.<br /> <br /> And Bloodlines 1 was sexist in some parts, let's be honest here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T02:41:06-07:00","id":1299157,"title":"","content":"Also the whole &quot;escapism&quot; thing is stupid. So many people want video games to be considered art, why not let them be art and allow video games to convey politics messages. Escapism is not art.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T03:12:17-07:00","id":1299159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299154#post1299154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, <b>vampire politics.</b> As in Machiavellian schemes for control over the city's territory and resources. Trying to usurp the power of those above you, and making pawns of those beneath you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, because young vs. old and Anarchs vs. Camarilla totally isn't a metaphor for actual political divides.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299154#post1299154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not politics about what gender pronouns you wish to go by, or about the current social climate happening in the middle east. We use role playing games to escape from reality, not be reminded of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You seem to be playing another Vampire than I did \u2013 compared to American rpgs of the time, Vampire was positively steeped in what is now called &quot;identity politics&quot; from day one, depicting unveiled homosexuality when the others were still very heteronormative. As for the middle east, did you have problems with seeing the cold war mirrored with Baba Yaga's Shadow Curtain and Brujah infiltrating the KGB? Or is it just bad when regions other than Europe and North America make an appearance ouside of being namedropped?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299154#post1299154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus, one of the people working on this game is spewing some bull crap about &quot;toxic masculinity&quot; being present in Bloodlines 1. No idea where she got that idea from, since I'm pretty sure the first game was equal opportunity for both genders.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh well, since I've already written the text for another site:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For the most simple example: Men aren't as sexualised as women, gay men don't exist.<br /> <br /> There are at least two major seductresses (Jeanette and VV), lots of female prostitutes and club-goers. Most of them are available for male and female player characters alike (because, as everyone knows, girl-on-girl is hot).<br /> The number of men that tried to seduce you and were halfway serious? One (Romero, if you're playing a female vampire).<br /> The number of men you could seduce that were conventionally attractive? Low, and all of them available only to a female character.<br /> In many cases, male-npc-seduction options worked on shlubs like Kilpatrik or Chunk who were played for laughs compared to the vamps Jeannette and VV. Was there even one middle-aged plain-looking lady that you could seduce?<br /> And while lots of women are bi (though I don't think any are actually lesbian, because hey, that would deny the male PC something), there is IIRC exactly one pair of male NPCs where one of them might possibly kinda sorta have been romantically interested in the other (Isaac Abrams to his childe). </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T03:32:18-07:00","id":1299161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299159#post1299159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are at least two major seductresses (Jeanette and VV), lots of female prostitutes and club-goers. Most of them are available for male and female player characters alike (because, as everyone knows, girl-on-girl is hot).<br /> The number of men that tried to seduce you and were halfway serious? One (Romero, if you're playing a female vampire).<br /> The number of men you could seduce that were conventionally attractive? Low, and all of them available only to a female character.<br /> In many cases, male-npc-seduction options worked on shlubs like Kilpatrik or Chunk who were played for laughs compared to the vamps Jeannette and VV. Was there even one middle-aged plain-looking lady that you could seduce?<br /> And while lots of women are bi (though I don't think any are actually lesbian, because hey, that would deny the male PC something), there is IIRC exactly one pair of male NPCs where one of them might possibly kinda sorta have been romantically interested in the other (Isaac Abrams to his childe).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>In addition, the only ghoul you get is female and is killed off near the end for emotional points. The only female toreador NPC is dressed in skimpy clothing (yes, I know she owns a strip club, but compare her to Isaac), no male strippers in sight, female armours are more skimpy than the male ones.<br /> <br /> It is a game from the 2004, so yeah the content is a bit dated. That is why updating it is just smart, the world has changed a -lot.-<br /> <br /> <br /> Personal things I want from the game? Actual role in the politics and actual vampire party members/allies. Bloodlines was amazing, but your character was still basically kept out of the meat of VtM.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T05:27:12-07:00","id":1299174,"title":"","content":"Plus there were mostly no female characters with any depth or any importance, and the ones who had importance had something else to hinder them. With the exception of Therese/VV (crazy as fuck) and Ming Xiao (a Kue-Jin and a Villain) the main &quot;roles&quot; in the society were male driven: Strauss, Nines, Jack,Lacroix,Gary, Bertram, Andrei,Isaac,Grouth and so on.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I think the best case scenario was the Giovanni's party: you had two women and two men you could discuss with.<br /> <br /> The two men were :<br /> 1) A buisness man of clear fame in trouble after a series a financial setback<br /> <br /> 2) A normal man anguished by the knowledge he was not a real giovanni, since his mother had an affair with someone.<br /> <br /> The two woman were:<br /> <br /> 1) A nymphomaniac who wanted to have sex in the mortuary of the Clan<br /> 2) A bad girl who got HIV from her crazy life of sex and drugs.<br /> <br /> So normal men...and SLUTS! Because WE like SLUTS. A woman to be interesting must be either a nymphomaniac or on drugs or a psycho.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 03-24-2019, 08:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T05:29:09-07:00","id":1299175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299161#post1299161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personal things I want from the game? Actual role in the politics and actual vampire party members/allies. Bloodlines was amazing, but your character was still basically kept out of the meat of VtM.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure about those. I mean, being part of a coterie is helpful, but gameplay with NPC allies can often feel clunky, so I see why they skipped out on it. And you had some allies, depending on who you supported - you could become buddies with the Anarchs, you could ally with Jeannette, Therese or both, you could become friends with the Nosferatu warren and VV...<br /> As for politics, those were absolutely involved in the game. Oftentimes, it was you getting manipulated as a pawn in someone else's scheme (first example: Jeanette asking you to hand over the Ocean House pendant), but in some others, you could throw a wrench in other people's plans, like deciding whether to kill the gargoyle to curry favor with Strauss or to help Abrams by convincing the stone guy to ally with the Anarchs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T05:46:44-07:00","id":1299179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299140#post1299140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> According to their website, the 6 clans are Toreador, Ventrue, Brujah, Tremere, Malkavian, and either Nosferatu, or Assamite.<br /> <br /> The Malkavian picture shows up in the trailer, and is clearly some kind of prison / asylum type area. As for the final picture, there's a lot of reading material stacked around the room, and it looks to be some kind of basement dwelling. Which is why I can't figure out which clan it represents.</div> </div> </div> </div>What no Gangrel? WTF!?!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2582-gangrel44","name":"Gangrel44","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T05:48:35-07:00","id":1299181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gangrel44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299179#post1299179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What no Gangrel? WTF!?!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Gangrels went Independent in Revisited's metaplot and are such in V5 to my knowledge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T05:54:26-07:00","id":1299186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gangrel44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299179#post1299179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What no Gangrel? WTF!?!</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, this is all massive amounts of guess-work right now, going from a set of pictures that maybe possibly kinda imply what clans might be in the game at launch. I'd suggest to just wait and see.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299181#post1299181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gangrels went Independent in Revisited's metaplot and are such in V5 to my knowledge.</div> </div> </div> </div>While that is true, they're still part of the Core 7 and Camarilla membership isn't exactly likely for a Thin-Blood anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T05:59:51-07:00","id":1299187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299186#post1299186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, this is all massive amounts of guess-work right now, going from a set of pictures that maybe possibly kinda imply what clans might be in the game at launch. I'd suggest to just wait and see.<br /> <br /> While that is true, they're still part of the Core 7 and Camarilla membership isn't exactly likely for a Thin-Blood anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>So it is. But I would presume that the game will still be a Camarilla and Anarch focused game as opposed to an Independent one. Hence I would think that its more likely that we'll get to see the Ministry than the Gangrel in the starting set of Clans.<br /> <br /> But I could be wrong, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T06:14:16-07:00","id":1299190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299161#post1299161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personal things I want from the game? Actual role in the politics and actual vampire party members/allies. Bloodlines was amazing, but your character was still basically kept out of the meat of VtM.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, please. Also, more schmoozing with useful mortals like contacts in the police for cover ups, the media for cover overs, angry mobs to provide distraction etc. VtM, including V5, describes the spheres of influence that clans typically have quite explicitly and I'd like get some of that instead of doing everything myself and depending on mortals' security blind spots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T06:18:47-07:00","id":1299191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299175#post1299175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure about those. I mean, being part of a coterie is helpful, but gameplay with NPC allies can often feel clunky, so I see why they skipped out on it. And you had some allies, depending on who you supported - you could become buddies with the Anarchs, you could ally with Jeannette, Therese or both, you could become friends with the Nosferatu warren and VV...<br /> As for politics, those were absolutely involved in the game. Oftentimes, it was you getting manipulated as a pawn in someone else's scheme (first example: Jeanette asking you to hand over the Ocean House pendant), but in some others, you could throw a wrench in other people's plans, like deciding whether to kill the gargoyle to curry favor with Strauss or to help Abrams by convincing the stone guy to ally with the Anarchs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, Redemption had a coterie and the story worked fine with it. In 2004, Bloodlines not having allies made sense as it was actually the very -first- game that used Half-Life 2's engine.<br /> <br /> But what I meant is that our PC could be actually a full member of the Camarilla, with peers to speak to and compete with. Rather than a glorified FedEx for elders of each faction. As much as I love Bloodlines, the fact is that it was very lonely as the PC was basically a pariah leashed by LaCroix. They met no fellow young vampires nor really got into the general life of a regular vampire. At most they were closer to humans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T06:38:41-07:00","id":1299195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299140#post1299140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> According to their website, the 6 clans are Toreador, Ventrue, Brujah, Tremere, Malkavian, and either Nosferatu, or Assamite.<br /> <br /> The Malkavian picture shows up in the trailer, and is clearly some kind of prison / asylum type area. As for the final picture, there's a lot of reading material stacked around the room, and it looks to be some kind of basement dwelling. Which is why I can't figure out which clan it represents.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, bugger. I had a nasty feeling that the Gangrel would lose out. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Oh, well. Early days, and I'm sure there'll be expansions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/100-jezmiller","name":"JezMiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T06:48:17-07:00","id":1299198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299156#post1299156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also I don't understand the fuss about the gender pronoun customization. It's a cosmetic choice you choose for your character, just like their hair color or clothing style, you can just have your character be cis at character creation and forget you ever seen the slider.<br /> <br /> And Bloodlines 1 was sexist in some parts, let's be honest here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see much of a problem with that, either. And I apologize if my previous statement gave that impression (I wrote that at like 4 in the morning). But people over on Steam started freaking out over it.<br /> <br /> Battletech did the same thing, by allowing players to choose which gender pronoun their character went by, and nobody seemed offended by it. And while I can see why that is something to be happy about, I personally don't see much of a point. If you want to play a character who identifies as either male or female, you could just make a character who is either male or female. and not have to worry about all the bigotry.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for Bloodlines 1, I've played that game at least 10 times before I stopped counting, and the only sexist thing in the entire game that I can remember is playing a female character during Romero's quest. If you're Appearance attribute is high enough (like 3, I think?) You can skip his quest by having sex with him.<br /> <br /> But hey, I guess Romero not being interested in having sex with male characters makes him a &quot;toxic man&quot; and not, you know, heterosexual? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> That's it... pretty much everything else in the game could be done regardless if you were male or female. I'm pretty sure there were even gay seduction options, if you wanted to explore them. Two that come to mind are Tommy Flayton, and Phil from the blood bank.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-24-2019, 10:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T07:16:17-07:00","id":1299200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299198#post1299198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see much of a problem with that, either. But people over on Steam started freaking out over it.<br /> <br /> Battletech did the same thing, by allowing players to choose which gender pronoun their character went by, and nobody seemed offended by it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Google &quot;battletech pronouns&quot;, I dare you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And while I can see why that is something to be happy about, I personally don't see much of a point. If you want to play a character who identifies as either male or female, you could just make a character who is either male or female. and not have to worry about all the bigotry. </div> </div> </div>Then, presumably, this option hasn't been implemented there for you, just like Captain Marvel and Black Panther weren't produced primarily for the people who got to see themselves in fiction from the day they were old enough to watch movies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299198#post1299198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Bloodlines 1, I've played that game at least 10 times before I stopped counting, and the only sexist thing in the entire game that I can remember is playing a female character during Romero's quest. If you're Appearance attribute is high enough (like 3, I think?) You can skip his quest by having sex with him.<br /> <br /> That's it... pretty much everything else in the game could be done regardless if you were male or female. I'm pretty sure there were even gay seduction options, if you wanted to explore them. Two that come to mind are Tommy Flayton, and that nurse guy who gets their throat torn out by Lily.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's two, one apparently added in later via patch, compared to how many lesbian and straight male-to-female advances?<br /> Also, I'm going out on a limb here and assume that you are male, non-trans and probably straight - in short, the demographic the game catered to. When it comes to sexism or its absence, please listen to those who are not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T07:22:43-07:00","id":1299202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299200#post1299200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Google &quot;battletech pronouns&quot;, I dare you.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You mean the one about identifying as a &quot;bear?&quot;<br /> <br /> That's part of a mod, it's not in the vanilla game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299200#post1299200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I'm going out on a limb here and assume that you are male, non-trans and probably straight - in short, the demographic the game catered to. When it comes to sexism or its absence, please listen to those who are not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm male, non-trans, and bi-curious in the sense that I don't fully know my sexuality, yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-24-2019, 10:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T07:36:48-07:00","id":1299205,"title":"","content":"First stuff I found regarding the topic:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://hornet.com/stories/battletech-gender-options/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://hornet.com/stories/battletech-gender-options/\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://hornet.com/stories/battletech-gender-options/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://hornet.com/stories/battletech-gender-options/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <a href=\"https://www.greenmangaming.com/newsroom/2018/04/25/battletech-gender-pronouns-generates-trolling-backlash/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.greenmangaming.com/newsr...ling-backlash/</a><br /> <a href=\"https://steamcommunity.com/app/637090/discussions/0/1696046342868409560/\" target=\"_blank\">https://steamcommunity.com/app/63709...6342868409560/</a><br /> <br /> So yeah, there was more than a bit of backlash.<br /> <br /> <br /> (That said, just to be clear: I'd say BL1's treatment of the topic was about average for its day. It's just that its day was 2004, and bringing sexuality into games was still... well, not new, but certainly not on the level of today. If Bloodlines 2 stuck to the same standard, it would be like bringing Start Trek TOS into the present and being proud for showing an interracial kiss on television.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T07:39:48-07:00","id":1299207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JezMiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299195#post1299195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, bugger. I had a nasty feeling that the Gangrel would lose out. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Oh, well. Early days, and I'm sure there'll be expansions.</div> </div> </div> </div>We don't know. People are literally just looking at the images and making guesses. Three of them obviously map, the others less so. They've also said that all future added Clan DLC would be free, so most of us are thinking that as Clans get released in TT, their mechanics will be able to be gamified and added to the core game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5704-thebiglarpnerd","name":"thebiglarpnerd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T07:43:01-07:00","id":1299208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299205#post1299205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First stuff I found regarding the topic:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://hornet.com/stories/battletech-gender-options/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://hornet.com/stories/battletech-gender-options/\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://hornet.com/stories/battletech-gender-options/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://hornet.com/stories/battletech-gender-options/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <a href=\"https://www.greenmangaming.com/newsroom/2018/04/25/battletech-gender-pronouns-generates-trolling-backlash/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.greenmangaming.com/newsr...ling-backlash/</a><br /> <a href=\"https://steamcommunity.com/app/637090/discussions/0/1696046342868409560/\" target=\"_blank\">https://steamcommunity.com/app/63709...6342868409560/</a><br /> <br /> So yeah, there was more than a bit of backlash.<br /> <br /> <br /> (That said, just to be clear: I'd say BL1's treatment of the topic was about average for its day. It's just that its day was 2004, and bringing sexuality into games was still... well, not new, but certainly not on the level of today. If Bloodlines 2 stuck to the same standard, it would be like bringing Start Trek TOS into the present and being proud for showing an interracial kiss on television.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Fair enough. Maybe I didn't notice much backlash, because we bought the game a while after it came out. If that's the case, then it might be safe to assume the outrage will eventually die down after a few months of the game's release?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T07:45:54-07:00","id":1299209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thebiglarpnerd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299207#post1299207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We don't know. People are literally just looking at the images and making guesses. Three of them obviously map, the others less so. They've also said that all future added Clan DLC would be free, so most of us are thinking that as Clans get released in TT, their mechanics will be able to be gamified and added to the core game.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I personally don't mind if the Tzimisce aren't made playable. I can see how Vicissitude would be all kinds of difficult to implement into the game. But I would love to have Lasombra and Setites become playable in the future. Especially since they hooked up with the Camarilla and Anarchs respectively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T08:09:05-07:00","id":1299215,"title":"","content":"Personally speaking, I think the most egregious and obnoxious example of real life politics needlessly interfering with the game would be Rudi.<br /> A gay, islamic Gangrel standing up for minorities and females who advocates for progressive causes wherever he goes and his nickname is &quot;the Bear Gangrel&quot;.<br /> Ok, if this is the type of character that you're interested in playing, hey, all the more power to you. However, I believe we can agree that some of what is in that character bio has never been an issue in VTM. Havens, feeding grounds, elitism, these were all typical VTM issues that vampires had to deal with. Misogynistic elders were not.<br /> Even the Ventrue, the oldest old boys' club in this setting, while they might have been biased towards European males, knew better. It was stated in the Revised Clanbook that any sire who would pass up on a talented non-White female childe on the basis of gender or race is an idiot and it would be his loss and, furthermore, both the Prince of London and the Ventrue Justicar were women. The oppressed minorities in Vampire: The Masquerade were always caitiffs and thin bloods, not real life minorities.<br /> Now, none of this means that there weren't issues in Bloodlines 1 that couldn't be fixed such as why would VV attend court in a stripper's outfit. But it does mean that If there is a conflict between the Toreador Primogen and the Ventrue Prince, I would like for it to be over feeding grounds, influence and ambition. Not because the Toreador Primogen is a woman being held back by her gender.<br /> <br /> So, for the love of God, don't pull a Rudi, Paradox Interactive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23725,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","user":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","date":". 03-24-2019, 11:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T08:12:53-07:00","id":1299217,"title":"","content":"So, just heard on a Steam thread that the game will <a href=\"https://twitter.com/VtM_Bloodlines/status/1108974806895071232\" target=\"_blank\">feature mod support</a>, and that there is a good possibility that we'll be able to decorate our Havens. Apparently, the premium version of the game offers a table, portrait and a stop sign.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardestadtTheEvenYounger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299215#post1299215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> *snip*</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> YES, exactly!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-24-2019, 11:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T08:18:58-07:00","id":1299218,"title":"","content":"Guys,Rudi is not some rarity. Gay people exist,Muslim people exist,black people exist. Revolutionary existed all through history. What is so incredibly hard to believe about Rudi?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T08:35:12-07:00","id":1299219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299218#post1299218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guys,Rudi is not some rarity. Gay people exist,Muslim people exist,black people exist. Revolutionary existed all through history. What is so incredibly hard to believe about Rudi?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing. And that's not what I was saying. If you like your Rudi, you can keep your Rudi.<br /> All that I was saying is that the things Rudi seems to represent and what he is fighting against, were never part of VtM and some people would like for it to not be part of the game.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T08:38:41-07:00","id":1299220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardestadtTheEvenYounger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299219#post1299219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing. And that's not what I was saying. If you like your Rudi, you can keep your Rudi.<br /> All that I was saying is that the things Rudi seems to represent and what he is fighting against, were never part of VtM and some people would like for it to not be part of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please, <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Carna\" target=\"_blank\">do tell that to Carna.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T08:53:37-07:00","id":1299225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardestadtTheEvenYounger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299215#post1299215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally speaking, I think the most egregious and obnoxious example of real life politics needlessly interfering with the game would be Rudi.<br /> A gay, islamic Gangrel standing up for minorities and females who advocates for progressive causes wherever he goes and his nickname is &quot;the Bear Gangrel&quot;.<br /> Ok, if this is the type of character that you're interested in playing, hey, all the more power to you. However, I believe we can agree that some of what is in that character bio has never been an issue in VTM. Havens, feeding grounds, elitism, these were all typical VTM issues that vampires had to deal with. Misogynistic elders were not.<br /> Even the Ventrue, the oldest old boys' club in this setting, while they might have been biased towards European males, knew better. It was stated in the Revised Clanbook that any sire who would pass up on a talented non-White female childe on the basis of gender or race is an idiot and it would be his loss and, furthermore, both the Prince of London and the Ventrue Justicar were women. The oppressed minorities in Vampire: The Masquerade were always caitiffs and thin bloods, not real life minorities.<br /> Now, none of this means that there weren't issues in Bloodlines 1 that couldn't be fixed such as why would VV attend court in a stripper's outfit. But it does mean that If there is a conflict between the Toreador Primogen and the Ventrue Prince, I would like for it to be over feeding grounds, influence and ambition. Not because the Toreador Primogen is a woman being held back by her gender.<br /> <br /> So, for the love of God, don't pull a Rudi, Paradox Interactive.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder what Vampire have you played in the last years.<br /> <br /> Just open D.C. By Night<br /> <br /> Marcus Vitel and Marissa<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Gradually Marcus\u2019 initial infatuation began to<br /> change, replaced by a slow burn that arose from deep<br /> within. Although Marcus cared for Marissa, <b>he could<br /> not bear to see a woman in control of so much.</b> She had<br /> all the power that he desired - power to make even<br /> Europe tremble. As long as she existed, he would never<br /> achieve his own dreams of domination. </div> </div> </div><br /> Marissa and her Clan<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Nosferatu and Malkavians were loyal to Marissa,<br /> and the Ventrue and Toreador in the South soon owed her<br /> enough boons to neutralize any challenge from them.<br /> Marissa\u2019s only real threat came from her own clan. The<br /> chantry in Washington, set up in the Octagon House, was<br /> primarily loyal to her. She had weeded out those who might<br /> pose threats to her reign during the war. <b>However, Clan<br /> Tremere decided that a woman could not run a chantry or<br /> lead one of their most important cities in the New World.</b><br /> They sent a replacement, Alexander Hanson. </div> </div> </div><br /> Hans Schmidt from Clan Tremere<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dr. Schmidt spends little time at the Octagon House.<br /> Instead, he likes stay either outside the city, alternating<br /> between comfortable mansions in Maryland and Virginia,<br /> or inside the National Archives or the Library of Congress.<br /> <b>Schmidt is a chauvinist and an Aryan supremacist. He<br /> discounts most women and all minorities.</b> He especially<br /> hates the Nosferatu. </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T08:53:51-07:00","id":1299226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299220#post1299220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please, <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Carna\" target=\"_blank\">do tell that to Carna.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, I'll tell Carna that her feminized House only appeared in V5 and is thus symptomatic of the changes made in it but first you gotta tell Meerlinda and Aisling Sturbridge and Therimna and Virstania and Malkgorzata and Mendacamina and Theresa Kymena; all of which are older than Carna (with the exception of Sturbidge but she is the signature character) that House Tremere didn't have a role for women until she came along.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T09:00:15-07:00","id":1299229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardestadtTheEvenYounger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299226#post1299226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, I'll tell Carna that her feminized House only appeared in V5 and is thus symptomatic of the changes made in it but first you gotta tell Meerlinda and Aisling Sturbridge and Therimna and Virstania and Malkgorzata and Mendacamina and Theresa Kymena; all of which are older than Carna (with the exception of Sturbidge but she is the signature character) that House Tremere didn't have a role for women until she came along.</div> </div> </div> </div>Take a look at the first paragraph of her bio. That wasn't part of her V5 characterization, but of the very first time the character appeared.<br /> Yes, Clan Tremere had a few exceptional women among its ranks. There always were exceptional women, in all periods of history. But the existence of a Joan of Arc, a Mary Shelley, a Mary Anning, a Catherine the Great do not mean they did not live in deeply misogynistic societies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T09:07:18-07:00","id":1299230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299218#post1299218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guys,Rudi is not some rarity. Gay people exist,Muslim people exist,black people exist. Revolutionary existed all through history. What is so incredibly hard to believe about Rudi?</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires are sociopathic assholes. Kindred society is the society of supernatural monster sociopathic assholes. There are no &quot;good&quot; vampires, or at least none that survive and succeed - take a look at Saulot and the Salubri for reference. In that context, Rudi feels naive.<br /> <br /> Edit: This is not to say Rudi cannot be gay, or Muslim. Both qualities exist among Vampires. It's just that the social activism and community organizer aspects should not have survived becoming a vampire. Rudi would make for an interesting PC, as the player and character grappled with their world falling apart. But as an NPC he feels like a strawman.<br /> <br /> Also, this discussion is spinning off from Bloodline 2. Can we bring the talk back on track?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":". 03-24-2019, 12:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T09:13:12-07:00","id":1299232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardestadtTheEvenYounger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299219#post1299219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing. And that's not what I was saying. If you like your Rudi, you can keep your Rudi.<br /> All that I was saying is that the things Rudi seems to represent and what he is fighting against, were never part of VtM and some people would like for it to not be part of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you sure? Cause I could swear this game had elements of old politics vs new ones,and of striving for change in a stagnant system since the beginning. Rudi does that,doesn't he, he justifies that using human leftist politics instead of purely vampiric politics.?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 03-24-2019, 12:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T09:16:39-07:00","id":1299234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299225#post1299225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wonder what Vampire have you played in the last years.<br /> <br /> Just open D.C. By Night<br /> <br /> Marcus Vitel and Marissa<br /> <br /> Marissa and her Clan<br /> <br /> Hans Schmidt from Clan Tremere</div> </div> </div> </div>Berlin by Night also had Heinrich Himmler as an unbondable Tremere Antitribu.<br /> Not only were these earlier books somewhat embarrassing exactly because of things like these, I believe you are mistaking the traits of certain canon characters versus the themes actually pursued in the story itself. Undoubtedly, anachronistic vampires will hold anachronistic beliefs but the examples of powerful female vampires or of color are much well know. The fact is that, prejudiced vampires notwithstanding, the game has never made a point of placing glass ceilings in front of any kind of vampire that we need to focus an whole videogame on shattering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T09:16:48-07:00","id":1299235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299230#post1299230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vampires are sociopathic assholes. Kindred society is the society of supernatural monster sociopathic assholes. There are no &quot;good&quot; vampires, or at least none that survive and succeed - take a look at Saulot and the Salubri for reference. In that context, Rudi feels naive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind the game is also about finding something to ground your morality in,something to stop the fall of your humanity. That something can be a political cause,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T09:18:40-07:00","id":1299237,"title":"","content":"With all that being said. I'd love to see what customization will be possible, I've storyteller a character that was a Malkavian version of Bowie. Could I create this one in this game,white suit and all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T09:18:56-07:00","id":1299238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299230#post1299230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vampires are sociopathic assholes. Kindred society is the society of supernatural monster sociopathic assholes. There are no &quot;good&quot; vampires, or at least none that survive and succeed - take a look at Saulot and the Salubri for reference. In that context, Rudi feels naive.<br /> <br /> Edit: This is not to say Rudi cannot be gay, or Muslim. Both qualities exist among Vampires. It's just that the <b>social activism and community organizer aspects should not have survived becoming a vampire</b>. Rudi would make for an interesting PC, as the player and character grappled with their world falling apart. But as an NPC he feels like a strawman.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like Critias or Menele you mean?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 03-24-2019, 12:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T09:20:10-07:00","id":1299239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299229#post1299229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Take a look at the first paragraph of her bio. That wasn't part of her V5 characterization, but of the very first time the character appeared.<br /> Yes, Clan Tremere had a few exceptional women among its ranks. There always were exceptional women, in all periods of history. But the existence of a Joan of Arc, a Mary Shelley, a Mary Anning, a Catherine the Great do not mean they did not live in deeply misogynistic societies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Undoubtedly true. But Canna's account is proven incorrect based on the fact that Tremere have had women among their most inner circle since its inception.<br /> Furthermore, I do admit to not having read Milwaukee by Night in quite some time. Am I wrong in believing that the book focused far more on, say, the city being surrounded by werewolves and on Gangrel hitting squads versus Canna's woes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23725,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","user":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","date":". 03-24-2019, 12:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T09:26:04-07:00","id":1299241,"title":"","content":"I've just realised who Rudi reminds me of...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Community_characters#Britta_Perry\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/static/images/icons/enwiki-25.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Community_characters#Britta_Perry\" target=\"_blank\"> List of Community characters - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Community_characters#Britta_Perry\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Community_characters#Britta_Perry </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16290-generallyconfused","name":"GenerallyConfused","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16290_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T09:28:42-07:00","id":1299242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299232#post1299232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you sure? Cause I could swear this game had elements of old politics vs new ones,and of striving for change in a stagnant system since the beginning. Rudi does that,doesn't he, he justifies that using human leftist politics instead of purely vampiric politics.?</div> </div> </div> </div>Striving for change in a stagnant system is indeed a theme of VtM, on this we agree. However, what I have issue with is not this theme, broadly speaking, but the usage of human leftist politics, to use your own words. That is definitely the injection of real life politics that the game can do without.<br /> <br /> It's the difference between having elves as a metaphor for minorities in The Witcher vs actually having the game featuring real world minorities in an oppressed role.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T09:29:23-07:00","id":1299243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299238#post1299238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like Critias or Menele you mean?</div> </div> </div> </div>And how well did that work out for them? Menele is apparently dead, and Critias something of a broken man. And Critias is sexist, refusing to allow girl into his boys school, where he teaches a 2,500 year old retrodyne philosophy of personal responsibility and toxic masculinity. What social activism is present in vampire community is carcinogenic.<br /> <br /> Also, at this point we don't know much about the game's characters or themes. Except the POV chases a Nosferatu around, some woman in pearls swings OO-Neg like its going out of style, and a blue nose in a suit likes the view out of a skyscraper. The only plot element/theme we know about is the blood trade. Everything else is speculation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T09:29:51-07:00","id":1299244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardestadtTheEvenYounger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299242#post1299242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Striving for change in a stagnant system is indeed a theme of VtM, on this we agree. However, what I have issue with is not this theme, broadly speaking, but the usage of human leftist politics, to use your own words. That is definitely the injection of real life politics that the game can do without.<br /> <br /> It's the difference between having elves as a metaphor for minorities in The Witcher vs actually having the game featuring real world minorities in an oppressed role.</div> </div> </div> </div>I respect that. Each should play the game the way they want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T09:41:41-07:00","id":1299248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardestadtTheEvenYounger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299234#post1299234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Berlin by Night also had Heinrich Himmler as an unbondable Tremere Antitribu.<br /> Not only were these earlier books somewhat embarrassing exactly because of things like these, I believe you are mistaking the traits of certain canon characters versus the themes actually pursued in the story itself. Undoubtedly, anachronistic vampires will hold anachronistic beliefs but the examples of powerful female vampires or of color are much well know. The fact is that, prejudiced vampires notwithstanding, the game has never made a point of placing glass ceilings in front of any kind of vampire that we need to focus an whole videogame on shattering.</div> </div> </div> </div>What video game are you talking about? Because I don't think I've heard anyone talking about needing a game to &quot;focus&quot; on it. The only things we know is that BL2 will allow you to select pronouns and that the game may take some stances on so far completely unknown issues. Perhaps they'll present white supremacists as evil rather than giving a &quot;both sides&quot; story. We'll see.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardestadtTheEvenYounger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299239#post1299239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Undoubtedly true. But Canna's account is proven incorrect based on the fact that Tremere have had women among their most inner circle since its inception.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I just said, no, that doesn't prove anything. Would you say that Elizabeth I. proves that 16th century England was not a misogynistic society? Would you say the same about Catherine II. and 18th century Russia?<br /> In fact, I seem to remember that the Order of Hermes and, resulting, House and Clan Tremere were actually among the few societies in the WoD that were called out as chauvinistic in previous editions as well.<br /> <br /> And if one reads what exactly Rudi's loresheet says, it becomes clear that his existence doesn't retcon all elders as misogynist either: &quot;[he] stands up for female Kindred in cities run by traditionally misogynistic elders&quot;. We've already established that there are such anachronistic elders. We can also assume that somewhere, some of them are running cities or parts of them, because that's what elders do. So Rudi can stand up for female Kindred in such cities without us having to also assume that all cities everywhere are run by misogynistic elders.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299230#post1299230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires are sociopathic assholes. Kindred society is the society of supernatural monster sociopathic assholes. There are no &quot;good&quot; vampires, or at least none that survive and succeed - take a look at Saulot and the Salubri for reference. In that context, Rudi feels naive.<br /> <br /> Edit: This is not to say Rudi cannot be gay, or Muslim. Both qualities exist among Vampires. It's just that the social activism and community organizer aspects should not have survived becoming a vampire. Rudi would make for an interesting PC, as the player and character grappled with their world falling apart. But as an NPC he feels like a strawman.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, we haven't seen what Rudi will become in 50 years. Idealistic neonates are part and parcel for the game and most definitely not limited to player characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T09:56:04-07:00","id":1299252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299248#post1299248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What video game are you talking about? Because I don't think I've heard anyone talking about needing a game to &quot;focus&quot; on it. The only things we know is that BL2 will allow you to select pronouns and that the game may take some stances on so far completely unknown issues. Perhaps they'll present white supremacists as evil rather than giving a &quot;both sides&quot; story. We'll see.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, we don't know, people are just concerned due to some statements by certain writers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299248#post1299248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I just said, no, that doesn't prove anything. Would you say that Elizabeth I. proves that 16th century England was not a misogynistic society? Would you say the same about Catherine II. and 18th century Russia?<br /> In fact, I seem to remember that the Order of Hermes and, resulting, House and Clan Tremere were actually among the few societies in the WoD that were called out as chauvinistic in previous editions as well</div> </div> </div> </div>What Carna's sire stated was &quot;They have never had a female in their ranks. What will they think?&quot; This is most definitely proven to be untrue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299248#post1299248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if one reads what exactly Rudi's loresheet says, it becomes clear that his existence doesn't retcon all elders as misogynist either: &quot;[he] stands up for female Kindred in cities run by traditionally misogynistic elders&quot;. We've already established that there are such anachronistic elders. We can also assume that somewhere, some of them are running cities or parts of them, because that's what elders do. So Rudi can stand up for female Kindred in such cities without us having to also assume that all cities everywhere are run by misogynistic elders.</div> </div> </div> </div>No one is claiming that Rudi is retconning anything. Using Milwaukee's example again, people would simply rather that the game stays focused on the werewolves surrounding the town and the Anubis Gangrel hitting squads who deal with it as opposed to having Rudi's concerns take center stage.<br /> <br /> At this point, it's entirely possible that Bloodlines 2 WON'T fall into this trap. As I stated before, people are simply somewhat concerned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T10:05:51-07:00","id":1299259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299230#post1299230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vampires are sociopathic assholes. Kindred society is the society of supernatural monster sociopathic assholes. There are no &quot;good&quot; vampires, or at least none that survive and succeed - take a look at Saulot and the Salubri for reference. In that context, Rudi feels naive.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit: This is not to say Rudi cannot be gay, or Muslim. Both qualities exist among Vampires. It's just that the social activism and community organizer aspects should not have survived becoming a vampire. Rudi would make for an interesting PC, as the player and character grappled with their world falling apart. But as an NPC he feels like a strawman.</b><br /> <br /> Also, this discussion is spinning off from Bloodline 2. Can we bring the talk back on track?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is silly because vampires are always trying to do things to make up for their crimes if they either have High Humanity, Want High Humanity, or are Brujah. It also ignores the &quot;joke&quot; or &quot;twist&quot; with Rudi that he can only make his social organizing and good deeds worse by his presence. But I suspect the reason that Rudi isn't well liked is because he's not a hot girl like Maldavis or Anita Wainwright. Both of whom are heavily into social activism.<br /> <br /> I say that as thinking THE ANARCH was one of the worst written books of Vampire: The Masquerade and Rudi was not a well-detailed character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-24-2019, 01:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T10:18:21-07:00","id":1299261,"title":"","content":"MRH created Vampire: The Masquerade in the counterculture district of Atlanta after driving through Gary and seeing the poverty as well as social devastation then driving into Chicago. It's always been an intensely political game and took a stand very early by including large number of black, female, and gay NPCs when that was controversial for a tabletop roleplaying game. It also dealt with black magic, satanic themes,redemption, and sex when those things were banned outright from Dungeons and Dragons thanks to the efforts of BADD.<br /> <br /> I think a big question is the fact that a lot of people are suddenly going to wonder what qualifies as POLITICS and need to take a moment to ask what they think is going to be talked about. Because when I hear V:TM and politics, this is what I think.<br /> <br /> * Corrupt politicians<br /> * Wealth inequality<br /> * The option to rescue someone getting beaten by white supremacists and killing them all, only to later have a mother ask you to see if you can pull her boy out of the gang.<br /> * Homelessness<br /> * Corporate coverups of unsafe products (Pentex!)<br /> * Jokes about how the locals only care about weed legalization<br /> * A corrupt church that is just a cover for a Setite cult and feeds off the runaways it &quot;helps&quot; vs. a rich but human one that wants to kick out all the homeless from the neighborhood.<br /> * The PCs investigate a young woman who has been assaulted horribly and vampires now want killed. She is the victim of a bad memory wipe and actually was fed on by vampires. They can kill her, fix the memory wipe, or help her get out of town. Maybe also kill the vampire but she can't expose him.<br /> <br /> WATCH_DOGS 2 is an intensely political game and it was just silly and fun.<br /> <br /> GRAND THEFT AUTO for all of its weirdness is also a very political game.<br /> <br /> Let's wait and see.<br /> <br /> I admit I'm VERY biased on this end because I write intensely political vampire fiction. All of the reviews of my books (which I THOUGHT were escapist) emphasize it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/_1tQwK2PnOA\" data-code=\"_1tQwK2PnOA\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/_1tQwK2PnOA/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-24-2019, 01:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T10:23:57-07:00","id":1299263,"title":"","content":"Hey, you got reviewed by Maven. That's cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T10:45:29-07:00","id":1299269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardestadtTheEvenYounger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299263#post1299263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, you got reviewed by Maven. That's cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was surprised and happy.<br /> <br /> She also liked it a lot. Mind you, I think if she ever DID review the Clan Novels she'd end up talking at great length about the psycho-sexual Freudian relationships of Lucita versus the Sabbat eating people.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T10:51:50-07:00","id":1299270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299261#post1299261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> * Corrupt politicians</div> </div> </div> </div>Excellent, can i gain control of them, or expose them to weaken a rival<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299261#post1299261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Wealth inequality</div> </div> </div> </div>Natural state of the world, gives me a base of people to use as a resource<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299261#post1299261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* The option to rescue someone getting beaten by white supremacists and killing them all, only to later have a mother ask you to see if you can pull her boy out of the gang.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, look, a chance to for me to pointlessly breach the Masquerade. Think i'll pass.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299261#post1299261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Homelessness</div> </div> </div> </div>Another resource to be aware of<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299261#post1299261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Corporate coverups of unsafe products (Pentex!)</div> </div> </div> </div>Can i leverage this to gain resources, influence or favours?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299261#post1299261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Jokes about how the locals only care about weed legalization</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure about this, tbh. Sure if it was an election thing i could use it to get some kind of swing somehow though<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299261#post1299261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* A corrupt church that is just a cover for a Setite cult and feeds off the runaways it &quot;helps&quot; vs. a rich but human one that wants to kick out all the homeless from the neighborhood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm, probably try to arrange for the setites to get ousted somehow and take over the operation. Maybe set up my own shelter, use the human to pressure the Setite operation and get the displaced homless funneled to my set up instead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299261#post1299261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* The PCs investigate a young woman who has been assaulted horribly and vampires now want killed. She is the victim of a bad memory wipe and actually was fed on by vampires. They can kill her, fix the memory wipe, or help her get out of town. Maybe also kill the vampire but she can't expose him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, fix the wipe is the obvious one, followed by either having her declared mentally unfit/unstable or put in a chemically induced coma if that isn't possible. Maybe get her out of town <i>after</i> a suscessful wipe. Killing is the last option<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16290-generallyconfused","name":"GenerallyConfused","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16290_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T10:54:29-07:00","id":1299273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299229#post1299229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Take a look at the first paragraph of her bio. That wasn't part of her V5 characterization, but of the very first time the character appeared.<br /> Yes, Clan Tremere had a few exceptional women among its ranks. There always were exceptional women, in all periods of history. But the existence of a Joan of Arc, a Mary Shelley, a Mary Anning, a Catherine the Great do not mean they did not live in deeply misogynistic societies.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Unless I'm mistaken, weren't the Gargoyles (the thing Tremere created specifically to combat the War Ghouls) originally developed by a female Tremere?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T11:01:34-07:00","id":1299275,"title":"","content":"Basically, I think that the POLITICS *finger wag* is probably just going to be in the NCIS and Law and Order way.<br /> <br /> There will be a lot of &quot;realistic&quot; adventure hooks to make it feel more grounded amid all the fleshmonsters and werewolves.<br /> <br /> We had this in the original game to an extent but it's also something in Grand Theft Auto.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T11:10:00-07:00","id":1299280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardestadtTheEvenYounger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299215#post1299215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The oppressed minorities in Vampire: The Masquerade were always caitiffs and thin bloods, not real life minorities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not entirely true. While caitiff and thin bloods may face greater discrimination, Kindred Society is still a feudal society prone to extreme social reproduction and bigotry. I bet you that any Domain in Europe even in our modern day would be 99.9% white. Hell, some of the book emphasize racist grandsires who destroy their childer's childer because they embraced minorities and &quot;contaminated the Blood&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T11:12:47-07:00","id":1299282,"title":"","content":"I hope the writers won't listen to the loud 4chan fans who have been trying to push some people out of the fandom with their \u201ckeep politics out of our vtm\u201d (vtm being a personal and political horror game.. so it sounds, to me, like saying \u201ckeep the government out of my nhs/medicaid\u201d)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T11:15:08-07:00","id":1299284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299280#post1299280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hell, some of the book emphasize racist grandsires who destroy their childer's childer because they embraced minorities and &quot;contaminated the Blood&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So, basically, an angry parent finding out their child is in a mix raced relationship?<br /> <br /> Anyways, while I'm not denying the possibility that real world politics may have been present in WoD to a certain extant. I never saw that as the primary focus of the game. I saw Masquerade as a game where I take on the role of the monster. What the hell do I care about offending people? I'm a god damn vampire, and I am forced to conduct something akin to sexual assault every time I feed.<br /> <br /> What's that, some ass hole is trying to oppress my life style choices? Gee, if only I had access to an entire array of super powers I could use to resolve the situation. Oh wait, I do!<br /> <br /> Being a vampire comes with an entire host of problems all it's own. Your character has much larger issues to worry about, than people being persecuted against on the other side of the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-24-2019, 02:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T11:19:13-07:00","id":1299285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardestadtTheEvenYounger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299226#post1299226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok, I'll tell Carna that her feminized House only appeared in V5 and is thus symptomatic of the changes made in it but first you gotta tell Meerlinda and Aisling Sturbridge and Therimna and Virstania and Malkgorzata and Mendacamina and Theresa Kymena; all of which are older than Carna (with the exception of Sturbidge but she is the signature character) that House Tremere didn't have a role for women until she came along.</div> </div> </div> </div>These women are exceptions not the rule. They're incredibly brilliant and had to do twice than their male peers to gain any recognition in the Clan, because the Elders (for obvious reasons) are sexist assholes, and still are. Look each one of them has an achievement to their name: Virstania invented Gargoyles, Aisling is the Regent of one of the most important cities in the US, etc. I don't like the idea of Carna very much, I like the whole struggle dynamic when it comes to Tremere's attitude toward gender (Vampires don't have civil rights groups, unless we mention the Carthians but they don't exist in VTM...) and &quot;House Carna&quot; sounds like a copout from facing those struggles head on and eliminates many interesting plot dynamics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T11:25:13-07:00","id":1299286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299284#post1299284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So, basically, an angry parent finding out their child is in a mix raced relationship?<br /> <br /> Anyways, while I'm not denying the possibility that real world politics may have been present in WoD to a certain extant. I never saw that as the primary focus of the game. I saw Masquerade as a game where I take on the role of the monster. What the hell do I care about offending people? I'm a god damn vampire, and I am forced to conduct something akin to sexual assault every time I feed.<br /> <br /> What's that, some ass hole is trying to oppress my life style choices? Gee, if only I had access to an entire array of super powers I could use to resolve the situation. Oh wait, I do!<br /> <br /> Being a vampire comes with an entire host of problems all it's own. Your character has much larger issues to worry about, than people being persecuted against on the other side of the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, you are a monster, you commit countless felonies night to night to survive. Yet, you don't shed all that makes you humanity outright (unless you're Sabbat, in which case good luck) so it's obvious that many vampires will maintain the attitudes, the politics, and the lifestyles they held close as mortals. Many vampires might even find their newly found &quot;powers&quot; as an opportunity to back the causes they believed in as mortals (Brujah are notorious for this, but so are some Toreador and Ventrue) Besides, real world politics, pandering to them, abusing them, or even outright supporting them is both a useful tool for vampires in the vicious circles of Kindred politics and a way to keep close to their humanity. It's a fine line to walk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T11:35:21-07:00","id":1299291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299286#post1299286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, you are a monster, you commit countless felonies night to night to survive. Yet, you don't shed all that makes you humanity outright (unless you're Sabbat, in which case good luck) so it's obvious that many vampires will maintain the attitudes, the politics, and the lifestyles they held close as mortals. Many vampires might even find their newly found &quot;powers&quot; as an opportunity to back the causes they believed in as mortals (Brujah are notorious for this, but so are some Toreador and Ventrue) Besides, real world politics, pandering to them, abusing them, or even outright supporting them is both a useful tool for vampires in the vicious circles of Kindred politics and a way to keep close to their humanity. It's a fine line to walk.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You mean, unless you're a Sabbat shovelhead, who are specifically meant to have short, violent unlives. The real Sabbat still recognize the importance of the Masquerade, because if they didn't, then vampires would have been exposed a long time ago.<br /> <br /> And yes, I prefer Sabbat over Camarilla. Prior to finding out about World of Darkness, most games I had been exposed to forced my character into the role of heroic protagonist who was out to make the world a better place. Masquerade was the first major game I can remember that gave me the option to see the story from the villain's point of view. That's the concept I fell in love with. I want to play a classic vampire, the kind of creature who inspired terror in people. Not the tortured, brooding teenager that has become so popular in mainstream media today.<br /> <br /> As you can probably guess, I also prefer to play Paths of Enlightenment, rather than the Road of Humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T11:39:11-07:00","id":1299295,"title":"","content":"Perhaps I am alone that I think House Carna exists solely to give Tremere a bunch of sexy witches.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299291#post1299291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You mean, unless you're a Sabbat shovelhead, who are specifically meant to have short, violent unlives. The real Sabbat still recognize the importance of the Masquerade, because if they didn't, then vampires would have been exposed a long time ago.<br /> <br /> And yes, I prefer Sabbat over Camarilla. Prior to finding out about World of Darkness, most games I had been exposed to forced my character into the role of heroic protagonist who was out to make the world a better place. Masquerade was the first major game I can remember that gave me the option to see the story from the villain's point of view. That's the concept I fell in love with. I want to play a classic vampire, the kind of creature who inspired terror in people. Not the tortured, brooding teenager that has become so popular in mainstream media today.<br /> <br /> As you can probably guess, I also prefer to play Paths of Enlightenment, rather than the Road of Humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Be you.<br /> <br /> I, on the other hand, am all about the heroic Anarchs vs. the Evil Elders and even Eviler Sabbat.<br /> <br /> Time will wear away your humanity and you will become the villain as Harvey Dent would say--but it doesn't have to be tonight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T11:46:26-07:00","id":1299296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299295#post1299295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Be you.<br /> <br /> I, on the other hand, am all about the heroic Anarchs vs. the Evil Elders and even Eviler Sabbat.<br /> <br /> Time will wear away your humanity and you will become the villain as Harvey Dent would say--but it doesn't have to be tonight.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're both playing the game wrong. (joke)<br /> <br /> Masquerade is about the Scions of the Camarilla, holding the seven pillars sustaining Civilization, defending them against the onslaught of short sighted anarchs and evil Sabbat.<br /> One day, the Masquerade may break and bring deadly illumination into our night shrouded society. But for tonight, thanks to the Elders of the Camarilla, the Cainite race survives.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T11:50:24-07:00","id":1299299,"title":"","content":"Personally, I could say this for the &quot;political&quot; stuff:<br /> <br /> If the game will be written with the intent of &quot;educating&quot; me on contemporary leftist talking points, instead of making a good Vampire story, I'm out.<br /> <br /> To make an example: the whole character of Damsel was a caricature and a joke in VTMB1. If this game will take characters like that completely seriously, nevermind posing as &quot;being in the right&quot;, I'm out. This is precisely, why I didn't like the V5 Brujah writeup, making the clan <i>about</i> social activism, not <i>using</i> it, or jsut being frequently connected to it.<br /> <br /> If every third NPC is some kind of leftist activist, or spouting buzzwords and those things coming up all the time in dialogues (hence, having the feeling of the writers wanting to lecture me on their favored ideology, instead of telling a vampire story, as above), I'm so fucking out.<br /> <br /> I'm okay with whatever pronouns. I'm okay with particular characters being driven and having strong oppinions on social or political questions, or having whatever identity. The whole thing depends on presentation and extent. I'm not okay with one-sided ideological preaching. If the game could avoid that, good.<br /> <br /> <br /> Yes, yes, WoD has always been political (and leftist), at its core, I'll be the first to admit that and I <i>liked</i> that, it was in concert with my feelings and thoughts about the world most of the time. Fuck, I did my degree partly because of Werewolf. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Vampire's war of the ages and eternal servitude and rebelling against it, Mage's &quot;what is <i>reality, or normalcy, </i>really?&quot; and freedom vs. safety, or Changeling's horror of burning out as growing up, those all had a <i>lot</i> of menaing for me. <br /> <br /> Yes, it also had social commentary and tried to represent characters others didn't back then and I liked that too. But it was like that in a more thoughtful, less preachy manner. Also, leftist narratives and thoughts changed and frequently, IMO, not for the better. You're free to disagree.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, to put it bluntly: if this game will be a shameless ideological propaganda piece, then, it's clearly targeted to a specific group and I'm not part of it.<br /> <br /> At this point, it could go both ways. To be fair, while the V5 Cam and Anarch books got me some very bad eye-rolling moments, most of them were a lot better, than I expected, based on the core book. Especially the Anarch on, I was fully prepared for much, <i>much</i> worse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 03-24-2019, 02:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T11:56:53-07:00","id":1299302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299295#post1299295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I, on the other hand, am all about the heroic Anarchs vs. the Evil Elders and even Eviler Sabbat.<br /> <br /> Time will wear away your humanity and you will become the villain as Harvey Dent would say--but it doesn't have to be tonight.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm skeptical about the idea of the Anarchs being heroic. Since I've been hearing several accounts regarding how they're prone to violence against those who don't sign with their movement. In other words, they have an Us vs Them mentality, and if you aren't with the Anarchs, then you're part of the problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T12:07:02-07:00","id":1299305,"title":"","content":"Yeah, never ever got the impression that the Anarchs were meant to be &quot;the goodies&quot;. Came as a real shock to see it being so prevalent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T12:15:50-07:00","id":1299307,"title":"","content":"Eh, it's not surprising for me at all.<br /> <br /> It's the same with real-life political activist groups and the writers are at least in-line in thought, or straight-on involved with several too. Also, connected to that, it's probably a target audience, so they could identify with it and play out their power fantasies. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T12:29:09-07:00","id":1299313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd call that an unfounded fear and personally am going to give both Hardsuit Labs and the writing team that has been hired, including former Bloodlines the benefit of that very easily dismissed doubt.<br /> <br /> I'll worry more about things like story pacing, engaging and balanced mechanics, interesting choices in character development than imaginary leftist boogiemen.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's entirelly possible, it'll be totally okay. It's possible it will be preachy and bad. I'll wait and see and won't preorder it, by any means, but I won't assume anything without seeing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T12:29:18-07:00","id":1299314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd call that an unfounded fear and personally am going to give both Hardsuit Labs and the writing team that has been hired, including former Bloodlines the benefit of that very easily dismissed doubt.<br /> <br /> I'll worry more about things like story pacing, engaging and balanced mechanics, interesting choices in character development than imaginary leftist boogiemen.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm giving this game a chance, too. But I'm not going to be one of those idiots who drops 60 dollars on a pre-order based purely on fanboy nostalgia. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'm waiting until we get more information about the game, before making any decisions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T12:31:24-07:00","id":1299315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299302#post1299302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm skeptical about the idea of the Anarchs being heroic. Since I've been hearing several accounts regarding how they're prone to violence against those who don't sign with their movement. In other words, they have an Us vs Them mentality, and if you aren't with the Anarchs, then you're part of the problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>That argument is a strange one to make in an action adventure RPG.<br /> <br /> There's not many ways but violence to deal with the Sabbat, Prince, werewolf, or a wassail suffering monster.<br /> <br /> Then again, I see most Vampire RPGs as similar to Bloodlines in that combat isn't the only part of the game but is a major part of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jamiemalk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299305#post1299305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, never ever got the impression that the Anarchs were meant to be &quot;the goodies&quot;. Came as a real shock to see it being so prevalent.</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit I'm confused as hell in the opposite direction that so many people think the Camarilla was a good thing or meant to be something you're supposed to support.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-24-2019, 03:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T12:34:53-07:00","id":1299317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299315#post1299315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That argument is a strange one to make in an action adventure RPG.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Is it? I think it's a perfectly sound argument.<br /> <br /> <b>Anarch:</b> &quot;Hey man, you agree that the Elders are a bunch of tyrannical ass holes, right?&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Random Vampire:</b> &quot;Sure!&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Anarch:</b> &quot;Well then, why don't you join up with us and fight the good fight against their oppression?&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Random Vampire:</b> &quot;No thanks. I'm not really one for politics. I think I'll just keep my head down and try not to step on anyone's toes.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Anarch:</b> &quot;Well then, you better keep walking, before this gets ugly, pal!&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Random Vampire:</b> &quot;What the fuck did I do?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T12:41:06-07:00","id":1299323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299291#post1299291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You mean, unless you're a Sabbat shovelhead, who are specifically meant to have short, violent unlives. The real Sabbat still recognize the importance of the Masquerade, because if they didn't, then vampires would have been exposed a long time ago.<br /> <br /> And yes, I prefer Sabbat over Camarilla. Prior to finding out about World of Darkness, most games I had been exposed to forced my character into the role of heroic protagonist who was out to make the world a better place. Masquerade was the first major game I can remember that gave me the option to see the story from the villain's point of view. That's the concept I fell in love with. I want to play a classic vampire, the kind of creature who inspired terror in people. Not the tortured, brooding teenager that has become so popular in mainstream media today.<br /> <br /> As you can probably guess, I also prefer to play Paths of Enlightenment, rather than the Road of Humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>VTM was originally based on the &quot;tortured brooding teenager&quot; archetype though. Anne Rice was a huge inspiration. But whatever, all power to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T12:43:33-07:00","id":1299326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299317#post1299317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is it? I think it's a perfectly sound argument.<br /> <br /> <b>Anarch:</b> &quot;Hey man, you agree that the Elders are a bunch of tyrannical ass holes, right?&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Random Vampire:</b> &quot;Sure!&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Anarch:</b> &quot;Well then, why don't you join up with us and fight the good fight against their oppression?&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Random Vampire:</b> &quot;No thanks. I'm not really one for politics. I think I'll just keep my head down and try not to step on anyone's toes.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Anarch:</b> &quot;Well then, you better keep walking, before this gets ugly, pal!&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Random Vampire:</b> &quot;What the fuck did I do?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Neutrality is a choice of sides when you're dealing with the fact the Prince can and will order neutral vampires to do whatever they want as one of the most basic vampire actions.<br /> <br /> <b>Random Vampire</b>: That was terrible. They were so mean.<br /> <br /> <b>Prince</b>: Good, which is why you will spy on them for me.<br /> <br /> <b>Random Vampire</b>: Wait what?<br /> <br /> <b>Prince</b>: *DOMINATE* YOU WILL SPY ON THEM.<br /> <br /> <b>Random Vampire</b>: Yes, I will.<br /> <br /> If that sounds unfair...<br /> <br /> Uh...isn't that EVERY ELEMENT OF VAMPIRE SOCIETY?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp