-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T12:57:03-07:00","id":1299341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299315#post1299315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit I'm confused as hell in the opposite direction that so many people think the Camarilla was a good thing or meant to be something you're supposed to support.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Camarilla provides security and stability to the Kindred. It ensures that vampiric society can be civil and peaceful, if not fair. In a Camarilla city, if you keep your head down, avoid the politics, and follow the rules, you stand a very good chance of being left alone to do whatever you want. You're under very little threat of being murdered of Diablerized.<br /> <br /> What the alternative? The anarch free states where the territory is divided into gangs and you'd better join one because, otherwise, no one will have your back if a vampire in a gang decides to take your stuff.<br /> Or the Sabbat with...well, everything.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T12:58:34-07:00","id":1299343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wtf does that even mean? Beyond the fact that a lot of media has had poor or demonizing depictions of mental health in vast contrast to the few things that have done it well. I am going to call complete bullshit on the idea that you can do better than the trite Fish Malk shit we've gotten so often before.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there are two ways Malkavians could legitimately go. Either do the work and portray mental illness correctly and accurately or make it clear that their Clan Bane is not in any way related to any real-world mental illness.<br /> Personally, I'd prefer the first one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardestadtTheEvenYounger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299341#post1299341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Camarilla provides security and stability to the Kindred. It ensures that vampiric society can be civil and peaceful, if not fair. In a Camarilla city, if you keep your head down, avoid the politics, and follow the rules, you stand a very good chance of being left alone to do whatever you want. You're under very little threat of being murdered of Diablerized.</div> </div> </div> </div>...unless at some point some elder thinks that you're a nuisance, in which case it's likely noone will lift a finger to help you while your unlife is being made hell or ended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T12:59:32-07:00","id":1299344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299330#post1299330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a lot of people who want to play Angel, Louis, Nick Knight, and Hannibal King (if not Blade himself aka Theo Bell).</div> </div> </div> </div>More like Spike, and Lestat.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T13:00:49-07:00","id":1299347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299326#post1299326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Neutrality is a choice of sides when you're dealing with the fact the Prince can and will order neutral vampires to do whatever they want as one of the most basic vampire actions.<br /> <br /> <b>Random Vampire</b>: That was terrible. They were so mean.<br /> <br /> <b>Prince</b>: Good, which is why you will spy on them for me.<br /> <br /> <b>Random Vampire</b>: Wait what?<br /> <br /> <b>Prince</b>: *DOMINATE* YOU WILL SPY ON THEM.<br /> <br /> <b>Random Vampire</b>: Yes, I will.<br /> <br /> If that sounds unfair...<br /> <br /> Uh...isn't that EVERY ELEMENT OF VAMPIRE SOCIETY?</div> </div> </div> </div>See, that prince clearly has no social skills or politics, so i doubt the dominate would take. Or that they would be prince very long, unless they were a Brujah that snapped people in half regularly.<br /> <br /> An even slightly competent Prince would offer a small carrot that could essencially worthless to them but very valuable to the Random. <i>Then</i> a little dominate mixed into the conversation to reinforce it.<br /> <br /> Or, even better, get one of the Anarchs and turn him into a sleeper agent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T13:01:31-07:00","id":1299348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Considering the crowd that is losing their blessed little minds over the news about having a better depiction of mental heath and pronoun options in their video game I'm not going to lose any sleep over said crowd.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The idea of people losing their shit over accurate representation of mental health issues is hilarious!<br /> <br /> <br /> Speaking of which, I've heard tale that the game will also enable us to pick mental derangements for our character, in addition to body type and pronouns. I'm very curious to see how this would affect game play, going forward.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T13:07:25-07:00","id":1299350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Given the comments so far out on Bloodlines 2. I suspect the former is the likely outcome.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which will suck because people want to play crazy seers and mad prophets.<br /> <br /> The Malkavians were conceived as the Trickster clan.<br /> <br /> Real life mental illness does not lend itself to Trickster.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T13:08:39-07:00","id":1299351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299343#post1299343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...unless at some point some elder thinks that you're a nuisance, in which case it's likely noone will lift a finger to help you while your unlife is being made hell or ended.</div> </div> </div> </div>The minute you become a vampire, you become blood linked to a 10000 years old monster who can and will use you in a plot that started back before the pyramids were built.<br /> Elders are just the hazards of being a vampire, no way to avoid it. You still have a better chance of becoming an Elder yourself in the Camarilla than anywhere else.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T13:10:30-07:00","id":1299352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299336#post1299336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that attempts to make Malkavians more like real life mental illness is the exact wrong approach and every time they do, they make the problem exponentially worse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Diagnosed severe anxiety and depression here, struggling with it, like what, 6 years now?<br /> <br /> Malkavians never bothered me. Yes, people sometimes go silly with them, but for the love of everything, they are insane vampires, their pre-existing (or not) ilnesses exaggerated by the Beast.<br /> <br /> Besides, talking to the lamp post was funny.<br /> <br /> As for gender pronouns, that's not a thing that disturbs me at all. I don't need it, but whatever, if it makes the game more enjoyable for people, sure, include them. I don't consider that preachy, just giving the option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T13:13:45-07:00","id":1299356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wtf does that even mean? Beyond the fact that a lot of media has had poor or demonizing depictions of mental health in vast contrast to the few things that have done it well. I am going to call complete bullshit on the idea that you can do better than the trite Fish Malk shit we've gotten so often before.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really?<br /> <br /> You want your character to just be unable to communicate or leave their haven for hours or days?<br /> Suddenly find three months have passed between scene transitons?<br /> Be litterally mindlocked in a stressful situation?<br /> <br /> <br /> None of those things are fun. Those are just <i>some</i> of the things i've had to deal with in real life. I wish people would stop trying to make my Malks be unliving nightmares mirroring reality and let them be fun<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T13:14:06-07:00","id":1299358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardestadtTheEvenYounger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299351#post1299351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The minute you become a vampire, you become blood linked to a 10000 years old monster who can and will use you in a plot that started back before the pyramids were built.<br /> <br /> Elders are just the hazards of being a vampire, no way to avoid it. You still have a better chance of becoming an Elder yourself in the Camarilla than anywhere else.</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing that I made a part of my books (that have NOTHING to do with my past experiences with the WOD) was that every Elder kind of resents vampires younger than them that aren't under their control or childer.<br /> <br /> Because they're competition for food and can bring attention to you.<br /> <br /> So, almost every Neonate gets harassed by Elders for seemingly no reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T13:16:10-07:00","id":1299359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299348#post1299348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea of people losing their shit over accurate representation of mental health issues is hilarious!</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it?<br /> <br /> Look at my avatar and you'll know what my favorite clan is.<br /> <br /> On my end, it's basically the view that some ideas are just not very good ones and you can't &quot;fix&quot; them. It's like if someone said, &quot;Let's redo the Ravnos! I want to DOUBLE DOWN on the fact they're Romani! Make them the most Romani clan ever!&quot;<br /> <br /> And, well, that's a REALLY dumb idea.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T13:18:09-07:00","id":1299360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299295#post1299295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps I am alone that I think House Carna exists solely to give Tremere a bunch of sexy witches.</div> </div> </div> </div>I got your back. Last night I was reading up on the lhiannan and thinking House Carna should not so much be a bloodline as a micro-sect of blood magic using vampire women. Sexy optional, but welcome.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T13:31:09-07:00","id":1299366,"title":"","content":"I'm a bit confused by the 'I thought x weren't supposed to be sympathetic/goodie two shoes'. I always thought the point was all your options kind of sucked: Cam, Anarch, Sabbat - doesn't matter, you're gonna be played, used, and partake in shitty stuff that's bad for *your choice of Path*. Every Clan brought something to the table that was worth considering, but everyone also sucked in one way or another - Brujah I imagine are simply the easiest to use for a mainstream-ish storyline while closing an eye or two to ignore the (sometimes glaring) problems. (Disclaimer: I like Brujah, there was a time I was a sucker for their archetype, I am still fond of them.) Depending on your table and what you wanted out of the game, one of these would fit better than the others - from brooding and troubled teenager with a dark past and a big secret (what's the cheesiest you got? I think the cheesiest I came across was a 'new 2nd Generation, embraced by Cain himself to do.... something something salvation') to absolute repentless monster (powerless geek going batshit crazy over power - kinda like the protagonist of the movie Chronicles you could say). That was part of the charm, no?<br /> <br /> Personally, I am thrilled about the trailer, it even got me into proper Masquerade mood again. The feeling was pretty much spot on for me. Won't preorder due to reasons, but will most likely buy it the second it is out if it's even approaching the first game's level, but with updated graphics and gameplay. <i>Especially </i>with mod support - that's a gift that keeps on giving.<br /> The naming of Disciplines as Powers is a bit weird to me right now, but then, it's still a ways to go, that is a detail that might well be changed (or maybe by joining a clan you get access to real disciplines, or there might be some other in-game reasoning, who knows).<br /> The Thinblood/Caitiff idea is interesting imo, curious to see it plays out.<br /> To me, the most decisive factors are: &quot;Does it capture the mood?&quot; and &quot;Is the writing on a similar level to Bloodlines? (If they manage the same cheek-in-tongue, I'd be delighted!)&quot;<br /> The rest would be common-place for any video game (balance, gameplay, possibilities of customization e.g. different approaches to the same problem, interactiveness/impact on the game world, graphics etc. etc.), and it of course won't be exempt from these criteria. Still, I appear to be far more optimistic than a lot of the people who've posted here.<br /> <br /> Sidenote on the whole politics debate: I agree the games have always been political. I also see people's point on 'hope it's not too x'- basically, I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6363_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6363\" data-vbnamecard=\"6363\">PM\u00e1rk</a> (assuming I got your point right): it shouldn't turn into preaching, same as Bloodlines didn't. Depict a variety of people, agendas, motivations etc., make sure none of these are totally without merit or at least relateable, and ideally none of these are obviously 'right' or 'good', and we should be good. Hell, a sympathetic 'leftist pandering' character's solution going sour while the unsympathetic 'evil rightist pandering' character had a good point would make for a fun quest, just to really strengthen the point that there are mostly shades of greys. Just make sure to include the inverse in some case, too.<br /> For example: I've always felt Bloodlines' storytelling somewhat favoured the Anarchs. They were the most sympathetic faction, yes, but for me at least they managed to make a very poor first impression, and on the first playthrough, I went solo simply because they pissed me off just as much as LaCroix (had I known about the non-LaCroix Camarilla ending, I'd have gone with that). You will find different people arguing for what is the most reasonable choice here (mostly boils down to Strau\u00df vs Anarchs vs Solitude, due to the nature of the other endings), and all of them will make good points. Same goes for how to interpret different characters and their actions: is Damsel sympathetic or not? What about Nines, Strau\u00df, Jack? The heavy dose of cheek-in-tongue satire only made things even better.<br /> I realize that 2004 was a very different time, and things need to be changed somewhat - I don't mind as long as I get a fun game. I <i>really </i>loved the Fishmalk- I also see how that can be problematic. Also also, though, I see the potential a more in-depth confrontation with mental illness could bring to the game. When it comes to the topics of inclusion, V:tM was quite progressive for it's time, I don't see why that trend shouldn't continue, and I don't expect it to somehow negatively impact my prefered style of playing, just as I didn't mind romance options in Dragon Age Inquisition that had nothing to do with my prefered style of playing. *snipped a bunch of stuff due to rambling*<br /> So yeah, it won't be exactly like Bloodlines, because times have changed. That's okay, we have, too. I just hope it will be a worthy successor, and I choose to be optimistic about it; nothing I have seen so far suggests otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T13:57:41-07:00","id":1299377,"title":"","content":"I have some hope that we'll be seeing some returning characters, though my favorites like Fat Larry, Chunk, Romero and V.V. are probably doubtful to appear, unfortunately. <br /> <br /> Maybe the Raptor can make another appearance. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T14:15:17-07:00","id":1299388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299377#post1299377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have some hope that we'll be seeing some returning characters, though my favorites like Fat Larry, Chunk, Romero and V.V. are probably doubtful to appear, unfortunately.<br /> <br /> Maybe the Raptor can make another appearance.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Fat Larry and Chunk would be SO cool!<br /> <br /> Why does the (probably Elder) kindred lady feel so familiar though?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T14:30:35-07:00","id":1299399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299366#post1299366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sidenote on the whole politics debate: I agree the games have always been political. I also see people's point on 'hope it's not too x'- basically, I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6363_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6363\" data-vbnamecard=\"6363\">PM\u00e1rk</a> (assuming I got your point right)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> it shouldn't turn into preaching, same as Bloodlines didn't. Depict a variety of people, agendas, motivations etc., make sure none of these are totally without merit or at least relateable, and ideally none of these are obviously 'right' or 'good', and we should be good. Hell, a sympathetic 'leftist pandering' character's solution going sour while the unsympathetic 'evil rightist pandering' character had a good point would make for a fun quest, just to really strengthen the point that there are mostly shades of greys. Just make sure to include the inverse in some case, too.<br /> For example: I've always felt Bloodlines' storytelling somewhat favoured the Anarchs. They were the most sympathetic faction, yes, but for me at least they managed to make a very poor first impression, and on the first playthrough, I went solo simply because they pissed me off just as much as LaCroix (had I known about the non-LaCroix Camarilla ending, I'd have gone with that). You will find different people arguing for what is the most reasonable choice here (mostly boils down to Strau\u00df vs Anarchs vs Solitude, due to the nature of the other endings), and all of them will make good points. Same goes for how to interpret different characters and their actions: is Damsel sympathetic or not? What about Nines, Strau\u00df, Jack? The heavy dose of cheek-in-tongue satire only made things even better. </div> </div> </div>Agree.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I realize that 2004 was a very different time, and things need to be changed somewhat </div> </div> </div>Somewhat. I really hope it won't to the extent V5's style and lookout changed in comparison to prior editions. I hope it'll have the gothic-punk VtM feel to it, because it won't work for me without that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - I don't mind as long as I get a fun game. I <i>really </i>loved the Fishmalk- I also see how that can be problematic. </div> </div> </div>I'd just say it's not meant to be depiction of real people struggling with mental disorders/illnesses, but a depiction of magically cursed insane vampire-prophets and it meant to be fun and it was fun. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also also, though, I see the potential a more in-depth confrontation with mental illness could bring to the game. </div> </div> </div>I could too, namely, very few people enjoying playing Malkavians.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When it comes to the topics of inclusion, V:tM was quite progressive for it's time, I don't see why that trend shouldn't continue, and I don't expect it to somehow negatively impact my prefered style of playing, just as I didn't mind romance options in Dragon Age Inquisition that had nothing to do with my prefered style of playing. *snipped a bunch of stuff due to rambling* </div> </div> </div>So, you know, I never had a problem with Fatima being a lesbian Muslim super-assasin warrior-woman from the middle ages and having a relationship with Lucita, another awesome warrior-woman from the same time. Never had a problem with Theo Bell being the signature Brujah, with his past as a slave having great importance. Yeah, WoD went for inclusion back then at it was good.<br /> <br /> Thing is, you could absolutely go too far with it, to the point, when it feels forced and just preaching and shouting &quot;oh, look, how awesomely diverse we are, please Polygon, give us a good review!!!!&quot;. If that was exacerbated by every second character and dialogues/story being preachy, well...<br /> <br /> I'm not saying it'll be like that. Hope not. It jsut has a potential to some level of that, IMO. Also again, giving the option for not just two gender pronouns is not like that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T14:41:11-07:00","id":1299402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299388#post1299388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fat Larry and Chunk would be SO cool!<br /> <br /> Why does the (probably Elder) kindred lady feel so familiar though?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Any Bloodlines-proprietary characters, we'll have to see. WW/Paradox doesn't own those, so they'd have to buy the rights to use them in the game. Or see what rights they've currently bought, with the references to them in BJD and V5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5704-thebiglarpnerd","name":"thebiglarpnerd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T14:43:02-07:00","id":1299403,"title":"","content":"I think the redhead is Victoria Ash<br /> Perhaps she's the one who offers the ex-thin pod camarilla membership.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T14:48:25-07:00","id":1299407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299399#post1299399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could too, namely, very few people enjoying playing Malkavians.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.pcgamer.com/hellblade-senuas-sacrifice-wins-big-at-the-2018-bafta-games-awards/\" target=\"_blank\">Yeah, who would ever play a realistically portrayed mental illness?</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T14:49:54-07:00","id":1299408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299399#post1299399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Somewhat. I really hope it won't to the extent V5's style and lookout changed in comparison to prior editions. I hope it'll have the gothic-punk VtM feel to it, because it won't work for me without that.<br /> <br /> [...]<br /> <br /> I'd just say it's not meant to be depiction of real people struggling with mental disorders/illnesses, but a depiction of magically cursed insane vampire-prophets and it meant to be fun and it was fun.<br /> <br /> <br /> [...]<br /> Thing is, you could absolutely go too far with it, to the point, when it feels forced and just preaching and shouting &quot;oh, look, how awesomely diverse we are, please Polygon, give us a good review!!!!&quot;. If that was exacerbated by every second character and dialogues/story being preachy, well...<br /> <br /> I'm not saying it'll be like that. Hope not. It jsut has a potential to some level of that, IMO. Also again, giving the option for not just two gender pronouns is not like that.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think we're about 99,999% on the same page. I know very little about V5, I have to admit, though. Seconding wanting some gothic punk.<br /> <br /> I totally get the point, and I wouldn't be sad one bit (thrilled, in fact) to see the Fishmalk make a comeback. However, distinguishing the two isn't always that easy for people, and I can see how people with mental health problems would want to see themselves included/represented truthfully rather than in a similar-looking-if-at-heart-conceptually-different caricature. A good in-depth storyline and gameplay (the possibilities for Horror!) with a Malkavian that also shines some light on real-world issues I could totally get behind if done right (which would be a lot harder than a fun Fishmalk. A lot.) People most likely would play Malkavians a lot less, though. (@Cifer I think dissonance of expectations and delivery would play a role - Bloodlines' Fishmalk is dear to many people, and they'd likely expect a comeback)<br /> <br /> Those worries are understandable and could ruin or impair an otherwise fun game though as of now, I do not share them (just old-fashioned faith in the old squad, I guess?). I also quite dislike Polygon and hope they don't put any credit at all to them. Not because of the idea, but because of what it came to represent.<br /> <br /> Btw: I guarantee someone is going to basically recreate Bloodlines 1 as a mod if at all possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 03-24-2019, 05:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T15:01:32-07:00","id":1299415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299388#post1299388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fat Larry and Chunk would be SO cool!<br /> <br /> Why does the (probably Elder) kindred lady feel so familiar though?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sounds very much like Nika Futterman, who voiced VV in Bloodlines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T15:08:48-07:00","id":1299418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299359#post1299359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is it?<br /> <br /> Look at my avatar and you'll know what my favorite clan is.<br /> <br /> On my end, it's basically the view that some ideas are just not very good ones and you can't &quot;fix&quot; them. It's like if someone said, &quot;Let's redo the Ravnos! I want to DOUBLE DOWN on the fact they're Romani! Make them the most Romani clan ever!&quot;<br /> <br /> And, well, that's a REALLY dumb idea.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I mean in an ironic sense.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;We're going to treat mental health issues with the proper respect they deserve.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> *everybody who hears the news breaks out into mass hysteria.*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T15:14:09-07:00","id":1299421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299350#post1299350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Malkavians were conceived as the Trickster clan.<br /> <br /> Real life mental illness does not lend itself to Trickster.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, you say that, but then take a look at real life psychopaths, who are extremely proficient at blending in with normal society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T15:14:23-07:00","id":1299422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299407#post1299407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://www.pcgamer.com/hellblade-senuas-sacrifice-wins-big-at-the-2018-bafta-games-awards/\" target=\"_blank\">Yeah, who would ever play a realistically portrayed mental illness?</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, couldn't read your link without disabling all my adblock and cookie protection, but from what wikipedia said, it sounds like the made something i would find <b><i>highly uncomfortable</i></b> to play. I don't want to have to wonder if my meds have stopped working. If there's going to be a mental illness in a game for the PC, it's better if it's a superpower/magic interpretation. Not Realistic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T16:14:00-07:00","id":1299448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299421#post1299421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, you say that, but then take a look at real life psychopaths, who are extremely proficient at blending in with normal society.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have often thought the longest ongoing prank by the entire clan is to pretend to be insane in a comicbook, or old-TV show style, when the norms are around. But they are not that insane and act as normal around each other as they can be.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T16:17:23-07:00","id":1299449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a major strawman and you know it. Not to mention that if the writing staff of the game is going to create a character that is playable then you know you're just trotting out that strawman. On top of that the gulf between &quot;nuanced mental illness depiction.&quot; and &quot;Hey a fish malk!&quot; is wide enough for a blue whale.<br /> <br /> Check out Helblade's development and get back to me about that when you have something more than that awful argument.<br /> <br /> So Really?<br /> <br /> You want your character to be a demonization of mental illness and fish Malkdom because you're too unwilling to actually put some effort into it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you read what i said about helblade?<br /> <br /> You're telling me that i'm <i><b>not allowed</b></i> to not want to have to deal with a realistic reminder of the kind of crap my brain does to me? That being able to play a someone with mental issues that <i><b>are not </b></i>goddamn torturous is a bad thing?<br /> <br /> Really?<br /> <br /> You might be one of the people who enjoys being able to play a game with realistic depictions of psychosis, but i can't just put my brain down and stop playing.<br /> <br /> So forgive my informed opinion as someone currently struggling with these kinds of issues for <i><b>wanting a game to provide enjoyable escape.</b></i><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T17:03:56-07:00","id":1299463,"title":"","content":"As someone loaded down with their own mental illnesses to the point of being a total shut-in: you did construct an (offensive, to me personally) strawman, and you don't speak for all of us.<br /> <br /> Mental illness is incredibly stigmatized, and it's very comforting to see a realistic, respectful depiction in fiction. If you watch the making-of videos of the aforementioned Hellblade, they consulted with people who suffered the same symptoms displayed in-game (including visual and auditory hallucinations) and all of them, as well, were thrilled to help let &quot;normal&quot; people experience what it's like.<br /> <br /> I'm not offended by the original VtM:B depiction of malks and mental illness (let's remember that there were &quot;mentally ill&quot; people in Grouse's mansion who were not Malkavian, depicted as murderous lunatics), and I wouldn't be offended if they include that depiction in the sequel, but a more nuanced, realistic, and respectful depiction would be absolutely admirable and preferred.<br /> <br /> VtM is also about a world far more miserable and gross than ours ever will be. It's not really the sort of game/theme/setting for escapism. It covers a lot of dark topics, and attempting to make VtM:B2 an escape for its players would neuter it as a game and a story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T17:17:03-07:00","id":1299465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299463#post1299463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As someone loaded down with their own mental illnesses to the point of being a total shut-in: you did construct an (offensive, to me personally) strawman, and you don't speak for all of us.<br /> <br /> Mental illness is incredibly stigmatized, and it's very comforting to see a realistic, respectful depiction in fiction. If you watch the making-of videos of the aforementioned Hellblade, they consulted with people who suffered the same symptoms displayed in-game (including visual and auditory hallucinations) and all of them, as well, were thrilled to help let &quot;normal&quot; people experience what it's like.<br /> <br /> I'm not offended by the original VtM:B depiction of malks and mental illness (let's remember that there were &quot;mentally ill&quot; people in Grouse's mansion who were not Malkavian, depicted as murderous lunatics), and I wouldn't be offended if they include that depiction in the sequel, but a more nuanced, realistic, and respectful depiction would be absolutely admirable and preferred.<br /> <br /> VtM is also about a world far more miserable and gross than ours ever will be. It's not really the sort of game/theme/setting for escapism. It covers a lot of dark topics, and attempting to make VtM:B2 an escape for its players would neuter it as a game and a story.</div> </div> </div> </div>What strawman? My own lived experience is a strawman now?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T17:31:27-07:00","id":1299468,"title":"","content":"Likening &quot;more respectful depiction of mental illness&quot; to &quot;total shut-in who can't leave the house&quot; (what I am) as a reason why it's unplayable and a bad idea is both a strawman (constructing your own argument to argue against, rather than arguing against the argument your opponent presented) and offensive (using my personal mental illnesses as an argument against a positive representation of my personal mental illnesses).<br /> <br /> If you are also a shut-in, then again: you do not speak for all of us, and I do not appreciate you trying to argue against positive representation by speaking as if your personal experiences supercede those of other mentally ill people (the people involved in Hellblade and myself included). A great many of us would very much adore more positive representation to help other people understand our condition better. It'd be great to be able to admit to mental illness in public without people immediately jumping to the mental image of muzzles, straight-jackets, and butcher-knives that VtM:B used to depict us.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T18:01:15-07:00","id":1299479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299468#post1299468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Likening &quot;more respectful depiction of mental illness&quot; to &quot;total shut-in who can't leave the house&quot; (what I am) as a reason why it's unplayable and a bad idea is both a strawman (constructing your own argument to argue against, rather than arguing against the argument your opponent presented) and offensive (using my personal mental illnesses as an argument against a positive representation of my personal mental illnesses).<br /> <br /> If you are also a shut-in, then again: you do not speak for all of us, and I do not appreciate you trying to argue against positive representation by speaking as if your personal experiences supercede those of other mentally ill people (the people involved in Hellblade and myself included). A great many of us would very much adore more positive representation to help other people understand our condition better. It'd be great to be able to admit to mental illness in public without people immediately jumping to the mental image of muzzles, straight-jackets, and butcher-knives that VtM:B used to depict us.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not respectful, realistic. I have gone through all the examples i gave. Those are real. I do not want them as part of a game that has provided so much welcome relief for many years. Being able to get into another character is very useful to me. Having the terminiolgy and rules to use as a baseline to marshal my thoughts against hallucinations was a godsend.<br /> <br /> <i><b>I</b></i> have never claimed to speak for anyone. What annoys me is people who do. You're housebound? I'm sorry to hear that, but i'm not going to claim your opinion doesn't matter because it doesn't agree with mine. There are already youtube videos that simulate mental conditions, i can't watch those. Why would i want to, i already know how bad it can be.<br /> <br /> I am just expressing my opinion, and admittedly getting angry when people are telling me i'm wrong for having that.<br /> <br /> And honestly, who actually thinks that &quot; mental image of muzzles, straight-jackets, and butcher-knives&quot;. Thats Victorian<br /> I can tell pretty much anyone i have mental issues, i have no shame about it, it doesn't come up in conversation much, but if some one asks i'll tell them. If they freak out about it, then that saves me time in finding out they're a waste of carbon later.<br /> <br /> Not speaking for anyone but me, so we're clear, just my situation, if that's allowed<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit, This is just going to give me issues, not coming back to this thread, clearly not welcome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":1037,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","user":"jamiemalk","date":". 03-24-2019, 09:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T18:15:45-07:00","id":1299484,"title":"","content":"Anyway, let's change the topic a bit. Anyone else here wants the game to have a &quot;no combat&quot; route? In the RPG I play social primaries all the time, and at least 5 Clans focus on social engineering and manipulating others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T18:48:21-07:00","id":1299488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299484#post1299484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, let's change the topic a bit. Anyone else here wants the game to have a &quot;no combat&quot; route? In the RPG I play social primaries all the time, and at least 5 Clans focus on social engineering and manipulating others.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that's likely but I hope it's minimal combat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T18:57:52-07:00","id":1299490,"title":"","content":"I believe I saw in an interview just today where Mitsoda was quoted as saying that a no kill play would not be possible, but that a minimal killing play would be viable. Some situations will certainly lead to violence it seems, but certainly not all (or possibly even most based on the quote, seemed like you could get away with very few kills if you went for that).<br /> <br /> So, I think a minimal combat approach is plausible, but I'd make sure every character can at least have something going for them when push comes to shove.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">-Red</span></b> V5 Fan Content: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1259556-v5-the-masquerade\" target=\"_blank\">The Masquerade</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256114-v5-tzimisce-and-vicissitude\" target=\"_blank\">Tzimisce and Vicissitude</a> (non Program take), <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1253331-loresheets-chicago\" target=\"_blank\">Loresheet: Chicago</a> (pre CbN V5), <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1251576-v5-resonance-flavor\" target=\"_blank\">Resonance Flavor</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1291918-v5-morality\" target=\"_blank\">Morality System</a> Project Manager, Developer, Community Outreach at <a href=\"https://www.huntersentertainment.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Entertainment</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6164-red-eye","name":"Red Eye","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6164_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T20:05:43-07:00","id":1299499,"title":"","content":"Outright preventing violence from the start, by the player, would limit options and choices for the character. That would limit the character development of the character, limit the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T20:15:18-07:00","id":1299500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Red Eye</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299490#post1299490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe I saw in an interview just today where Mitsoda was quoted as saying that a no kill play would not be possible, but that a minimal killing play would be viable. Some situations will certainly lead to violence it seems, but certainly not all (or possibly even most based on the quote, seemed like you could get away with very few kills if you went for that).<br /> <br /> So, I think a minimal combat approach is plausible, but I'd make sure every character can at least have something going for them when push comes to shove.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Of course it wouldn't be possible. What the hell are you expecting to do with the antagonists of the story? Talk them out of their evil ways?<br /> <br /> Or maybe you could stake them, and entomb the body somewhere?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T20:18:20-07:00","id":1299502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299500#post1299500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Of course it wouldn't be possible. What the hell are you expecting to do with the antagonists of the story? Talk them out of their evil ways?<br /> <br /> Or maybe you could stake them, and entomb the body somewhere?</div> </div> </div> </div>Tie them to a sarcophagus and drop them into the ocean?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24824-notempathic","name":"NotEmpathic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24824_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T21:43:15-07:00","id":1299511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299500#post1299500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Of course it wouldn't be possible. What the hell are you expecting to do with the antagonists of the story? Talk them out of their evil ways?<br /> <br /> Or maybe you could stake them, and entomb the body somewhere?</div> </div> </div> </div>Are these rhetorical questions, and if not why are they directed at me? I'm confused as to when I made any such implications.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">-Red</span></b> V5 Fan Content: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1259556-v5-the-masquerade\" target=\"_blank\">The Masquerade</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256114-v5-tzimisce-and-vicissitude\" target=\"_blank\">Tzimisce and Vicissitude</a> (non Program take), <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1253331-loresheets-chicago\" target=\"_blank\">Loresheet: Chicago</a> (pre CbN V5), <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1251576-v5-resonance-flavor\" target=\"_blank\">Resonance Flavor</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1291918-v5-morality\" target=\"_blank\">Morality System</a> Project Manager, Developer, Community Outreach at <a href=\"https://www.huntersentertainment.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Entertainment</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6164-red-eye","name":"Red Eye","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6164_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T00:26:46-07:00","id":1299533,"title":"","content":"Well sometimes you could talk people out of their evil ways.<br /> <br /> Like the Gangrel pretending to be the Punisher.<br /> <br /> And sometimes they were Brother Vick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T02:29:58-07:00","id":1299548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299500#post1299500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course it wouldn't be possible. What the hell are you expecting to do with the antagonists of the story? Talk them out of their evil ways?</div> </div> </div> </div>Tell their crimes to the Prince? Frame them for your crimes to the Prince? Manipulate events so they lose their power? Remind them of their lost Humanity? Debate them out of existence?<br /> <br /> If you think a story can only end with you killing someone, you may be lacking in imagination.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1037_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1037\" data-vbnamecard=\"1037\">jamiemalk</a><br /> Even if they choose to go for a realistic portrayal of mental illness, it would still be only one clan in 5+ that may not be playable for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3118,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","user":"Cifer","date":". 03-25-2019, 08:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T05:03:48-07:00","id":1299561,"title":"","content":"TBH different ways to solve conflicts specially ways that don't force me to add dots on strenght or melee are very appreciated and one of the most important things IMO(third since mood and narrative are the priorites), like i was replaying bloodlines RN as a Ventrue focusing on social, knowing that the last sequence of the game is a huge combat only sequence i basically started to add dots on firearms but then i remembered that guns are very useless on boss fights specially with the teleporting bosses like the Tzimisce so here i go add dots on strenght and melee and was similar to what happened when i played with my Nosferatu i was focusing on stealth but in the middle of the game i had to add tons of dots in potence and strenght and melee","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24396,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24396-queer-snake","user":"Queer Snake","date":". 03-25-2019, 08:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24396-queer-snake","name":"Queer Snake","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T06:02:22-07:00","id":1299569,"title":"","content":"The Bloodlines 2 video trailer looks quite good. I'm eager to see what clans are available. Based on the small number of &quot;coming soon&quot; clan circle icons and pics attached to them, I expect we'll see the Ventrue, Toreador, Brujah, Nosferatu, Tremere and either Malkavian or Gangrel. My fervent hope is that add-ons will allow for All six of these clans to be available as well as Ministry of Set and the Banu Haqim. I'd LOVE if a Lasombra and Hecata/Giovanni add on were developed, as Lasombra has been developed for V5 already and the Hecata are in development right now with Onyx Path, which one would hope would result in Paradox communicating closely with the developing teams in their licensees to for accuracy. I know that Tzimisce and Ravnos have yet to be announced in any form of media, but wouldn't it be grand if between Onyx Path, Modiphius and Paradox, we could get all 13 clans developed on on our PC's for a computer game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T06:39:26-07:00","id":1299578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Red Eye</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299511#post1299511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are these rhetorical questions, and if not why are they directed at me? I'm confused as to when I made any such implications.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not directed at anybody in particular. Was just using a general sense of the word &quot;you.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Queer Snake</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299561#post1299561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">TBH different ways to solve conflicts specially ways that don't force me to add dots on strenght or melee are very appreciated and one of the most important things IMO(third since mood and narrative are the priorites), like i was replaying bloodlines RN as a Ventrue focusing on social, knowing that the last sequence of the game is a huge combat only sequence i basically started to add dots on firearms but then i remembered that guns are very useless on boss fights specially with the teleporting bosses like the Tzimisce so here i go add dots on strenght and melee and was similar to what happened when i played with my Nosferatu i was focusing on stealth but in the middle of the game i had to add tons of dots in potence and strenght and melee</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, the trailer shows you using telekinesis to retrieve a weapon. I can see that power also being applied to stealth mechanics, like how tossing things around the environment worked in Bloodlines 1.<br /> <br /> As for guns being useless: Try to Uzi, Flamethrower and Assault Rifle. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-25-2019, 09:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T07:08:32-07:00","id":1299585,"title":"","content":"Just chiming in, but<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299468#post1299468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you are also a shut-in, then again: you do not speak for all of us, and I do not appreciate you trying to argue against positive representation by speaking as if your personal experiences supercede those of other mentally ill people</div> </div> </div> </div>That goes both ways, you know. Neither of your experiences and viewpoints are more or less relevant, or justified than the other's.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It'd be great to be able to admit to mental illness in public without people immediately jumping to the mental image of muzzles, straight-jackets, and butcher-knives that VtM:B used to depict us. </div> </div> </div>I know full well that mental illness is still stigmatized. Part of it is understandable, but as always a lot of it is unfair and untrue.<br /> <br /> However, we're not living in the 19th century any more. Stereotypes and fears ar still around, to some extent, but in the West, you won't get locked into an asylum, by having anxiety and depression problems, or the like. Heck, it's gotten to be hard to find <i>anybody</i> on the internet, who aren't saying they have some kind of issue. I think most people could make a distinction between Malkavians and mentally ill real people (and they could understand that Malkavians aren't supposed to be a depiction of the later), nevertheless between real people and those in VTMB, who got to be mind-fucked by a truly insane mad scientist vampire.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T07:25:27-07:00","id":1299589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299585#post1299585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know full well that mental illness is still stigmatized. Part of it is understandable, but as always a lot of it is unfair and untrue.<br /> <br /> However, we're not living in the 19th century any more. Stereotypes and fears ar still around, to some extent, but in the West, you won't get locked into an asylum, by having anxiety and depression problems, or the like. Heck, it's gotten to be hard to find <i>anybody</i> on the internet, who aren't saying they have some kind of issue. I think most people could make a distinction between Malkavians and mentally ill real people (and they could understand that Malkavians aren't supposed to be a depiction of the later), nevertheless between real people and those in VTMB, who got to be mind-fucked by a truly insane mad scientist vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet stigmatization remains a very real and sometimes lethal problem. So much so that in the US, one of the basic rules seems to be &quot;don't call the police to deal with a mentally ill person&quot; for the simple reason that they might get shot rather than calmed down or subdued. &quot;Autistic&quot; is still being used by many news organizations as a synonym for &quot;completely lacking in common sense or empathy.&quot;<br /> <br /> Realistic and empathic portrayal of mental illnesses in high-profile media can help change public perception. Fishmalks can do their part in perpetuating stereotypes somewhere between &quot;mentally ill people are goofy and shouldn't be taken seriously&quot; and &quot;mentally ill people are dangerous and unpredictable.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3118,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","user":"Cifer","date":". 03-25-2019, 10:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T07:54:52-07:00","id":1299597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Queer Snake</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299561#post1299561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">TBH different ways to solve conflicts specially ways that don't force me to add dots on strenght or melee are very appreciated and one of the most important things IMO(third since mood and narrative are the priorites), like i was replaying bloodlines RN as a Ventrue focusing on social, knowing that the last sequence of the game is a huge combat only sequence i basically started to add dots on firearms but then i remembered that guns are very useless on boss fights specially with the teleporting bosses like the Tzimisce so here i go add dots on strenght and melee and was similar to what happened when i played with my Nosferatu i was focusing on stealth but in the middle of the game i had to add tons of dots in potence and strenght and melee</div> </div> </div> </div>The best socially solvable quest has to be the gargoyle one. Nothing like blackmailing Strauss over the Gargoyle, then convincing it to join the Anarchs AND telling Isaac who created it. All of this with just your guile and cleverness as your weapons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T09:18:53-07:00","id":1299618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299589#post1299589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yet stigmatization remains a very real and sometimes lethal problem. So much so that in the US, one of the basic rules seems to be &quot;don't call the police to deal with a mentally ill person&quot; for the simple reason that they might get shot rather than calmed down or subdued. &quot;Autistic&quot; is still being used by many news organizations as a synonym for &quot;completely lacking in common sense or empathy.&quot;<br /> <br /> Realistic and empathic portrayal of mental illnesses in high-profile media can help change public perception. Fishmalks can do their part in perpetuating stereotypes somewhere between &quot;mentally ill people are goofy and shouldn't be taken seriously&quot; and &quot;mentally ill people are dangerous and unpredictable.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this has a lot more to say about your cops in America than the public perceptions of mental illness tbh. From the training videos I've seen the attitude is treat everyone like they are going to try and kill you, if they do not comply,be ready to shoot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16290-generallyconfused","name":"GenerallyConfused","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16290_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T09:21:40-07:00","id":1299619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GenerallyConfused</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299618#post1299618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this has a lot more to say about your cops in America than the public perceptions of mental illness tbh. From the training videos I've seen the attitude is treat everyone like they are going to try and kill you, if they do not comply,be ready to shoot.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet minorities like people of colour or the mentally ill do get shot proportionally more often.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T09:23:27-07:00","id":1299622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299619#post1299619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yet minorities like people of colour or the mentally ill do get shot proportionally more often.</div> </div> </div> </div>They also cause crime and violence, and are carrying and using firearms, proportionally more often.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T09:27:21-07:00","id":1299623,"title":"","content":"On another note: Since when did &quot;Malkavian&quot; become synonymous to &quot;mentally ill&quot;? Isn't the whole point of the Malkavians that their insanity is supernatural and alien in nature? Isn't the fact that we are comparing that to real mental illnesses the real problem?<br /> <br /> This problem is approached from completely the wrong direction and, if approached from the right angle, can actually be solved super easily. We need to get rid of the idea that Malkavian madness is (or should be) somehow related to real mental illness, and instead make it abundantly clear that the Malkavian's madness is supernatural in nature and has absolutely nothing to do with real mental illness. After doing that, we can do whatever we want with the Malkavians, we can make them as fishy as we want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T09:28:13-07:00","id":1299624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299619#post1299619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yet minorities like people of colour or the mentally ill do get shot proportionally more often.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's my point. Cops training encourages this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16290-generallyconfused","name":"GenerallyConfused","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16290_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T09:55:43-07:00","id":1299634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299623#post1299623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On another note: Since when did &quot;Malkavian&quot; become synonymous to &quot;mentally ill&quot;? Isn't the whole point of the Malkavians that their insanity is supernatural and alien in nature? Isn't the fact that we are comparing that to real mental illnesses the real problem?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, they are mad prophets, they are the Clan of the Moon, aka, Lunatics. They are are insane, not just mentally ill. They are pretty much the extreme version of the Victorian archetype and way beyond &quot;regular&quot; mental illness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This problem is approached from completely the wrong direction and, if approached from the right angle, can actually be solved super easily. We need to get rid of the idea that Malkavian madness is (or should be) somehow related to real mental illness, and instead make it abundantly clear that the Malkavian's madness is supernatural in nature and has absolutely nothing to do with real mental illness. After doing that, we can do whatever we want with the Malkavians, we can make them as fishy as we want. </div> </div> </div>I'd say their madness could resemble real mental illnesses (that's how the game always treated it), but I always treated it as being more extreme, more insidious. Think Arkham Asylum instead of your regular mental health center. It's getting exaggerated by the Beast (or caused by the Curse, if they didn't have problems before the embrace).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T10:01:59-07:00","id":1299637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299634#post1299634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, they are mad prophets, they are the Clan of the Moon, aka, Lunatics. They are are insane, not just mentally ill. They are pretty much the extreme version of the Victorian archetype and way beyond &quot;regular&quot; mental illness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you say the same could or should apply to the Ravnos?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T10:15:39-07:00","id":1299643,"title":"","content":"Just want to throw in that my view of Clan Malkavian is that there are indeed very loud and visible members with outright madness that rings loud and clear for everyone to see. And there are those who &quot;only&quot; get a more subtle things that don't make them into raving madmen 24/7. So just like with the Nosferatu, who I think I can recall can get members so monsterous or with such deformities that they can't either be left to exist or leave the sewers, and its kind of the same with the Malkavian. Some will have very powerful effects from their weakness and some will have less so. Life isn't fair and the inheritance of Malkav isn't either.<br /> <br /> EDITED: But while I think it should be treated with respect and with some research going into the types presented in the game, I think that beyond the potential PC Malkavian, the other two Malkavians in Bloodlines felt well done to me so that's an ok level to reach for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":970,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","user":"Gurkhal","date":". 03-25-2019, 01:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T10:19:23-07:00","id":1299645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299637#post1299637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would you say the same could or should apply to the Ravnos?</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you expand on this? I'm not sure what you're getting at","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16290-generallyconfused","name":"GenerallyConfused","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16290_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T10:40:21-07:00","id":1299651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299643#post1299643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just want to throw in that my view of Clan Malkavian is that there are indeed very loud and visible members with outright madness that rings loud and clear for everyone to see. And there are those who &quot;only&quot; get a more subtle things that don't make them into raving madmen 24/7. So just like with the Nosferatu, who I think I can recall can get members so monsterous or with such deformities that they can't either be left to exist or leave the sewers, and its kind of the same with the Malkavian. Some will have very powerful effects from their weakness and some will have less so. Life isn't fair and the inheritance of Malkav isn't either.<br /> <br /> EDITED: But while I think it should be treated with respect and with some research going into the types presented in the game, I think that beyond the potential PC Malkavian, the other two Malkavians in Bloodlines felt well done to me so that's an ok level to reach for.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Twins and Grout were done rather well, I agree. Especially Grout, who I considered to be totally sane for the first stretch of his mansion.<br /> If they find space for both extremes (fishmalk, 100% realistic depiction) and everything in between, I'd be happy. Would also keep you guessing everytime you meet a Malk. There's likely no right answer, and in the end, I hope they go with what makes for a better/more immersive experience.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T10:58:24-07:00","id":1299656,"title":"","content":"Going a bit on a rant here, but I always wanted to play a Malkavian inspired by Alice Liddell from American McGee's Alice and Alice: Madness Returns, but so far I never had the chance because I always end up playing Vampire the Requiem with my mates instead of Vampire the Masquerade (I suppose I could make a Ventrue with the Malkovian bloodline, or a Mekhet with the Malkavia disease, but it's not the same). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T11:42:30-07:00","id":1299666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299656#post1299656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going a bit on a rant here, but I always wanted to play a Malkavian inspired by Alice Liddell from American McGee's Alice and Alice: Madness Returns, but so far I never had the chance because I always end up playing Vampire the Requiem with my mates instead of Vampire the Masquerade (I suppose I could make a Ventrue with the Malkovian bloodline, or a Mekhet with the Malkavia disease, but it's not the same). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>The lack of a 'proper' Malkavian Clan or equivalent substitute was what kept me off of Requiem for a long time (well Malkavian and Tzcimisce), so I can relate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T11:42:54-07:00","id":1299667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GenerallyConfused</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299645#post1299645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you expand on this? I'm not sure what you're getting at</div> </div> </div> </div>The main criticism about the Ravnos is that they're a walking Roma stereotype with basically every &quot;gypsy&quot; prejudice thrown in, up to a clan weakness that makes them prone to vice and crime. Would you say that they would be less tone-deaf if it was clarified that they're totally not real Roma, but a supernatural form and their penchant for vice is exaggerated by the Beast?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T12:05:08-07:00","id":1299677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299622#post1299622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They also cause crime and violence, and are carrying and using firearms, proportionally more often.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you just? Whew, okay. Damn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T12:09:02-07:00","id":1299679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299622#post1299622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They also cause crime and violence, and are carrying and using firearms, proportionally more often.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Flagged for racism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T12:13:21-07:00","id":1299685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299667#post1299667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main criticism about the Ravnos is that they're a walking Roma stereotype with basically every &quot;gypsy&quot; prejudice thrown in, up to a clan weakness that makes them prone to vice and crime. Would you say that they would be less tone-deaf if it was clarified that they're totally not real Roma, but a supernatural form and their penchant for vice is exaggerated by the Beast?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you'd have to ask the people who are saying that. I've never thought they were actually meant to be &quot;real gypsies&quot;. In much the same way that other clans are based on loose stereotypes, any adult can easily see the difference. I bought the gypies book, it was hilariously bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16290-generallyconfused","name":"GenerallyConfused","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16290_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T12:37:01-07:00","id":1299693,"title":"","content":"I think as originally written the Ravnos were rather stereotypical but I believe there is a good concept there that has never been realized. Its fine to say Ravnos embrace from among the Roma stock occasionally and draw some inspiration from that. People love the Setites for their Egyptian motif and Giovanni are quite popular so there is nothing inherently wrong with drawing similar lines with the Ravnos and in fact it can be virtuous to highlight the positives of a traditionally misunderstood culture.<br /> <br /> I think obviously where they went wrong is with their weakness. Saying all ravnos are liars and thieves and then tying it to a racial group is a recipe for disaster. If it had been along the lines of the V20 Dark Ages weakness all along where they are compelled to indulge in their virtue or vice as well as broadening the clan background as they did to include indian, eastern European, and maybe even more Asian influences you could have a much deeper clan that would not be shunned as much as they have been historically. To me its a don't throw the baby out with the bathwater scenario and I hope the stigma attached to the Ravnos lessens in the future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Hecata are a sect not a clan.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24211-frontline989","name":"Frontline989","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T12:45:28-07:00","id":1299696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GenerallyConfused</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299685#post1299685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you'd have to ask the people who are saying that. I've never thought they were actually meant to be &quot;real gypsies&quot;. In much the same way that other clans are based on loose stereotypes, any adult can easily see the difference. I bought the gypies book, it was hilariously bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same here.<br /> <br /> There are plenty of Romani people around here, where I live. I got that the Ravnos, as their most shallow, most stereotypical corebook depiction were basically the trickster gypsi archetype. Never got me to judge real-world people aroud me in accordance to it. Also, let's face it: it's a <i>popular</i> archetype.<br /> <br /> But surprise-surprise, not every Italian is an incestous banker either. I'm able to handle archetypes/tropes for what they are, not as a generalization of real people.<br /> <br /> Hell, maybe as an in-world lore, the said archetype might be the result of the Ravnos' influence, not the other way around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T12:50:13-07:00","id":1299697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frontline989</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299693#post1299693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think as originally written the Ravnos were rather stereotypical but I believe there is a good concept there that has never been realized. Its fine to say Ravnos embrace from among the Roma stock occasionally and draw some inspiration from that. People love the Setites for their Egyptian motif and Giovanni are quite popular so there is nothing inherently wrong with drawing similar lines with the Ravnos and in fact it can be virtuous to highlight the positives of a traditionally misunderstood culture.<br /> <br /> I think obviously where they went wrong is with their weakness. Saying all ravnos are liars and thieves and then tying it to a racial group is a recipe for disaster. If it had been along the lines of the V20 Dark Ages weakness all along where they are compelled to indulge in their virtue or vice as well as broadening the clan background as they did to include indian, eastern European, and maybe even more Asian influences you could have a much deeper clan that would not be shunned as much as they have been historically. To me its a don't throw the baby out with the bathwater scenario and I hope the stigma attached to the Ravnos lessens in the future.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree.<br /> <br /> Generally, I'm glad I came in with Revised and left out the more... let's say, <i>unrefined</i> parts of the lore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T13:11:35-07:00","id":1299703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299623#post1299623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On another note: Since when did &quot;Malkavian&quot; become synonymous to &quot;mentally ill&quot;? Isn't the whole point of the Malkavians that their insanity is supernatural and alien in nature? Isn't the fact that we are comparing that to real mental illnesses the real problem?<br /> <br /> This problem is approached from completely the wrong direction and, if approached from the right angle, can actually be solved super easily. We need to get rid of the idea that Malkavian madness is (or should be) somehow related to real mental illness, and instead make it abundantly clear that the Malkavian's madness is supernatural in nature and has absolutely nothing to do with real mental illness. After doing that, we can do whatever we want with the Malkavians, we can make them as fishy as we want.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is literally what they did in 5th Edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T13:12:59-07:00","id":1299705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299622#post1299622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They also cause crime and violence, and are carrying and using firearms, proportionally more often.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you please give a link to a serious, non-partizan, factual study, regarding the topic? Or a good site with statistics?<br /> <br /> Not asking to be contrary, I'm genuinely interested in the facts behind this. I just want to know, if the notion that minorities in the US (or really, anywhere in the first world, like Great Brittain, Germany, France, etc.) are having a proportionally bigger problem with gun violence and illegal gun usage, than the majority population, is true, or not, based on hard numbers, not just perception.<br /> <br /> If no, then, it seems to be really a quasi-racist ingrained prejudice in the police, from there. If, however, yes, that asks a lot of other social and economical questions which wouldn't be solved by not talking about it. <br /> <br /> Also, it's just a hunch, but I don't think mentally ill people are just feared, because regular people, including cops, feel they couldn't trust in their reactions and that is highly stressfull, thus, they leave a hard impression, but I don't think it's really a big portion of crime and violence, especially firearm usage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T13:15:27-07:00","id":1299706,"title":"","content":"The mentally ill are much much MUCH more likely to have violence DONE to them than commit violence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T13:17:49-07:00","id":1299707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299623#post1299623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On another note: Since when did &quot;Malkavian&quot; become synonymous to &quot;mentally ill&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Uhhhhh? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The Malkavian insight is supernaturally mystical in origin. But the clan has always made it very clear that their madness can manifest in almost any kind of diagnosis. Some may be able to blend in as functional members of society, at least for a time. While others may be raving, incoherent gibbering messes.<br /> <br /> There is a very good reason why nobody in their right mind wants to be anywhere near a Malkavian if they have any choice in the matter. They're completely unpredictable, and that makes them difficult to deal with at best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T13:39:24-07:00","id":1299714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299706#post1299706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The mentally ill are much much MUCH more likely to have violence DONE to them than commit violence.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is likely true, but when you're a cop, I think having to deal with someone, who don't have the same reactions &quot;normal&quot; people do, that's unpredictable and terr\u00edfying and leaves a lasting impression, regardless of how frequent it actually is. Same with drug users, drunk people and the like, I guess. It's just a higher &quot;oh shit, what they would do?&quot; factor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T14:20:35-07:00","id":1299731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299705#post1299705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could you please give a link to a serious, non-partizan, factual study, regarding the topic? Or a good site with statistics?<br /> <br /> Not asking to be contrary, I'm genuinely interested in the facts behind this. I just want to know, if the notion that minorities in the US (or really, anywhere in the first world, like Great Brittain, Germany, France, etc.) are having a proportionally bigger problem with gun violence and illegal gun usage, than the majority population, is true, or not, based on hard numbers, not just perception.<br /> <br /> If no, then, it seems to be really a quasi-racist ingrained prejudice in the police, from there. If, however, yes, that asks a lot of other social and economical questions which wouldn't be solved by not talking about it.<br /> <br /> Also, it's just a hunch, but I don't think mentally ill people are just feared, because regular people, including cops, feel they couldn't trust in their reactions and that is highly stressfull, thus, they leave a hard impression, but I don't think it's really a big portion of crime and violence, especially firearm usage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know about non-partisan since I am not that familiar with American politics and related groups, but I'll try: The <a href=\"https://www.naacp.org/latest/preventing-gun-violence/\" target=\"_blank\">NAACP</a> lists Afro-American men as the victims of roughly 50% of all gun-related deaths, despite making up about 6% of the population. This <a href=\"https://www.hks.harvard.edu/sites/default/files/centers/wiener/programs/pcj/files/PoliceandPublicDiscourseBlackonBlackViolence.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">paper </a>goes more into depth regarding black-on-black violence. Also <a href=\"https://www.naacp.org/criminal-justice-fact-sheet/\" target=\"_blank\">NAACP</a> Afro-Americans are more likely to go to prison/make up a larger part of the incarcerated population. According to <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Race_and_crime_in_the_United_States#Homicide\" target=\"_blank\">wikipedia</a>, Afro-Americans were responsible for slightly more than half of all homicides from 1980 to 2008, the majority of that intraracial (83% of Whites killed by Whites, 94% of Afro-Americans killed by Afro-Americans).<br /> I did some (very basic, since it wasn't the focus) research on this topic two years ago when writing a term paper on gangsta rap culture and poverty and I think there is a bureau with statistics for this, but damned if I remember the name. If I remember correctly, the problem is essentially this: Afro-Americans are more likely to shoot other Afro-Americans, in e.g. gang wars, robberies, heated fights. This is a result of growing up in urbanized, oftentimes poor and/or criminalized areas ('ghettos'). The former (and some bias) leads to more Afro-Americans missing a parent who is in jail, which in turn promotes poverty (you often need two fully employed adults to be able to pay for rent and stuff), which in turn creates more fertile ground for criminal activities (not to mention the emotional damage etc.). Now add racist history (and the resulting lack of generations of 'accumulated successes' that so many people take for granted), racist policies (targeting marijuana or crack as a dangerous drug over cocaine for example) and add a crab-bucket-like effect on top, and you get a hellish environment that favours those willing to commit violence.<br /> [Point of my paper, btw, was that gangsta rap is both empowering to a degree (e.g. by making it big you get to fulfill the dream of having money and being 'free' of the ghetto, it is a celebration of Afro-American culture, hiphop enjoys prestige with society at large, it offers a creative outlet for negative and destructive emotions etc etc.) as well as destructive (glorifying gangsta lifestyle creates an atmosphere that is beneficial to a criminal lifestyle, perpetuating the problems, and it is actually hard to truly become 'free' of the ghetto due to ties established).]<br /> <br /> Disclaimer: I tried to approach this topic purely academically, no bias or racial profiling in mind. I do not mean to disparage Afro-Americans nor their culture. Ignoring that Afro-Americans are more likely to shoot each other or be involved in violent crimes against one another however leads to the situation you may find in the USA in certain areas, where their living space is flooded with violence that they are helpless to face because authorities and media prefer to ignore it and let the problem 'sort itself out'. Ignoring that they are more likely to commit crimes that will get them sent to prison, and the effect that has on their community, does not help solve the problem, either. It needs to be talked about, in-depth, to make people realize how the situation came to pass, so that every American citizen realizes their stake in this and so they realize the problematic elements in their community and rise against them.<br /> <br /> Finally, I apologize for this rant that went far more off-topic than I wanted to go, but somehow couldn't stop, and now that it's gotten so long I don't want to just delete it ^^&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> On the topic of 'minimal violence runs': I'd love it if Bloodlines 2 offered the same amount of freedom of approach that Bloodlines did. Talking to people, sneaking around problems, using Disciplines or being outright violent to achieve the same goal = awesomeness and high replay value. If they could also keep that for the whole game rather than 2/3rds of it, it would be much appreciated =D<br /> I imagine something similar to Deus Ex: Human Revolution, where except for very few boss fights, you could go for a no-kill route or even ghost run.<br /> That, btw, would also totally be awesome: a distinction between a violent but non-lethal and a brutal lethal approach. You could argue something similar could be pulled of for social interaction, too: blackmailing Malcolm was a different kind of job from tricking Chuck into believing you to have authority or whatnot.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T14:50:24-07:00","id":1299742,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8542_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8542\" data-vbnamecard=\"8542\">Wormwood</a> Thank you and let me say I think I agree with your conclusions and oppinion.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T17:15:24-07:00","id":1299782,"title":"","content":"QUOTE=PM\u00e1rk;n1299705]<br /> <br /> Could you please give a link to a serious, non-partizan, factual study, regarding the topic? Or a good site with statistics?<br /> <br /> Not asking to be contrary, I'm genuinely interested in the facts behind this. I just want to know, if the notion that minorities in the US (or really, anywhere in the first world, like Great Brittain, Germany, France, etc.) are having a proportionally bigger problem with gun violence and illegal gun usage, than the majority population, is true, or not, based on hard numbers, not just perception.<br /> <br /> If no, then, it seems to be really a quasi-racist ingrained prejudice in the police, from there. If, however, yes, that asks a lot of other social and economical questions which wouldn't be solved by not talking about it.<br /> <br /> Also, it's just a hunch, but I don't think mentally ill people are just feared, because regular people, including cops, feel they couldn't trust in their reactions and that is highly stressfull, thus, they leave a hard impression, but I don't think it's really a big portion of crime and violence, especially firearm usage.[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> Between 1980-2008, African-Americans accounted for roughly 52% of ALL homicides in the US (interestingly, about 93% of their victims were other African-Americans). Only about 3-11% of guns used in these crime are legally purchased (per 2014 FBI) - some years it may be as high as 15%.<br /> <br /> Per the FBI Uniform Crime Reports, in 2008 African-American youths, about 16% of the youth population, accounted for 52% of juvenile violent crime arrests, including roughly 58% of youth arrests for homicide and 67% for robbery.<br /> <br /> Urbanization and the drug trade are HUGE factors, which make easy demographic and morbidity/mortality comparison to other countries difficult. Also compounding this is the reluctance of some countries to publish complete statistics (looking at you, UK) as well as using different definitions of certain crimes (i.e. any crime in the US where the perpetrator is carrying a gun is a gun crime, whether or not the gun was brandished or used -- In the UK, it is only reported as a gun crime if the gun was used, the victim injured or killed, and the perpetrator found GUILTY of the gun's usage).<br /> <br /> The mentally ill are not feared - people with &quot;altered mental status&quot; make first responders nervous. This includes people who are drunk, high, agitated patients off their medications, people suffering from health issues altering their behavior, etc. These situations can be very stressful for ALL involved - speaking as both a paramedic and tactical paramedic.<br /> <br /> Painting law enforcement as &quot;racist&quot; or having &quot;ingrained prejudice&quot; is a facile and lazy argument (NOT that you are making it). Racism abounds in all sections of society, just as false cries of oppression and victimization. Again, a complicated issue. As first responders have great powers, they should be watched closely and held accountable to a higher level.<br /> <br /> Sources (DOJ, FBI, etc);<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.bjs.gov/content/pub/pdf/htus8008.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://bjs.ojp.gov/sites/bjs/files/images/2021-02/OGimage_0.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.bjs.gov/content/pub/pdf/htus8008.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"> Home </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.bjs.gov/content/pub/pdf/htus8008.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.bjs.gov/content/pub/pdf/htus8008.pdf </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The Bureau of Justice Statistics (BJS) is the United States' primary source for criminal justice statistics that cover a wide range of topics. </div> </div> </div><br /> Cooper, Alexia (2012). Homicide Trends in the United States, 1980-2008.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/homicides-fall-to-lowest-rate-in-four-decades-133967273.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.prnewswire.com/content/dam/prnewswire/homepage/LIGHT_PRNewswire_By-Cision_Stacked.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/homicides-fall-to-lowest-rate-in-four-decades-133967273.html\" target=\"_blank\"> Homicides Fall to Lowest Rate in Four Decades </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/homicides-fall-to-lowest-rate-in-four-decades-133967273.html\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/homicides-fall-to-lowest-rate-in-four-decades-133967273.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> /PRNewswire-USNewswire/ -- The nation's homicide rate fell to 4.8 homicides per 100,000 U.S. residents in 2010, its lowest level in four decades, the Bureau of... </div> </div> </div><br /> Unnever, James (2011). A Theory of African American Offending: Race, Racism, and Crime. Routledge.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.bjs.gov/content/pub/pdf/fv9311.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://bjs.ojp.gov/sites/bjs/files/images/2021-02/OGimage_0.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.bjs.gov/content/pub/pdf/fv9311.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"> Home </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.bjs.gov/content/pub/pdf/fv9311.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.bjs.gov/content/pub/pdf/fv9311.pdf </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The Bureau of Justice Statistics (BJS) is the United States' primary source for criminal justice statistics that cover a wide range of topics. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Cheers,<br /> <br /> Ken","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3370-ken-winland","name":"Ken Winland","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T17:50:52-07:00","id":1299794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299731#post1299731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> *snip*</div> </div> </div> </div>I live in Georgia, and when we turn on the news, it seems like every day we hear of not one, but several crimes involving minority figures robbing, assaulting, killing, or possessing drugs.<br /> <br /> But when it comes to majority members doing the same thing, we get maybe 1 or 2 accounts of them a month.<br /> <br /> Now I'm not saying law enforcement officers aren't racist, but I highly doubt they're sitting around going <i>&quot;well, this guy's white. I guess we can let him steal and murder without consequence.&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-25-2019, 08:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T18:13:57-07:00","id":1299801,"title":"","content":"We did a discussion of this in a political science class and discussing demographics and studies being used for political gain.<br /> <br /> There's a certain skewering of law enforcement elements that makes the issue a &quot;if, and, or but&quot; when dealing with the question of, &quot;Do minorities commit more crimes than the majority?&quot; The short version being, &quot;Yes and no.&quot;<br /> <br /> What are the complicating questions?<br /> <br /> * Are we talking per capita?<br /> * What sort of crimes are we talking about?<br /> * Are the crimes violent crimes or are they crimes like casual drug use (maraujana) or prostitution?<br /> * Are the police responding to crimes by minorities more than they are the majority?<br /> * Are they the minorities or the POOR who minorities are dispoportionately the membership of?<br /> * Which minority group are you talking about?<br /> * Where is the sample being taken from.<br /> <br /> Generally speaking, the numbers start getting very skewed if you remove nonviolent crimes from the issue and compare the averages of minorities to majorites on the same level of income.<br /> <br /> In Kentucky, for example, poor whites are disproportionately more likely to commit violent crimes than poor blacks.<br /> But the numbers even out elsewhere.<br /> <br /> Am I making sense?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-25-2019, 09:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T18:24:03-07:00","id":1299805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299623#post1299623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On another note: Since when did &quot;Malkavian&quot; become synonymous to &quot;mentally ill&quot;? Isn't the whole point of the Malkavians that their insanity is supernatural and alien in nature? Isn't the fact that we are comparing that to real mental illnesses the real problem?<br /> <br /> This problem is approached from completely the wrong direction and, if approached from the right angle, can actually be solved super easily. We need to get rid of the idea that Malkavian madness is (or should be) somehow related to real mental illness, and instead make it abundantly clear that the Malkavian's madness is supernatural in nature and has absolutely nothing to do with real mental illness. After doing that, we can do whatever we want with the Malkavians, we can make them as fishy as we want.</div> </div> </div> </div>When did the Malkavians become &quot;mentally Ill&quot;? since the books represented their clan drawback/weakness as mostly real mental diagnoses, with only a few vampire or supernatural specific ones (Like sanguinary Animism)<br /> <br /> I can agree with what you say in this post at least; it can be solved by divorcing Malkavians from real mental illness. But that's not where the game is at in general. It's a good Houserule, but not canon. I actually like the way the Clan Bane works with V5 because it's a trigger that has a mechanical penalty; All Malkavians are reliably affected in similar ways, and it's firmer on a comparison to other clans. But it's still generally tied to real mental illness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T18:26:18-07:00","id":1299806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299801#post1299801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We did a discussion of this in a political science class and discussing demographics and studies being used for political gain.<br /> <br /> There's a certain skewering of law enforcement elements that makes the issue a &quot;if, and, or but&quot; when dealing with the question of, &quot;Do minorities commit more crimes than the majority?&quot; The short version being, &quot;Yes and no.&quot;<br /> <br /> What are the complicating questions?<br /> <br /> * Are we talking per capita?<br /> * What sort of crimes are we talking about?<br /> * Are the crimes violent crimes or are they crimes like casual drug use (maraujana) or prostitution?<br /> * Are the police responding to crimes by minorities more than they are the majority?<br /> * Are they the minorities or the POOR who minorities are dispoportionately the membership of?<br /> * Which minority group are you talking about?<br /> * Where is the sample being taken from.<br /> <br /> Generally speaking, the numbers start getting very skewed if you remove nonviolent crimes from the issue and compare the averages of minorities to majorites on the same level of income.<br /> <br /> In Kentucky, for example, poor whites are disproportionately more likely to commit violent crimes than poor blacks.<br /> But the numbers even out elsewhere.<br /> <br /> Am I making sense?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes. Basically, people living in crappier conditions are more likely to commit crimes, likely out of desperation, or just pent up anger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T18:37:57-07:00","id":1299809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illithid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299805#post1299805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When did the Malkavians become &quot;mentally Ill&quot;? since the books represented their clan drawback/weakness as mostly real mental diagnoses, with only a few vampire or supernatural specific ones (Like sanguinary Animism)<br /> <br /> I can agree with what you say in this post at least; it can be solved by divorcing Malkavians from real mental illness. But that's not where the game is at in general. It's a good Houserule, but not canon. I actually like the way the Clan Bane works with V5 because it's a trigger that has a mechanical penalty; All Malkavians are reliably affected in similar ways, and it's firmer on a comparison to other clans. But it's still generally tied to real mental illness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Howdy,<br /> <br /> I agree - linking what everyday society regards as mental illness to Malkavian behavior/outlook can be fraught with socially loaded assumptions. They are supernatural, in some cases beggar conventional ideas of sanity. Any traditional application of mental illness underlies mortal/human assumptions. After all, we are talking about a game where characters suck blood, kill, rob and delight in arcane occult beliefs.<br /> <br /> This is also very politically loaded, with regards to the gaming community.<br /> <br /> Cheers,<br /> <br /> Ken","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3370-ken-winland","name":"Ken Winland","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T00:07:24-07:00","id":1299875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299806#post1299806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yes. Basically, people living in crappier conditions are more likely to commit crimes, likely out of desperation, or just pent up anger.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are also much, much more likely to be convicted than a rich person guilty of the same offence and are given harsher sentences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4259-eddie-fiori","name":"Eddie Fiori","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T02:52:42-07:00","id":1299891,"title":"","content":"On to the game, in terms of my hopes.<br /> <br /> No &quot;good&quot; or &quot;bad&quot; endings in terms of morality. If i want to do a full on use, abuse and backstab my way to the top or a help everyone and be vampire batman, they should both have a satisfactory end. One of the reasons i got put off from the first game was the heavy emphasis on the anarch path.<br /> <br /> Template wise, the New Vegas endings would be the ideal. All the factions have good and bad sides, and you get to pick what fits with your character better. Sure, some endings are everything ended up going to hell, but none are blatent &quot;you picked wrong&quot;, here's a nonstandard death.<br /> <br /> Sure, if you cripple everyone and leave the place a wreck, lay on some &quot;and then the sabbat came and killed everyone and turned the city into a living nightmare&quot; but just because i didn't turn the place into a shining beacon of equality and justice (which in my opinion should lead to the worst ending, because WoD) it would be disheartening to have Theo Bell turn up and shotgun my head off...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16290-generallyconfused","name":"GenerallyConfused","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16290_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T03:04:34-07:00","id":1299894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GenerallyConfused</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299891#post1299891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No &quot;good&quot; or &quot;bad&quot; endings in terms of morality. If i want to do a full on use, abuse and backstab my way to the top or a help everyone and be vampire batman, they should both have a satisfactory end. One of the reasons i got put off from the first game was the heavy emphasis on the anarch path.</div> </div> </div> </div>How so? There were five endings, three of them could be considered good, one of them Anarch, but the Camarilla and Independent endings were generally positive too. To actually &quot;lose&quot;, you had to either throw in your lot with the guy who was in utterly over his head or the lady who constantly showed how untrustworthy she was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T04:17:54-07:00","id":1299902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GenerallyConfused</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299891#post1299891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On to the game, in terms of my hopes.<br /> <br /> No &quot;good&quot; or &quot;bad&quot; endings in terms of morality. If i want to do a full on use, abuse and backstab my way to the top or a help everyone and be vampire batman, they should both have a satisfactory end. One of the reasons i got put off from the first game was the heavy emphasis on the anarch path.<br /> <br /> Template wise, the New Vegas endings would be the ideal. All the factions have good and bad sides, and you get to pick what fits with your character better. Sure, some endings are everything ended up going to hell, but none are blatent &quot;you picked wrong&quot;, here's a nonstandard death.<br /> <br /> Sure, if you cripple everyone and leave the place a wreck, lay on some &quot;and then the sabbat came and killed everyone and turned the city into a living nightmare&quot; but just because i didn't turn the place into a shining beacon of equality and justice (which in my opinion should lead to the worst ending, because WoD) it would be disheartening to have Theo Bell turn up and shotgun my head off...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> According to their website, you can either try using your choice of allies to figure out the mysteries surrounding your creation and who's pulling the strings behind the situation, or you can focus more on establishing your own power base among kindred society. That sounds a lot better than being a glorified assassin, like we were in Bloodlines 1.<br /> <br /> Not trash talking Bloodlines 1, it's the game that introduced me to this wonderful franchise to begin with; but I would like to see alternate solutions to problems than just beating it over the head until it stops moving. Social and Mental abilities in the first game were typically rare, and typically restricted to side quests. If you wanted to resolve a real problem, it always came down to violence. Which is a little disappointing for a game who's narrative is about how everybody's trying to deceive and manipulate each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T05:01:01-07:00","id":1299905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299894#post1299894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How so? There were five endings, three of them could be considered good, one of them Anarch, but the Camarilla and Independent endings were generally positive too. To actually &quot;lose&quot;, you had to either throw in your lot with the guy who was in utterly over his head or the lady who constantly showed how untrustworthy she was.</div> </div> </div> </div>As i said, i didn't know about the Strauss camarilla ending, which leaves getting blown up, getting sunk to the bottom of the ocean, doing a Cartman &quot;Screw you guys, I'm going home&quot; and the Anarch one. None of which sounded like they would be satisfying.<br /> <br /> I wasn't able to get the game when it came out, and by the time i was thinking about getting it, these were the endings everyone i knew were talking about, which was dissapointing, as i loved Arcanum, also made by troika games.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299902#post1299902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> According to their website, you can either try using your choice of allies to figure out the mysteries surrounding your creation and who's pulling the strings behind the situation, or you can focus more on establishing your own power base among kindred society. That sounds a lot better than being a glorified assassin, like we were in Bloodlines 1.<br /> <br /> Not trash talking Bloodlines 1, it's the game that introduced me to this wonderful franchise to begin with; but I would like to see alternate solutions to problems than just beating it over the head until it stops moving. Social and Mental abilities in the first game were typically rare, and typically restricted to side quests. If you wanted to resolve a real problem, it always came down to violence. Which is a little disappointing for a game who's narrative is about how everybody's trying to deceive and manipulate each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, i wouldn't be put up or down by the everyone's new favourite courier/assassin. It's the basic model. Giving you options as to how you can go about it would be better.<br /> <br /> Deal with this Nasty Ventrue Buisness Man<span style=\"font-size:8px\"> (TM)</span> . Ok, kill him, frame him, blackmail him, mess with his herd, stage a masquerade breach so the SI will deal with him or sell out the quest giver to score some blue blood favours. That's what i'd hope for, not an obligitory extended parkor chase/fight.<br /> <br /> Also, just a pie in the sky dream, but i'd like not to be forced to play 1st person.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16290-generallyconfused","name":"GenerallyConfused","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16290_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T07:27:43-07:00","id":1299946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardestadtTheEvenYounger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299341#post1299341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Camarilla provides security and stability to the Kindred. It ensures that vampiric society can be civil and peaceful, if not fair.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heeeey, sounds to me basically like real world societies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299707#post1299707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a very good reason why nobody in their right mind wants to be anywhere near a Malkavian if they have any choice in the matter. They're completely unpredictable, and that makes them difficult to deal with at best.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uhm, maybe that could be why in the real world people become wary of the mentally ill? Potential unpredictability?<br /> (I'm not saying it's true, just a random guess)<br /> <br /> Heeeeeeeey, waitaminute... Could this be actually... Talking about real world stuff by NOT talking about it?<br /> Too bad it's an art almost forgotten by nowadays authors, or maybe dismissed easily.<br /> <br /> (An art that, I'm realizing, MarkRein Hagen was very good at)<br /> <br /> By the way talking about the videogame I'm increasingly superexcited at every interview and preview. I'm very positive about it<br /> Speaking of the little circlet for clans in the official website, after checking them I don't think Malkavians will be left out from the first release. I'm actually having hard time finding one that's fitting for the Gangrel.<br /> And I wouldn't be too surprised if the Lasombra were playable in the base game, without DLCs<br /> Makes sense since out of &quot;extra 6&quot; clans they were the less &quot;exotic&quot; and more aligned with the original 7 in concept, more standard vampire fiction.<br /> Coupled with the Camarilla joining could be a way to &quot;canonize&quot; the Lasombra as a pillar of the setting<br /> #Lasombraantitribuwereright<br /> <br /> I'm hoping there will be a 3rd person camera, because in bloodlines I really enjoy watching my guy or gal running and jumping around and stalking prey and moving stealthily","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Ever since the Followers of Set rebranded themselves as The Ministry, I can barely keep a straight face around them.&quot; - Ramona","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","name":"Ravnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15944_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T10:43:01-07:00","id":1299998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ken Winland</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299782#post1299782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Between 1980-2008, African-Americans accounted for roughly 52% of ALL homicides in the US (interestingly, about 93% of their victims were other African-Americans). Only about 3-11% of guns used in these crime are legally purchased (per 2014 FBI) - some years it may be as high as 15%.<br /> <br /> Per the FBI Uniform Crime Reports, in 2008 African-American youths, about 16% of the youth population, accounted for 52% of juvenile violent crime arrests, including roughly 58% of youth arrests for homicide and 67% for robbery.<br /> <br /> Urbanization and the drug trade are HUGE factors, which make easy demographic and morbidity/mortality comparison to other countries difficult. Also compounding this is the reluctance of some countries to publish complete statistics (looking at you, UK) as well as using different definitions of certain crimes (i.e. any crime in the US where the perpetrator is carrying a gun is a gun crime, whether or not the gun was brandished or used -- In the UK, it is only reported as a gun crime if the gun was used, the victim injured or killed, and the perpetrator found GUILTY of the gun's usage).</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you too, for the info!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The mentally ill are not feared - people with &quot;altered mental status&quot; make first responders nervous. This includes people who are drunk, high, agitated patients off their medications, people suffering from health issues altering their behavior, etc. These situations can be very stressful for ALL involved - speaking as both a paramedic and tactical paramedic. </div> </div> </div>Yes, although I used &quot;fear&quot;, I more or less thought about that, thank you for confirming it as someone out on the field.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Painting law enforcement as &quot;racist&quot; or having &quot;ingrained prejudice&quot; is a facile and lazy argument (NOT that you are making it). Racism abounds in all sections of society, just as false cries of oppression and victimization. Again, a complicated issue. As first responders have great powers, they should be watched closely and held accountable to a higher level. </div> </div> </div>Agree, wholeheartedly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sources (DOJ, FBI, etc);<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.bjs.gov/content/pub/pdf/htus8008.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://bjs.ojp.gov/sites/bjs/files/images/2021-02/OGimage_0.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.bjs.gov/content/pub/pdf/htus8008.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"> Home </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.bjs.gov/content/pub/pdf/htus8008.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.bjs.gov/content/pub/pdf/htus8008.pdf </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The Bureau of Justice Statistics (BJS) is the United States' primary source for criminal justice statistics that cover a wide range of topics. </div> </div> </div><br /> Cooper, Alexia (2012). Homicide Trends in the United States, 1980-2008.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/homicides-fall-to-lowest-rate-in-four-decades-133967273.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.prnewswire.com/content/dam/prnewswire/homepage/LIGHT_PRNewswire_By-Cision_Stacked.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/homicides-fall-to-lowest-rate-in-four-decades-133967273.html\" target=\"_blank\"> Homicides Fall to Lowest Rate in Four Decades </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/homicides-fall-to-lowest-rate-in-four-decades-133967273.html\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/homicides-fall-to-lowest-rate-in-four-decades-133967273.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> /PRNewswire-USNewswire/ -- The nation's homicide rate fell to 4.8 homicides per 100,000 U.S. residents in 2010, its lowest level in four decades, the Bureau of... </div> </div> </div><br /> Unnever, James (2011). A Theory of African American Offending: Race, Racism, and Crime. Routledge.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.bjs.gov/content/pub/pdf/fv9311.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://bjs.ojp.gov/sites/bjs/files/images/2021-02/OGimage_0.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.bjs.gov/content/pub/pdf/fv9311.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"> Home </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.bjs.gov/content/pub/pdf/fv9311.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.bjs.gov/content/pub/pdf/fv9311.pdf </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The Bureau of Justice Statistics (BJS) is the United States' primary source for criminal justice statistics that cover a wide range of topics. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Cheers,<br /> <br /> Ken </div> </div> </div>Thank you again!<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T10:49:27-07:00","id":1300001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299801#post1299801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We did a discussion of this in a political science class and discussing demographics and studies being used for political gain.<br /> <br /> There's a certain skewering of law enforcement elements that makes the issue a &quot;if, and, or but&quot; when dealing with the question of, &quot;Do minorities commit more crimes than the majority?&quot; The short version being, &quot;Yes and no.&quot;<br /> <br /> What are the complicating questions?<br /> <br /> * Are we talking per capita?<br /> * What sort of crimes are we talking about?<br /> * Are the crimes violent crimes or are they crimes like casual drug use (maraujana) or prostitution?<br /> * Are the police responding to crimes by minorities more than they are the majority?<br /> * Are they the minorities or the POOR who minorities are dispoportionately the membership of?<br /> * Which minority group are you talking about?<br /> * Where is the sample being taken from.<br /> <br /> Generally speaking, the numbers start getting very skewed if you remove nonviolent crimes from the issue and compare the averages of minorities to majorites on the same level of income.<br /> <br /> In Kentucky, for example, poor whites are disproportionately more likely to commit violent crimes than poor blacks.<br /> But the numbers even out elsewhere.<br /> <br /> Am I making sense?</div> </div> </div> </div>In short: yes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> These things are always complicated.<br /> <br /> Though, in my eyes, speaking about these problems and trends are important. Speaking about them like &quot;this and this minority is predisposed to this and this crime, because it's 'in their blood' &quot;or something like that is abhorrent and I'd never, <i>ever</i> stand behind something like that. But if there's a problem in certain demographical groups, it's doing no good to anyone to pretend it's not there, but we have to talk about it honestly, with considering all the social and economical causes and working for improving on it.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T13:18:51-07:00","id":1300054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299946#post1299946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of the little circlet for clans in the official website, after checking them I don't think Malkavians will be left out from the first release. I'm actually having hard time finding one that's fitting for the Gangrel.<br /> And I wouldn't be too surprised if the Lasombra were playable in the base game, without DLCs<br /> Makes sense since out of &quot;extra 6&quot; clans they were the less &quot;exotic&quot; and more aligned with the original 7 in concept, more standard vampire fiction.<br /> Coupled with the Camarilla joining could be a way to &quot;canonize&quot; the Lasombra as a pillar of the setting<br /> #Lasombraantitribuwereright</div> </div> </div> </div>Two of them look obviously like <b>Tremere </b>and <b>Ventrue</b>.<br /> The one with blood everywhere and smashed window could be <b>Brujah</b>, but I first guessed <b>Malkavian</b>. I'd say Brujah now.<br /> The windowless hallway looks to me like it might be underground , which hints <b>Nosferatu</b>, but it might be some sort of institution or disreputable hangout where a <b>Malkavian</b> goes.<br /> The first picture with the fireplace is the least obvious in my opinion. I assume that <b>Toreador</b> will make it into the base game and none the pictures, perhaps besides the Ventrue one, fit better. It looks comfortable and affluent. That fits the Camarilla as a whole and maybe clans like Tzimisce, Giovanni (not Hecata as a whole), the Ministry and Lasombra, in that order. I expect something more avant garde or flamboyant from Toreador.<br /> The last one on the right (&quot;bonus&quot;) looks like some sort of office. Not that many clans are strongly associated with that sort of work. Ventrue and Tremere have fancier place to work in different ways. The Ministry would probably show some where they receive people. <b>Nosferatu</b> have reason to keep plenty of documents as information brokers and <b>Assamite</b> work could require a lot of information too, about law and whomever they investigate. The bonus label might be significant: Assamites are still something of a novelty in the average VtM game. Nosferatu aren't, but their gameplay might be especially unique and it's not the sort of clan you'd expect the player character join by choice. But both those points also apply to Malkavians.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T13:58:58-07:00","id":1300078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1300001#post1300001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In short: yes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> These things are always complicated.<br /> <br /> Though, in my eyes, speaking about these problems and trends are important. Speaking about them like &quot;this and this minority is predisposed to this and this crime, because it's 'in their blood' &quot;or something like that is abhorrent and I'd never, <i>ever</i> stand behind something like that. But if there's a problem in certain demographical groups, it's doing no good to anyone to pretend it's not there, but we have to talk about it honestly, with considering all the social and economical causes and working for improving on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I recommend watching the documentary 13th for a good conversation about how political forces actively attempted to persecute black Americans by making crimes out of drugs widely used by them (the war on Pot being a war on Black Americans according to its premise).<br /> <br /> But this is off topic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T19:37:59-07:00","id":1300174,"title":"","content":"Just realized, I don't know how becoming Nosferatu (if possible) will affect our character's appearance / body type.<br /> <br /> Maybe it lets you recustomize your character, or maybe your appearance is randomly generated? I'd be disappointed if it came with a stock template transformation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-26-2019, 10:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T23:44:17-07:00","id":1300479,"title":"","content":"My guess is that Nosferatu (and possibly Malkavian) will be a bonus clan, with somewhat altered character generation and game play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4259-eddie-fiori","name":"Eddie Fiori","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T23:49:00-07:00","id":1300480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eddie Fiori</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1300479#post1300479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My guess is that Nosferatu (and possibly Malkavian) will be a bonus clan, with somewhat altered character generation and game play.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> On the clan section page, one of the teaser pictures is some kind of mental asylum, so it's a safe bet that at the very least Malkavians will be one of the 6 or 7 clans released at initial launch. As for Nosferatu, it's more difficult to tell. The final teaser pic on the clan page shows some kind of basement, or crappy apartment building. Which honestly could be anything between Nosferatu, Gangrel, or possibly Assamite.<br /> <br /> <br /> ALSO: want to point out that the developers have said they want you to explore each of the different clans and find out how they work, before you choose which one to join. This, to me, suggests that the clans will have much more distinct play styles from each other than they did in Bloodlines 1. Which is very, very good to hear! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T00:44:27-07:00","id":1300487,"title":"","content":"&quot;Bigger longer sewers. Just sewers. Only sewers&quot; Cara Ellison, lead writter<br /> <br /> If the sewers are etched into her mind, that might suggest the Nos will be fairly prevalent, but if picking your clan is how they're going it would be harder to implement for them. Then again V5 Nos aren't shown as being nearly as hideous in their paper dolls picture, which makes it much easier to just give you a stat penalty and just carry on.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16290-generallyconfused","name":"GenerallyConfused","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16290_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T00:50:28-07:00","id":1300488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GenerallyConfused</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1300487#post1300487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Bigger longer sewers. Just sewers. Only sewers&quot; Cara Ellison, lead writter<br /> <br /> If the sewers are etched into her mind, 