a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T09:57:32-07:00","id":1300866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GenerallyConfused</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1300764#post1300764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't really get the feeling that they need it anymore though. The V5 art makes them look App 1 for the most part, especially for today's standards. They look like they've got skin conditions or burns, but hardly twisted monsters shunned and feared by any who see them. In Dark Ages, they'd still probably be reviled but the fear of leprosy isn't so prevalent anymore and most people don't jump to &quot;Ugly, must be God's judgement&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>The reused MMO concept art isn't super applicable though when the Clan writeup literally says 'they turn into a caricature of Murnau's version' and it calls out lookling like burn victims, people with growths/tumors, etc. It's more about giving people ideas, and allowing them to do things like *GASP!* makeup and prosthetics to cover up deformities rather than constantly rely on powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5704-thebiglarpnerd","name":"thebiglarpnerd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T03:13:50-07:00","id":1301048,"title":"","content":"Old World of Darkness is fraught with stereotypes oh my god. Leaked pictures of a mental asylum? Must be Malkavian! Sewers? Nosferatu. Crappy apartment? Totally Gangrel. It's not like the characters are defined by their personality instead of their clan right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T03:41:17-07:00","id":1301050,"title":"","content":"But theoretically those images are representing the clan stereotypes i think","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24396-queer-snake","name":"Queer Snake","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T05:05:31-07:00","id":1301058,"title":"","content":".<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thebiglarpnerd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1300866#post1300866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The reused MMO concept art isn't super applicable though when the Clan writeup literally says 'they turn into a caricature of Murnau's version' and it calls out lookling like burn victims, people with growths/tumors, etc. It's more about giving people ideas, and allowing them to do things like *GASP!* makeup and prosthetics to cover up deformities rather than constantly rely on powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't know that they'd lifted this from the MMO bucket, but the choice of art is an important decision, especially in the clan write up section. Only four of the eight look like they <i>might </i>have something wrong with their faces, and none of them have visible physical deformities.<br /> <br /> Just having a slightly messed up face is, well, kinda weak for the clan that is meant to be horrific. The book is horrible in terms of style and clarity overall, but this section in particular is very poorly set up to explain the Nosferatu flaw visually.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1301048#post1301048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Old World of Darkness is fraught with stereotypes oh my god. Leaked pictures of a mental asylum? Must be Malkavian! Sewers? Nosferatu. Crappy apartment? Totally Gangrel. It's not like the characters are defined by their personality instead of their clan right?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Stereotypes are very useful to story telling though. So long as you stay away from overtly negative real world ones, like many point at the Ravnos as being a bad example of. Having a clan stereotype gives a base that lets players come up with better stand out characters, and also gives them a &quot;comfortable&quot; niche that they can use to see if they have an affinity for the clan. Not all stereotypes are bad, and a lot have a grain of truth in them somewhere. Pretty much everyone has &quot;stereotypical&quot; mental images of certain groups, and designing characters to conform to or buck these trends is fairly central to storytelling in any medium.<br /> <br /> Introducing new players to a setting can use stereotypes to make adjusting easier by giving a shorthand that almost everyone will grasp very easily. Those stereotypes you're listing are nothing to do with characters, they are clan related, and with good reasons. If a Malkavian wants to blend in, being around a concentration of people who act erratically by &quot;normal&quot; standards is a reasonable choice. Nosferatu hanging around sewers, is again a fairly reasonable choice, there are large homeless populations that form communities in real world city sewers that they can blend into. Not sure how a crappy apartment would nod in the direction of a Gangrel though<br /> <br /> Now, to reiterate, <b><i>Negative Stereotypes Are Bad </i></b>but not all stereotypes are negative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16290-generallyconfused","name":"GenerallyConfused","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16290_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T15:09:17-07:00","id":1301160,"title":"","content":"Anyone else think it's silly that people on Steam are saying they won't be buying the game because they've heard that it will be predominantly featured in 1st person mode?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T15:29:54-07:00","id":1301167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1301160#post1301160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone else think it's silly that people on Steam are saying they won't be buying the game because they've heard that it will be predominantly featured in 1st person mode?</div> </div> </div> </div>No? I mean, there are probably people who won't be buying the game because it's not a MOBA or it isn't set in the Dark Ages. Different people are looking for different things in games and I'd rather have people not buy something than buy it, be unhappy with it and endlessly gripe about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T15:35:53-07:00","id":1301170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1301167#post1301167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No? I mean, there are probably people who won't be buying the game because it's not a MOBA or it isn't set in the Dark Ages. Different people are looking for different things in games and I'd rather have people not buy something than buy it, be unhappy with it and endlessly gripe about it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would actually love to see a Bloodlines inspired Dark Ages game. Being a Nosferatu and stalking through the church's catacombs would be fun. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T16:09:16-07:00","id":1301177,"title":"","content":"I already said i would prefer a 3rd person option at least. If it's got parkor then 1st person sounds like an awful idea. In fact, unless it's a shooter, i can't see why being locked to 1st person would be a good thing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16290-generallyconfused","name":"GenerallyConfused","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16290_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T16:47:52-07:00","id":1301187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GenerallyConfused</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1301177#post1301177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I already said i would prefer a 3rd person option at least. If it's got parkor then 1st person sounds like an awful idea. In fact, unless it's a shooter, i can't see why being locked to 1st person would be a good thing</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> From what I've heard, it sounds like combat will be primarily melee focused. Though I would be surprised if guns were not featured at least somewhat. But yeah, I can see how first person parkour would get very disorienting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T19:40:59-07:00","id":1301205,"title":"","content":"By the way, I think I remember one of the developers mentioning in an interview when discussing the power sets that we'll be able to FLY in this game?<br /> <br /> The power sets for the Thin Bloods are Mist Form, Telekinesis, and Chiropteran, the last of which deals with bats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T19:44:13-07:00","id":1301206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1301205#post1301205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, I think I remember one of the developers mentioning in an interview when discussing the power sets that we'll be able to FLY in this game?<br /> <br /> The power sets for the Thin Bloods are Mist Form, Telekinesis, and Chiropteran, the last of which deals with bats.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They talked about a gliding power, which roughly matches to the TBA power Levitation, like Telekinesis matches to Far Reach. It's all gamified mechanics, it's not like it's going to match directly to the tabletop.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5704-thebiglarpnerd","name":"thebiglarpnerd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T03:45:06-07:00","id":1301264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1301187#post1301187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I've heard, it sounds like combat will be primarily melee focused. Though I would be surprised if guns were not featured at least somewhat. But yeah, I can see how first person parkour would get very disorienting.</div> </div> </div> </div>It worked in Mirror's Edge, so it's probably a question of execution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T05:52:22-07:00","id":1301284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thebiglarpnerd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1300866#post1300866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reused MMO concept art isn't super applicable though when the Clan writeup literally says 'they turn into a caricature of Murnau's version' and it calls out lookling like burn victims, people with growths/tumors, etc. It's more about giving people ideas, and allowing them to do things like *GASP!* makeup and prosthetics to cover up deformities rather than constantly rely on powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was hoping someone would point out this. Read the book, don't stop at the pictures. It's a good book if you give it a chance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GenerallyConfused</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1301058#post1301058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just having a slightly messed up face is, well, kinda weak for the clan that is meant to be horrific. The book is horrible in terms of style and clarity overall, but this section in particular is very poorly set up to explain the Nosferatu flaw visually.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alas, on this I agree completely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1301160#post1301160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone else think it's silly that people on Steam are saying they won't be buying the game because they've heard that it will be predominantly featured in 1st person mode?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. Some people have real difficulties playing in that mode. My sister gets headache sometimes and a friend of mine gets nauseated.<br /> It always boils down to different strokes for different people. Nothing bad with that.<br /> <br /> Personally I would miss a 3rd person mode greatly. I like to see my character in the CRPGs I play.<br /> The 3rd person mode gives the idea of living the adventure in a similar way than reading a book or watching a movie, and I like that. Not everyone is in for the &quot;virtual reality&quot; approach.<br /> I'm not saying I won't buy the game if it doesn't have a 3rd person mode, but I'd surely be less happy without that option.<br /> <br /> As for Dark Ages, I would totally dig a game about the fall and rise of House Tremere <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Ever since the Followers of Set rebranded themselves as The Ministry, I can barely keep a straight face around them.&quot; - Ramona","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","name":"Ravnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15944_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T06:32:33-07:00","id":1301291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GenerallyConfused</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1301058#post1301058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just having a slightly messed up face is, well, kinda weak for the clan that is meant to be horrific. The book is horrible in terms of style and clarity overall, but this section in particular is very poorly set up to explain the Nosferatu flaw visually.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't simplify their curse as just having a &quot;slightly messed up face&quot; as they are, indeed, ugly. They are so ugly that it causes penalties on social interactions but in addition to that, they also have penalties against trying to disguise themselves. This extends not only to the mundane like makeup or prosthetics but it affects Mask of a Thousand Faces and Imposter's Guise as well. They can still use the other powers in Obfuscate without that penalty, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6149-malfean90","name":"Malfean90","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T06:52:43-07:00","id":1301292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malfean90</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1301291#post1301291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wouldn't simplify their curse as just having a &quot;slightly messed up face&quot; as they are, indeed, ugly. They are so ugly that it causes penalties on social interactions but in addition to that, they also have penalties against trying to disguise themselves. This extends not only to the mundane like makeup or prosthetics but it affects Mask of a Thousand Faces and Imposter's Guise as well. They can still use the other powers in Obfuscate without that penalty, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's one of my favourite tweaks in V5. In revised I was &quot;well, Mask is a level 3 power, even neonates can have that&quot; and made no sense for Nosferatu living hidden and such.<br /> So adding difficulties to use Mask of a Thousand Faces was a good call. That route is still viable for those that liked it but it's less cheap.<br /> And really if you chose to play a Nos you didn't want a cheap curse to begin with.<br /> Reminds me I never had the chance to play a Nos. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Hopefully Bloodlines 2 will give me a partial satisfaction for that","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Ever since the Followers of Set rebranded themselves as The Ministry, I can barely keep a straight face around them.&quot; - Ramona","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","name":"Ravnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15944_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T08:14:55-07:00","id":1301314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1301284#post1301284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was hoping someone would point out this. Read the book, don't stop at the pictures. It's a good book if you give it a chance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ayup. BUT MUH ART!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5704-thebiglarpnerd","name":"thebiglarpnerd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T08:28:22-07:00","id":1301316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malfean90</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1301291#post1301291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wouldn't simplify their curse as just having a &quot;slightly messed up face&quot; as they are, indeed, ugly. They are so ugly that it causes penalties on social interactions but in addition to that, they also have penalties against trying to disguise themselves. This extends not only to the mundane like makeup or prosthetics but it affects Mask of a Thousand Faces and Imposter's Guise as well. They can still use the other powers in Obfuscate without that penalty, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was exactly what i was saying, a brief skin of the Nos section gives the impression that a messed up face is the basic flaw. Even in the text, it is fairly weak on the description. You can say they're leaving it wide open for interpretation, but it's bad for giving actual flavour to the write up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16290-generallyconfused","name":"GenerallyConfused","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16290_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T09:14:50-07:00","id":1301325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GenerallyConfused</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1301316#post1301316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That was exactly what i was saying, a brief skin of the Nos section gives the impression that a messed up face is the basic flaw. Even in the text, it is fairly weak on the description. You can say they're leaving it wide open for interpretation, but it's bad for giving actual flavour to the write up.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't know, I'm reading the description of their bane right now and it seems pretty clear to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6149-malfean90","name":"Malfean90","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T09:29:59-07:00","id":1301327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malfean90</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1301325#post1301325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I don't know, I'm reading the description of their bane right now and it seems pretty clear to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the small paragraph at the end does make itself clear, but most of the Nosferatu write up does not. A quick skim makes it look like messed up faces, not repulsive, is their flaw.<br /> <br /> For a book aimed at new players, that's not good. I know what Nosferatu were before, and this section made me think they'd taken a different approach. Put simply, it did a bad job of saying &quot;Nosferatu&quot; to me.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16290-generallyconfused","name":"GenerallyConfused","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16290_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T09:57:22-07:00","id":1301333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GenerallyConfused</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1301058#post1301058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.<br /> <br /> Didn't know that they'd lifted this from the MMO bucket, but the choice of art is an important decision, especially in the clan write up section. Only four of the eight look like they <i>might </i>have something wrong with their faces, and none of them have visible physical deformities.<br /> <br /> Just having a slightly messed up face is, well, kinda weak for the clan that is meant to be horrific. The book is horrible in terms of style and clarity overall, but this section in particular is very poorly set up to explain the Nosferatu flaw visually.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd just point at the Revised clan depictions and call it a day. Honestly, V20 didn't really do it for me either, but V5 even less so.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Stereotypes are very useful to story telling though. So long as you stay away from overtly negative real world ones, like many point at the Ravnos as being a bad example of. Having a clan stereotype gives a base that lets players come up with better stand out characters, and also gives them a &quot;comfortable&quot; niche that they can use to see if they have an affinity for the clan. Not all stereotypes are bad, and a lot have a grain of truth in them somewhere. Pretty much everyone has &quot;stereotypical&quot; mental images of certain groups, and designing characters to conform to or buck these trends is fairly central to storytelling in any medium.<br /> <br /> Introducing new players to a setting can use stereotypes to make adjusting easier by giving a shorthand that almost everyone will grasp very easily. Those stereotypes you're listing are nothing to do with characters, they are clan related, and with good reasons. If a Malkavian wants to blend in, being around a concentration of people who act erratically by &quot;normal&quot; standards is a reasonable choice. Nosferatu hanging around sewers, is again a fairly reasonable choice, there are large homeless populations that form communities in real world city sewers that they can blend into. Not sure how a crappy apartment would nod in the direction of a Gangrel though<br /> <br /> Now, to reiterate, <b><i>Negative Stereotypes Are Bad </i></b>but not all stereotypes are negative. </div> </div> </div><br /> Yup, that's what people tend to forget, when smirking at stereotypes and tropes and clich\u00e9s and such. They <i>work</i>. Either because they touch upon some bigger concept or universal idea, or because they have, at least some of the truth in them. I'd say even negative stereotypes have that, it's just, they tend to lead to persecution, rather than positive solutions.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T09:59:35-07:00","id":1301336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GenerallyConfused</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1301327#post1301327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, the small paragraph at the end does make itself clear, but most of the Nosferatu write up does not. A quick skim makes it look like messed up faces, not repulsive, is their flaw.<br /> <br /> For a book aimed at new players, that's not good. I know what Nosferatu were before, and this section made me think they'd taken a different approach. Put simply, it did a bad job of saying &quot;Nosferatu&quot; to me.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I wouldn't say it did a bad job, at least in my opinion, however I did find that the Nosferatu description before the archetypes was considerably shorter compared to the rest of the clans. A little disappointing for sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6149-malfean90","name":"Malfean90","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T13:32:07-07:00","id":1301390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1301292#post1301292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's one of my favourite tweaks in V5. In revised I was &quot;well, Mask is a level 3 power, even neonates can have that&quot; and made no sense for Nosferatu living hidden and such.<br /> So adding difficulties to use Mask of a Thousand Faces was a good call. That route is still viable for those that liked it but it's less cheap.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interestingly, the penalty is almost entirely counteracted by the Blood Potency bonus you get on your discipline rolls. The Bane Severity can only ever get one dot higher than the bonus (on odd BP values). A Nosferatu Elder is not as good at mimicking other people as a Malkavian or Banu Haqim Elder might be, but they're most likely still better than a Nosferatu Neonate of weaker blood.<br /> Funnily enough, the same applies to the Toreador Bane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T23:41:53-07:00","id":1301533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thebiglarpnerd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1301314#post1301314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ayup. BUT MUH ART!</div> </div> </div> </div>I KNOW RIGHT?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1301390#post1301390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interestingly, the penalty is almost entirely counteracted by the Blood Potency bonus you get on your discipline rolls. The Bane Severity can only ever get one dot higher than the bonus (on odd BP values). A Nosferatu Elder is not as good at mimicking other people as a Malkavian or Banu Haqim Elder might be, but they're most likely still better than a Nosferatu Neonate of weaker blood.<br /> Funnily enough, the same applies to the Toreador Bane.</div> </div> </div> </div>I still have to try the game in actual play, so this outcome escaped my attention.<br /> <br /> I would say it's kind of a downer for me, but it's not irrelevant if we think about it.<br /> Elder Vs Elder, the Toreador/Nos still have 3 dice less than elders of other clans. Not really something to scoff off.<br /> <br /> The funny thing happens when a Nos elder tries to use Mask against a Toreador elder while standing in an ugly sewer...<br /> And the Tremere servant humiliates them both: &quot;Baron! That's the Nosferatu Primogen in disguise!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Ever since the Followers of Set rebranded themselves as The Ministry, I can barely keep a straight face around them.&quot; - Ramona","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","name":"Ravnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15944_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T16:30:16-07:00","id":1302039,"title":"","content":"I also want to give my two cents about the game since there are still no real updates or further reveals. There are 3 things that really concern me at the moment?<br /> <br /> 1. The transition from thin-blood to a full clan member. I know this is possible via diablerie, but honestly it just sounds like a bit of a forced plot. The idea, according to the developers, is for the PC to make a more informed decision about which clan they would like to join. OK, so far so good. Problem with that is it's very difficult to invent a way to join a clan rationally without involving diablerie. Retroactive &quot;revelation&quot; of your clan wouldn't work in particular for Nosferatu and Malkavian, whose curses would be more noticeable, not to mention even if your sire is revealed you are still thin-blood. Ok, let's say you diablerize a clan member - since you've just spent time learning about the clans and, therefore, they know whoyou are it seems a bit weird that some of them would be ok with a diablerie. Toreador, Ventrue and Tremere would all have issues with it. I won't pre-order anything until they reveal how this is handled.<br /> <br /> 2. Tremere houses. Unlike a lot of people in this thread I actually like House Carna. Yes, I know her arguments are not that solid and yes I know she is a product of the growing feminist perspective in the setting, but I'm actually relieved to finally not be Pyramid-bound as a long time Tremere fan and player. Sure, the Pyramid is one of the cool things, it ties into the <b>actual </b>Tremere weakness, makes you paranoid and anxious, restricts character concepts and actions, offers great power and protection at a cost of personal freedom. Cool, but after so many years of that I'm actually tired of having such a monolithic clan. Now, finally, Tremere are split into social, political and paradigm lines and it's finally exciting to make a decision about what kind of Tremere you want to be, not to mention that a bazillion character concepts suddenly became plausible. Traditionalist Camarilla vs Anarch-leaning progressive Camarilla, elitist or inclusive (when it comes to siring), monolithic or cellular, hermetic paradigm or old magic paradigm, strict hierarchy or flat hierarchy with more personal freedom, established vs struggling. For the above reasons I'm really <b>hoping </b>they introduce two houses for clan Tremere, even if this requires more content. Otherwise the whole talk about being in sync with V5 is false. Hell, even give some Thaumaturgy variation based on whether you're a House Tremere hermetic or a House Carna witch, that would be fun.<br /> <br /> 3. Actual content. I mainly lurk around the Bloodlines 2 facebook group and someone just sent me a screenshot of Hardsuit Labs confirming that the entire content of the release (yes, including side quests) will be roughly 25-30 hours. Ok. For a game that's been in development for 3 years (at least) this is nothing. As a regular gamer I've played narrative-heavy games with many branching paths that easily give you 70-80 hours of gameplay, at least. Even if we account for story DLCs in the future I can't see VtM:B2 to have more than 40-45 hours of gameplay. That's quite disappointing.<br /> <br /> So, I'm still waiting for Hardsuit Labs to convince me this game is worth it. Maybe they nailed the atmosphere, who knows, but I need to see some actual content and to get some answers for the above concerns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3567-dobyk","name":"Dobyk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3567_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T02:22:17-07:00","id":1302146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dobyk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1302039#post1302039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, let's say you diablerize a clan member - since you've just spent time learning about the clans and, therefore, they know whoyou are it seems a bit weird that some of them would be ok with a diablerie. Toreador, Ventrue and Tremere would all have issues with it. I won't pre-order anything until they reveal how this is handled.</div> </div> </div> </div>License to commit diablerie is one of the greatest boons you can dangle in front of a Thinblood (or anyone, for that matter). The Camarilla does it sometimes when calling out bloodhunts and Anarchs often just don't care as long as they're not the ones being munched on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T03:20:10-07:00","id":1302150,"title":"","content":"25-30 hours it's pretty much standard for non open-world RPG, especially if they have strong branching paths.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://howlongtobeat.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://howlongtobeat.com/</a><br /> <br /> <br /> Bloodlines 1 was 28 hours<br /> Human Revolution takes 29<br /> Deus Ex 1 takes 28<br /> The Witcher 2 takes 33<br /> Tyranny takes 32<br /> Tides of Numenera 32<br /> <br /> <br /> So it's really not a deviaton from the standard.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T03:21:17-07:00","id":1302151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dobyk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1302039#post1302039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. Actual content. I mainly lurk around the Bloodlines 2 facebook group and someone just sent me a screenshot of Hardsuit Labs confirming that the entire content of the release (yes, including side quests) will be roughly 25-30 hours. Ok. For a game that's been in development for 3 years (at least) this is nothing. As a regular gamer I've played narrative-heavy games with many branching paths that easily give you 70-80 hours of gameplay, at least. Even if we account for story DLCs in the future I can't see VtM:B2 to have more than 40-45 hours of gameplay. That's quite disappointing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. A game that's been in dev for 3 years giving me 30 hours of actual gameplay? That's good in my opinion.<br /> <br /> But more than that, it's important to consider: While it might take ~30 hours to play through the game, does this also account for variations of the gameplay? Different ways to do quests? Replayability through getting different moments and dialogue by picking other Clans, other personalities, and/or also trying out different character builds?<br /> <br /> Because those are the things that can turn &quot;30 hours to get through everything&quot; into a much larger actual number through that sheer replayability, variations and trying different approaches. And from what I heard, the replayability will be a big thing.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> And to mention, before somebody says that RPGs of ye olde used to take much longer...<br /> Yeah, those RPGs also didn't need elaborate voice acting, custom made cutscenes and model animations for all sorts of events. It was much easier to fill a game with gargantuan amounts of story simply by using creativity, the map/script editor and a good document manager.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 04-03-2019, 01:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T03:29:17-07:00","id":1302152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1302151#post1302151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> And to mention, before somebody says that RPGs of ye olde used to take much longer...<br /> Yeah, those RPGs also didn't need elaborate voice acting, custom made cutscenes and model animations for all sorts of events. It was much easier to fill a game with gargantuan amounts of story simply by using creativity, the map/script editor and a good document manager.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Even more all of those old RPGs are pretty much proto-open world with non linear development : Baldur's Gate, Planescape, Fallout, Kotor, Gothic.and so on.<br /> <br /> If you want to take comparison for Bloodlines you must look at Deux Ex, since that's the paragon of that school of RPGs.<br /> And 25-30 hours is pretty much in line with the RPG Deus Ex like.<br /> <br /> <br /> The more branches the main story has , the less you can develop the game in lenght: that's why Heavy Rain or Detroit Become Human, who have big branching stories, takes about 15 hours to get the ending. Same for some RPG very branch-focused like Age of Decadence, which requires 22 hours, main quest + extras.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 04-03-2019, 06:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T03:44:43-07:00","id":1302155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1302151#post1302151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> EDIT:<br /> And to mention, before somebody says that RPGs of ye olde used to take much longer...<br /> Yeah, those RPGs also didn't need elaborate voice acting, custom made cutscenes and model animations for all sorts of events. It was much easier to fill a game with gargantuan amounts of story simply by using creativity, the map/script editor and a good document manager.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The map for Daggerfall was so massive, it took 3 days to walk from one end of it to the other. Ah, the days when Bethesda actually put effort into their game design, instead of depending on modders to finish their work for them...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T04:02:16-07:00","id":1302157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1302155#post1302155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The map for Daggerfall was so massive, it took 3 days to walk from one end of it to the other. Ah, the days when Bethesda actually put effort into their game design, instead of depending on modders to finish their work for them...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeeeah, it was. But it also was...lots and lots of just 'same' landscape filler. The Daggerfall map, IMO, was HUGE quantity over quality.<br /> Now, maps like the one of Ultima 7 on the other hand...those were big, *and* pretty much all parts were so hand-assembled, that you wanted to explore every nook and cranny, expecting something new.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 04-03-2019, 01:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T04:37:38-07:00","id":1302163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1302155#post1302155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The map for Daggerfall was so massive, it took 3 days to walk from one end of it to the other. Ah, the days when Bethesda actually put effort into their game design, instead of depending on modders to finish their work for them...</div> </div> </div> </div>You do realize that the &quot;walk 3 days&quot; thing came to pass because everything was procedurally generated, right? Only a few things were tweaked afterward. If you were content with everything looking kinda the same, you could probably have a landscape that you can walk through for 3 months. Still not the mark of a good game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T06:03:45-07:00","id":1302177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1302157#post1302157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeeeah, it was. But it also was...lots and lots of just 'same' landscape filler. The Daggerfall map, IMO, was HUGE quantity over quality.<br /> Now, maps like the one of Ultima 7 on the other hand...those were big, *and* pretty much all parts wre so hand-assembled, that you wanted to explore every nook and cranny, expecting something new.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Perhaps, but I've been looking at the previous Elder Scrolls games (I started with Morrowind, never got to play the first 2) and I've noticed a recurring pattern. Every sequel in the series keeps reducing the amount of content available for players to actually role play with, in favor of improving the graphics. If I remember correctly, Daggerfall actually let you select your own background, which would have a tangible effect on specific creatures in the world. For example, if you had a previous relationship with Daedric Cults, then such creatures would have been less hostile towards you.<br /> <br /> No idea why they haven't given you the option of joining a religious faction since Morrowind, either. I'm not counting the Knights of the Nine expansion for Oblivion, because that didn't really feel like you were a member of the Imperial Cult. But during the events of Morrowind, you could join the church, and get sent on religious themed quests, such as going on pilgrimages, or curing the sick! You also couldn't advance in guild ranks, unless you had a high enough mastery of the skills associated with that guild.<br /> <br /> But that's no longer the case. Now it's just you joining the faction, doing a mediocre quest chain, and suddenly they elect you their new leader. It doesn't feel like you've earned it, and it comes across as a random assortment of dungeon diving missions. And as for backgrounds, they seem to have defaulted to you just being a random character who ends up in prison for some reason that is never explained!<br /> <br /> I'm a role player, not a power gamer. I'm fine with an RPG not having much in the way of visual appeal, as long as there is plenty of content for me to enjoy myself with!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-03-2019, 09:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T07:05:15-07:00","id":1302192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1299677#post1299677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did you just? Whew, okay. Damn.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did I do what, exactly? What's the problem with what I said? I looked it up before I said it, and it's factual and true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T07:47:46-07:00","id":1302207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1302192#post1302192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did I do what, exactly? What's the problem with what I said? I looked it up before I said it, and it's factual and true.</div> </div> </div> </div>Statistics, or it didn't happen. Show your work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9015-zee-patrick","name":"zee PaTrick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T10:00:07-07:00","id":1302254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zee PaTrick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1302207#post1302207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Statistics, or it didn't happen. Show your work.</div> </div> </div> </div>This got shown earlier in the thread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Between 1980-2008, African-Americans accounted for roughly 52% of ALL homicides in the US (interestingly, about 93% of their victims were other African-Americans). Only about 3-11% of guns used in these crime are legally purchased (per 2014 FBI) - some years it may be as high as 15%.<br /> <br /> Per the FBI Uniform Crime Reports, in 2008 African-American youths, about 16% of the youth population, accounted for 52% of juvenile violent crime arrests, including roughly 58% of youth arrests for homicide and 67% for robbery.<br /> <br /> Urbanization and the drug trade are HUGE factors, which make easy demographic and morbidity/mortality comparison to other countries difficult. Also compounding this is the reluctance of some countries to publish complete statistics (looking at you, UK) as well as using different definitions of certain crimes (i.e. any crime in the US where the perpetrator is carrying a gun is a gun crime, whether or not the gun was brandished or used -- In the UK, it is only reported as a gun crime if the gun was used, the victim injured or killed, and the perpetrator found GUILTY of the gun's usage).<br /> <br /> The mentally ill are not feared - people with &quot;altered mental status&quot; make first responders nervous. This includes people who are drunk, high, agitated patients off their medications, people suffering from health issues altering their behavior, etc. These situations can be very stressful for ALL involved - speaking as both a paramedic and tactical paramedic.<br /> <br /> Painting law enforcement as &quot;racist&quot; or having &quot;ingrained prejudice&quot; is a facile and lazy argument (NOT that you are making it). Racism abounds in all sections of society, just as false cries of oppression and victimization. Again, a complicated issue. As first responders have great powers, they should be watched closely and held accountable to a higher level.<br /> <br /> Sources (DOJ, FBI, etc);<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.bjs.gov/content/pub/pdf/htus8008.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://bjs.ojp.gov/sites/bjs/files/images/2021-02/OGimage_0.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.bjs.gov/content/pub/pdf/htus8008.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"> Home </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.bjs.gov/content/pub/pdf/htus8008.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.bjs.gov/content/pub/pdf/htus8008.pdf </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The Bureau of Justice Statistics (BJS) is the United States' primary source for criminal justice statistics that cover a wide range of topics. </div> </div> </div><br /> Cooper, Alexia (2012). Homicide Trends in the United States, 1980-2008.<br /> <a href=\"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/homicides-fall-to-lowest-rate-in-four-decades-133967273.html\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.prnewswire.com/news-rele...133967273.html</a><br /> Unnever, James (2011). A Theory of African American Offending: Race, Racism, and Crime. Routledge.<br /> <a href=\"https://www.bjs.gov/content/pub/pdf/fv9311.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.bjs.gov/content/pub/pdf/fv9311.pdf</a> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't know about non-partisan since I am not that familiar with American politics and related groups, but I'll try: The <a href=\"https://www.naacp.org/latest/preventing-gun-violence/\" target=\"_blank\">NAACP</a> lists Afro-American men as the victims of roughly 50% of all gun-related deaths, despite making up about 6% of the population. This <a href=\"https://www.hks.harvard.edu/sites/default/files/centers/wiener/programs/pcj/files/PoliceandPublicDiscourseBlackonBlackViolence.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">paper </a>goes more into depth regarding black-on-black violence. Also <a href=\"https://www.naacp.org/criminal-justice-fact-sheet/\" target=\"_blank\">NAACP</a> Afro-Americans are more likely to go to prison/make up a larger part of the incarcerated population. According to <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Race_and_crime_in_the_United_States#Homicide\" target=\"_blank\">wikipedia</a>, Afro-Americans were responsible for slightly more than half of all homicides from 1980 to 2008, the majority of that intraracial (83% of Whites killed by Whites, 94% of Afro-Americans killed by Afro-Americans).<br /> I did some (very basic, since it wasn't the focus) research on this topic two years ago when writing a term paper on gangsta rap culture and poverty and I think there is a bureau with statistics for this, but damned if I remember the name. If I remember correctly, the problem is essentially this: Afro-Americans are more likely to shoot other Afro-Americans, in e.g. gang wars, robberies, heated fights. This is a result of growing up in urbanized, oftentimes poor and/or criminalized areas ('ghettos'). The former (and some bias) leads to more Afro-Americans missing a parent who is in jail, which in turn promotes poverty (you often need two fully employed adults to be able to pay for rent and stuff), which in turn creates more fertile ground for criminal activities (not to mention the emotional damage etc.). Now add racist history (and the resulting lack of generations of 'accumulated successes' that so many people take for granted), racist policies (targeting marijuana or crack as a dangerous drug over cocaine for example) and add a crab-bucket-like effect on top, and you get a hellish environment that favours those willing to commit violence.<br /> [Point of my paper, btw, was that gangsta rap is both empowering to a degree (e.g. by making it big you get to fulfill the dream of having money and being 'free' of the ghetto, it is a celebration of Afro-American culture, hiphop enjoys prestige with society at large, it offers a creative outlet for negative and destructive emotions etc etc.) as well as destructive (glorifying gangsta lifestyle creates an atmosphere that is beneficial to a criminal lifestyle, perpetuating the problems, and it is actually hard to truly become 'free' of the ghetto due to ties established).]<br /> <br /> Disclaimer: I tried to approach this topic purely academically, no bias or racial profiling in mind. I do not mean to disparage Afro-Americans nor their culture. Ignoring that Afro-Americans are more likely to shoot each other or be involved in violent crimes against one another however leads to the situation you may find in the USA in certain areas, where their living space is flooded with violence that they are helpless to face because authorities and media prefer to ignore it and let the problem 'sort itself out'. Ignoring that they are more likely to commit crimes that will get them sent to prison, and the effect that has on their community, does not help solve the problem, either. It needs to be talked about, in-depth, to make people realize how the situation came to pass, so that every American citizen realizes their stake in this and so they realize the problematic elements in their community and rise against them.<br /> <br /> Finally, I apologize for this rant that went far more off-topic than I wanted to go, but somehow couldn't stop, and now that it's gotten so long I don't want to just delete it ^^&quot;<br /> <br /> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24824-notempathic","name":"NotEmpathic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24824_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T10:55:55-07:00","id":1302270,"title":"","content":"Jeez, I asked Ventrue Life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9015-zee-patrick","name":"zee PaTrick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T11:18:14-07:00","id":1302277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1302177#post1302177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that's no longer the case. Now it's just you joining the faction, doing a mediocre quest chain, and suddenly they elect you their new leader. It doesn't feel like you've earned it, and it comes across as a random assortment of dungeon diving missions. And as for backgrounds, they seem to have defaulted to you just being a random character who ends up in prison for some reason that is never explained!</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't want to go too much OT... but you summed up Morrowind here, just saying.<br /> Sure it was cool as a character toolkit, you had more factions, it was true 3-dimensional gameplay (thanks to levitate and a lot of underwater)... but quest-wise it was very repetitive<br /> Oblivion was good quest-wise, but bad in all other aspects IMHO<br /> I've come to prefer Skyrim with time, maybe I'm just getting old. Who knows<br /> <br /> Btw currently playing Bloodlines again. Thank you very much guys<br /> <br /> I tried to make a not-optimized build and the game is still too easy. Sure I die sometimes, but nothing too unbeatable if I stop being mingy with the ammo<br /> <br /> Two well known issues I still find most annoying, I can't help it.<br /> <br /> 1) Compared to Dominate and Dementation, Presence is useless in social interactions (probably is useless on the whole). But this issue I'm confident it will be addressed in the sequel<br /> <br /> 2) Persuasion is a must to complete quest in alternate ways most of the time. I found myself putting dots in research to get Persuasion at least at 5 eventually. Compared to other social skills or social disciplines it's really too much more useful and satisfying. Sad. I don't know how they will address this in the sequel. We'll see.<br /> <br /> The thing I found myself very annoyed by is the fact that money is basically handled like gold pieces in medieval RPGs. Due to tradition of the genre I suppose. And it feels ugly.<br /> Money in VtM should not be something you keep track of single coin after single coin. You should have a resource trait or something that says how much your income is (your weekly allowance if you want) and you play accordingly. It would feel more like a modern day world.<br /> In the first game your only investment possible was to become associate of Venus and get some money sometimes. Cool, but only once.<br /> Also what you can buy with money is just ammo. Sometimes a cooler weapon but mostly you need it for ammo.<br /> Wish you could buy things and employees: stuff for your haven, contacts, info, a car with a driver, corrupt policemen, gangsters, domains, a club to feed within, the blood bank, the whole hospital, your personal skyscraper... (ok I'm exaggerating but you got what I mean)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Ever since the Followers of Set rebranded themselves as The Ministry, I can barely keep a straight face around them.&quot; - Ramona","edited":{"userid":15944,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","user":"Ravnos","date":". 04-03-2019, 02:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","name":"Ravnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15944_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T11:39:25-07:00","id":1302283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1302150#post1302150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">25-30 hours it's pretty much standard for non open-world RPG, especially if they have strong branching paths.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://howlongtobeat.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://howlongtobeat.com/</a><br /> <br /> <br /> Bloodlines 1 was 28 hours<br /> Human Revolution takes 29<br /> Deus Ex 1 takes 28<br /> The Witcher 2 takes 33<br /> Tyranny takes 32<br /> Tides of Numenera 32<br /> <br /> <br /> So it's really not a deviaton from the standard.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You got me there, now that you list those it makes more sense. In my calculation, if all extra clans and story DLCs bring a total of 40 hours gameplay, then let's say 3 playthroughs would be 120, which is good in my book","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3567-dobyk","name":"Dobyk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3567_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T11:41:36-07:00","id":1302284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1302146#post1302146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">License to commit diablerie is one of the greatest boons you can dangle in front of a Thinblood (or anyone, for that matter). The Camarilla does it sometimes when calling out bloodhunts and Anarchs often just don't care as long as they're not the ones being munched on.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but I guess it's more of a personal issue for me. I guess I could rationalise it as personal revenge, but still. Maybe it's just me. <br /> <br /> What about the Tremere houses? Many people in the discord server think they'd be in the game anyway since it's confirmed to be in sync with V5, but no variations for Thaumaturgy tho. What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3567-dobyk","name":"Dobyk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3567_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T11:52:05-07:00","id":1302288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1302277#post1302277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wish you could buy things and employees: stuff for your haven, contacts, info, a car with a driver, corrupt policemen, gangsters, domains, a club to feed within, the blood bank, the whole hospital, your personal skyscraper... (ok I'm exaggerating but you got what I mean)</div> </div> </div> </div>You might be able to do so in Bloodlines 2, since I believe they said you can focus on your own advancement in kindred society, instead of trying to find out answers behind why you were embraced, and by who. I really, really want to be able to establish my own power base in this game. Even if it's just a small territory! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And yes, you will have the option to customize your haven. One of the special versions of the game even comes with some free decorations to put up around your home!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T20:17:15-07:00","id":1302427,"title":"","content":"So we know that Bloodlines 2 will allow you to choose different body types for your character. Unfortunately, we don't know much about what that entails. Whether they are a pre-set option, or if the game has some kind of slider system that allows you to customize your look. Regardless, I've come up with some concept ideas for characters I would like to play in game.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Nosferatu:</b> Very Muscular - while the emaciated beggar is an iconic body type for members of the Nosferatu clan, I'm amused by the idea of how different it would be to prowl the sewers as a roided out monster. Maybe something similar to Killer Croc, from the Arkham games. I know that we probably won't be able to make something that massive, but applying the Nosferatu curse on to a stereotypical Brujah would probably be fun.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ventrue:</b> Fat, or Obese - I am honestly surprised that I haven't heard of this before. Ventrue are supposed to be the clan of wealthy aristocrats and big business tycoons. Why have I not seen any fat people among their ranks!? You'd think somebody who fits the criteria for joining them would have been prone to a life of excess before their embrace.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Brujah:</b> Lean, or Gaunt - In contrast to my burly Nosferatu, I find it amusing that a member of clan Brujah would actually have the build of a 90 pound weakling. The clan as a whole may be synonymous with the motorcycle fetish, but they are also recognized for their burning passion, and desire to change the system. Nobody says you have to be an ex-military operative, or street gang enforcer to satisfy that condition!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Toreador:</b> Old, or Ugly - Don't lie, you all want to try something like this! A member of the Rose clan, who's long past their prime, but manages to get by due to a combination of wealth and fame. I'm thinking something along the lines of Hugh Hefner, or Ron Jeremy...<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Also, I found this!</b></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/186qdjRofqE\" data-code=\"186qdjRofqE\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/186qdjRofqE/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T20:29:28-07:00","id":1302430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1302427#post1302427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Ventrue:</b> Fat, or Obese - I am honestly surprised that I haven't heard of this before. Ventrue are supposed to be the clan of wealthy aristocrats and big business tycoons. Why have I not seen any fat people among their ranks!? You'd think somebody who fits the criteria for joining them would have been prone to a life of excess before their embrace.<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/186qdjRofqE\" data-code=\"186qdjRofqE\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/186qdjRofqE/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>I am perfectly sure that I've seen a line or two in a core book, probably Revisited, that the Embrace shrivels organs and rids the body of much of its excessive body fat leading to a slim body type. That's probably a way to propagate the &quot;vampires are sexy&quot; stereotype&quot; according to modern views on beauty but that's the in-game explination I can think of.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T20:33:45-07:00","id":1302432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1302430#post1302430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am perfectly sure that I've seen a line or two in a core book, probably Revisited, that the Embrace shrivels organs and rids the body of much of its excessive body fat leading to a slim body type. That's probably a way to propagate the &quot;vampires are sexy&quot; stereotype&quot; according to modern views on beauty but that's the in-game explination I can think of.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, I definitely remember it mentioning that most of the body's fluids with the exception of that used for pigmentation and saliva is converted into vitae. As well as the vampire's body starting to wither and shrivel if they allow themselves to starve. But I don't recall anything about loss of body fat.<br /> <br /> But if that's the case, maybe I should get embraced, as part of an easy weight loss program! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-04T03:57:52-07:00","id":1302510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dobyk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1302284#post1302284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about the Tremere houses? Many people in the discord server think they'd be in the game anyway since it's confirmed to be in sync with V5, but no variations for Thaumaturgy tho. What do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>We don't know how strongly the clans feature in the game. If the Tremere are a major faction, I would expect the schism to make an appearance. Perhaps you get to support one or the other faction in their bid for dominance in the local chantry. That said, I don't think there will be much of a mechanical difference beyond &quot;choose cool boon A or B&quot; - certainly not something on the scale of the difference between two clans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-04T04:16:24-07:00","id":1302515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1302510#post1302510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We don't know how strongly the clans feature in the game. If the Tremere are a major faction, I would expect the schism to make an appearance. Perhaps you get to support one or the other faction in their bid for dominance in the local chantry. That said, I don't think there will be much of a mechanical difference beyond &quot;choose cool boon A or B&quot; - certainly not something on the scale of the difference between two clans.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> At first, I was hoping that the mention of &quot;factions&quot; meant the difference between Camarilla, Anarch and Sabbat. But then I heard that 5th edition has apparently split vampire society up into a loose assortment of gangs, rather than unified sects. Now I'm not sure how it will work in the grander scheme of things.<br /> <br /> It's also possible that each of the playable clans might be its own independent faction, and you're competing to see who emerges as the dominant power in Seattle's blood trade.Though that seems unlikely, as that would mean they'd have to almost completely rework the game's story every time they release a new clan DLC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-04T04:49:12-07:00","id":1302519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1302515#post1302515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At first, I was hoping that the mention of &quot;factions&quot; meant the difference between Camarilla, Anarch and Sabbat. But then I heard that 5th edition has apparently split vampire society up into a loose assortment of gangs, rather than unified sects.</div> </div> </div> </div>It hasn't. There's still the Camarilla and Anarch split, which is the most likely fault line in the game. Of course, if you thought that Anarchs were a <i>unified</i> sect, well...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-04T09:01:52-07:00","id":1302575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1302432#post1302432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well, I definitely remember it mentioning that most of the body's fluids with the exception of that used for pigmentation and saliva is converted into vitae. As well as the vampire's body starting to wither and shrivel if they allow themselves to starve. But I don't recall anything about loss of body fat.<br /> <br /> But if that's the case, maybe I should get embraced, as part of an easy weight loss program! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, its instant result but with some unavoidable side effects of a permanent nature. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-04T09:55:34-07:00","id":1302594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1302288#post1302288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You might be able to do so in Bloodlines 2, since I believe they said you can focus on your own advancement in kindred society, instead of trying to find out answers behind why you were embraced, and by who. I really, really want to be able to establish my own power base in this game. Even if it's just a small territory! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That would be very cool. And yeah definetly a small domain. I didn't mean something like a very big business empire.<br /> Something like the local mall, or the local hospital, or the art school. Something like that. That kind of domain would be cool to manage. Not to make the game a management game, but just to give the feel that you can play that kind of vampire if you are so inclined.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1302430#post1302430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am perfectly sure that I've seen a line or two in a core book, probably Revisited, that the Embrace shrivels organs and rids the body of much of its excessive body fat leading to a slim body type. That's probably a way to propagate the &quot;vampires are sexy&quot; stereotype&quot; according to modern views on beauty but that's the in-game explination I can think of.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't remember this, but it would be unsurprising coming from the Revised era. In that edition there was a very AnneRice-ization of the vampire physiology, in the sense that the embrace had some evident effects in the appearance.<br /> <br /> I do remember a passage where it was explained that some Sire made their childer shave before the embrace, because the appearance of the childer gets &quot;frozen&quot; at the one they had at the time of the embrace. Cutting the hair would make them regrow quickly at the lenght they had when embraced. Very Interview with the Vampire style.<br /> <br /> While I do also remember a passage in some older edition where it was stated that hair and fingernails would keep growing almost normally even after the embrace (the explanation was that dead bodies do that for a time, but I don't now if it's true).<br /> In Chicago by Night there was at least one or two overweight vampire characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Ever since the Followers of Set rebranded themselves as The Ministry, I can barely keep a straight face around them.&quot; - Ramona","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","name":"Ravnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15944_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-04T11:04:24-07:00","id":1302605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1302594#post1302594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That would be very cool. And yeah definetly a small domain. I didn't mean something like a very big business empire.<br /> Something like the local mall, or the local hospital, or the art school. Something like that. That kind of domain would be cool to manage. Not to make the game a management game, but just to give the feel that you can play that kind of vampire if you are so inclined.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The video I linked on the previous page goes on to say Bloodlines 2 will more prominently feature social interaction and establishing contacts then the first game did.<br /> <br /> Very, very eager to hear more details about this particular mechanic! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T11:27:36-07:00","id":1302877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1302594#post1302594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't remember this, but it would be unsurprising coming from the Revised era. In that edition there was a very AnneRice-ization of the vampire physiology, in the sense that the embrace had some evident effects in the appearance.<br /> <br /> I do remember a passage where it was explained that some Sire made their childer shave before the embrace, because the appearance of the childer gets &quot;frozen&quot; at the one they had at the time of the embrace. Cutting the hair would make them regrow quickly at the lenght they had when embraced. Very Interview with the Vampire style.<br /> <br /> While I do also remember a passage in some older edition where it was stated that hair and fingernails would keep growing almost normally even after the embrace (the explanation was that dead bodies do that for a time, but I don't now if it's true).<br /> In Chicago by Night there was at least one or two overweight vampire characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't been able to find this section again so maybe I was mis-remembering.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T12:49:13-07:00","id":1302904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1302594#post1302594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I don't remember this, but it would be unsurprising coming from the Revised era. In that edition there was a very AnneRice-ization of the vampire physiology, in the sense that the embrace had some evident effects in the appearance.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I remember reading something about vampires being able to make permanent alterations to their appearance by spending Willpower and repeatedly changing themselves over a long period of time. Eventually, they force the change to stick, though I don't fully remember the specific details on how that works in universe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T02:12:13-07:00","id":1303270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1302877#post1302877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I haven't been able to find this section again so maybe I was mis-remembering.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>No, I've seen it as well. It includes the line &quot;One seldom sees a stout vampire&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4259-eddie-fiori","name":"Eddie Fiori","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-08T14:08:16-07:00","id":1303611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eddie Fiori</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1303270#post1303270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, I've seen it as well. It includes the line &quot;One seldom sees a stout vampire&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah, well. It was just an idea I had for fun. Hopefully, they can still be big and muscular, though. Really want that Nosferatu beef cake idea made manifest. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-08T22:42:41-07:00","id":1303718,"title":"","content":"There's nothing wrong with a little <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/El_Diablo_Verde\" target=\"_blank\"> Diablo Verde</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4259-eddie-fiori","name":"Eddie Fiori","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-09T19:49:49-07:00","id":1303867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dobyk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1302039#post1302039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also want to give my two cents about the game since there are still no real updates or further reveals. There are 3 things that really concern me at the moment?<br /> 1. The transition from thin-blood to a full clan member. I know this is possible via diablerie, but honestly it just sounds like a bit of a forced plot. The idea, according to the developers, is for the PC to make a more informed decision about which clan they would like to join. OK, so far so good. Problem with that is it's very difficult to invent a way to join a clan rationally without involving diablerie. Retroactive &quot;revelation&quot; of your clan wouldn't work in particular for Nosferatu and Malkavian, whose curses would be more noticeable, not to mention even if your sire is revealed you are still thin-blood. Ok, let's say you diablerize a clan member - since you've just spent time learning about the clans and, therefore, they know whoyou are it seems a bit weird that some of them would be ok with a diablerie. Toreador, Ventrue and Tremere would all have issues with it. I won't pre-order anything until they reveal how this is handled.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that you forget that this is a game and it doesn't have to (really won't in many ways) follow the book's rules.<br /> Diablerie; Drinking blood of an elder and an Assamite potion are all ways of officially getting a better generation in (One edition or another) which _could_ manifest the clan.<br /> But, giving them the ability to buy up Blood potency from Zero to One could work, It's within the broad generalities of Thinblood Alchemy to reinforce clan heritage (for Caitiff) and only a small rules bend to do it to an official Thinblood. <br /> A few Bloodlines can even convert you; notable parties being Children of Osiris and Baali, even for Pander I think the ritual officially changes the blood, where Settites will accept you, but your in clan disciplines and weakness doesn't mystically change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-12T15:13:19-07:00","id":1304520,"title":"","content":"It appears that Bloodlines 2 is trying to copy the massive success of Skyrim by mimicing its opening. To wit:<br /> <br /> - The protagonist starts out as a nobody just minding their own business.<br /> - A bunch of goons aligned against the establishment show up and start a thing.<br /> - The establishment shows up and end the thing, arresting everyone involved including you.<br /> - You are carted off somewhere where the establishment decides it's easiest to just murder the lot of you.<br /> - As you are about to be executed a ruckus happens that results in a big fire.<br /> - As everyone is trying to save their hides you escape amidst the chaos.<br /> <br /> And that's discounting how Skyrim and Bloodlines 2 are of the fifth iteration, while both games' prequels in the third iteration, Morrowind and Bloodlines 1, were very rough and buggy but they were held together by hopes, dreams, heart and excellent storytelling and worldbuilding. I do hope that Paradox isn't going to try and sell me this game seven times over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-12T17:07:24-07:00","id":1304537,"title":"","content":"In all fairness, a lot of video games follow a similar formula. Hell, Bloodlines 1 isn't that different really.<br /> <br /> If you're going to have both (1) fairly open character creation and (2) characters thrust into the plot ASAP, you're going to get something pretty close to this. &quot;You're a nobody&quot; means your background can be the most flexible since you don't have to worry about history interacting with the set plot. Disruptive NPCs show up to ensure that action happens instead of you spending a few years training or whatever. Everyone is out to save themselves/seek personal power to ensure that the PC is the one left to actually do the plot instead of them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-13T01:12:45-07:00","id":1304591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1304520#post1304520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It appears that Bloodlines 2 is trying to copy the massive success of Skyrim by mimicing its opening. To wit:</div> </div> </div> </div>As long as they don't copy the unskippable 5 minute cart ride that I can by now quote verbatim, I'd be fine with that.<br /> Other than that: What Heavy Arms says. The setup is just pretty basic and useful. I doubt Skyrim was the first one to make use of it and if people tried to copy the success of Skyrim, the opening is the last part where I'd look for inspiration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-13T09:05:46-07:00","id":1304630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1304520#post1304520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It appears that Bloodlines 2 is trying to copy the massive success of Skyrim by mimicing its opening. To wit:<br /> <br /> - The protagonist starts out as a nobody just minding their own business.<br /> - A bunch of goons aligned against the establishment show up and start a thing.<br /> - The establishment shows up and end the thing, arresting everyone involved including you.<br /> - You are carted off somewhere where the establishment decides it's easiest to just murder the lot of you.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me it more sounds like it starts off very similiarly to...Bloodlines 1 :P<br /> Also as Heavy Arms said, the general premise isn't too different from a couple other stories. I don't think they thought of Skyrim when coming up with this at all.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\