 </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What is wrong with V5? I love its interpretation of the setting and themes.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's pretty awful on every level and is more Requiem than Masquerade?<br /> <br /> There are plenty of criticims all over the forum, as i'm sure you've noticed...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16290-generallyconfused","name":"GenerallyConfused","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16290_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T01:48:48-07:00","id":1307991,"title":"","content":"The least negative I can be with V5 is this<br /> <br /> It's an internally consistent game based on it's themes, but those themes don't match the feel of the evolution of Masquerade since 1st ed to where we are at either revised or V20 (not that V20 did anything new with the feel for the most part) It is in it's theme and mechanics, closer to Requiem than a Masquerade edition. That is the main Crux of the issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T07:10:40-07:00","id":1308021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1307579#post1307579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So according to what I've heard, there will only be 5 clans at initial launch, not including the Thin Bloods as the apparent &quot;bonus clan.&quot;<br /> <br /> Looking at the website teasers, it doesn't seem like Nosferatu will be one of those five. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Guess I need to start looking for a different clan for my first playthrough.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What makes you say that? the fifth clan teaser screams nosferatu to me. If i were to guess. The five clans are :<br /> <br /> 1. Toreador<br /> 2. Ventrue<br /> 3. Brujah<br /> 4. Tremere<br /> 5. Nosferatu","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T07:38:36-07:00","id":1308023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackshade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1308021#post1308021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> What makes you say that? the fifth clan teaser screams nosferatu to me. If i were to guess. The five clans are :<br /> <br /> 1. Toreador<br /> 2. Ventrue<br /> 3. Brujah<br /> 4. Tremere<br /> 5. Nosferatu</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm looking at the teasers for the website, and the one that originally looked like it could be Nosferatu / Assamite has been replaced by the Thin Bloods. Now the final teaser is the asylum that started overflowing with blood from the trailer. Which means the clans as they are presented now are Toreador, Ventrue, Brujah, Tremere, Malkavian and Thin Blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T08:09:39-07:00","id":1308030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1308023#post1308023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm looking at the teasers for the website, and the one that originally looked like it could be Nosferatu / Assamite has been replaced by the Thin Bloods. Now the final teaser is the asylum that started overflowing with blood from the trailer. Which means the clans as they are presented now are Toreador, Ventrue, Brujah, Tremere, Malkavian and Thin Blood.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's the one i am refering to. Looks more like a abandoned building/warehouse to me. An asylum seems like a stretch. But we will find out soon enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T09:49:38-07:00","id":1308051,"title":"","content":"So how does everybody feel about the thinblood discliplines? They seem to be a lot more powerful then in canon. Mentalism is Thaumaturgy movement of the mind, Nebulation is the mist abilities of protean (but better) and Chiropteran is basicaly animalisme mixed with classic levitation. Pretty good if you ask me. They might even give some clan discliplines a run for their money.<br /> <br /> What i am wondering is whether we will lose these dicliplines if we choose to join a clan or we get to keep it. If its the former then it might give incentive to remain a thinblood (assuming thats a option).But i could also see a scenario where we will keep the thinblood discliplines and the clan discliplines will stack on top of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24527,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","user":"blackshade","date":". 04-26-2019, 12:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T09:56:50-07:00","id":1308052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1307988#post1307988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What is wrong with V5? I love its interpretation of the setting and themes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Anything 'wrong' with V5 is in the eye of the beholder, just like any new editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5704-thebiglarpnerd","name":"thebiglarpnerd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T10:15:47-07:00","id":1308056,"title":"","content":"I have to admit, I am a bit disappointed one of the possible clans turned out to be &quot;thin blood&quot;.<br /> We already knew were going to start as one, now there's one spot less for actual clans with actual vampires.<br /> <br /> Can you tell I don't like thin bloods?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T10:24:00-07:00","id":1308059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackshade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1308051#post1308051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So how does everybody feel about the thinblood discliplines? They seem to be a lot more powerful then in canon. Mentalism is Thaumaturgy movement of the mind, Nebulation is the mist abilities of protean (but better) and Chiropteran is basicaly animalisme mixed with classic levitation. Pretty good if you ask me. They might even give some clan discliplines a run for their money.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it has been mentioned that they're somewhat going with the VRev idea of &quot;Thinbloods can make up their own disciplines based on what they think a vampire should be able to do&quot;, which is fine by me. I assume they'll continue with the other clans by taking up their general themes and feels, but probably tweaking them for what makes sense to use in a video game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackshade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1308051#post1308051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What i am wondering is whether we will lose these dicliplines if we choose to join a clan or we get to keep it. If its the former then it might give incentive to remain a thinblood (assuming thats a option).But i could also see a scenario where we will keep the thinblood discliplines and the clan discliplines will stack on top of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a good question. From a gamedesign point of view, it seems unlikely that you'd lose them because half of them are related to level traversal. Saying &quot;Hey, you're now a proud and noble Ventrue! Congrats! Also, forget about all that cool floating and sliding and misting you used to do.&quot; doesn't sound like it would be satisfying for the player.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T10:24:55-07:00","id":1308060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardestadtTheEvenYounger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1308056#post1308056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to admit, I am a bit disappointed one of the possible clans turned out to be &quot;thin blood&quot;.<br /> We already knew were going to start as one, now there's one spot less for actual clans with actual vampires.<br /> <br /> Can you tell I don't like thin bloods?</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, it's already been announced that there will be additional clans available as free DLC post release.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T13:20:49-07:00","id":1308098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illithid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1307991#post1307991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The least negative I can be with V5 is this<br /> <br /> It's an internally consistent game based on it's themes, but those themes don't match the feel of the evolution of Masquerade since 1st ed to where we are at either revised or V20 (not that V20 did anything new with the feel for the most part) It is in it's theme and mechanics, closer to Requiem than a Masquerade edition. That is the main Crux of the issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel that the &quot;evolution&quot; Masquerade has went through deprived the game of its original depth and themes, I absolutely adore that V5 is closer to 1st ed Masquerade than V20 or any of the other editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T13:22:26-07:00","id":1308099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardestadtTheEvenYounger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1308056#post1308056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to admit, I am a bit disappointed one of the possible clans turned out to be &amp;quot;thin blood&amp;quot;.<br /> We already knew were going to start as one, now there's one spot less for actual clans with actual vampires.<br /> <br /> Can you tell I don't like thin bloods?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thinbloods are a central part of the experience now, and in my opinion a much better canvas to write a personal horror story than full vampires. I'm glad that they are a playable option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T13:25:04-07:00","id":1308100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GenerallyConfused</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1307990#post1307990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's pretty awful on every level and is more Requiem than Masquerade?<br /> <br /> There are plenty of criticims all over the forum, as i'm sure you've noticed...</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty awful on every level? Because it's not a self-aggrandizing power fantasy where your character is little more than a walking repository of cool powers? Because it dared to live up to the original promise of Masquerade?<br /> <br /> And your tone implies that Requiem is also an awful game, which is patently untrue. If anything both V5 and Requiem are miles more mature in inteperation than all the previous edition of Masquerade that came before 1e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T13:26:37-07:00","id":1308101,"title":"","content":"The original promise of Masquerade lasted 1 year. In 1992 Second Edition was already out with very different themes and focus, themes and focus that lasted from 1992 to july 2018.<br /> <br /> So vampire the Masquerade has been 1\u00b0 ed for...1 year.<br /> <br /> And has been something very different for...26 years.<br /> <br /> So, if you like only what Masquerade was for 1 year, and don't like what it was for 26 it's simple: you don't like Vampire the Masquerade.<br /> <br /> Which is good: Requiem is a wonderful game. In its own coherence even V5 might be good, but it's something very different from what The Masquerade was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 04-26-2019, 04:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T13:37:43-07:00","id":1308104,"title":"","content":"All the criticism I've seen so far about V5 is &quot;Where are my powers?&quot;, &quot;Why can't I play a 9th Generation Elder from the get go?&quot;, &quot;Why can't I play a Path of Enlightenment?&quot;, and &quot;Why is Humanity so strict?&quot;<br /> <br /> The only valid criticism I've seen so far concern the art and the controversies, which I agree should be addressed. The rest is all old guards hating on the new (which is ironic because V5 isn't new at all, but more of a remake of 1st edition)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T13:47:50-07:00","id":1308107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1308101#post1308101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The original promise of Masquerade lasted 1 year. In 1992 Second Edition was already out with very different themes and focus, themes and focus that lasted from 1992 to july 2018.<br /> <br /> So vampire the Masquerade has been 1\u00b0 ed for...1 year.<br /> <br /> And has been something very different for...26 years.<br /> <br /> So, if you like only what Masquerade was for 1 year, and don't like what it was for 26 it's simple: you don't like Vampire the Masquerade.<br /> <br /> Which is good: Requiem is a wonderful game. In its own coherence even V5 might be good, but it's something very different from what The Masquerade was.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is the Masquerade? It has always tried to be a game of personal and political horror, yet there was a dissonance with the kind of themes it wanted to present and the player base it actually attracted. As time went on it lost its focus especially with V20, with more disciplines than I can count and so many bloodlines and factions and open secrets that it's mind boggling to think that the game can be taken seriously as a horror game.<br /> <br /> The way I see it V5 wants to take 20 steps back and avoid all the holes VTM has walked into since it's inception. It's a remake of sorts, one I welcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T13:52:14-07:00","id":1308111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackshade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1308051#post1308051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What i am wondering is whether we will lose these dicliplines if we choose to join a clan or we get to keep it. If its the former then it might give incentive to remain a thinblood (assuming thats a option).But i could also see a scenario where we will keep the thinblood discliplines and the clan discliplines will stack on top of it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think I remember hearing that as a Thin Blood, you only get to choose ONE of the three power sets, as opposed to having them all at once. So that might balance things out. It could also explain why in what little footage we've seen so far, they don't show off more than one power set at a time.<br /> <br /> As for incentive to remain one, they recently had a Twitch Stream where they revealed that being a Thin Blood would not be a viable strategy for what the game plans to throw at you later down the line. If you want to survive in the world of kindred, you're heavily encouraged (if not required) to join one of the full clans.<br /> <br /> I think this is a good idea, because Thin Bloods should always be reminded of the fact they are bottom tier garbage, who will never be considered equal to one of the clans, unless they commit to joining one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-26-2019, 05:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T14:41:30-07:00","id":1308125,"title":"","content":"Pretty please let's not start yet another edition war.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T15:12:49-07:00","id":1308135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1308100#post1308100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pretty awful on every level? Because it's not a self-aggrandizing power fantasy where your character is little more than a walking repository of cool powers? Because it dared to live up to the original promise of Masquerade?<br /> <br /> And your tone implies that Requiem is also an awful game, which is patently untrue. If anything both V5 and Requiem are miles more mature in inteperation than all the previous edition of Masquerade that came before 1e.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't call V5 &quot;awful of every level&quot;; tough it's most certainly not my favorite edition; but I also don't believe you need to be a thinblood or a 13th Generation neonate in order to play a game of political horror.<br /> Sure, if you just want to play a 4th Generation Brujah with Potence and Celerity 9, you're missing the point of the game. However, playing an Elder is not, necessarily, no more than self aggrandizement. There are horrors inherent to being that old and possessing that much power.<br /> <br /> For instance, in defense of generations, I do enjoy playing a low-ish Generation Ventrue that is part of a specific dynasty and has to deal with all the responsibilities that entails; suddenly, you're not just having to fulfill the expectations of a sire but also of a grandsire, great-grandsire and maybe even that of a Methuselah Ancestor.<br /> Of course, you can still do that in V5 but there's a different between playing a 13th Generation Ventrue who most of his ancestors won't even know he exists and a 7th Generation one who literally has Ancients looking over his shoulder to ensure he is not embarrassing them. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T15:30:33-07:00","id":1308142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1308111#post1308111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this is a good idea, because Thin Bloods should always be reminded of the fact they are bottom tier garbage, who will never be considered equal to one of the clans, unless they commit to joining one.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an unfair way to look at it, and somehow fuels the player prejudice against Thinbloods as a playable concept. For one thing Thinbloods don't suffer the Beast as much as other clans which is a blessing that no doubt many Elders envy, for another, they can walk in the sun, which is something else full vampires covet.<br /> <br /> From an OOC perspective I want to see a Thinblood story, a classic underdog story about night to night survival without over the top action and cool powers. Just you, the hunger, your vicious Kindred and the long night.<br /> <br /> I don't want to perpetuate the idea that the lower your Generation the more &quot;fun&quot; you have, Because that only results in more player who commit diablerie without even thinking of the consequences and who pour all their freebies into the generation background without much thought.<br /> <br /> We all hate That Guy, let's not encourage more people to be That Guy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T15:59:26-07:00","id":1308155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1308142#post1308142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's an unfair way to look at it, and somehow fuels the player prejudice against Thinbloods as a playable concept. For one thing Thinbloods don't suffer the Beast as much as other clans which is a blessing that no doubt many Elders envy, for another, they can walk in the sun, which is something else full vampires covet.<br /> <br /> From an OOC perspective I want to see a Thinblood story, a classic underdog story about night to night survival without over the top action and cool powers. Just you, the hunger, your vicious Kindred and the long night.<br /> <br /> I don't want to perpetuate the idea that the lower your Generation the more &quot;fun&quot; you have, Because that only results in more player who commit diablerie without even thinking of the consequences and who pour all their freebies into the generation background without much thought.<br /> <br /> We all hate That Guy, let's not encourage more people to be That Guy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> According to the dev diaries, when asked about what Thin Bloods are, they mentioned something about them being able to survive in daylight for like 5 minutes or so, before they started burning. As opposed to pure vampires, which burn instantly. And even that's not all that impressive, since any pure vampire can replicate the same feat with a high enough mastery of Fortitude. Plus, they said this game won't have a day-night cycle, so the whole surviving in daylight thing is a moot point that won't be presented in game.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for committing diablerie without thinking of the consequences... that's actually how players should be treating it! Hell, that's how it's presented within the game's lore itself. A bunch of young, foolish kindred think they've figured out a fast track to power, and only find out too late that this kind of power comes with a price. If every vampire were aware that they could potentially lose control of their body, nobody would be tempted to engage in Diablerie to begin with!<br /> <br /> <br /> I agree on some level that Underdog stories can be fun, and I've even come up with some ideas of my own for stories like that. But in every game that gives me the option to do so, I always, always pick evil as my first play through. I don't want to be a worthless Thin Blood, begging for scraps off my master's plate throughout the whole game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-26-2019, 07:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T19:27:39-07:00","id":1308222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1308100#post1308100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pretty awful on every level? Because it's not a self-aggrandizing power fantasy where your character is little more than a walking repository of cool powers? Because it dared to live up to the original promise of Masquerade?<br /> <br /> And your tone implies that Requiem is also an awful game, which is patently untrue. If anything both V5 and Requiem are miles more mature in inteperation than all the previous edition of Masquerade that came before 1e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good grief. It's the least mature version i've seen, it's heavy handed and at the same time handwringing and gimicky. Surely it's not out of line to want more Masquerade than Requiem in a <i>Masquerade</i> game? It's regressed the game back to it's least enjoyable form.<br /> <br /> Don't ask what's wrong with the edition if you don't want to see the well established points...<br /> <br /> This kind of statement makes <i>you</i> That Guy as far as i'm concerned, as you're heavily suggesting &quot;Wrong Fun&quot;.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16290-generallyconfused","name":"GenerallyConfused","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16290_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T19:35:47-07:00","id":1308224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GenerallyConfused</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1308222#post1308222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Good grief. It's the least mature version i've seen, it's heavy handed and at the same time handwringing and gimicky. Surely it's not out of line to want more Masquerade than Requiem in a <i>Masquerade</i> game? It's regressed the game back to it's least enjoyable form.<br /> <br /> Don't ask what's wrong with the edition if you don't want to see the well established points...<br /> <br /> This kind of statement makes <i>you</i> That Guy as far as i'm concerned, as you're heavily suggesting &amp;quot;Wrong Fun&amp;quot;.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>What is the most enjoyable form? Are you going to play adventure, travel around the world for artifacts? Okay, that\u2019s fine. Are you going to play mercenaries hunting for the rarest blood? That\u2019s fine too. How about flipping tables and playing Diablerie campaigns? Okay, why not. How about the Nights of Prophecies stories? Why not. Should I mention Factor Chaos? What about Samuel Haig-<br /> <br /> Well I personally think Vampire is not the game for this, because I consider Vampire to be about politics, close up, local horror, politics, social backstabbing, politics, humiliation, thirst, politics, playing semblants, religion, politics, ambitions, favor exchanges among monsters, using ideologies to one\u2019s personal goals, and of course, politics. But that\u2019s just me. Maybe I'm wrong, maybe I'm That Guy, a fun hater. Serves me right for wanting some depth and uniqueness besides shallow power fantasy and edge for edge's sake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-27T04:27:11-07:00","id":1308278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1308224#post1308224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What is the most enjoyable form? Are you going to play adventure, travel around the world for artifacts? Okay, that\u2019s fine. Are you going to play mercenaries hunting for the rarest blood? That\u2019s fine too. How about flipping tables and playing Diablerie campaigns? Okay, why not. How about the Nights of Prophecies stories? Why not. Should I mention Factor Chaos? What about Samuel Haig-</div> </div> </div> </div>Hand on my heart, i was actually going to say the Haight era was better, but didn't think I'd need to be that specific.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1308224#post1308224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well I personally think Vampire is not the game for this, because I consider Vampire to be about politics, close up, local horror, politics, social backstabbing, politics, humiliation, thirst, politics, playing semblants, religion, politics, ambitions, favor exchanges among monsters, using ideologies to one\u2019s personal goals, and of course, politics. But that\u2019s just me. Maybe I'm wrong, maybe I'm That Guy, a fun hater. Serves me right for wanting some depth and uniqueness besides shallow power fantasy and edge for edge's sake.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Depth? V5 is about as deep as a puddle. I've played games that have all used this list of what the game is about. I never played a diab campaign, never played lower than starting generation allowed. Depth was giving all of these oppertunities in the same game. not going, &quot;Ok, you're all blood junkie losers, hope you like feeding scenes, 'cos there's going to be a lot of 'em&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16290-generallyconfused","name":"GenerallyConfused","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16290_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-27T05:18:05-07:00","id":1308282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GenerallyConfused</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1308278#post1308278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hand on my heart, i was actually going to say the Haight era was better, but didn't think I'd need to be that specific.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Depth? V5 is about as deep as a puddle. I've played games that have all used this list of what the game is about. I never played a diab campaign, never played lower than starting generation allowed. Depth was giving all of these oppertunities in the same game. not going, &amp;quot;Ok, you're all blood junkie losers, hope you like feeding scenes, 'cos there's going to be a lot of 'em&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>V5 is about as deep as a puddle but the Haight era was good apparently. I admit V5 is flawed, but it's not as flawed as that logic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-27T05:47:39-07:00","id":1308287,"title":"","content":"Well since the Chaos factor era was also the early 2nd edition era, with the Corebook 2nd ed, Book of Nod, Dark Colony, Under a Blood Red Moon, the Player Guide to the Sabbat, Chicago by Night 2nd ed, A World of Darkness, the first clanbooks and so on I suppose we can agree that was surely a better era than this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-27T06:31:16-07:00","id":1308294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1308100#post1308100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pretty awful on every level? Because it's not a self-aggrandizing power fantasy where your character is little more than a walking repository of cool powers?</div> </div> </div> </div>How is playing a Brujah, Toreador, Ventrue, or Tremere not a self-aggrandizing power fantasy? For that matter, how is giving Thin Bloods more power and customization than they had before not also doing the same thing? If it's true that Thin Bloods are supposed to represent the oppressed minority, then making them the largest population of vampires, with the ability to swap out power sets on the fly, is the absolute worst way to represent that.<br /> <br /> <br /> You want a story that gets personal horror across? Go back to my earlier comment regarding how Thin Bloods are bottom tier garbage. They will never be treated like equals, not unless they're willing to commit one of the greatest crimes in human society (murder) and one of the greatest sins imaginable (consuming another's soul for power). While at the same time, placing their mind and body at great risk of possession by the victim they just killed.<br /> <br /> In one of the Gentleman Gamer's live play videos, they were doing a Sabbat campaign, where one of the players (a Caitiff) diablerized a pack member, who had been lobotomized by a shotgun blast to the head. Later that morning, he ended up suffering a terrible daymare, and when he woke up the next night, he had flesh crafted the vampire's face into his own stomach!<br /> <br /> The general consensus is that &quot;power always has a price.&quot; And just because your players want to beef their characters up to be as strong as possible, does not mean the game can't invoke an emotional roller coaster of horror.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-27-2019, 09:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-27T12:48:14-07:00","id":1308371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1308294#post1308294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How is playing a Brujah, Toreador, Ventrue, or Tremere not a self-aggrandizing power fantasy? For that matter, how is giving Thin Bloods more power and customization than they had before not also doing the same thing? If it's true that Thin Bloods are supposed to represent the oppressed minority, then making them the largest population of vampires, with the ability to swap out power sets on the fly, is the absolute worst way to represent that.<br /> <br /> <br /> You want a story that gets personal horror across? Go back to my earlier comment regarding how Thin Bloods are bottom tier garbage. They will never be treated like equals, not unless they're willing to commit one of the greatest crimes in human society (murder) and one of the greatest sins imaginable (consuming another's soul for power). While at the same time, placing their mind and body at great risk of possession by the victim they just killed.<br /> <br /> In one of the Gentleman Gamer's live play videos, they were doing a Sabbat campaign, where one of the players (a Caitiff) diablerized a pack member, who had been lobotomized by a shotgun blast to the head. Later that morning, he ended up suffering a terrible daymare, and when he woke up the next night, he had flesh crafted the vampire's face into his own stomach!<br /> <br /> The general consensus is that &quot;power always has a price.&quot; And just because your players want to beef their characters up to be as strong as possible, does not mean the game can't invoke an emotional roller coaster of horror.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know what, I actually agree with everything you said. When power has consequences it stops being a power fantasy. Well said.<br /> <br /> I guess we reached a nice conclusion for this argument.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-27T13:48:55-07:00","id":1308378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1308371#post1308371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know what, I actually agree with everything you said. When power has consequences it stops being a power fantasy. Well said.<br /> <br /> I guess we reached a nice conclusion for this argument.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Seems so. Reminds me of another video talking about why fantasy settings don't feature everybody on the planet becoming magic users, if it has so many advantages over mundane applications. The answer being that magic should have rules and consequences that deter people from trying to use it for every solution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-28T08:09:52-07:00","id":1308474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1308101#post1308101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The original promise of Masquerade lasted 1 year. In 1992 Second Edition was already out with very different themes and focus, themes and focus that lasted from 1992 to july 2018.<br /> <br /> So vampire the Masquerade has been 1\u00b0 ed for...1 year.<br /> <br /> And has been something very different for...26 years.<br /> <br /> So, if you like only what Masquerade was for 1 year, and don't like what it was for 26 it's simple: you don't like Vampire the Masquerade.<br /> <br /> Which is good: Requiem is a wonderful game. In its own coherence even V5 might be good, but it's something very different from what The Masquerade was.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, nothing to add to that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-28T08:19:40-07:00","id":1308475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1308104#post1308104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All the criticism I've seen so far about V5 is &quot;Where are my powers?&quot;,</div> </div> </div> </div>Missing stuff that existed for 26 years is a valid point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Why can't I play a 9th Generation Elder from the get go?&quot;, </div> </div> </div>Elders were part of the game and setting and playable for 26 years. Missing them is a valid point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Why can't I play a Path of Enlightenment?&quot;, </div> </div> </div>The game not having a central moral system, instead having multiple moralities, even truly monstrous ones among them, but more mild, just &quot;different&quot; ones too. missing that aspect is a valid point. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and &quot;Why is Humanity so strict?&quot; </div> </div> </div>A totally, totally valid point, if one doesn not like the premise of the Touchstone mechanic, or that the Tenets are cosmic truths in the chronicle, like D&amp;D alignments.<br /> <br /> I'd say the same as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12142\" data-vbnamecard=\"12142\">Undead rabbit</a> , if you think all those things are good changes, well, you didn't really like what Masquerade was for 26 years of its existence. That's okay, but many did. Fortunately, Requeim was caterd to you and now V5 too. Unfortunately, there's no Vampire game, which is actively supported with official material, for us. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The only valid criticism I've seen so far concern the art and the controversies, which I agree should be addressed. </div> </div> </div>Good.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The rest is all old guards hating on the new (which is ironic because V5 isn't new at all, but more of a remake of 1st edition) </div> </div> </div>That's an extremely, <i>extremely</i> shallow and dismissive view on the whole issue, but it was discussed many times on these boards and I don't have the inclination to start it anew.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-28T08:38:09-07:00","id":1308476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1308107#post1308107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What is the Masquerade? It has always tried to be a game of personal and political horror, yet there was a dissonance with the kind of themes it wanted to present and the player base it actually attracted. As time went on it lost its focus especially with V20, with more disciplines than I can count and so many bloodlines and factions and open secrets that it's mind boggling to think that the game can be taken seriously as a horror game.</div> </div> </div> </div>You say &quot;dissonance<i>&quot;, </i>I say it had many themes and styles of playing it and that it was one of its strengths. You could play small-time pesonal horror, if you wanted, you could play action-horror, global conspiracies, occult adventures, dark urban fantasy, whatever. For me, it wasn't a bug, it was a feature, not a lack of focus, but a wealth of material. No it wasn't <i>just</i> a srict (personal) horror game and I liked that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The way I see it V5 wants to take 20 steps back and avoid all the holes VTM has walked into since it's inception. It's a remake of sorts, one I welcome. </div> </div> </div>I'll say again what I've said in the other thread a few days ago: people like you, among them some writers of the game never came to terms with what Masquerade actually became, which many people actually liked and VtM always had it's unhealthy share of elitism, stemming from those people. Because of that, Requiem came to be and many people hated it and outright rejected it and it never became that succesfull as Masquerade. Then V20 came along and it was good, everyone had their preferred Vampire version with their preferred playstyle, apporoach to worldbuilding, aesthetics, power level and so on. Then V5 started the whole damn thing again, trying to force one particular style of play and setting on the whole fanbase, because that is &quot;how Vampire should be&quot; for some.<br /> <br /> Look, what you and people like you don't understand, is that it's not a question of what is the more valid, or &quot;better&quot; take on Vampire. All are totally valid and enjoyable games. The problem is that you're trying to say to us that we're wrong to miss the things we liked in the older editions and we're wrong to criticize the game because of it, because of all that heavy-handed changes and restrictiveness in places, compared to the old game. That you're trying to say that we've had badwrongfun with the old game, because that's not what Vamprie is &quot;supposed to be about&quot;. Well, not for you, maybe, but it was for many. However, you've had Requiem and now have V5 too and we have no prospect for new stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-28T12:05:15-07:00","id":1308500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1308125#post1308125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty please let's not start yet another edition war.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, please. Instead of kicking around negative energy at each other and constantly arguing all across the forum about which version if good/bad/best maybe you should all live and let live? Don't like V5? Okay, that's fine, you have twenty-six years of material,including a &quot;greatest hits&quot; edition (V20), to fall back on. I'll agree that it certainly has it's flaws but people are allowed to enjoy V5 and shouldn't have to deal with others talking down to them because of it. On the other side of the coin, it's perfectly valid to not like V5 too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6149-malfean90","name":"Malfean90","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-28T13:31:20-07:00","id":1308518,"title":"","content":"Anyway to go back to the topic of Bloodlines 2, to me the gameplay seems heavily geared toward combat and this is a little worrying, like I can't think of any non-combat application for the Thinblood disciplines. All I'm saying is that if I want to play a Toreador socialite with a gun in her purse that she only uses as a last resort I should be able to, ya know? What do you guys think about this?<br /> <br /> I doubt it would even have the Social/Mental/Physical spread of the first game. I find it odd because the first game was criticized for the lack of end game social options, and if they're going to throw away that entirely I don't see how the game can live up to VTM's extremely varied playstyles.<br /> <br /> We should be able to talk our way through most situations, sort of like the first half of the first game, but for the entire game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12561,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","user":"Shawarbaaz","date":". 04-28-2019, 04:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-28T14:01:16-07:00","id":1308522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1308518#post1308518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway to go back to the topic of Bloodlines 2, to me the gameplay seems heavily geared toward combat and this is a little worrying, like I can't think of any non-combat application for the Thinblood disciplines.</div> </div> </div> </div>The developers (or whoever is doing the interviews) have stated the exact opposite. This game will feature far more dialogue and social interaction than Bloodlines 1 did. In fact, people will actually respond to you differently, in accordance with who your allies are, and how you choose to maneuver through the world of kindred. Compare this to Bloodlines 1, where you were pretty much forced into being a member of the Camarilla, until the final part of the game, when you passed the point of no return.<br /> <br /> As for non combat applications, that's a sign you're thinking too small. They could easily be worked into stealth and exploration playstyles. Such as the Chiropteran's ability to glide through the air, or Nebulation's ability to slip through air vents and other tight spaces. Or Mentalism's ability to create distractions by throwing objects around the environment. Something which was present in Bloodlines 1, as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-28T14:07:54-07:00","id":1308524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1308522#post1308522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The developers (or whoever is doing the interviews) have stated the exact opposite. This game will feature far more dialogue and social interaction than Bloodlines 1 did. In fact, people will actually respond to you differently, in accordance with who your allies are, and how you choose to maneuver through the world of kindred. Compare this to Bloodlines 1, where you were pretty much forced into being a member of the Camarilla, until the final part of the game, when you passed the point of no return.<br /> <br /> As for non combat applications, that's a sign you're thinking too small. They could easily be worked into stealth and exploration playstyles. Such as the Chiropteran's ability to glide through the air, or Nebulation's ability to slip through air vents and other tight spaces. Or Mentalism's ability to create distractions by throwing objects around the environment. Something which was present in Bloodlines 1, as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's good to hear. Though we could use more mind whammy powers like Dominate and Presence to help in dialogue (with mortals). And maybe the ability to specialize in one type of play-style over the other.<br /> <br /> I'll wait for more information and see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-28T15:20:13-07:00","id":1308536,"title":"","content":"So do you remain as a Thin blood or do you get to choose a clan later? Hopefully it you get to choose a clan later(and hopefully early in the game) that will help you choose your play style.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","name":"Grimmi05","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T01:32:55-07:00","id":1308626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimmi05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1308536#post1308536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So do you remain as a Thin blood or do you get to choose a clan later? Hopefully it you get to choose a clan later(and hopefully early in the game) that will help you choose your play style.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's been noted that you will actually have to choose a clan and cannot remain a Thin-Blood. We'll see whether that happens via Diablerie or some other unknown mechanism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T05:21:29-07:00","id":1308646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimmi05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1308536#post1308536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So do you remain as a Thin blood or do you get to choose a clan later? Hopefully it you get to choose a clan later(and hopefully early in the game) that will help you choose your play style.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Apparently, you choose your clan about 1/3rd of the way into the game. And this decision will be mandatory, since a Thinblood would not be capable of surviving the challenges the game is going to throw your way.<br /> <br /> The reason why it takes so long, is because the developers want to properly flesh out each clan, and have the players get introduced to how they work, before making a decision on which one to join.<br /> <br /> The clans in Bloodlines 1 were almost identical in their playstyle. The only exceptions to this being the Malkavians (who were more of a comedic gimmick), and the Nosferatu (who might have been bugged, because I was able to spend most of the game on the surface).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T04:38:02-07:00","id":1309400,"title":"","content":"So, the first clan reveal are <a href=\"https://www.pcgamer.com/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2-brujah-reveal/\" target=\"_blank\">The Brujah.</a><br /> <br /> I can't help but notice in the article, they mention being able to keep your Thin Blood disciplines if you join the Brujah. I don't know if that's something unique to this clan, or if they were just speaking in general. But should be something to keep an eye on.<br /> <br /> Not sure how I feel about physical disciplines like Celerity and Potence having distinct powers, instead of being subsequent upgrades to your overall attributes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T06:28:41-07:00","id":1309425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1309400#post1309400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, the first clan reveal are <a href=\"https://www.pcgamer.com/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2-brujah-reveal/\" target=\"_blank\">The Brujah.</a><br /> <br /> I can't help but notice in the article, they mention being able to keep your Thin Blood disciplines if you join the Brujah. I don't know if that's something unique to this clan, or if they were just speaking in general. But should be something to keep an eye on.<br /> <br /> Not sure how I feel about physical disciplines like Celerity and Potence having distinct powers, instead of being subsequent upgrades to your overall attributes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where's Presence?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T07:14:37-07:00","id":1309433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardestadtTheEvenYounger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1309425#post1309425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where's Presence?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Don't know. I didn't even notice that, until you brought it up!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T07:30:39-07:00","id":1309436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1309433#post1309433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Don't know. I didn't even notice that, until you brought it up!</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope they're not removing the social Disciplines, that'd leave my favorite clan a bit undermanned.<br /> <br /> &quot;So here's the Ventrue. They have Fortitude and that's about it. Caine hated them.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T07:37:05-07:00","id":1309440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardestadtTheEvenYounger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1309436#post1309436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I hope they're not removing the social Disciplines, that'd leave my favorite clan a bit undermanned.<br /> <br /> &quot;So here's the Ventrue. They have Fortitude and that's about it. Caine hated them.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That would be monumentally stupid, considering they told us they want to focus more heavily on social interaction this time around.<br /> <br /> At the moment, the only explanation I can think of is the part in the article where it says you'll get to keep your Thin Blood powers. Since I've also read you only get to pick one of them (not all 3), I suspect that the one you pick might end up replacing Presence upon joining the Brujah.<br /> <br /> That, or they simply haven't finished the discipline yet, because their website hasn't been updated with the new Brujah as of the time of writing this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T07:50:03-07:00","id":1309446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1309400#post1309400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure how I feel about physical disciplines like Celerity and Potence having distinct powers, instead of being subsequent upgrades to your overall attributes.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a V5 thing and it's IMO <i>very</i> welcome. Yes, Celerity was a powerhouse, but it was a pretty boring one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T07:53:56-07:00","id":1309447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1309446#post1309446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a V5 thing and it's IMO <i>very</i> welcome. Yes, Celerity was a powerhouse, but it was a pretty boring one.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> For me, it's just weird. I read through the section in my books which deciphers Myths and Facts, and remember the part which states vampires being able to move faster than the eye can see was a Myth. Now I find out about <b>Unseen Storm</b>, and suddenly it's like <i>&quot;Oh, nevermind. Now you DO get to teleport!&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T10:24:04-07:00","id":1309470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1309440#post1309440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That would be monumentally stupid, considering they told us they want to focus more heavily on social interaction this time around.<br /> <br /> At the moment, the only explanation I can think of is the part in the article where it says you'll get to keep your Thin Blood powers. Since I've also read you only get to pick one of them (not all 3), I suspect that the one you pick might end up replacing Presence upon joining the Brujah.<br /> <br /> That, or they simply haven't finished the discipline yet, because their website hasn't been updated with the new Brujah as of the time of writing this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, from what I understood during the interview, your explanation is correct. They mentioned that due to you having been embraced as a thin blood, upon joining a clan you will be &quot;both a little more and a little less&quot; than a regular member that was directly embraced in the Brujah clan. That means you will keep 1 of the TB disciplines, and learn 2 of the Brujah (and I assume it's the same for the rest of the clans).<br /> <br /> Even with this design decision, I wish you could pick which 2 disciplines you will learn, so that you could pick Presence+Potence as your combo instead of having Potence+Celerity as the default. Otherwise, the Brujah PC can have very high social stats, but all their disciplines will be combat oriented. <br /> <br /> But I'm not bummed very much by this since they confirmed the game will have modding support. This means that if the game is good, the modding community will embrace it, and one of the first mods ever will be &quot;have all your clan's disciplines if you want to&quot;. And if the game is not good, than it doesn't matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25197-cookiesorcerer","name":"CookieSorcerer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T12:25:42-07:00","id":1309487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CookieSorcerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1309470#post1309470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, from what I understood during the interview, your explanation is correct. They mentioned that due to you having been embraced as a thin blood, upon joining a clan you will be &quot;both a little more and a little less&quot; than a regular member that was directly embraced in the Brujah clan. That means you will keep 1 of the TB disciplines, and learn 2 of the Brujah (and I assume it's the same for the rest of the clans).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh gods damn it, I didn't even have to finish reading that whole thing, before I realized they're going to use this as an excuse for leaving out the more &quot;difficult&quot; to program Disciplines. How are things like Animalism and Protean going to work, if 2 of the Thin Blood powers are pretty much redundant versions of what they're capable of?<br /> <br /> The whole point of diablerizing your way to 13th generation is that you <b>cease to be a Thin Blood,</b> and become a fully legitimate vampire. The knowledge that we eventually become a true vampire was the only thing allowing me to tolerate starting off as a worthless, boot licking halfbreed.<br /> <br /> I might have been willing to accept the explanation that since you started as a Thin Blood, you didn't receive a proper education on clan disciplines. But since the earlier portions leading up to you joining the clan involves interacting with them and learning how they do things, that excuse wouldn't make much sense.<br /> <br /> Also, not having Presence means that the Brujah players are now being forced into the stereotypical role of a bunch of violent malcontents, who's response to the situation is to bash people's heads in, rather than talk things out.<br /> <br /> So much for Bloodlines 2 focusing on social interaction...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-02-2019, 03:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T13:28:42-07:00","id":1309497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1309487#post1309487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So much for Bloodlines 2 focusing on social interaction...</div> </div> </div> </div>Brujah will be the clan for people who want to solve their problems with their fist. Toreador wil likely get Presence and Auspex. So they will be the social clan. Ventrue will certainly get Dominate but i dont think they will get Presence. I think they want every clan to have their own unique discliplines. So they will probably get Fortitude as their second disclipline.<br /> <br /> Tremere will likely get two paths of Thaumaturgy (path of blood has to be one of them). Last clan wil get Animalisme/Obfuscate (Nosferatu) or Obfuscate/Dementation (Malkavian). I would honestly like it if there is no overlap in discliplines between the clans. This gives the game great replay value. If you want to experience every disclipline you have to replay the game with every clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T13:35:41-07:00","id":1309499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1309487#post1309487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh gods damn it, I didn't even have to finish reading that whole thing, before I realized they're going to use this as an excuse for leaving out the more &quot;difficult&quot; to program Disciplines. How are things like Animalism and Protean going to work, if 2 of the Thin Blood powers are pretty much redundant versions of what they're capable of?</div> </div> </div> </div>First, they're using different rules - there are only two separate powers per discipline, plus some upgrades for those two. Picking two powers out of Animalism and Protean is really not a particularly difficult matter at that point. Of course, it's highly likely that Gangrel won't be in the game at start anyway.<br /> Second, they've made clear what the main reason for the choice is: Cutting down decision paralysis. Six powers per character (plus weapons, plus &quot;human&quot; abilities) is about right for a relatively fast combat system.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1309487#post1309487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, not having Presence means that the Brujah players are now being forced into the stereotypical role of a bunch of violent malcontents, who's response to the situation is to bash people's heads in, rather than talk things out.<br /> <br /> So much for Bloodlines 2 focusing on social interaction...</div> </div> </div> </div>Because everyone knows that playing a social character without Presence is completely impossible. In fact, the designers in the Twitch stream went to great lengths to emphasize the philosopher/rabble duality of the clan and considered the &quot;Brujah automatically get high physical traits&quot; of BL1 something to move away from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T13:36:03-07:00","id":1309500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackshade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1309497#post1309497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Brujah will be the clan for people who want to solve their problems with their fist. Toreador wil likely get Presence and Auspex. So they will be the social clan. Ventrue will certainly get Dominate but i dont think they will get Presence. I think they want every clan to have their own unique discliplines. So they will probably get Fortitude as their second disclipline.<br /> <br /> Tremere will likely get two paths of Thaumaturgy (path of blood has to be one of them). Last clan wil get Animalisme/Obfuscate (Nosferatu) or Obfuscate/Dementation (Malkavian). I would honestly like it if there is no overlap in discliplines between the clans. This gives the game great replay value. If you want to experience every disclipline you have to replay the game with every clan.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They could still solve problems with their fists, if they wanted to. Having access to Presence would just give them an alternative to doing so, if the player runs into a problem they don't think they'll be able to <i>&quot;rip and tear&quot;</i> their way out of.<br /> <br /> At this point, it's looking an awful lot like the clans are going to function as traditional RPG classes, with Brujah filling in the role of Fighter / Barbarian.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3118_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3118\" data-vbnamecard=\"3118\">Cifer</a> Sure, a Brujah can try to initiate dialogue without Presence, but nowhere near to the same extent. Presence is the discipline that allows the Philosopher Kings to inspire the troops, organize rallies and instigate riots. It's the often overlooked discipline that allows them to remain serious contenders in the world of vampire politics.<br /> <br /> Stripping that away leaves the rabble as exactly what their reputation paints them as. Nothing more than brutish thugs, who are only good for cracking skulls, and aren't worthy of respect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-02-2019, 04:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T14:26:23-07:00","id":1309506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1309500#post1309500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3118_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3118\" data-vbnamecard=\"3118\">Cifer</a> Sure, a Brujah can try to initiate dialogue without Presence, but nowhere near to the same extent. Presence is the discipline that allows the Philosopher Kings to inspire the troops, organize rallies and instigate riots. It's the often overlooked discipline that allows them to remain serious contenders in the world of vampire politics.<br /> <br /> Stripping that away leaves the rabble as exactly what their reputation paints them as. Nothing more than brutish thugs, who are only good for cracking skulls, and aren't worthy of respect.</div> </div> </div> </div>So since there is no human with Presence, all humans are brutish thugs? Funnily enough, older editions nearly always emphasized that the reign of a Prince who relied overly on their disciplines rather than political savvy is generally a short one.<br /> The game creators mentioned that playing a Brujah as a social/combat hybrid character would be viable - in fact, one even said that his first character concept in the full game would be a sweet little girl who always tries talking first, but isn't afraid of kicking ass if that fails. When it comes to what is and isn't possible in the game, I think I'll take their word over yours.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T14:34:44-07:00","id":1309510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1309506#post1309506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">in fact, one even said that his first character concept in the full game would be a sweet little girl</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Does that imply we'll be able to play as children, in addition to adults? Because that would be rather interesting to see how they pull it off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T14:47:07-07:00","id":1309514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1309500#post1309500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing more than brutish thugs, who are only good for cracking skulls, and aren't worthy of respect.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, a Brujah?<br /> <br /> Just kidding, just kidding, I see your point. And I agree. Of course you can be social without Presence but the clans were given their particular disciplines for a reason. The absence of Presence insinuates that the Brujah lose their society building skills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T15:42:54-07:00","id":1309527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1309500#post1309500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, a Brujah can try to initiate dialogue without Presence, but nowhere near to the same extent. Presence is the discipline that allows the Philosopher Kings to inspire the troops, organize rallies and instigate riots. It's the often overlooked discipline that allows them to remain serious contenders in the world of vampire politics.<br /> <br /> Stripping that away leaves the rabble as exactly what their reputation paints them as. Nothing more than brutish thugs, who are only good for cracking skulls, and aren't worthy of respect.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is assuming that presence will be an actual social discipline and not just a debuff and stun like in BL1. Still, the Anarch guide stresses that Brujah influence mortals more than I remember from previous games, so hopefully they'll have some sort of advantage to doing that.<br /> <br /> Although that doesn't seem likely, judging by their website entry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","user":"Spencer from The Hills","date":". 05-02-2019, 06:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T16:02:42-07:00","id":1309531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1309510#post1309510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does that imply we'll be able to play as children, in addition to adults? Because that would be rather interesting to see how they pull it off.</div> </div> </div> </div>Little as in petite stature, not as in age.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T16:53:23-07:00","id":1309541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1309499#post1309499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Cutting down decision paralysis. Six powers per character (plus weapons, plus &quot;human&quot; abilities) is about right for a relatively fast combat system.</div> </div> </div> </div>A choice I'm not very happy with. As a classic monster fan, I loved the premise of vampires being able to whip out all these cool, supernatural abilities. It hearkened back to the glory days of the vampire mythos, instead of following the trends of today, where pop culture vampires are pretty much restricted to Potence, Celerity and Dominate. While all the other abilities that made them so famous are relegated to the realm of myth and superstition.<br /> <br /> Hopefully, they'll offer a more diverse power set for the non-physical disciplines, like Dominate, Thaumaturgy and Auspex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-02-2019, 07:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-03T03:31:50-07:00","id":1309610,"title":"","content":"I am not happy with the &quot;starting as a thin.blood and then advance to full vampire&quot; approach and I am not happy with the &quot;Brujahs are for bashing, not for social play&quot; approach. These are, IMO, quite questionable design decisions. I want to be able to play regular clans, with their regular Disciplines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4259-eddie-fiori","name":"Eddie Fiori","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-03T03:49:46-07:00","id":1309613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eddie Fiori</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1309610#post1309610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not happy with the &quot;starting as a thin.blood and then advance to full vampire&quot; approach and I am not happy with the &quot;Brujahs are for bashing, not for social play&quot; approach. These are, IMO, quite questionable design decisions. I want to be able to play regular clans, with their regular Disciplines.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was fine with the Thin Blood start, as I was under the impression it was just an extended &quot;tutorial&quot; section, while you took the time to get properly introduced to each clan. But now that it looks like you'll retain some Thin Blood features, even though you're <i>supposed to become a full fledged vampire,</i> my opinion of it has plummeted significantly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-04T05:34:31-07:00","id":1309889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's purely a gamification thing because losing your starting powers when you become a full clan member would likely irritate people. Especially those that are not tt players.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not really, since at least 2 of those Thin Blood powers are greatly expanded upon with full clan disciplines.<br /> <br /> Animalism is a much more diverse form of Chiropteran.<br /> <br /> While Protean also gives you the power to turn into mist, in addition to far more interesting shapeshifting capabilities.<br /> <br /> I don't think anybody who's actually familiar with the lore cares about Thin Blood abilities. We all know they're weak, gimmicky powers when compared to what a proper clan member is able to bring to the table. I would have been perfectly fine with the Thin Blood's disciplines being more of an &quot;appetizer&quot; before you join a clan and gain access to some real power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-04T05:47:20-07:00","id":1309893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1309889#post1309889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think anybody who's actually familiar with the lore cares about Thin Blood abilities. We all know they're weak, gimmicky powers when compared to what a proper clan member is able to bring to the table. I would have been perfectly fine with the Thin Blood's disciplines being more of an &quot;appetizer&quot; before you join a clan and gain access to some real power.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm familiar with the lore and I care about Thin Blood abilities. Both the V20 &quot;I think that's what vampires should be able to do, right?&quot; approach and the V5 &quot;let's counterfeit us some discipline powers by mixing stuff together&quot; approach seem quite interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T06:01:52-07:00","id":1310732,"title":"","content":"Well, Tremere is the next clan revealed and Auspex and Blood Sorcery will be their disciplines. What do you think about that? Personally, I am intrigued about the playability of astral projection, the second power of Auspex. It seems interesting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IFKGdJiF_2s\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IFKGdJiF_2s\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IFKGdJiF_2s\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IFKGdJiF_2s </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://venturebeat.com/2019/05/08/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2-with-the-tremere-there-will-be-blood-magic/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://venturebeat.com/2019/05/08/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2-with-the-tremere-there-will-be-blood-magic/\" target=\"_blank\"> Vercel Security Checkpoint </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://venturebeat.com/2019/05/08/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2-with-the-tremere-there-will-be-blood-magic/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://venturebeat.com/2019/05/08/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2-with-the-tremere-there-will-be-blood-magic/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> What do you bet is the next? I would say Ventrue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T06:32:52-07:00","id":1310735,"title":"","content":"Since they're not going by any particular order, I'd give even odds to Toreador, Ventrue and Nosferatu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T08:11:47-07:00","id":1310748,"title":"","content":"If they meant for the Clans to all have unique disciplines, they've just shot themselves in the foot. Now, whatever they do, the Toreador will always either share Celerity with the Brujah or Auspex with the Tremere.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1310735#post1310735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since they're not going by any particular order, I'd give even odds to Toreador, Ventrue and Nosferatu.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I'd bet whatever you want that the Malkavians will be playable, not the Nosferatu.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T09:01:32-07:00","id":1310758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardestadtTheEvenYounger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1310748#post1310748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they meant for the Clans to all have unique disciplines, they've just shot themselves in the foot. Now, whatever they do, the Toreador will always either share Celerity with the Brujah or Auspex with the Tremere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Taking five clans out of the core seven, I don't think there is a distribution that gets everyone two unique disciplines. Not when three clans have Auspex and another three have Presence. If Tremere had Dominate and Thau, that would leave Presence and Fortitude for Ventrue, which overlaps with Toreador.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardestadtTheEvenYounger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1310748#post1310748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I'd bet whatever you want that the Malkavians will be playable, not the Nosferatu.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess we'll see. They both require extensive sub-systems, either for sneaking around the hub worlds or for portraying their mental state. I think the former may be easier to implement, considering the designers have already said that they're going for a more true-to-life depiction of mental illness compared to the &quot;mad prophet&quot; version of BL1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T09:18:05-07:00","id":1310764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1310758#post1310758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Taking five clans out of the core seven, I don't think there is a distribution that gets everyone two unique disciplines. Not when three clans have Auspex and another three have Presence. If Tremere had Dominate and Thau, that would leave Presence and Fortitude for Ventrue, which overlaps with Toreador.</div> </div> </div> </div>They could have given the Tremere two different types of Thaumaturgy. Maybe something fire based?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1310758#post1310758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess we'll see. They both require extensive sub-systems, either for sneaking around the hub worlds or for portraying their mental state. I think the former may be easier to implement, considering the designers have already said that they're going for a more true-to-life depiction of mental illness compared to the &quot;mad prophet&quot; version of BL1.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. I think the Malkavians are more likely simply because, out of the three clan images left on the website, one obviously represents the Toreador, another the Ventrue and the third strikes me more as the cells in a mental asylum rather than sewers.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T09:58:48-07:00","id":1310769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardestadtTheEvenYounger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1310764#post1310764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They could have given the Tremere two different types of Thaumaturgy. Maybe something fire based?</div> </div> </div> </div>From a game design point of view, not really. Most non-combat path of blood powers translate rather poorly to a video game, so we're left with the combat stuff. Fire is... more combat stuff. And both of them tend towards artillery powers. Of course, it's possible that they might create different powers for different clans, so Toreador Celerity might not be the same as Brujah Celerity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardestadtTheEvenYounger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1310764#post1310764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True. I think the Malkavians are more likely simply because, out of the three clan images left on the website, one obviously represents the Toreador, another the Ventrue and the third strikes me more as the cells in a mental asylum rather than sewers.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's that strange place with the leaking faucet from the trailer. I don't think we know anything about it beyond &quot;some run-down place&quot; - which would make for a good hideout for both a Nosferatu and a Malkavian.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T12:34:44-07:00","id":1310789,"title":"","content":"Surprised Tremere got Auspex. I really thought they were going to give each clan their own unique discliplines. But it seems likely there will be overlap in discliplines between clans now. Unless Toreador are out (higly unlikely).They are so many different thaumaturgy paths to choose from. Why not keep Auspex for Toreador?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24527,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","user":"blackshade","date":". 05-08-2019, 03:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T14:12:28-07:00","id":1310810,"title":"","content":"I get the feeling that even if some Clans have overlap of Disciplines, which they are bound to eventually, that they will still focus on different powers from those Disciplines for each Clan. It's just keeping it down to two Disciplines makes it easier to limit the overlap as much as possible. At least that's my take.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The only consistent wisdom is in knowing you know nothing&quot; ~ Socrates <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1197-imthestein","name":"Imthestein","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1197_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T14:57:23-07:00","id":1310817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackshade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1310789#post1310789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Surprised Tremere got Auspex. I really thought they were going to give each clan their own unique discliplines. But it seems likely there will be overlap in discliplines between clans now. Unless Toreador are out (higly unlikely).They are so many different thaumaturgy paths to choose from. Why not keep Auspex for Toreador?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would have been fine with there being two different paths of Thaumaturgy for Tremere. That way, Auspex would have less likelihood of overlapping, if that is the way the developers plan to go about handling this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T15:05:22-07:00","id":1310820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1310769#post1310769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's that strange place with the leaking faucet from the trailer. I don't think we know anything about it beyond &quot;some run-down place&quot; - which would make for a good hideout for both a Nosferatu and a Malkavian.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a theory going around that the whole wave of blood thing is actually part of a Malkavian hallucination. The fact that the scene can be a reference to <a href=\"https://youtu.be/HNnCL0q3EuI\" target=\"_blank\">The Shining</a>, and that the blood wave starts out in the aslyum area pretty much confirms that it's a Malkavian hideout.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T21:08:06-07:00","id":1310913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1310758#post1310758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Taking five clans out of the core seven, I don't think there is a distribution that gets everyone two unique disciplines. Not when three clans have Auspex and another three have Presence. If Tremere had Dominate and Thau, that would leave Presence and Fortitude for Ventrue, which overlaps with Toreador.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would have been possible before they announced Tremere: Brujah get Celerity and Potence, Torries get Auspex and Presence, Ventrue get Dominate and Fortitude, Malks get Obfuscate and Dementation, and Gangrel get Protean and Animalism. Or, Tremere get two types of wooj.<br /> <br /> That said, my money's on Torries, Ventrue, and Nos for the last three. Discipline-wise, Auspex+Presence, Dominate+Fortitude, and Obfuscate+Animalism. (Maybe replace Nos with Malks, Obfuscate+Dementation?) Then Gangrel as the first DLC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T03:27:21-07:00","id":1310952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1310913#post1310913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then Gangrel as the first <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">DLC</span></b></span>.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://memegenerator.net/img/images/400x/1152280.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD 