 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T07:58:54-07:00","id":1310977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1310913#post1310913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It would have been possible before they announced Tremere: Brujah get Celerity and Potence, Torries get Auspex and Presence, Ventrue get Dominate and Fortitude, Malks get Obfuscate and Dementation, and Gangrel get Protean and Animalism. Or, Tremere get two types of wooj.<br /> <br /> That said, my money's on Torries, Ventrue, and Nos for the last three. Discipline-wise, Auspex+Presence, Dominate+Fortitude, and Obfuscate+Animalism. (Maybe replace Nos with Malks, Obfuscate+Dementation?) Then Gangrel as the first DLC.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, except that it sounds like they might wait on Malkavians so they can assure they do mental illness justice. Also, they said they are basing this on V5 which means no Dementation. But I do think when they do Malkavians they will do Auspex and Dominate and focus on those powers relating to Dementation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The only consistent wisdom is in knowing you know nothing&quot; ~ Socrates <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1197-imthestein","name":"Imthestein","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1197_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T08:02:03-07:00","id":1310980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imthestein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1310977#post1310977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, they said they are basing this on V5 which means no Dementation. But I do think when they do Malkavians they will do Auspex and Dominate and focus on those powers relating to Dementation.</div> </div> </div> </div>So far, they've used a mixed approach - the Thin Bloods seem a little more V20 with their &quot;I think that's what vampires should be able to do&quot; approach to disciplines rather than alchemy and shifting disciplines by blood resonance. And Tremere Blood Sorcery is called Thaumaturgy. So I'd say all bets are off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T09:28:43-07:00","id":1311001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1310960#post1310960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Free DLC, in fact, but do go on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, still don't care for &quot;DLC&quot;s, free or not. It's sad that the industry has pushed to &quot;Release before everything is actually included&quot; over time.<br /> Actual proper expansion packs are a different beast - and they're something I gladly pay for. I'd also give monetary support in Early Access development or sort of a Patreon.<br /> But please: Have the game actually fully completed on proper release.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 05-09-2019, 12:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T10:05:10-07:00","id":1311006,"title":"","content":"I think the problem is that you're assuming that them releasing entirely free additional content after release is somehow making the base game &quot;incomplete.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's not like devs never released free map packs/factions/etc or anything for download in the era before DLC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T10:30:56-07:00","id":1311012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1311001#post1311001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, still don't care for &quot;DLC&quot;s, free or not. It's sad that the industry has pushed to &quot;Release before everything is actually included&quot; over time.<br /> Actual proper expansion packs are a different beast - and they're something I gladly pay for. I'd also give monetary support in Early Access development or sort of a Patreon.<br /> But please: Have the game actually fully completed on proper release.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are releasing a, presumably, proper expansion pack called &quot;Season of the Wolf&quot; which will feature werewolves.<br /> It's not as if Gangrel are a requirement for the game being completed, anyway. They're not even Camarilla anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T10:34:46-07:00","id":1311013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1310980#post1310980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So far, they've used a mixed approach - the Thin Bloods seem a little more V20 with their &amp;quot;I think that's what vampires should be able to do&amp;quot; approach to disciplines rather than alchemy and shifting disciplines by blood resonance. And Tremere Blood Sorcery is called Thaumaturgy. So I'd say all bets are off.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see it as all bets being off. Thin-bloods likely join a clan like they do in V5 even if their powers are different. As for Thaumaturgy, V5 even says the Tremere call Blood Sorcery Thaumaturgy instead.<br /> <br /> That being said, I'm far from believing this will be a one to one translation from V5. At the end of the day this is a videogame and they have to change things to accommodate that. All I'm saying is that they said they are using V5 as the base so we need to keep that in mind","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The only consistent wisdom is in knowing you know nothing&quot; ~ Socrates <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1197-imthestein","name":"Imthestein","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1197_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T22:09:41-07:00","id":1311154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardestadtTheEvenYounger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1311012#post1311012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They're not even Camarilla anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not like we have to join the Camarilla until the very end of the game before making a choice of allegiances, either. It outright states on their website that there are different factions vying for control of the blood trade, and we get to decide which ones to help out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-15T09:25:22-07:00","id":1312313,"title":"","content":"Disappointingly, the Brujah and Toreador's Celerity powers are identical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-15T10:01:15-07:00","id":1312331,"title":"","content":"I'm curious about the intended function of Presence, since it's first level power seems to be almost entirely focused on providing a distraction. Does this mean we can expect to see some kind of team work missions, where we need to keep the crowd off somebody else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-15T10:06:52-07:00","id":1312332,"title":"","content":"It probably just works like the courtesans in AC 2.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://portforward.com/games/walkthroughs/Assassins-Creed-II/Assassins-Creed-II-large-766.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> You can use Presence and then send the crowds to distract guards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-15T16:37:57-07:00","id":1312440,"title":"","content":"A lot of these choices aren't ideal if you want a perfect V5 experience but on the other hand, I don't think any of them are inappropriate for a Thin Blooded diablerist. It's one of the reasons why I didn't have a problem with no out of clan disciplines for the Los Angeles Fledgling.<br /> <br /> I mean, you're like a month old at best (assuming time progression happens at all and it's not all one insane night with Caine laughing his ass off).<br /> <br /> OF COURSE you're not going to be able to learn out of your Clan Disciplines.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-15T20:00:15-07:00","id":1312477,"title":"","content":"So it seems like the overlapping disciplines are going to be identical to each other, instead of getting different powers, like I've been told is a feature of 5th edition.<br /> <br /> This makes me very concerned for my beloved Nosferatu, since they don't have a unique discipline to identify their clan with. Potence is the &quot;signaure&quot; power of the Brujah, which I am taken to believe that none of the other clans will have access to it. That leaves Obfuscate and Animalism for their possible abilities.<br /> <br /> Problem is, Obfuscate would overlap with Malkavians, and Animalism would overlap with the Gangrel, assuming they're the first DLC clan.<br /> <br /> I think it's pretty much a given that the Ventrue signature power is going to be Dominate. So unless they give Malkavians Dementation, their only available disciplines would be Obfuscate and Auspex. The former would clash with the potentially signature ability for the Nosferatu, and the later is already shared by the Tremere, meaning that it can't be considered a signature ability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-15T21:10:24-07:00","id":1312482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1312477#post1312477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's pretty much a given that the Ventrue signature power is going to be Dominate. So unless they give Malkavians Dementation, their only available disciplines would be Obfuscate and Auspex. The former would clash with the potentially signature ability for the Nosferatu, and the later is already shared by the Tremere, meaning that it can't be considered a signature ability.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed on Dominate, but I'm guessing the Nos signature is going to be Obfuscate, and Malks will get Dementation + Auspex if they appear in the initial release at all. Stealth is really the biggest part of playing a Nos.<br /> <br /> Sure, Dementation isn't a Discipline in V5\u2014but there's no sign of Amalgam powers in Bloodlines 2, and I don't think they'd include Malkavians without some element of infectious madness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-15T21:35:52-07:00","id":1312485,"title":"","content":"Been trying to think of which Thin Blood power to go with for each clan. Here's what I've come up with so far.<br /> <br /> <b>Clan Brujah</b> = <i>Nebulation:</i> A super strong, super fast berserker, who can become intangible at will?<br /> <br /> <b>Clan Tremere</b> = <i>Mentalism:</i> Ignoring the fact that telekinetic abilities are already available in the form of alternate paths of Blood Sorcery, I think moving objects with your mind fits the theme of clan Tremere as blood magicians.<br /> <br /> <b>Clan Toreador</b> = <i>Nebulation:</i> The ability to appear and vanish in a cloud of mist is probably great for putting on a show for the masses. And what is a Toreador, without a captivated audience?<br /> <br /> <b>Clan Ventrue</b> = <i>Chiropteran:</i> Taking inspiration from Requiem, the Ventrue in that game have Animalism as one of their clan disciplines. Also, I think the idea of gliding over the city's rooftops as one of the kindred elite sounds pretty cool.<br /> <br /> <b>Clan Malkavian</b> = <i>Mentalism:</i> It's a well established character trope for those with mental instability to have access to psychic powers.<br /> <br /> <b>Clan Gangrel</b> = <i>Undecided:</i> Will wait until we have more information about the Wolf DLC.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-16T02:06:35-07:00","id":1312513,"title":"","content":"I think the coming discipline spreads are relatively obvious:<br /> <br /> Ventrue: <b>Dominate</b> + Fortitude<br /> Nosferatu: <b>Obfuscate</b> + Animalism<br /> Malkavian: <b>Dementation</b> + Auspex<br /> Gangrel: <b>Protean</b> + (either Animalism or Fortitude)<br /> <br /> They're not sticking strictly to V5 (or they would have called Thaumaturgy Blood Sorcery instead), so I doubt they'll let themselves be thwarted from their idea of &quot;1 signature discipline + 1 common discipline&quot; by Malkavians going back to Dominate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-16T04:54:00-07:00","id":1312534,"title":"","content":"If I don't get to make a <a href=\"https://youtu.be/XUhVCoTsBaM\" target=\"_blank\">Pillar Men</a> inspired Toreador, I will be very disappointed with this game's character creation options.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-16T05:14:14-07:00","id":1312539,"title":"","content":"Given Dementation no longer exists, I don't think we'll see it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-16T05:18:38-07:00","id":1312541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_