_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Queer Snake</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1313762#post1313762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope next week is my dear Nosferatu</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They better. None of the clans revealed so far are designed for a Stealth Run playthrough. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-22T17:40:09-07:00","id":1313768,"title":"","content":"Gangrel!<br /> <br /> Malkavian!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-22T18:03:22-07:00","id":1313769,"title":"","content":"There's been an argument made that next week might be Lasombra. Given they hinted in the Ventrue stream that not all of the Clans at release will be Clans from BL1 I think this makes Lasombra likely. I love Nosferatu, but Nosferatu was admittedly considered hard mode in BL1. Plus, with them adding Clans as free DLCs I think we'll see Nosferatu added to include things like Sewers as well as stealth gameplay.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The only consistent wisdom is in knowing you know nothing&quot; ~ Socrates <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1197-imthestein","name":"Imthestein","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1197_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-22T18:04:59-07:00","id":1313770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imthestein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1313769#post1313769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's been an argument made that next week might be Lasombra. Given they hinted in the Ventrue stream that not all of the Clans at release will be Clans from BL1 I think this makes Lasombra likely. I love Nosferatu, but Nosferatu was admittedly considered hard mode in BL1. Plus, with them adding Clans as free DLCs I think we'll see Nosferatu added to include things like Sewers as well as stealth gameplay.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Alternatively, it might be the Assamites. Since we don't have a stealth based clan, yet. Adding Lasombra would only double up on the aristocratic Ventrue. Plus, their two other disciplines are &quot;signature&quot; powers of the Brujah and Ventrue clans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-22T18:07:51-07:00","id":1313771,"title":"","content":"Banu Haqim is possible, but in that case you have them using Blood Sorcery which then doubles up with the Tremere signature power. Either way I think we're likely to see some sort of doubling up of powers unfortunately and the Brujah are the most likely to see their powers copied given Celerity is used by Toreador as well. There are only so many Disciplines, especially in V5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The only consistent wisdom is in knowing you know nothing&quot; ~ Socrates <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1197-imthestein","name":"Imthestein","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1197_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-22T18:09:49-07:00","id":1313772,"title":"","content":"It should be noted that of all the Clans the Brujah are the only ones with a purely physical power set, so they'll still be unique in that regard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The only consistent wisdom is in knowing you know nothing&quot; ~ Socrates <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1197-imthestein","name":"Imthestein","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1197_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-22T18:17:07-07:00","id":1313774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imthestein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1313771#post1313771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Banu Haqim is possible, but in that case you have them using Blood Sorcery which then doubles up with the Tremere signature power. Either way I think we're likely to see some sort of doubling up of powers unfortunately and the Brujah are the most likely to see their powers copied given Celerity is used by Toreador as well. There are only so many Disciplines, especially in V5.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not necessarily. They still called it Thaumaturgy in the Tremere reveal, so the Assamites would probably still have Quietus. They're both a form of Blood Sorcery, but they offer different powers / traditions from each other.<br /> <br /> Just like how the Malkavians could still possess the Dementation themed version of Dominate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-22-2019, 09:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-22T18:32:27-07:00","id":1313776,"title":"","content":"I just checked and you're right. So maybe we'll see Banu Haqim with Obfuscate and Quietus. As for Malkavians, I've been assuming they'll give them Auspex and Dominate using the Dementation powers much like you're suggesting. But I think with Malkavians they'll be looking to add something else to the gameplay as well. I feel like every Clan added will be adding something specific to the game beyond just Disciplines. Gangrel are looking to be added with Werewolves and shapeshifting powers for example (assuming that is what is happening with Season of the Wolf)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The only consistent wisdom is in knowing you know nothing&quot; ~ Socrates <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1197-imthestein","name":"Imthestein","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1197_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-22T18:37:52-07:00","id":1313777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imthestein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1313776#post1313776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just checked and you're right. So maybe we'll see Banu Haqim with Obfuscate and Quietus. As for Malkavians, I've been assuming they'll give them Auspex and Dominate using the Dementation powers much like you're suggesting. But I think with Malkavians they'll be looking to add something else to the gameplay as well. I feel like every Clan added will be adding something specific to the game beyond just Disciplines. Gangrel are looking to be added with Werewolves and shapeshifting powers for example (assuming that is what is happening with Season of the Wolf)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sadly, this stuff about the clans only having access to 2 of their disciplines, and making some of the &quot;common&quot; disciplines exclusive signature powers has me nervous about the final list of clans. Because if their goal is to make the clans overlap less with each other, then that means they've severely restricted the number of options available to choose from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-23T00:28:46-07:00","id":1313800,"title":"","content":"On the one hand, it seems quite possible now that other clans are in the running now. Then again, I think it's most likely that the fifth clan will be one for a stealth run as that's what's currently missing. That almost certainly means Obfuscate, so no Lasombra. The Big 13 clans that come to mind would be the Ministry and the Banu Haqim. I would ordininarily tend towards Banu Haqim, but the producer has called them by their old, embarrasing name &quot;Assamites&quot; a few times on stream, which I don't think would have happened if they'd really focused on them and made them a playable clan. The Ministry would be an interesting choice, but their disciplines have a lot of overlap with the signature disciplines of others. Assuming Obfuscate is considered signature, they've got three signature-worthy disciplines with Serpentis/Protean, Presence <i>and</i> Obfuscate.<br /> <br /> So... yeah, I don't know. It's possible that they were talking hypothetically about DLC clans, but it did sound as if they were hinting at what the fifth clan might be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-23T00:33:21-07:00","id":1313802,"title":"","content":"I would bet for the Nosferatu being the last clan released, I believe that Obfuscate adds more to the game than Protean or malkavian Dominate. And, as they have shown pictures of underground and sewers, I imagine that they have developed this part of the city. With Gangrels you have to deep in the wilderness to fully feel the clan territory, and that is more difficult than to build some sewers, I think. And with Malkavians, in spite of being one of my favorites or may be because of this, I hope that the developers give them the deep and complexity that true madness deserve, I hope something about them in the line of Call of Cthulhu, not the goofy and cartoonish insanity that some people enjoy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-23T04:16:38-07:00","id":1313814,"title":"","content":"While I'm curious to see how the developers plan to tackle a more serious portrayal of mental illness in the form of Malkavians, I would really, really like to see the Nosferatu as the next clan. I'm okay with waiting for Malkavian DLC, especially if they feel like they need more time to flesh stuff out. But they already showed a Nosferatu in the trailer, and if that turns out to just be a tease, then I shall be quite disappointed with the lack of one of my favorite clans in the game.<br /> <br /> Besides, I hear you get a second chance at character creation after joining one of the clans, and I feel like the Nosferatu would open up a whole new series of customization options that the other clans wouldn't be able to match. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-23T06:32:47-07:00","id":1313831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1313814#post1313814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>While I'm curious to see how the developers plan to tackle a more serious portrayal of mental illness in the form of Malkavians,</b> I would really, really like to see the Nosferatu as the next clan. I'm okay with waiting for Malkavian DLC, especially if they feel like they need more time to flesh stuff out. But they already showed a Nosferatu in the trailer, and if that turns out to just be a tease, then I shall be quite disappointed with the lack of one of my favorite clans in the game.<br /> <br /> Besides, I hear you get a second chance at character creation after joining one of the clans, and I feel like the Nosferatu would open up a whole new series of customization options that the other clans wouldn't be able to match. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>5th Edition establishes the Malkavians aren't mentally ill, they're neuroatypical (i.e. their condition is not mental illness but a magically different way of viewing the universe).<br /> <br /> Which resolves all my issues with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-23T06:43:08-07:00","id":1313834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1313831#post1313831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5th Edition establishes the Malkavians aren't mentally ill, they're neuroatypical (i.e. their condition is not mental illness but a magically different way of viewing the universe).<br /> <br /> Which resolves all my issues with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is being repeated again and again and I wonder where it comes from.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Core Rules, page 76</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">All Malkavians suffer mental<br /> illness following the Embrace -<br /> sometimes accentuating an existing<br /> condition, other times adding a new<br /> dimension to their instability.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-23T06:43:55-07:00","id":1313835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1313831#post1313831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 5th Edition establishes the Malkavians aren't mentally ill, they're neuroatypical (i.e. their condition is not mental illness but a magically different way of viewing the universe).<br /> <br /> Which resolves all my issues with it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ...<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> So... what's their clan weakness, now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-23T06:47:05-07:00","id":1313836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1313834#post1313834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is being repeated again and again and I wonder where it comes from.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, good! They didn't get rid of the craziness! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-23T07:00:33-07:00","id":1313842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1313831#post1313831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 5th Edition establishes the Malkavians aren't mentally ill, they're neuroatypical (i.e. their condition is not mental illness but a magically different way of viewing the universe).<br /> <br /> Which resolves all my issues with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quick nit to pick: No, they're not &quot;neuroatypical&quot; because of magically different/skewed viewpoints. Being neuroatypical (I'm autistic, myself) can be a complex and often difficult set of neurological, social and cognitive circumstances for one to deal with, and I would appreciate it if neuroatypicality wasn't used as a placeholder term for what V5 Malkavians deal with. It's cheap, and innacurate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-23T07:03:57-07:00","id":1313843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1313842#post1313842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Quick nit to pick: No, they're not &quot;neuroatypical&quot; because of magically different/skewed viewpoints. Being neuroatypical (I'm autistic, myself) can be a complex and often difficult set of neurological, social and cognitive circumstances for one to deal with, and I would appreciate it if neuroatypicality wasn't used as a placeholder term for what V5 Malkavians deal with. It's cheap, and innacurate.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I fall under the spectrum as well (Aspergers) and wasn't sure if the condition was neurological, or psychological. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-23-2019, 10:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-23T09:36:45-07:00","id":1313863,"title":"","content":"Well, it could be said with new terms or even neologisms, but the base problem is that the stereotypical Malkavian could easily became a mockery of mental illness. In Bloodlines 1 being the Malkavian character was just being rare, may be with some personality disorder of the second axis of the DSM, probably schicotipycal or schizoid personality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-23T09:59:36-07:00","id":1313865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1313835#post1313835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> So... what's their clan weakness, now?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Clan Bane is 'pick an Attribute Category (Social, Mental or Physical) at creation. When you have a Bestial Failure or Compulsion, for the scene you take penalties to dice pools in that category equal to the Bane Severity'. So you can fluff it as any mental illness you want rather than being limited by Derangements (which are no longer a system anyway).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-23T12:55:40-07:00","id":1313886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1313865#post1313865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The Clan Bane is 'pick an Attribute Category (Social, Mental or Physical) at creation. When you have a Bestial Failure or Compulsion, for the scene you take penalties to dice pools in that category equal to the Bane Severity'. So you can fluff it as any mental illness you want rather than being limited by Derangements (which are no longer a system anyway).</div> </div> </div> </div>More specifically that attribute is being affected because of how your derangement manifests (and they do still call it a derangement). An example being a Malkavian that sometimes experiences physical sensations as voices rather than feeling them and this causes a -1 penalty (his Bane Severity is 1) to all physical pools as the voices become too distracting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The only consistent wisdom is in knowing you know nothing&quot; ~ Socrates <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1197-imthestein","name":"Imthestein","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1197_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-23T13:15:32-07:00","id":1313893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1313842#post1313842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Quick nit to pick: No, they're not &quot;neuroatypical&quot; because of magically different/skewed viewpoints. Being neuroatypical (I'm autistic, myself) can be a complex and often difficult set of neurological, social and cognitive circumstances for one to deal with, and I would appreciate it if neuroatypicality wasn't used as a placeholder term for what V5 Malkavians deal with. It's cheap, and innacurate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am also neuroatypical and find it awesome we have the Malks. YMMV.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-23T17:37:54-07:00","id":1313944,"title":"","content":"W<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imthestein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1313886#post1313886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More specifically that attribute is being affected because of how your derangement manifests (and they do still call it a derangement). An example being a Malkavian that sometimes experiences physical sensations as voices rather than feeling them and this causes a -1 penalty (his Bane Severity is 1) to all physical pools as the voices become too distracting.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I mean when I say 'no derangement rules' is there's no list of 'pick this thing and get this (sometimes heinous, sometimes not at all penalizing) mental illness' derangements.. It allows you to fluff it whatever way you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-23T17:39:24-07:00","id":1313946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1313944#post1313944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">W<br /> <br /> What I mean when I say 'no derangement rules' is there's no list of 'pick this thing and get this (sometimes heinous, sometimes not at all penalizing) mental illness' derangements.. It allows you to fluff it whatever way you want.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I'm sorry for the misunderstanding. Yeah, I'm liking this better so far as it gives a mechanical downside that is consistent across the board.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The only consistent wisdom is in knowing you know nothing&quot; ~ Socrates <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1197-imthestein","name":"Imthestein","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1197_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-23T18:32:40-07:00","id":1313960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1313893#post1313893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am also neuroatypical and find it awesome we have the Malks. YMMV.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love the Malkavians, personally. They've been one of my favorite Clans since I started playing VtM in the first place. Their Clan symbol is going to be one of my next tattoos, in fact. It wasn't the Malkavians that I had a problem with. It was your characterization of the Clan as neuroatypical, which is different from having a psychiatric illness or disorder.<br /> <br /> Now, there's overlap between the purely psychological and the neurological, but the overarching theme of the Clans is &quot;madness&quot;, and not &quot;atypical neurological circumstances&quot;. There are some odd exceptions that popped up over the years, such as the completely neurological Sydenham's chorea (St. Vitus' Dance) found in the <b>Dark Ages: Vampire</b> Derangements, but even that was explained as an intentional anachronistic mistake to reflect the time period of the setting. Outlying instances like that aside, there's been plenty of ink spilled since 2nd edition to build the Malkavians into something more than just simplistic pranksters, goofballs and plot-oracles who &quot;see things differently&quot;.<br /> <br /> Lots of people see things &quot;differently&quot;, whether neuotypical, atypical, mentally ill or not. Thinking or seeing things in new and different ways is simply part of being an individual. That's hardly a Curse (unless you would prefer to be part of a hive-mind, in which case, you have my apologies and sympathy). An incurable, supernaturally enhanced mental illness, however, <i>is</i> a Curse. I generally take umbrage with neuroatypicality AND mental illness being portrayed as a sort of &quot;accidental superpower&quot;, where the atypical mind is treated as a misunderstood or underutilized skill. It's common enough to be a trope, and it does a disservice to those who suffer from mental illness or deal with atypical neurology by misrepresenting us and what we deal with.<br /> <br /> I don't begrudge the Clan a single prankster, goofball or oracle, though. These are creatures of the mind, of varied thought and also one of the most diverse Clans. There's going to be a lot of interesting individuals. With Auspex, Dominate/Dementation and Obfuscate at their disposal, hijinks and revealed secrets are bound to follow. Their success, for what success there is, was never due to their &quot;madness&quot;, though. It was in spite of it. They, above any other, are a Clan of people who are <i>coping with their Curse</i> (or not, as is the case for the MANY Malkavians who knowingly destroy themselves within a single human lifetime following the Embrace).<br /> <br /> This isn't the cimematic delusions of <i>A Beautiful Mind</i>. This is the gothic, crumbling, facade of sanity or an utter lack thereof, railed against or worked with by turns, as portrayed in Lovecraft or Poe. It's true that the Curse, like any Clan Curse, can be dealt with. It can possibly be temporarily appeased. In the end, though, a Malkavian can never get better, and they've got nothing but time to get <i>worse</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","date":". 05-23-2019, 09:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-23T21:11:53-07:00","id":1313983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1313960#post1313960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lots of people see things &quot;differently&quot;, whether neuotypical, atypical, mentally ill or not. Thinking or seeing things in new and different ways is simply part of being an individual. That's hardly a Curse (unless you would prefer to be part of a hive-mind, in which case, you have my apologies and sympathy). An incurable, supernaturally enhanced mental illness, however, <i>is</i> a Curse. I generally take umbrage with neuroatypicality AND mental illness being portrayed as a sort of &quot;accidental superpower&quot;, where the atypical mind is treated as a misunderstood or underutilized skill. It's common enough to be a trope, and it does a disservice to those who suffer from mental illness or deal with atypical neurology by misrepresenting us and what we deal with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, because living in a society who's customs are virtually alien to the neuroatypical mindset really makes one feel like they have super powers... Oh, no wait... it makes us question our own intelligence, when we constantly struggle to comprehend something that comes naturally to everyone around us. Nothing inspires self loathing, like the thought that you'll never be accepted by the society you were raised in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-24-2019, 12:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-23T21:48:37-07:00","id":1313987,"title":"","content":"It can be a blessing and a curse.<br /> <br /> Certainly, it hurts your ability to relate to other people but I also believe those people not understanding is on them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-24T01:42:53-07:00","id":1314009,"title":"","content":"I share and understand the Azraelfirestorm argumentation, when he talks about superpowers I think he refers to the high intelligence that is related with being crazy in lot of movies, like A beautiful mind, when in fact it is the exception. The divine touch, the vision of madness as something related with the gods had pre-scyencitfical origins and we still maintain some of this view. The psychology is a very recent science, we barely understand the origins of half the disorders and common people still think about madness as some form of enlightening, and this have permeated the vampire books too. Vampire books are not immune to this myths about the disorders, myths and common misconceptions that sound as a mockery when you study and dedicate your life to work with this disorders. The disorders generate suffering, deep suffering, that is the reason because they are compiled in clinical handbooks, not are just being rare and have some touch of extravaganzza.<br /> <br /> When they wrote Vampire first and second edition, there were lot of prejudices about gypsies and muslims that permeated the writtings about Ravnos and Assamites, the have corrected them with the pass of the years, in part because the society has changed in his visions of these soft racism. But society had no changed in their visions of mentally disorders in the same way, we still maintain the same wrong ideas about what a disorder is that we have 25 years ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-24T03:06:05-07:00","id":1314024,"title":"","content":"Generally, I believe a large amount of abuse and prejudice against those with different thought processes exist. However, not only am I so but many lifelong associates. Their way of looking at the world should not be stigmatized.<br /> <br /> And yes, there is a correlation between high intelligence and the spectrum.<br /> <br /> One doesn't necessarily lead to the other but the idea of enlightenment and different thoughts shouldn't be thown out.<br /> <br /> But again, look at my sigil for how I think the Malkavians are already the most awesome clan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-24T03:18:42-07:00","id":1314026,"title":"","content":"There is no scientifically demonstrated correlation between intelligence and autism, I am sorry, it is a false myth. Furthermore, what it is intelligence? The psychologists, and I am, can not converge in only one description of the term. I am a fan of the malkavians my self, but I can not blind me to the misconceptions they led to most of the people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-24T17:40:16-07:00","id":1314209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justycar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1314026#post1314026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is no scientifically demonstrated correlation between intelligence and autism, I am sorry, it is a false myth. Furthermore, what it is intelligence? The psychologists, and I am, can not converge in only one description of the term. I am a fan of the malkavians my self, but I can not blind me to the misconceptions they led to most of the people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but it's the relationship to the Malkavians that I think is worth exploring.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-26T07:35:51-07:00","id":1314538,"title":"","content":"i am really torn on which clan to choose. They all seem fun to use with their own signature disclipline. I am sure my decision will become easier once we see actual footage. But right now, i am leaning towards a social clan for my first playthrough. So that means Ventrue or Toreador. i think these two clans will play a bit similar to each other, so i dont expect to pick up the other clan for my second playthrough.<br /> <br /> For my second playthrough i am leaning towards Tremere because they are basically hard mode and blood boil seems to be the most devastating ability in the game. So i would love to play around with that. But if the game is good, i expect to play the game atleast 3 times. Picking up one of the thinblood discliplines for each playthrough. That will also be a tough decision on its own. Which thinblood discipline fits which clan the best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-26T08:09:33-07:00","id":1314544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/_m_FUXxzhMY\" data-code=\"_m_FUXxzhMY\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/_m_FUXxzhMY/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-27T14:22:47-07:00","id":1314795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1314544#post1314544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/_m_FUXxzhMY\" data-code=\"_m_FUXxzhMY\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/_m_FUXxzhMY/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>W..wait, so is there going to be a third-person pov option? I've yet to see one. Also, what's with every Discipline being accompanied by an obvious hand gesture? I was immediately reminded of first person games like <i>Hexen</i> from the 90s. That and Force users from Star Wars... Stylistically, it's a departure both from how Disciplines were generally handled in Bloodlines 1 and even how they're portrayed in any edition of the tabletop game. I don't think it'll immediately put people unfamiliar with VtM off from getting into the game, but I find it a bit annoying. I'm more concerned with the camera options, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-27T14:45:27-07:00","id":1314802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1314795#post1314795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> W..wait, so is there going to be a third-person pov option? I've yet to see one. Also, what's with every Discipline being accompanied by an obvious hand gesture? I was immediately reminded of first person games like <i>Hexen</i> from the 90s. That and Force users from Star Wars... Stylistically, it's a departure both from how Disciplines were generally handled in Bloodlines 1 and even how they're portrayed in any edition of the tabletop game. I don't think it'll immediately put people unfamiliar with VtM off from getting into the game, but I find it a bit annoying. I'm more concerned with the camera options, though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've heard that 3rd person view may be used for certain cutscenes and battle animations. But otherwise, the game is going to be predominately focused on a 1st person mode.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-27T14:47:58-07:00","id":1314804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1314795#post1314795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> W..wait, so is there going to be a third-person pov option? I've yet to see one. Also, what's with every Discipline being accompanied by an obvious hand gesture? I was immediately reminded of first person games like <i>Hexen</i> from the 90s. That and Force users from Star Wars... Stylistically, it's a departure both from how Disciplines were generally handled in Bloodlines 1 and even how they're portrayed in any edition of the tabletop game. I don't think it'll immediately put people unfamiliar with VtM off from getting into the game, but I find it a bit annoying. I'm more concerned with the camera options, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what we know so far, I think it'll be first person only.<br /> As for the gestures, it's simply good ui design - let your players know that their button press has been noticed and they're doing something cool and supernatural.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-27T15:05:48-07:00","id":1314811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1314804#post1314804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what we know so far, I think it'll be first person only.<br /> As for the gestures, it's simply good ui design - let your players know that their button press has been noticed and they're doing something cool and supernatural.</div> </div> </div> </div>I.e. Skyrim-esque<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01