lass=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Diablerie is fine as long as you don't get caught or its sanctioned via Blood Hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're afraid of getting caught, then you haven't diablerized enough rivals!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-12T17:31:04-07:00","id":1318155,"title":"","content":"20 Minutes of Gameplay Footage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/_oYJAnhvgNk\" data-code=\"_oYJAnhvgNk\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/_oYJAnhvgNk/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Some observations:<br /> <br /> * I like the apartment and it's a lot nicer than anything you'd normally get in Seattle.<br /> <br /> * The Atrium is our new club.<br /> <br /> * BAD DANCING RETURNS!<br /> <br /> * Without sounding sexist, Elif makes me very Thirsty. Which is appropriate for a vampire.<br /> <br /> * She's a Tremere too. I wonder if she's House Carnae since they're the sexy vampires.<br /> <br /> * The Nosferatu are new designs.<br /> <br /> * Apparently, Thin Bloods of Nosferatu lineage can be horribly deformed.<br /> <br /> * Our adventure takes us into the &quot;Jungle&quot; which is giving me strong Dishonored flashbacks.<br /> <br /> * Is it weird that I'm uncomfortable beating up as many female NPCs as I am in this level?<br /> <br /> * Slugg can be bargained with, killed, or stolen from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-12T17:37:08-07:00","id":1318156,"title":"","content":"I think the biggest question we need answered is: Will bad dancing let us gain Humanity, if we leave it alone for a few minutes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-12T18:01:00-07:00","id":1318161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1318156#post1318156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the biggest question we need answered is: Will bad dancing let us gain Humanity, if we leave it alone for a few minutes?</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume that Bad Dancing Thin Blood is the ancestor of Commander Shepard the Dhampyr.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-12T18:08:29-07:00","id":1318162,"title":"","content":"Huh, now I'm confused. From the looks of things, the player had Thaumaturgy and Potence, in addition to Nebulation.<br /> <br /> A test build, perhaps?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-13T14:50:26-07:00","id":1318314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1318162#post1318162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh, now I'm confused. From the looks of things, the player had Thaumaturgy and Potence, in addition to Nebulation.<br /> <br /> A test build, perhaps?</div> </div> </div> </div>The YouTuber Outstar, who used to work in the videogame industry, said this was likely a test build where they just gave it a bunch of powers so they could show things off. It wasn't indicative of a normal character. I think it's important to keep in mind that it did say Pre-Alpha so a lot is going to be mishmashed a bit and things will likely change a great deal by release.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The only consistent wisdom is in knowing you know nothing&quot; ~ Socrates <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1197-imthestein","name":"Imthestein","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1197_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-14T04:05:08-07:00","id":1318441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1318155#post1318155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> * She's a Tremere too. I wonder if she's House Carnae since they're the sexy vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div> She mentioned &quot;the Pyramid&quot; when talking about her organization, and wears something mimicking an alchemical symbol. House Carnae is more neo-pagan and rejects the Pyramid. So, I kind of doubt it. <br /> <br /> Though, there seems to be some voice versus text differences there - the actual text said &quot;my organization&quot; while the voice said &quot;the Pyramid.&quot; So, it could have been a mistake. And not like the necklace is any strong indication of anything. She just doesn't give a Carnae vibe at all to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-14T04:43:24-07:00","id":1318446,"title":"","content":"I was hoping the &quot;factions&quot; would have referred to Camarilla, Anarch and possibly Sabbat. But during the gameplay demo, this Penny character mentions 4 different locations to meet up with them.<br /> <br /> 4 locations: The Bar, the Coffee Shop, the Club, and the Parking Garage.<br /> <br /> Now I'm curious as to who they are. Since I highly doubt the Sabbat would have the patience necessary to set up a private meeting, or try to gradually recruit you throughout the game. They seem like the kind of people who are either <i>&quot;join or die&quot;</i> mentality.<br /> <br /> And if the 4th faction are independent, then they wouldn't even try to recruit you at all!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-14T18:03:45-07:00","id":1318573,"title":"","content":"<br /> My thoughts on the 18 minute video.<br /> <br /> * Love they got the same newscaster for the place.<br /> <br /> * Nice apartment. Much nicer than the Santa Monica one.<br /> <br /> * I'm iffy about the first person view. I want to see my Malkavian's pimp outfit.<br /> <br /> * The bad dancing is back!<br /> <br /> * I hope they get Lacuna Coil and Halestorm for the music.<br /> <br /> * I love the cell shading art as it will probably age much better than CGI. Like Borderlands it nicely stays cartoonish as well as sexy.<br /> <br /> * I love the sexy Tremere model even if she's flirting a bit too hard for no flirtation back.<br /> <br /> * I think jumping off the side of a building should be a Masquerade violation.<br /> <br /> * I appreciate the fact the Nosferatu want to take in a horribly disfigured Thin Blood.<br /> <br /> * I'm not overwhelmed so far with the combat as I don't actually give a shit about combat in this game. No one played V:TM:B for its fighting.<br /> <br /> * The fighting in the game looks a lot like Dishonored and that's not necessarily a bad thing. Except people already tried to do that with DARK and I'm literally the only person on the planet who played that crappy game.<br /> <br /> * I like the fact that we're getting options for Intimidation, Persuasion, Humanity, and other options. We're learning from Fallout 4.<br /> <br /> * I feel like Deadpool in the, &quot;Is it more sexist or not sexist?&quot; scene given I feel bad for beating to death realistic women NPCs with pipes. Way more than I do with dudes.<br /> <br /> * We have options on betraying on our backers in multiple ways as well as non-violent ways of resolving the conflict.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-14T18:29:27-07:00","id":1318577,"title":"","content":"So, here's another video of somebody playing the game who <b>might be</b> better at handling the combat than the IGN video was. You guys go ahead and decide!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/w3sOTLWUKGs\" data-code=\"w3sOTLWUKGs\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/w3sOTLWUKGs/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1318573#post1318573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> * I feel like Deadpool in the, &quot;Is it more sexist or not sexist?&quot; scene given I feel bad for beating to death realistic women NPCs with pipes. Way more than I do with dudes.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, if they're shooting at me with assault rifles and semi automatic pistols, they're an enemy just like everyone else!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-14-2019, 09:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-15T00:46:02-07:00","id":1318625,"title":"","content":"FYI, the newscaster is Brian Mitsoda, the head writer of both bloodlines games. He voiced the TV news anchor from the first game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8306-wissenschaft","name":"Wissenschaft","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-16T00:32:38-07:00","id":1318811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1318446#post1318446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was hoping the &quot;factions&quot; would have referred to Camarilla, Anarch and possibly Sabbat. But during the gameplay demo, this Penny character mentions 4 different locations to meet up with them.<br /> <br /> 4 locations: The Bar, the Coffee Shop, the Club, and the Parking Garage.<br /> <br /> Now I'm curious as to who they are. Since I highly doubt the Sabbat would have the patience necessary to set up a private meeting, or try to gradually recruit you throughout the game. They seem like the kind of people who are either <i>&quot;join or die&quot;</i> mentality.<br /> <br /> And if the 4th faction are independent, then they wouldn't even try to recruit you at all!</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that faction might not be as general as the normal vampire sects. After all, being part of a sect doesn't mean you have to like everyone in that sect. Similar to the factional divide between LaCroix and Strauss.<br /> <br /> We may see a similar intra-camarilla divide in this game between two faction leaders. Or it might be two different factions of Anarchs. There might also be some thin-bloods trying to organize. (Which could be a particularly big thing if your character is a former thin-blood, in a &quot;remember your roots&quot; kind of way. (Duskborn are also more typically the type to run with the Anarchs when they get organized. So they could also be an Anarch faction.))","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24666-ravian","name":"Ravian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-16T05:50:09-07:00","id":1318836,"title":"","content":"While &quot;independent&quot; might not be a general sect, I think that rejecting the three Sects could be an option. Assuming that Sabbat is an option at all - the current books seem more &quot;shovelhead-y&quot; Sabbat than anything worth looking at, but the game might change that. Granted, we might also have a switch of direction with OPP and Morpheus taking over the writing now, but so far we only have Cam and Anarch as sect options, so I'm not really sure that video game will include a Sabbat option. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * Apparently, Thin Bloods of Nosferatu lineage can be horribly deformed. </div> </div> </div> Missed this before, but wanted to point it out. Thin Blood of any clan can manifest their parent clan's flaw, be they Tremere, Nosferatu, Malkavian, Tziminsce, whatever. In V5, you take it as a Flaw during character creation, though storywise, its basically random chance. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * I appreciate the fact the Nosferatu want to take in a horribly disfigured Thin Blood. </div> </div> </div> Note that they only do this after Slugg managed to thrive in his own territory and get important information, to make a name for himself, and that's after rejecting him a first time. &quot;We're prepared to give him another look in exchange for some information.&quot; The Nos just want to use him, not help out of some kind of altrustic or familial impulse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-16T09:25:16-07:00","id":1318880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1318836#post1318836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Note that they only do this after Slugg managed to thrive in his own territory and get important information, to make a name for himself, and that's after rejecting him a first time. &quot;We're prepared to give him another look in exchange for some information.&quot; The Nos just want to use him, not help out of some kind of altrustic or familial impulse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, and Slugg explains that he's been working as an information broker for years, and the kindred still treated him like crap. They never brought him up in the ranks, and only came to him when they wanted something out of him. The whole reason he starts gathering protection (I'm assuming ghouls?) is because he wanted to be treated with some respect for once.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-16T10:37:10-07:00","id":1318892,"title":"","content":"Masked girl gets punched repeatedly in the face.<br /> <br /> +10 Desire Resonance after being drained of all blood.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;What kind of fetishes did you have, lady?&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-21T18:34:59-07:00","id":1320039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/aKfTe06l6k0\" data-code=\"aKfTe06l6k0\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/aKfTe06l6k0/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> If Outstar's speculation is correct, The Pioneers sound really interesting. I think I might side with them for a first play through option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-06T18:55:15-07:00","id":1322682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1318880#post1318880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yup, and Slugg explains that he's been working as an information broker for years, and the kindred still treated him like crap. They never brought him up in the ranks, and only came to him when they wanted something out of him. The whole reason he starts gathering protection (I'm assuming ghouls?) is because he wanted to be treated with some respect for once.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind you, Kindred are assholes in general.<br /> <br /> Slugg may not be THAT differently treated.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-06T20:04:07-07:00","id":1322693,"title":"","content":"So, has anybody else noticed that the powers listed for each discipline are called <i>&quot;Active&quot;</i> abilities? This has me hoping that we might also see some Passive abilities at some point in the game.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, I'm also nervous that said passives will be these vague <i>&quot;power ups&quot;</i> of the Active abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-08T13:42:38-07:00","id":1334519,"title":"","content":"So far the game looks dissapointing to me. The combat is atrocious and the animation dont inspire any confidence. Just compare it to cyberpunk or dying light 2 and it reality falls short. The should postpone it. March 2020 is too early for this game. No way they will polish this game enough before launch. i reality hope i am wrong about all this but it looks to be an average game at best<br /> .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24527,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","user":"blackshade","date":". 09-08-2019, 04:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-08T14:06:57-07:00","id":1334526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackshade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1334519#post1334519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So far the game looks dissapointing to me. The combat is atrocious and the animation dont inspire any confidence. Just compare it to cyberpunk or dying light 2 and it reality falls short. The should postpone it. March 2020 is too early for this game. No way they will polish this game enough before launch. i reality hope i am wrong about all this but it looks to be an average game at best<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>I think people who want photorealistic graphics in every game are a big part of what's wrong with the industry today.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-08T14:41:07-07:00","id":1334535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1334526#post1334526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think people who want photorealistic graphics in every game are a big part of what's wrong with the industry today.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Indeed, plus the footage is PRE-ALPHA, so of course it's got some kinks to work out.<br /> <br /> That being said, I did notice in one demo play that the character's head clipped backwards into their torso, after the player slugged them in the face.<br /> <br /> It reminded me of the scene in the opening of Bloodlines 1, where they simulated decapitating your sire, by just flipping their head upside down. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-08T16:30:32-07:00","id":1334550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1334526#post1334526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think people who want photorealistic graphics in every game are a big part of what's wrong with the industry today.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who's asking for photorealism in every game?<br /> <br /> In general, people investing in something that's supposed to be a AAA quality game, want appropriately good graphics. If the creators want to do a stylistic thing? Cool! Plenty of games are popular without photorealism, but they have a strong (often unique and endearing) visual style to them. But half-assing it so the game like it quality photorealism from a decade ago just makes the game look bad and outdated. People want &quot;every&quot; game to have a purposeful visual style, which is not something wrong with the industry.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-08T19:21:50-07:00","id":1334569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackshade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1334519#post1334519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So far the game looks dissapointing to me. The combat is atrocious and the animation dont inspire any confidence. Just compare it to cyberpunk or dying light 2 and it reality falls short. The should postpone it. March 2020 is too early for this game. No way they will polish this game enough before launch. i reality hope i am wrong about all this but it looks to be an average game at best<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Looks like the combat and animation will match well with the original Bloodlines then; which had the same issues, but OOZED personality and atmosphere.<br /> <br /> And it's a classic.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm more concerned with Bloodlines 2's writing and characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-09T12:07:47-07:00","id":1334690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1334526#post1334526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think people who want photorealistic graphics in every game are a big part of what's wrong with the industry today.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think people who can't respect other people's opinion are a big part of what's wrong with society today nevermind any industry.<br /> <br /> Did i even mention graphics? What has graphics to do with anything i said? i said bad combat and animations.But now that you have mentioned it, yeah the graphics aren't that great either.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-09T12:07:47-07:00","id":1334691,"title":"","content":"double post","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-09T12:12:07-07:00","id":1334693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1334569#post1334569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Looks like the combat and animation will match well with the original Bloodlines then; which had the same issues, but OOZED personality and atmosphere.<br /> <br /> And it's a classic.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm more concerned with Bloodlines 2's writing and characters.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So are okay with a 2020 game having the same shitty animations and combat as a 2004 game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-09T13:45:25-07:00","id":1334710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackshade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1334693#post1334693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So are okay with a 2020 game having the same shitty animations and combat as a 2004 game?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I played the absolute hell out of Bloodlines 1, losing count of how many times I finished the story after 10 or so play throughs.<br /> <br /> Animation doesn't have to be AAA perfection, as long as the <a href=\"https://youtu.be/yxH1gG913Og\" target=\"_blank\">story is enjoyable</a> enough to keep me coming back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-09-2019, 04:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-09T17:08:57-07:00","id":1334738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackshade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1334693#post1334693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So are okay with a 2020 game having the same shitty animations and combat as a 2004 game?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Will it have a similar atmosphere, music, and personality Bloodlines had?<br /> <br /> Then yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-10T04:49:18-07:00","id":1334818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackshade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1334519#post1334519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So far the game looks dissapointing to me. The combat is atrocious and the animation dont inspire any confidence. Just compare it to cyberpunk or dying light 2 and it reality falls short. The should postpone it. March 2020 is too early for this game. No way they will polish this game enough before launch. i reality hope i am wrong about all this but it looks to be an average game at best<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Combat is my biggest fear for the game. It looked really, really bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-10T10:37:26-07:00","id":1334886,"title":"","content":"The combat did look awful but, on a more hopeful note, I feel that it speaks well of them to make the &quot;Pioneers&quot; and the Camarilla two separate factions. Usually, you'd expect old money, antiquated, trying to hold on to their power City Founders-type of characters to be tailor made for the Camarilla. That they are leaves me hopeful for the subtlety of the writing and the complexity of the characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-11T13:28:31-07:00","id":1335185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1334818#post1334818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Combat is my biggest fear for the game. It looked really, really bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a understatement. Some of the worst combat i have ever seen. Anybody thinking they are going to fix this before launch is fooling themselves. Can't believe people are buying into 'this is pre alpha gameplay' marketing bullshit.<br /> <br /> Will the end result be better then what we have seen so far? ofcourse, but not by enough to make it any good. We are 6 months from release. We have all seen this many times in the past. If the game looks mediocre this close to release, it will be mediocre by release. This game won't be the exception.<br /> <br /> I am sure vtm hardcore fans will enjoy it, just cause it's a game in their beloved universe but i was just hoping for a game that can compete with the best of the genre in the year 2019/2020 not early 2000s. This universe has so much potential for a great rpg, it's a shame they gave the rights to a mediocre studio like hardsuit labs. I am sorry if i sound harsh but have they ever made a good game?<br /> <br /> But who knows i might be wrong about all this and i get to eat my words. Here is hoping.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-11T13:30:37-07:00","id":1335186,"title":"","content":"I think the combat should be clunky and chaotic because the game should discourage you from trying to go on a killing spree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-11T13:54:37-07:00","id":1335192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1335186#post1335186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the combat should be clunky and chaotic because the game should discourage you from trying to go on a killing spree.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm curious to hear about the different feeding methods, because they mentioned a Light, Full and Lethal feeding.<br /> <br /> Up to now, I thought the demo player was draining people to death in combat, but apparently that's not the case. They're draining them to the point of knocking them unconscious, which has me wondering if this game will allow for other ways to incapacitate enemies, without having to outright kill them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-11T14:03:47-07:00","id":1335193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackshade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1335185#post1335185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a understatement. Some of the worst combat i have ever seen. Anybody thinking they are going to fix this before launch is fooling themselves. Can't believe people are buying into 'this is pre alpha gameplay' marketing bullshit.<br /> <br /> Will the end result be better then what we have seen so far? ofcourse, but not by enough to make it any good. We are 6 months from release. We have all seen this many times in the past. If the game looks mediocre this close to release, it will be mediocre by release. This game won't be the exception.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>If there's anything I've noticed about Paradox, it's that they don't just churn out games and then forget about them. They continue to support it's development for years to come. Games like Crusader Kings and Stellaris are still getting new updates and DLC to this day. And usually, this DLC adds new mechanics, or greatly improves upon the game's original design.<br /> <br /> I'm not naive enough to think this game will be perfect upon release (then again, neither was Bloodlines 1), but looking at the previous work Paradox has been involved in, I'm inclined to believe things will improve over time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-11T14:41:21-07:00","id":1335195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1335193#post1335193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If there's anything I've noticed about Paradox, it's that they don't just churn out games and then forget about them. They continue to support it's development for years to come. Games like Crusader Kings and Stellaris are still getting new updates and DLC to this day. And usually, this DLC adds new mechanics, or greatly improves upon the game's original design.<br /> <br /> I'm not naive enough to think this game will be perfect upon release (then again, neither was Bloodlines 1), but looking at the previous work Paradox has been involved in, I'm inclined to believe things will improve over time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Paradox is just the publisher not the developer unlike the games you mentioned. Hardsuit labs makes the game and they have a shady track record.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-12T02:22:22-07:00","id":1335284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1335186#post1335186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the combat should be clunky and chaotic because the game should discourage you from trying to go on a killing spree.</div> </div> </div> </div>Combat in Pathologic 2 is slow and lethal and discouraging from any battle but ones you are sure you have an advantage in. Combat in Bloodlines 2 just looks badly made.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T11:15:11-07:00","id":1336606,"title":"","content":"Third faction reveal finally, it's the Anarchs!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T14:36:43-07:00","id":1336667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1336606#post1336606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Third faction reveal finally, it's the Anarchs!</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it? They're led by a &quot;Baron&quot;, but it seems more like a business that does dirty work for the other factions (for the time being).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T14:41:38-07:00","id":1336669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1336667#post1336667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it? They're led by a &quot;Baron&quot;, but it seems more like a business that does dirty work for the other factions (for the time being).</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking that myself. The way it reads is that they're a goal-oriented Coterie of mercenaries (definitely in the business and political sense, maybe also the military sense) who will work for whoever's willing to throw cash their way, and the leader is simply appropriating the title of Baron to make it clear that they have power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25611-gilbythefat","name":"GilbyTheFat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25611_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T14:52:18-07:00","id":1336675,"title":"","content":"Crime Lord Ventrue is actually one of the ideas I had for my first attempt at doing an Anarch playthrough. So if this Baron faction is organized like a crime syndicate, that's perfect!<br /> <br /> Now as to the fact that only those on the top of the hierarchy have ever met the guy in person... hmmm, I wonder if a power hungry newcomer to the scene can find some way to take advantage of that? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T14:58:23-07:00","id":1336676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1336675#post1336675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Crime Lord Ventrue is actually one of the ideas I had for my first attempt at doing an Anarch playthrough. So if this Baron faction is organized like a crime syndicate, that's perfect!<br /> <br /> Now as to the fact that only those on the top of the hierarchy have ever met the guy in person... hmmm, I wonder if a power hungry newcomer to the scene can find some way to take advantage of that? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm honestly surprised Masquerade never had a criminal empire of Kindred form as a Sect at some point during the metaplot.<br /> <br /> The identity of the top dog being a mystery to most Kindred in the city? Sounds like the way the Ventrue Directorate are described, with their identities being completely unknown to most even within Clan Ventrue...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25611-gilbythefat","name":"GilbyTheFat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25611_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T15:06:29-07:00","id":1336679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GilbyTheFat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1336676#post1336676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm honestly surprised Masquerade never had a criminal empire of Kindred form as a Sect at some point during the metaplot.<br /> <br /> The identity of the top dog being a mystery to most Kindred in the city? Sounds like the way the Ventrue Directorate are described, with their identities being completely unknown to most even within Clan Ventrue...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well the Giovanni and Followers of Set could more or less fill that role. But I would imagine most vampires wouldn't be interested in running a criminal empire, because organized crime tends to attract government attention, which the vampires are trying their best to avoid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T15:11:13-07:00","id":1336680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1336679#post1336679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well the Giovanni and Followers of Set could more or less fill that role. But I would imagine most vampires wouldn't be interested in running a criminal empire, because organized crime tends to attract government attention, which the vampires are trying their best to avoid.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure there's more than enough Kindred among the Giovanni, the Setites, Ravnos, Assamite Warriors, even enterprising Ventrue Autarkis who would think they're good enough to dodge government attention (even if they later learn they overestimated their talent in such matters).<br /> <br /> I could even see Caitiff who decide to throw in with such an organisation. A lot of crime comes from hardship and the need to cut corners at the expense of the law, and that's a lot of Clanless right there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25611-gilbythefat","name":"GilbyTheFat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25611_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T15:14:43-07:00","id":1336683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GilbyTheFat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1336676#post1336676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm honestly surprised Masquerade never had a criminal empire of Kindred form as a Sect at some point during the metaplot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering what Sects are, forming one around a criminal empire seems... a little on the small side, really. One or several vampires would probably form one, but that seems more like a coterie-size endeavour rather than something you'd actually need hundreds or thousands of vampires for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T15:18:08-07:00","id":1336685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1336683#post1336683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering what Sects are, forming one around a criminal empire seems... a little on the small side, really. One or several vampires would probably form one, but that seems more like a coterie-size endeavour rather than something you'd actually need hundreds or thousands of vampires for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not if you're going for a global conspiracy which aims to monopolise the criminal world and ensure that the multitude of Kindred of other Sects who find themselves relying on the criminal underworld now have to owe them. Especially if you get into the <i>really</i> big guns like unsanctioned war-profiteering that requires a global network to accomplish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25611-gilbythefat","name":"GilbyTheFat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25611_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-19T06:51:21-07:00","id":1336857,"title":"","content":"It requires a global network of humans. Global crime it's a human business, that can be an asset to vampires but not an end in itself. Vampire sects are organized arround vampire business and vampirical ends.<br /> <br /> Such a network would be an asset for anyone, but it's one that all vampires (and other nightfolk) want to have, and thus nobody has it. To put it simply, &quot;the multitude of Kindred of other Sects who find themselves relying on the criminal underworld&quot; aren't going to owe you anything because they're going to infiltrate and manipulate your organizations much like they do right now. Jyhad stile.<br /> Lasombra aren't going to &quot;ask&quot; the Ventrue for their assets in criminal ventures if they need one, they're going to wriggle themselves into these, maybe foster an opposing crime syndicate, because they hate the Ventrue's guts (and if they get in a conflict and end killing the Ventrue owning the circus, all the better). Most likely, this is already happening somewhere in the Jyhad","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 09-19-2019, 09:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-19T17:21:33-07:00","id":1336963,"title":"","content":"The more interviews I read from the creators of the game, the less interested I become. <br /> <br /> If this game does suck(which it very well might), at least I'll always have Bloodlines and Redemption to fall back on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-19T17:29:01-07:00","id":1336967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GilbyTheFat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1336685#post1336685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not if you're going for a global conspiracy which aims to monopolise the criminal world and ensure that the multitude of Kindred of other Sects who find themselves relying on the criminal underworld now have to owe them. Especially if you get into the <i>really</i> big guns like unsanctioned war-profiteering that requires a global network to accomplish.</div> </div> </div> </div>Trying to erect such a monopoly when the Camarilla is dominant in your city without being part of it seems unwise. Trying it against the Sabbat seems suicidal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-19T17:36:10-07:00","id":1336969,"title":"","content":"So the idea that the Baron doesn't actually exist, and in reality, the lieutenants are sharing power among each other has some merit to it for an Anarch movement. But I can't imagine the other members of the faction would be very pleased to hear they're being manipulated like that. I mean, I understand why the system might be considered necessary, for a species as selfish and predatory as vampires have proven themselves to be. But it seems like it goes against what the Anarch movement stands for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-19T23:45:07-07:00","id":1337033,"title":"","content":"Are we sure that The Baron=The Anarchs? They are never mentioned in the Baron page. I think that the Baron is a neutral-faction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 09-20-2019, 02:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-20T04:42:15-07:00","id":1337059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1337033#post1337033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are we sure that The Baron=The Anarchs? They are never mentioned in the Baron page. I think that the Baron is a neutral-faction.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No outright confirmation, I guess. But their faction description seems pretty much in lined with Anarch ideology.<br /> <br /> OFF THE GRID<br /> It\u2019s hard to know just how many vampires swear allegiance to The Baron of Aurora. In parts, that\u2019s because very few of Seattle\u2019s Kindred have actually met him. Acting through his lieutenants, he <b>has taken in the city\u2019s destitute, defiant and desperate</b>, turning them into a ruthlessly disciplined force with hands in every shady deal.<br /> <br /> <b>Where a less prudent man might turn such capital into a bid for Princedom, he has so far been content to stay in the back-alleys of his turf, hoard favors, and brutally defend his business interests.</b><br /> <br /> <br /> So we have a faction leader who's willing to take in everybody's cast offs, and isn't obsessed with taking over the whole city. They have enough power to live comfortably, and uses their resources and connections to maintain that comfortable life style as much as possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-20-2019, 07:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-20T05:26:47-07:00","id":1337067,"title":"","content":"I don't see any ideology there. It sounds like they're exploiting the more vulnerable kindred. Quite Setite in a way. Although, if there are any Setites there and the game is following V5, I could see this as some sort of Anarch long game after more proud, principled, Brujah attempts failed. Not that only a member of the Ministry or any one clan would be capable, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","user":"Spencer from The Hills","date":". 09-20-2019, 08:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-20T05:52:02-07:00","id":1337073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1337067#post1337067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see any ideology there. It sounds like they're exploiting the more vulnerable kindred. Quite Setite in a way. Although, if there are any Setites there and the game is following V5, I could see this as some sort of Anarch long game after more proud, principled, Brujah attempts failed. Not that only a member of the Ministry or any one clan would be capable, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Now that you mention it, the hoarding favors bit does sound pretty Setite. I would love if The Ministry became a future clan DLC. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-20T21:56:41-07:00","id":1337209,"title":"","content":"Its a great way to show the anarchs aren't default good guys. This looks like a sign that BL2 will be less black and white than BL1 where the anarchs were obvious good guys and the Camarilla obvious bad guys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8306-wissenschaft","name":"Wissenschaft","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-22T06:15:36-07:00","id":1337318,"title":"","content":"So, something I didn't notice until like a 5th or 6th look at The Baron faction page, Mr. Ferris Wheel guy is depicted on the background artwork.<br /> <br /> Me thinks this potential crime syndicate may be looking to capitalize on all the 'new blood' that's been introduced? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-22T18:51:43-07:00","id":1337412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1337318#post1337318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Me thinks this potential crime syndicate may be looking to capitalize on all the 'new blood' that's been introduced? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>If they aren't murdering them like Dominic.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-22T20:16:51-07:00","id":1337434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1337412#post1337412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If they aren't murdering them like Dominic.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Maybe &quot;Mr. Stabby&quot; just doesn't like people giving away spoilers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T17:44:22-07:00","id":1339089,"title":"","content":"4th Faction reveal.<br /> <br /> The Newcomers, who seem to be the Tremere, or Pyramid that was alluded to in the demo video.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-09T15:29:47-07:00","id":1340509,"title":"","content":"Final Faction Revealed: The Unseen.<br /> <br /> Disappointed it's not the Sabbat, but this confirms Nosferatu will eventually be made playable. So I can be happy about that.<br /> <br /> It also seems to indicate that most (if not all) of the factions are subsidiaries of the Camarilla as a whole. I'm not completely sure about The Baron, but it seems like both the Pioneers and the Newcomers are working alongside Camarilla interests. At least until they amass enough power to climb out from under their boot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T16:32:38-07:00","id":1341735,"title":"","content":"You know, I was going to make my first Ventrue side with The Baron, as part of &quot;came from nothing&quot; type of background. But now, I think I want to make them side with The Unseen.<br /> <br /> There's just something oddly intriguing about the thought of a Lord dressed in tattered rags and lurking around the slimy underbelly of the city's streets and sewers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T16:53:26-07:00","id":1341739,"title":"","content":"For those who posted concerns that the game couldn't be ready by the original release date, the game's release has been pushed back to later in 2020.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T18:12:11-07:00","id":1341750,"title":"","content":"I'd rather see it delayed than rushed out the door.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T02:01:37-07:00","id":1341817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1341750#post1341750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd rather see it delayed than rushed out the door.</div> </div> </div> </div>But will it be a true Bloodlines successor if it's actually finished at release?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T04:09:22-07:00","id":1341834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1341750#post1341750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd rather see it delayed than rushed out the door.</div> </div> </div> </div>Better it got pushed back to later in the year than get released with a load of flaws and then get buried a month later when Cyberpunk 2077 comes out and takes all the attention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25611-gilbythefat","name":"GilbyTheFat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25611_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T13:18:46-07:00","id":1341931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GilbyTheFat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1341834#post1341834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Better it got pushed back to later in the year than get released with a load of flaws and then get buried a month later when Cyberpunk 2077 comes out and takes all the attention.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes. This. Shout it from the roof-tops. Write this as a guiding philosophy on the wall in letters of fire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T19:02:03-07:00","id":1341987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1341931#post1341931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yes. This. Shout it from the roof-tops. Write this as a guiding philosophy on the wall in letters of fire.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what tone to interpret this as having. Half of my brain is going &quot;see, people get it&quot; and the other half is yelling &quot;OY! MATE! GRPGR IS BEING SARCASTIC!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25611-gilbythefat","name":"GilbyTheFat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25611_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T19:42:39-07:00","id":1341995,"title":"","content":"Okay, so if I understand the situation correctly, all of the playable factions are subsidiaries to The Camarilla itself. They technically fall under its umbrella, but they have their own objectives they're trying to achieve. This would explain why &quot;The Baron&quot; is willing to perform dirty jobs for folks like the Camarilla, and their faction page makes no mention at all of any kind of Anarch movement.<br /> <br /> It could also explain why some factions which we would normally assume to be clan specific are willing to extend their hand to members of other clans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T02:10:51-07:00","id":1342038,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't be too sure about that. After all, there is no longer an umbrella - the Camarilla has massively pulled back from its &quot;everyone is part of us&quot; approach and now only contains the people they think are valuable. Everyone else is technically an Anarch, even though they do business with and get bullied by the Camarilla.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T04:26:50-07:00","id":1342052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1342038#post1342038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't be too sure about that. After all, there is no longer an umbrella - the Camarilla has massively pulled back from its &quot;everyone is part of us&quot; approach and now only contains the people they think are valuable. Everyone else is technically an Anarch, even though they do business with and get bullied by the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What I mean to say is that they are sub-factions within the organization itself. They may technically be considered members of the Camarilla, but their ultimate goals lie elsewhere outside of Cross' plans.<br /> <br /> After all, it seems very strange for the Camarilla to hand any degree of territory over to the Anarchs, now that they've officially declared themselves split from the sect. And once again, The Baron's page makes no reference to the Anarchs at all. They come across more as a mercenary crime syndicate, than a bunch of rebels fighting for freedom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-18-2019, 07:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T05:02:55-07:00","id":1342056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1342052#post1342052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I mean to say is that they are sub-factions within the organization itself. <b>They may technically be considered members of the Camarilla</b>, but their ultimate goals lie elsewhere outside of Cross' plans.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they most likely aren't. Again: The new Camarilla are the 1%. Everyone else is not part of the ivory tower, even though many of them still won't be able to ignore a Prince's decrees. Compared to pre-V5, it's basically reversed:<br /> Previously, everyone was (nominally) part of the Cam, including many members who just wanted to be left alone. Declaring yourself an Anarch was a political statement that conveyed your rejection of the system.<br /> Now, being part of the Camarilla means being special - it means the Prince thinks you're worth the danger of staying in contact with in times of the Second Inquisition. If you're not worth that, you're nominally an Anarch, which means the faction called Anarchs contains quite a few people who aren't interested in actual Anarch beliefs and would rather be part of the Camarilla again if they could.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T09:05:22-07:00","id":1342090,"title":"","content":"My impression of the Camarilla in this game is that they're exclusive, but they impose their authority over everyone else too. And as described in their paragraph on the website, &quot;The Long Game&quot;, they do so in such a way that benefits most outsiders enough to deter revolution. A bit like Invictus. The other factions don't necessarily accept it because they like it, but because they don't have the resources or strategy to do anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T05:47:36-07:00","id":1343752,"title":"","content":"Thank god, it got postponed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T10:59:43-07:00","id":1343810,"title":"","content":"So maybe you can clarify something for me cause there are some red flags for me in there, from what ive seen and read from interviews:<br /> <br /> From all i have seen so far, bloodlines 2 wont connect in any way to bloodlines 1. Different city, different storyline, different characters...why even name it bloodlines 2 if it has nothing to do with bloodlines 1?<br /> To be fair i found bloodlines 1 already was ill named as the game has nothing to do with bloodlines. A better name could have been &quot;Blood of Caine&quot;<br /> <br /> Also bloodlines 2 choosing your own pronouns? Meh...you know in general...sure why not. Not a big issue in most games but vampires? Can you imagine any prince going with this? Imagine a fledlling walking up tp the prince and demanding to be called &quot;ze zer zers&quot;<br /> I see a pile of ash right there. I simply cant imagine any vampire giving a shit....you know the guys who are so traditional they dont get computers? they sure as hell wont fly with self made pronouns. Again in general - why not. But in an RPG with a vampire / medieval / antiquity setting? sorry immersion breaking.<br /> <br /> Similiar starting as thin blood and gaining a clan? No. Starting as mortal sounds a nice approach as did the Vampire:Redemption. Then becoming a ghoul and then a vampire? i think thats cool but would be a huge scale thing im not sure they would take the time to develop properly.<br /> Also NWoD is a fail to me. personal preference sure but i greatly prefer Owod<br /> <br /> Other than that bloodlines 2 looks like a fun game, just that almost no one in the team was involved with the first one either making this look like a cash grab and i fear it wont be near the genius of the first","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","name":"Orkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T11:20:24-07:00","id":1343816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orkar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1343810#post1343810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So maybe you can clarify something for me cause there are some red flags for me in there, from what ive seen and read from interviews:<br /> <br /> From all i have seen so far, bloodlines 2 wont connect in any way to bloodlines 1. Different city, different storyline, different characters...why even name it bloodlines 2 if it has nothing to do with bloodlines 1?<br /> To be fair i found bloodlines 1 already was ill named as the game has nothing to do with bloodlines. A better name could have been &quot;Blood of Caine&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The game will take place in the same universe (as in: you might find references to BL1 characters and events here or there). Other than that, it will aim to replicate the feeling of Bloodlines 1 - which makes it the best a successor can do considering the multiple endings of the first game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orkar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1343810#post1343810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also bloodlines 2 choosing your own pronouns? Meh...you know in general...sure why not. Not a big issue in most games but vampires? Can you imagine any prince going with this? Imagine a fledlling walking up tp the prince and demanding to be called &quot;ze zer zers&quot;<br /> I see a pile of ash right there. I simply cant imagine any vampire giving a shit....you know the guys who are so traditional they dont get computers? they sure as hell wont fly with self made pronouns. Again in general - why not. But in an RPG with a vampire / medieval / antiquity setting? sorry immersion breaking.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the pronouns will go beyond he/she/they. And singular they has first been used in the 14th century, meaing it predates most American Princes. Other than that: Go on, try and call Sasha Vykos by a pronoun they don't want to be called. I'm sure that will turn out well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orkar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1343810#post1343810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Similiar starting as thin blood and gaining a clan? No. Starting as mortal sounds a nice approach as did the Vampire:Redemption. Then becoming a ghoul and then a vampire? i think thats cool but would be a huge scale thing im not sure they would take the time to develop properly.<br /> Also NWoD is a fail to me. personal preference sure but i greatly prefer Owod</div> </div> </div> </div>The game is not set in the nWoD. Also, according to 5th edition rules, Thinbloods can canonically gain a clan by diablerizing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orkar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1343810#post1343810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other than that bloodlines 2 looks like a fun game, just that almost no one in the team was involved with the first one either making this look like a cash grab and i fear it wont be near the genius of the first</div> </div> </div> </div>If the genius of the first comes from its writing, I'd say Brian Mitsoda being onboard is a pretty good sign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3118,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","user":"Cifer","date":". 10-26-2019, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T11:35:33-07:00","id":1343819,"title":"","content":"You do get my hopes up...i still worry but you know if its a good game im all on board and im glad they postponed. still i relaly hope the writing will be great and care first about the lore and not twitter mobs. And they...not sure about old english but wasnt it only used in direct dialogue like your majesties? not sure it was used in third person like &quot;their majesties want&quot; afaik its always been &quot;his majesty&quot; or &quot;her majesty&quot; not firm in old english. <br /> but anyway we wont deal with vampirs that old mostly i guess and its something different if a fledgeling wants to be called they. If ypu are old an dpowerfull enough you can be called whatever you like but a new vampire gts to kiss asses and not demand special treatment","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","name":"Orkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T12:45:42-07:00","id":1343835,"title":"","content":"Asking to be called by you appropriate pronouns is not &quot;special treatment&quot; and it takes a pretty unsettling perspective to consider it such.<br /> <br /> The fact that you consider it something worthy of being killed over is extremely distressing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T12:59:41-07:00","id":1343841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1343835#post1343835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that you consider it something worthy of being killed over is extremely distressing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're taking that one a biiiiit far out of context here, implying that's their RL attitude. There are many thing not worth getting killed over in RL that in Vampire tend to mean you're either dead or bound to get quite negative consequences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 10-26-2019, 04:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T13:14:15-07:00","id":1343845,"title":"","content":"Eh, I think you're making a bigger deal out of pronouns than they really are. I mean, a Prince doesn't have much obligation to remember a neonate's <i>name</i> either, but somehow, they often manage (and many modern names did not exist in medieval times either!). Compared to the eccentricities that dealing with many Malkavians requires, remembering one out of three words doesn't seem particularly hard.<br /> <br /> As for &quot;twitter mobs&quot;, remember that Vampire has always been among the first. When GenCon was a massive sausage fest, the vampire booth had female fans clustered around it. When D&amp;D was completely heteronormative, Vampire had gay, lesbian and bisexual NPCs. When dressing in women's clothes was something other RPGs only ever contained for comedic purposes, Vampire had several transgender NPCs in the clan books. The representation was often clumsy by today's standards, but if you're complaining that Vampire goes outside of the bounds of heteronormativity, you may be between 20 and 30 years too late.<br /> A video game decoupling the choice of gender from the choice of body shape is really... such a small change that I can't quite fathom how many people are up in arms against it. But it means the world to some people who feel that games see them and their lives now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T13:17:24-07:00","id":1343846,"title":"","content":"Singling out pronouns as worthy of comment is bizarre, and linking it to threats to one's life or unlife stands out as a questionable thing to say. All the more so given disproportionately high rates of violence directed at transgender people in the US compared to literally any other identifiable demographic group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T13:36:50-07:00","id":1343852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1343835#post1343835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Asking to be called by you appropriate pronouns is not &quot;special treatment&quot; and it takes a pretty unsettling perspective to consider it such.<br /> <br /> The fact that you consider it something worthy of being killed over is extremely distressing.</div> </div> </div> </div>in the appropriate vampie prince setting. Similiar example - i got absolutely no issues with people being openly gay IRL i have gay friends and tried homosexual sex once. BUT if a game set in medieval europe would have openly gay couples its immersion breaking cause that didnt happen in that context. Were there gay people in medieval europe? sure. But the moment they were found out they got killed. well except scandinavia for the most part.<br /> <br /> I cant see a prince who stems from say 1500 turkey were women were literal slaves, gays were killed on spot and trans wasnt even an idea in existance seeing a fledgling who wants to be called &quot;she her hers&quot; despite definitely looking male, not taking a huge issue. well maybe except the fledgling is malkavian or nosferatu and so deformed you seriously cant tell. otherwise any prince embrased prior to 2000 - meaning every single one - will at best be confused at worst disgusted. vampirs post 2000 may indeed be much more in favor of that but this stuff isnt even yet implemented in mortal society what makes you thionk vampirs, who change much slower, will use it?<br /> <br /> As example - i never took issue with ampire society at large though you might say its ectraordinarely progressive with females ahving the same rights millennia before mortals had that idea but it wasnt born out pf progressive vampire movements its simply - you got power, you get to decide stuff and since sex is of no concern in terms of disciplines, bridging biological gaps - perfect. you get homosexual vampirs - sure why not as pre monotheistic cultures were acceptuing of this and it just stuck through the christian / muslim period. the world changed vampires didnt. the pronoun thing is to my knowledge a totally new thing and i dont see vampires adapting to that before mortals do.<br /> <br /> And since it seems of importance i might add that im personally queer so...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","name":"Orkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T14:07:32-07:00","id":1343861,"title":"","content":"History is a lot more colourful than most history books lead one to believe. For example, take the whole &quot;openly gay&quot; thing. Ever heard of <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6QaBYLAOaSY\" target=\"_blank\">Julie d'Aubigny</a> (who should really be considered patron saint of chaotic neutral bards everywhere)?<br /> <br /> Neopronouns are just that - new. But the idea of shifting gender isn't. There were several societies where people could in certain instances change the gender they were seen as by the public. There were biologically female pharaohs who declared themselves male. There were ruling queens who used the male title &quot;rex&quot; rather than &quot;regina&quot; because the latter mostly meant &quot;wife of a king&quot;. Vampires should understand that better than most - after all, there are lots and lots of female Princes rather than Princesses.<br /> In the end, every &quot;always&quot; and &quot;never&quot; in the annals of history has so many asterisks after it that one can easily justify quite a bit if one only wants to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T15:04:02-07:00","id":1343870,"title":"","content":"The whole problem can be boiled to a rather simple issue: VtM wants dramatic anachronisms out of its elders, and then didn't put in the work to give them verisimilitude.<br /> <br /> So what they care and don't care about doesn't really follow any logic... which means they tend to get weird about stuff that can get very off-putting.<br /> <br /> The problem is that a vampire that's survived 500 years has had to adapt to a huge amount of changes to human culture. That vampire's probably had to re-learn the language they spoke while alive at least three or four times if they want to understand what modern humans are saying. Adapting is effectively a necessity to maintaining power, so even if an older vampire might not get or care about a new cultural trend, they've had to deal with changing cultural trends for centuries. Killing neonates over such matters is just a good way to portray that you're weak, reactionary, and too out of touch to avoid getting overthrown.<br /> <br /> So when you say, &quot;oh a vampire from back in the day would kill young vampires for.... being young vampires used to modern norms,&quot; it's always going to feel weird; at best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T23:18:23-07:00","id":1343927,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Heavy Arms;n1343870]The problem is that a vampire that's survived 500 years has had to adapt to a huge amount of changes to human culture./QUOTE]<br /> Not neccesarily. First the language. language changes very gradually. We now speak a different englsih than 100 years ago but you can still understand your grandparents. You can still read and unerstand shakespear even though that english is drasticly different. You actually have good chances of understanding english from 1300 AD at least in written form. And the changes happen ever so slightly that it snot too hard to keep track so no you dont have to relearn a language and you got centuries to keep up before you cant understand people anymore. Also this very point is often totally ignored when dealing with very old vampires awaking from torpor which can be argued that with the correct Auspex power you either cna learn while in torpor or indeed directly communicate thoughts and the other understands in his own language.<br /> <br /> Cultural norms in Kainite society barely change, and elder kainites tend to be very withdrawn from mortal society to begin with so you can get away with not adapting perfectly. Also its not like mortals wouldnt have walking anachronisms and people who cant adapt to new cultural norms. Or just dont want to.<br /> Also there is always cultures that see it different. Lets take the gay example - by far most people on the glbe still think being gay is a monstrousity, a perverse abnormality. Leave the US and western europe behind and having an issue with gay people is perfectly fine, heck in some areas you can legally kill gay people. Now for vampires - elders can have any cultural background and are supposed to be anachronistic. they quickly learned as fledgelings when adapting was far easier, that in vampire society you have to accept kainite rules, go on and thell the Drakon being gay is sick. dare. But that was for over millenia the dominant position among mortls. Vampires didnt adapt to that did they? Vampires didnt strip female kainites of their rights just because christians and muslims did. They upheld THEIR rules cause kainites are difficult to change in special for mortal pressures. This is a major reason why neonates are still embraced . to help an out of touch clan keeping up. Its not the elders learning how to use computers, they embrace fledgelings who have that knowledge.<br /> <br /> So one of these cherished rules is - elders rule the young. The young are expendable. Fledglings who misbehave can be killed by their sires at their whim. <br /> Vampires are evil predators who stopped being human. If you kill humans for nourishment and have the beast in you i kinda doubt your compassion levels are high. Huting someones feelings is of no concern, heck most elders dont even have human feelings anymore.<br /> Speaking up to a prince is a bold move that can cost someone his unlife. We see in bloodlines 1 that you are supposed to be put down for merely existing. They hunt thin bloods for sport. What do you imagine they do with a neonate who demands to be called certain pronouns? Only malkavians can get away with it as it will be seen as part of their derangement. And a hidiously disfigured nosferatu may be asked if hes male or female. And yes i highly doubt vampires would be aware of social gender. You could become a thing like Yorak and be called it though.<br /> <br /> So yes sure i get that WoD was always very progressive - and where it fits im all for it like femape empowerement among kainites or mages, absolutely. Pronouns? i gotta scratch my head i dont see that fitting indeed it seems out of place and immersion breaking. Remember warhorse studios kingdome come deliverance outrage that there aint enough black people in it? yeah cause medieval bohemia of 1400 hasnt seen black people, the best you could get were the moors who would pass as italian if you gie them italian wardrobes instead of their traditional garb they are basicly white and even they were rare. Im all for diversity where it fits but not at the cost of immersion. You want to amke a game with choosable pronouns? perfect, it would actually imrpove scifi games in a setting in the future or fantasy games with new worlds where this is just a thing. But i take issue with putting these things where they are out of place<br /> <br /> Cifer said history was more colorfull and yes being a history buff i agree hence i said being homosexual in medieval europe worked in pre christian scandinavia. it worked perfectly fine in pre christian europe. But wherever christianity was you had a really hard time being gay. Lesbian is different as that was never stated to be a problem in the bible. Just like masturbation for men was seen as evil but not for women cause they cant &quot;waste seed&quot;<br /> But history, while there always will be some exception, still has cultural norms and going against those meant a lot of hardship, trouble, possibly death. Did such people exist? sure but it was hell for them. You want to depict an openly gay guy in medieval bohemia...sure but be prepared it wont be politicly correct, if he lives he will be mocked and shunned.<br /> <br /> To end this point - in our modern progessive left wing world we still have a majority of the population taking an issue with chosen pronouns and most people think its stupid. I experience first hand how civilised caring humans tell me such pronouns are stupid. So if even the majority of modern day WESTERN humans - lets jsut ignore the vast majority of the world spopulation - doesnt accept chosen pronouns...what makes you think vampires will who are stuck in a century old mindset?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","name":"Orkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T00:08:12-07:00","id":1343930,"title":"","content":"Why are you so invested in being against something that affects you not at all and makes the game more enjoyable for others? It literally will not impact your playthrough unless you want it to.<br /> <br /> Have you even played the first game? For all your &quot;elders are out of date and don't use computers,&quot; you seem to have forgotten that the Prince in Bloodlines 1 emails you personally on multiple occasions, and you are never killed for talking back to him. And this was in the early 2000s, when personal computers were far less ubiquitous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T02:50:30-07:00","id":1343945,"title":"","content":"I played Redemption - kinda the first game, and bloodlines, yes. First we dont know for sure if Lacroix personally writes and sends those emails or has some neonate doing it for him dictating the text. Second, Lacroix, and Strauss for that matter, are both pretty young for &quot;elders&quot; barely 3 centuries, Strauss even complains about Lacroix being way too young for a prince.<br /> <br /> When we speak about age we might wanna clarify. You are usually considered an Ancillae until 200-300 years of age, roughly. And for Kainites it seems the odler you get the harder it is for you to keep up with changes, giving elder vampires usually a very anachronistic touch - and they are indeed very out of touch. Meanwhile some very human failures just transmorph in kindred society - you may say racism is basicly non existant among kindred as even former slave owners trat black vampires with respect but at the same time clans are grossly stereotyped and all the racism just transferred from skin color to blood in your veins.<br /> Also i dunno about the US but the computers depicted in the game remind more of early to late 80s and in the 2000s i dont know anyone who didnt have a working PC with windows 98+<br /> I mean the ingame consoles run on Dos...<br /> <br /> why am i ivested...cause its a troubling sign of putting inclusivity above story. That happened a lot int he media of the alst years. Gjostbusters 2016, Captain Marvel, Star Trek Discovery, Mass Effect 4, The new Wolfenstein, battlefield 5, Disney Star Wars - it was one desaster after the other because inclusion was more important than story, character development, canon / lore or historical accuracy. and i have fears that this might seep into bloodlines as well. Lazy writers thinking being gay, female or black IS a storyarch and development<br /> If the prince or elders are into PC culture my immersion is done. Its a game about monstrous bloody killers with no conscience loosing their humanity. if anyone is not PC its vampires. Werewolfs? Mages? Heck sure why not but Kindred? See next, Baali stop torturing people when they say they dont like it?<br /> If you play a prince sure everyone will kiss your ass and use whatever pronoun you want. But when im playing a fledgeling / thinblood i expect to be treated like shit and abused and definitely my wellbeing wont be a concern of anyone else. Played the first game? if you didnt suck up to Lacroix there was trouble and if it werent for Nines intervention - who is very young - Lacroix would have killed you without a second thought just because you exist","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4364,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","user":"Orkar","date":". 10-27-2019, 05:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","name":"Orkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T03:23:15-07:00","id":1343948,"title":"","content":"First, American age systems work differently than European ones. Since the average age of Kindred in the US is lower, elder status can be attained much earlier than in Europe - after all, there are no &quot;real&quot; elders around to laugh at you.<br /> <br /> Second, again, I feel like you're overthinking the whole pronoun thing. Yes, the Prince won't particularly care who you are. Funnily enough, they'll usually remember your name, your sire, your clan, your boons and your domain. But then one out of three words is too much?<br /> <br /> As for the &quot;disasters&quot;, about half of those were among my favorite movies/games in the last years (plus, had quite a bit of success at the box office), so... maybe they just were not for your tastes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T03:57:36-07:00","id":1343952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1343948#post1343948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for the &quot;disasters&quot;, about half of those were among my favorite movies/games in the last years (plus, had quite a bit of success at the box office), so... maybe they just were not for your tastes?</div> </div> </div> </div>All of these started out strong cause everyone wanted more star wars, star trek, ghostbusters, battlefield, mass effect etc. Sure it was npstalgia and hope. Then when people realised the new stuff was total shit sales declined drasticly. Disney is severly struggling with new Star Wars and actually loosing money. Captain Marvel 2 is cancelled and her character wont appear int he next step of Marvel. The captain amrvel comics sell abysmally, you see star wars toys not being bought and Hasbro cancelled their cooperation with disney.<br /> Mass Effect 4 is hated by most fans and killed the franchise, same for Wolfenstein. Discovery struggles since season 2 and is loosing money, no one wants to buy rights to it either. Id call that failures.<br /> <br /> And i could give you examples of horrible writing with each. Example from discovery - sonar in space? Shooting stars in space? did the writers finish high school? I mean Mauler needed 6 hours speaking time just listing the plot holes in a 2 hour star wars movie.<br /> <br /> You can still like all of these examples but by all means we can objectively look at they are bad. And they are bad because they arent storydriven but agenda driven. Old Star Trek had black, female and even gay characters and fans loved it cause it was well written and thec haracters were natural not all about their sexuality. And shitting on lore is where i quit - first black action hero....and nobody remembers wesley snipes? Aka Blade? First female captain....yeah that was janeway....and so on. Just ignoring what happened to spin a not true narrative.<br /> And Battlefield 5 took actual history and rewrote it to fit a narrative rather than showing what actually happened or highlight the characters of color or females who actually achieved great things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","name":"Orkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T04:14:57-07:00","id":1343955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orkar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1343945#post1343945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First we dont know for sure if Lacroix personally writes and sends those emails or has some neonate doing it for him dictating the text.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does it really matter? The point is that vampires adapt more than they hold on to mortal hang ups. LaCroix doesn't have fledglings or neonates killed for corresponding with him via email instead of sending formal handwritten letters using a quill and parchment. LaCroix also understands that killing fresh vampires is a bad look for a Prince that's already in a weak position with vampires that don't like that sort of heavy handed use of the Traditions, so he uses his &quot;mercy&quot; to try to get the player character killed in suicide missions so he doesn't have to worry about Nines starting a revolt against him. In other words, LaCroix is a demonstration that vampires adapt to cultural norms when it's in their best interests, instead of treating anything that might requires them to change a little as a death-sentence level insult.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Second, Lacroix, and Strauss for that matter, are both pretty young for &quot;elders&quot; barely 3 centuries, Strauss even complains about Lacroix being way too young for a prince. </div> </div> </div>We don't actually have any idea how old Strauss is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And for Kainites it seems the odler you get the harder it is for you to keep up with changes, giving elder vampires usually a very anachronistic touch - and they are indeed very out of touch. </div> </div> </div>Again though, this is completely slapdash in application. Smiling Jack is, officially, over 400 years old. What does he do in any book or other media that really betrays that age? He's generally presented as easily passing for a much younger vampire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> why am i ivested...cause its a troubling sign of putting inclusivity above story. </div> </div> </div>No, it really isn't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That happened a lot int he media of the alst years. Gjostbusters 2016, Captain Marvel, Star Trek Discovery, Mass Effect 4, The new Wolfenstein, battlefield 5, Disney Star Wars - it was one desaster after the other because inclusion was more important than story, character development, canon / lore or historical accuracy. and i have fears that this might seep into bloodlines as well. </div> </div> </div>Fuck no not this again.<br /> <br /> Ghostbusters 2016? Not a great movie, but there's more than ample evidence that it would have done fine as a decent movie if not for an active attempt to review bomb it. People that actually saw the movie generally gave it positive reviews.<br /> <br /> Captain Marvel grossed over $1.1 billion in ticket sales alone... so... what disaster exactly?<br /> <br /> Discovery is hard to give too many metrics on because it's CBS All Access, so it's an inherently more limited audience, but the reviews have largely been positive, and it got picked up for a third season so... no sign of it failing at being a TV show any time soon.<br /> <br /> Mass Effect Andromeda was a meh, not a disaster, mostly because it was boring not because of being too inclusive (ME is a pretty inclusive franchise before that).<br /> <br /> Wolfenstein: Youngblood (I have to assume you're talking about this here) did poorly because, like ME: Andromeda, it just wasn't an interesting story. It's not because it has female protagonists shoved in your face.<br /> <br /> Battlefield 5 was a bad game, and trying to blame it on inclusivity is silly. Also... women service in combat in WWII... complaining about historical accuracy in BF 5 on that ground is absurd given some of the other content such as weapons that hadn't been invented yet being in there.<br /> <br /> Disney Star Wars? Despite all the Internet hate is doing just fine. The only significant failure for them so far is... Solo... the one where they go back to focusing on a white guy. So far the new trilogy and Rogue One have done well both financially and critically.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, calling this a list of disasters is just grossly misrepresenting reality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lazy writers thinking being gay, female or black IS a storyarch and development </div> </div> </div>Treating old vampires and anachronistic when it comes to punishing minorities but having them adapt to other aspects of modern life with ease is worse than lazy writing.<br /> <br /> But yes, tokenism is bad. That's why we want great diversity of creators rather than just actors and visuals in video games... because that's how we get more real representation instead of token characters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the prince or elders are into PC culture my immersion is done. </div> </div> </div>Define &quot;PC culture&quot; in a meaningful fashion that's doesn't make it at least 50 years old for Elders to have started to adapt to; and possibly some (esp. Brujah or minority-in-life) vampires to start deciding they like.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Its a game about monstrous bloody killers with no conscience loosing their humanity. </div> </div> </div>It's also a game about vampires that have to <b>blend in with humans</b> in order to feed from them. That means... keeping up with human culture.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But when im playing a fledgeling / thinblood i expect to be treated like shit and abused and definitely my wellbeing wont be a concern of anyone else. </div> </div> </div>That really has nothing to do with pronouns or inclusivity. Fledglings are literally considered children in vampire society and have the rights of children in human society; though this means they're largely off-limits because you have to go through their sire first like parent in mortal society. Thin-bloods have even less rights and if &quot;they asked me to use new fangled pronouns&quot; is what gets them killed... it's a pretty strange situation or they were going to get killed anyway and that was just an excuse (and not one that needs to be included in BL2 for any sane reason).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> if you didnt suck up to Lacroix there was trouble and if it werent for Nines intervention - who is very young - Lacroix would have killed you without a second thought just because you exist </div> </div> </div>Not sucking up to LaCroix mostly results in him Dominating you.<br /> <br /> And LaCroix had the right to kill you being your Embrace was illegal. Not because fledgkings are inherently subject to execution by the Prince on a whim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T04:43:40-07:00","id":1343959,"title":"","content":"Oh fuck the &quot;zombie-argument&quot; about Disney all over again<br /> <br /> <br /> I'll quote myself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1326644#post1326644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Ehm... sorry but do you know what you are talking about?<br /> <br /> <br /> Star Wars the new Trilogy is one of the biggest commercial hit Disney ever had,<br /> <br /> <br /> The Last Jedi made 1.3 billions at the box office<br /> And The Force Awakens 2 billions.<br /> <br /> <br /> while<br /> <br /> The Phantom Menace 1 billion<br /> The Attack of the Clones made 650 millions<br /> Revenge of the Sith made 850 millions<br /> <br /> <br /> Which means that with only 2 films out they almost surpassed the whole second trilogy.<br /> <br /> The Force Awakens isthe biggest hit in the star wars story, and The Last Jedi is the second one.<br /> <br /> <br /> If you take in account the revenue produced by the 4 star wars film we had since the start of the new trilogy (Force Awakens, Rogue One, Solo and Last Jedi) you have a marvelous revenue of 4.8 billions of dollars (4 film) compared to the 4.3 billions generated by every film since a New Hope to the Revenge of the Sith , which means that Disney has made in 4 years more profit than Lucas did in 28.<br /> <br /> Average revenue for the Disney era films is 1.2 billions, against the 843 millions for the second trilogy and the 630 per film of the original trilogy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Captain Marvel's movie made 1.12 billions at the box office and is currently the second highest grossing film of the year, and the 9th Marvel movie by revenue (oh and the 5th is the &quot;woke&quot; Black Panther)<br /> <br /> Only the 4 Avengers movie, Black Panther, Civil War and Iron Man 3 made more money than Captain Marvel.<br /> Captain Marvel made more money than Iron Man 1 and two combined, or Thor 1 and 2 combined and so on.<br /> <br /> Taking in account every Disney film since ever, Captain Marvel is the 13 highest grossin film in Disney's history, and Black Panther is the 5th.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Disney has been a colossus on the rise since EVER, and it has never &quot;gone broke&quot;.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i0.wp.com/disneynews.us/wp-content/uploads/2016/10/Disney-Annual-Income-in-billions-1.png?resize=641%2C371&amp;ssl=1\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Disney's profits are rising steadily since 2009<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As for Andromeda? A bugfest rushed during development with such great technical issues it became a meme. Andromeda didn't went down because it was &quot;woke&quot;, it went down because bioware has died of starvation and deadlines.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Get out from 4chan, that's not the real world, and buy the Financial Times, the Economist or some serious shit.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 10-27-2019, 07:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T04:56:31-07:00","id":1343960,"title":"","content":"Yes and you totally fail to take into account the whys. Like movies finally shown in china - which adds 200-300 million.<br /> The production cost - if you spend 500 Million on the movie and advertising making 400 Million is still a loss. Meanwhile Joker only cost 50M to make and made 750M so far being much more profitable than any disney or marvel movie in this decade (yes including dead pool)<br /> Inflation - might be ignored in a 20 year scale but does play a part as does general wealth growth. More people have money to spend on movies, more will<br /> <br /> It does NOT take into account abysmal merchandise sales or Hasbro quitting cooperation with Disney. While the movies sound like making a lot of money, the real wealth comes from merchandise and that is plummeting.<br /> <br /> Also you dont take into account that ofc those movies sold well in cinema because there was huge pre existing hype. Many went to see Captain Marvel cause it was said you NEED to see this if you want to get avengers endgame.<br /> <br /> Disney themselves openly stated that Johnsins Movie was a total failure. And now they panic over the new one and are still doing reshoots cause test audiences hated it. And that has a LOT to do with Rey being a Mary Sue par excelance.<br /> <br /> Ghostbusters was hated cause it took a huge dump on what came before, and cause it was terribly acted and written. Same can be said for Discovery which takes a huge dump on all canon lore before it and Michael being totally unlikable. Solo was also hated for bad writing, including redoing the entire millenium falcon lore and making Lando being pansexual. Not that i would care what his sexuality is but why do we need to know that? Original star wars never told us if Palpatine is gay or vader trans or if chewie is really justa a furry.<br /> if you want to depict that give it meaning. or just dont mention it.<br /> <br /> Also im not saying you cant have female, gay, lesbian, black or wahtever protagonists and make something great. Look at broke back mountain. The issue is tokenism and carying more about outrage than acutally writing a compelling story. <br /> <br /> Also the same people who get blamed to downvote certain movies are often the same that totally loved Lara Croft, Captain janeway, Xena or Storm. Or blade. Almost no one dislikes those new things because of gender or race but because of shitty writing that seems to correlate with a mindset of &quot;we got a black lesbian in the game thats enough who needs writing when we got representation&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4364,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","user":"Orkar","date":". 10-27-2019, 08:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","name":"Orkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T04:58:13-07:00","id":1343961,"title":"","content":"Pal you don't really know what you are talking about.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orkar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1343952#post1343952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All of these started out strong cause everyone wanted more star wars, star trek, ghostbusters, battlefield, mass effect etc. Sure it was npstalgia and hope. Then when people realised the new stuff was total shit sales declined drasticly.<br /> <br /> <br /> Disney is severly struggling with new Star Wars and actually loosing money.</div> </div> </div> </div>No it is not, it's making profit out of it since 2018.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://screenrant.com/disney-star-wars-revenue-profit-box-office/\" target=\"_blank\">https://screenrant.com/disney-star-w...it-box-office/</a><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#4D4D4D\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Six years after Disney purchased Lucasfilm to bring back the </span></span></span><a href=\"https://screenrant.com/tag/star-wars/\" target=\"_blank\"><b><i>Star Wars</i></b></a><span style=\"color:#4D4D4D\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"> franchise, the Mouse House has already turned a profit on their $4 billion investment.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#4D4D4D\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>According to </b></span></span></span><b><a href=\"https://www.cnbc.com/2018/10/30/six-years-after-buying-lucasfilm-disney-has-recouped-its-investment.html\" target=\"_blank\"><i>CNBC</i></a><span style=\"color:#4D4D4D\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">, </span></span></span><i>Star Wars</i></b><span style=\"color:#4D4D4D\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b> is an immensely profitable asset for Disney. I</b>n addition to the box office gross (which exceeds the Lucasfilm sales price on its own), there's also been a considerable amount of revenue generated by other sources - like home media sales. </span></span></span><i>Star Wars</i><span style=\"color:#4D4D4D\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"> also remains a merchandising giant with plenty of toys and tie-in materials for each film release. No exact profit margin was provided, but comScore analyst Paul Dergarabedian says Disney has </span></span></span><i>&quot;more than made back&quot;</i><span style=\"color:#4D4D4D\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"> their initial $4 billion.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Captain Marvel 2 is cancelled and her character wont appear int he next step of Marvel. </div> </div> </div>No it is not, this is just a fake news<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.inverse.com/article/59497-captain-marvel-2-brie-larson-rumor-overlord-dvd-dicktor-von-doomcock\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.inverse.com/article/5949...r-von-doomcock</a><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#F6C200\"><span style=\"font-family:Oswald\"><span style=\"font-size:54px\">A</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">nasty rumor about Brie Larson and the future of Captain Marvel in the Marvel Cinematic Universe began circulating over the weekend claiming Disney has lost confidence in the actress and </span></span></span><a href=\"https://www.inverse.com/article/53945-captain-marvel-2-release-date-plot-brie-larson\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Captain Marvel 2</i></a><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"> is in jeopardy. But these unconfirmed reports feel like a fabrication by what we might as well call the white nationalist fringe of the entertainment news industry.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://screenrant.com/captain-marvel-movie-future-mcu-phase-4/\" target=\"_blank\">https://screenrant.com/captain-marve...e-mcu-phase-4/</a><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#4D4D4D\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">The success of </span></span></span><i>Captain Marvel</i><span style=\"color:#4D4D4D\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"> makes a sequel seem inevitable, <b>so it wasn't a shock when </b></span></span></span><b><a href=\"https://screenrant.com/captain-marvel-2-movie-confirmed-marvel/\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Captain Marvel 2</i> was confirmed to be in development</a></b><span style=\"color:#4D4D4D\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b> at San Diego Comic-Con 2019</b>. It's not expected to be part of Phase 4, and </span></span></span><a href=\"https://screenrant.com/marvel-phase-5-movies-mcu-secret-announcement-sdcc/\" target=\"_blank\">may fit into Phase 5</a><span style=\"color:#4D4D4D\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"> instead. No date has been officially announced, and the cast (aside from Brie Larson) is a mystery. Even Larson herself isn't sure </span></span></span><a href=\"https://screenrant.com/captain-marvel-2-filming-update-brie-larson/\" target=\"_blank\">when <i>Captain Marvel 2</i> will go into production</a><span style=\"color:#4D4D4D\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">. The earliest it can hit theaters is 2022, as Marvel still has three movies coming out that year. One is </span></span></span><i>Black Panther 2</i><span style=\"color:#4D4D4D\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">, which is set for a May release; two unrevealed movies are scheduled for February and July. Other than </span></span></span><i>Captain Marvel 2</i><span style=\"color:#4D4D4D\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">, candidates for these slots are </span></span></span><a href=\"https://screenrant.com/tag/guardians-of-the-galaxy-3/\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 3</i></a><span style=\"color:#4D4D4D\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">, </span></span></span><i>Blade</i><span style=\"color:#4D4D4D\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">, and </span></span></span><a href=\"https://screenrant.com/tag/fantastic-four/\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Fantastic Four</i></a><span style=\"color:#4D4D4D\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 10-27-2019, 08:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T05:03:48-07:00","id":1343964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orkar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1343960#post1343960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Hasbro quitting cooperation with Disney.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Disney themselves openly stated that Johnsins Movie was a total failure. </div> </div> </div><br /> You will have to provide source for these statements. Because I can't find it anywhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T05:15:26-07:00","id":1343966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orkar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1343952#post1343952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All of these started out strong cause everyone wanted more star wars, star trek, ghostbusters, battlefield, mass effect etc. Sure it was npstalgia and hope. Then when people realised the new stuff was total shit sales declined drasticly. Disney is severly struggling with new Star Wars and actually loosing money. Captain Marvel 2 is cancelled and her character wont appear int he next step of Marvel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you have a reputable source for those? Because from what I last heard, the next Star Wars has <a href=\"https://www.cbr.com/star-wars-rise-of-skywalker-boycott-presales-empty-threat/\" target=\"_blank\">ridiculous pre-sales numbers</a> and I couldn't find anything about a Captain Marvel 2 cancellation, only <a href=\"https://www.digitalspy.com/movies/a29416992/captain-marvel-sequel-brie-larson-update/\" target=\"_blank\">articles saying</a> that it won't be coming before 2022, but is definitely being worked on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mass Effect 4 is hated by most fans and killed the franchise, same for Wolfenstein. </div> </div> </div>As far as I recall, the problems of ME4 had relatively little to do with its writing and a lot with game design and animation problems.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orkar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1343952#post1343952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Discovery struggles since season 2 and is loosing money, no one wants to buy rights to it either. Id call that failures.<br /> <br /> And i could give you examples of horrible writing with each. Example from discovery - sonar in space?</div> </div> </div> </div>The famously rigid science of Star Trek - tell me again what can all be accomplished by reversing the polarity of something?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orkar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1343952#post1343952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can still like all of these examples but by all means we can objectively look at they are bad. And they are bad because they arent storydriven but agenda driven. Old Star Trek had black, female and even gay characters and fans loved it cause it was well written and thec haracters were natural not all about their sexuality. And shitting on lore is where i quit - first black action hero....and nobody remembers wesley snipes? Aka Blade? First female captain....yeah that was janeway....and so on. Just ignoring what happened to spin a not true narrative.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think anyone claimed that Georgiou was the first female captain. And no, old Star Trek did not have gay characters - the first one to appear at all in a movie was 2016 Sulu. There were a few veiled allegories and references, but nothing solid. I'll give you Blade, but I'd say the representation was on a far different level when compared to Black Panther or Luke Cage. Let Blade be played by a white actor, nothing in the movie would have to change. Replace T'Challa or Luke by a white character and their plots fall apart.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And Battlefield 5 took actual history and rewrote it to fit a narrative rather than showing what actually happened or highlight the characters of color or females who actually achieved great things. </div> </div> </div>Battlefield 5 should be considered from two sides: The singleplayer, where to my knowledge, you play the first campaign as a member of a resistance group who traditionally didn't care about gender because they had to take who they could get. And the multiplayer, where... well, where Battlefield 1 allowed the famous &quot;three players riding on a camel blazing flamethrowers&quot; stunt, so let's just abandon the pretense that Battlefield multiplayer was ever historically accurate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T05:26:10-07:00","id":1343968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orkar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1343960#post1343960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes and you totally fail to take into account the whys. Like movies finally shown in china - which adds 200-300 million.<br /> The production cost - if you spend 500 Million on the movie and advertising making 400 Million is still a loss.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, you are making up numbers.<br /> <br /> The Last Jedi budget was 317 million dollars.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.filmla.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/08/2017_film_study_v3-WEB.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.filmla.com/wp-content/up...udy_v3-WEB.pdf</a><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> While the Force Awakens budget was around 400 million (Marketing included by the way)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://financebuzz.com/how-much-did-star-wars-the-force-awakens-cost-to-make\" target=\"_blank\">https://financebuzz.com/how-much-did...s-cost-to-make</a><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://deadline.com/2018/03/star-wars-the-last-jedi-box-office-movie-profits-1202351603/\" target=\"_blank\">https://deadline.com/2018/03/star-wa...ts-1202351603/</a><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">Disney landed its fourth film in the top 10, hitting the top spot with the </span></span><a href=\"https://deadline.com/tag/rian-johnson/\" target=\"_blank\">Rian Johnson</a><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">-directed sequel to the J.J. Abrams </span></span><a href=\"https://deadline.com/2016/03/star-wars-the-force-awakens-movie-profit-2015-lucasfilm-disney-1201726142/\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Star Wars</i> relaunch in 2015</a><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">. Even though it would be hard to imagine eclipsing the relaunch\u2019s gross \u2014 highest domestic grossing movie of all-time with $936M and third highest worldwide with $2.07 billion \u2014 </span></span><i>The Last Jedi</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"> continued Disney\u2019s year end dominance, to the point where the studio is sucking all the oxygen out of the holiday corridor. Its $220M opening was the second biggest ever (trailing only the $247.9M opening of </span></span><i>The Force Awakens</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">). Johnson, who previously directed the edgy indies </span></span><i>Looper</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"> and </span></span><i>Brick</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">, didn\u2019t serve up a by-the-numbers retread here. He killed off a beloved original character and left more questions than answers about the connection between Daisy Ridley\u2019s Jedi Rey and Adam Driver\u2019s villainous Kylo Ren. Some felt the edge might have shortened </span></span><i>Last Jedi</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">\u2018s legs, but that\u2019s like criticizing an Aaron Judge home run because it hit a light post and didn\u2019t clear Yankee Stadium. </span></span><i>The Last Jedi</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"> was an enormous performer for Disney, with a $1.3 billion global gross. While LucasFilm removed top-tier young directors like Colin Trevorrow and Phil Lord &amp; Chris Miller from the helm of other </span></span><i>Star Wars</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"> films, Johnson was subsequently set in a deal </span></span><a href=\"https://deadline.com/2017/11/star-wars-new-film-trilogy-rian-johnson-lucasfilm-star-wars-the-last-jedi-1202204843/\" target=\"_blank\">to create a freestanding <i>Star Wars</i> branded trilogy</a><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">, taking place in another galaxy with new characters. Clearly, Lucasfilm believes The Force is strong in this one.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-family:Balto\">THE BOTTOM LINE</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><b>When Bob Iger agreed to pay $4 billion for Lucasfilm, even he probably didn\u2019t imagine that profit from the first three films \u2014 <i><a href=\"https://deadline.com/2016/03/star-wars-the-force-awakens-movie-profit-2015-lucasfilm-disney-1201726142/\" target=\"_blank\">Force Awakens</a>, </i><i>Last Jedi </i>and spinoff <i><a href=\"https://deadline.com/2017/04/rogue-one-box-office-profit-2016-1202054697/\" target=\"_blank\">Rogue One</a> \u2014 </i>would earn back close to 40% of that purchase price, with collective profits just over $1.5 billion. The $417.5M profit on <i>Last Jedi </i>is -46% from <i>Force Awakens </i>$780.1M</b>. Participations and residuals total $98.7M, down from <i>Force Awakens\u2019 </i> $143.5M, which were lofty in part from Harrison Ford\u2019s big payday. Disney is right back at it with Memorial Day weekend\u2019s <i>Solo: A Star Wars Story </i>and <i>Star Wars: Episode IX </i>due out on Dec. 20, 2019, with Abrams back in the driver\u2019s seat. The cash on cash return ratio is a healthy 1.72. We can only imagine what the Top 10 will look like if Disney inhales Fox and adds its X-Men and other franchises to the Disney arsenal. Landing four films in the Top 10 is illustrative of Disney\u2019s position as far and away the most dominant major movie studio we have seen in decade</span></span> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://screenrant.com/star-wars-8-last-jedi-box-office-domestic-worldwide/\" target=\"_blank\">https://screenrant.com/star-wars-8-l...tic-worldwide/</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#4D4D4D\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Now that </span></span></span><a href=\"https://screenrant.com/tag/star-wars-8/\" target=\"_blank\"><b><i>Star Wars: The Last Jedi</i></b></a><span style=\"color:#4D4D4D\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"> has been in theaters for about a month, the record will show that the film is a box office success. Lucasfilm's latest blockbuster, of course, is the sequel to 2015's </span></span></span><a href=\"https://screenrant.com/tag/star-wars-7/\" target=\"_blank\"><i>The Force Awakens</i></a><span style=\"color:#4D4D4D\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">, which rewrote the record books en route to a whopping $936.6 million domestic haul and more than $2 billion worldwide. Because </span></span></span><i>Episode VII</i><span style=\"color:#4D4D4D\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"> was such a well-received hit, it was widely expected </span></span></span><i>Last Jedi</i><span style=\"color:#4D4D4D\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"> would be one of the biggest films of the year - even if it couldn't match the output of its predecessor. After all, </span></span></span><i>The Force Awakens</i><span style=\"color:#4D4D4D\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"> was a once-in-a-lifetime cinematic event that arrived a decade after </span></span></span><i>Revenge of the Sith</i><span style=\"color:#4D4D4D\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"> and more than 30 years following the original trilogy. No film, even another </span></span></span><i>Star Wars</i><span style=\"color:#4D4D4D\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">, could top it.<br /> <br /> <br /> While it was generally accepted </span></span></span><i>The Last Jedi</i><span style=\"color:#4D4D4D\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"> wouldn't rival </span></span></span><i>The Force Awakens</i><span style=\"color:#4D4D4D\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">' gaudy numbers, there was some outside chatter about its box office performance after it took </span></span></span><a href=\"https://screenrant.com/jumanji-pitch-perfect-3-opening-weekend-box-office/\" target=\"_blank\">a 69 percent hit in it second weekend</a><span style=\"color:#4D4D4D\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">. That, combined with </span></span></span><i>Episode VIII</i><span style=\"color:#4D4D4D\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"> being the most divisive entry in the franchise, seemed to spell trouble for Lucasfilm in these early day of the </span></span></span><i>Star Wars</i><span style=\"color:#4D4D4D\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"> renaissance. <b>However, those concerns are hardly warranted, and the figure illustrate that </b></span></span></span><b><i>The Last Jedi</i></b><span style=\"color:#4D4D4D\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b> is one of the most successful films of all-time.</b><br /> <br /> <b>Most projections had the movie pegged for about $200 million in its first three days, but it far surpassed that with $220 million - the second biggest debut in history. To put that number in perspective, </b></span></span></span><b><a href=\"https://screenrant.com/tag/justice-league/\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Justice League</i></a><span style=\"color:#4D4D4D\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"> has earned $227.1 million for its </span></span></span><i>entire Stateside run</i><span style=\"color:#4D4D4D\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"> and </span></span></span><a href=\"https://screenrant.com/tag/wolverine-3/\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Logan</i></a><span style=\"color:#4D4D4D\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"> made $226.2 million. Though </span></span></span><i>The Last Jedi</i><a href=\"https://screenrant.com/last-jedi-box-office-jumanji-insidious/\" target=\"_blank\">eventually lost the top spot on the weekend charts</a><span style=\"color:#4D4D4D\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"> to </span></span></span><a href=\"https://screenrant.com/tag/jumanji/\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Jumanji: Welcome to the Jungle</i></a><span style=\"color:#4D4D4D\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">, it quickly ascended the charts, becoming the highest-grossing film of 2017 in the blink of an eye. Before the calendar flipped to 2018, </span></span></span><i>Star Wars 8</i><span style=\"color:#4D4D4D\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"> had </span></span></span><a href=\"https://screenrant.com/star-wars-last-jedi-box-office-1-billion-2017/\" target=\"_blank\">already unseated fellow Disney blockbuster <i>Beauty and the Beast</i></a><span style=\"color:#4D4D4D\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"> and crossed the $500 million mark. As of this writing, </span></span></span><i>The Last Jedi</i><span style=\"color:#4D4D4D\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"> has earned $576.8 million domestically and has an outside chance of passing </span></span></span><i>The Avengers</i></b><span style=\"color:#4D4D4D\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b> for fifth place before its run is done.</b></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><i>The Last Jedi</i><span style=\"color:#4D4D4D\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"> is nearing $600 million domestically, and that figure alone would ensure it makes a nice profit for Lucasfilm. But that's just the tip of the iceberg. Like several other tentpoles before it, </span></span></span><i>Episode VIII</i><span style=\"color:#4D4D4D\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"> played around the world, taking advantage of an increasingly important international box office. When the global numbers are taken into account, there's no denying </span></span></span><i>The Last Jedi</i></b><span style=\"color:#4D4D4D\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b> is a monumental success</b>.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://screenrant.com/star-wars-last-jedi-most-profitable-films-2017/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://static0.srcdn.com/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/Rey-in-the-Last-Jedi.jpg?w=1600&amp;h=900&amp;fit=crop\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://screenrant.com/star-wars-last-jedi-most-profitable-films-2017/\" target=\"_blank\"> Star Wars: The Last Jedi Is 2017's Most Profitable Blockbuster </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://screenrant.com/star-wars-last-jedi-most-profitable-films-2017/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://screenrant.com/star-wars-last-jedi-most-profitable-films-2017/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> What an investment! </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <a href=\"http://deadline.com/2018/03/star-wars-the-last-jedi-box-office-movie-profits-1202351603/\" target=\"_blank\"><i>D<b>eadline</b></i></a><b><span style=\"color:#4D4D4D\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">'s countdown of the top 10 most profitable blockbusters of 2017 (based on numbers calculated by their experts) ended by proclaiming </span></span></span><i>Star Wars 8</i><span style=\"color:#4D4D4D\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"> as the winner. With $995.8 million in revenue earned against total expenses (marketing, etc.) of $578.3 million, </span></span></span><i>The Last Jedi</i></b><span style=\"color:#4D4D4D\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b> is thought to be $417.5 million in the black. That's enough to bankroll the productions of two </b></span></span></span><b><i>Last Jedis</i></b><span style=\"color:#4D4D4D\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b> and still have $17.5 million to spare</b>. This is why the galaxy far, far away is one of the industry's leading tentpoles.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 10-27-2019, 08:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T07:06:02-07:00","id":1343983,"title":"","content":"I think it's worth pointing out that going from an argument that greater access to representation would only confuse and enrage old vampires (when there's a broad and growing body of scholarship pointing to the invention of heterosexuality as a relatively recent development in western history), to one that greater access to representation has been rejected in modern pop entertainment (as soundly rejected by Undead Rabbit, who brought receipts in the form of links) is itself a major moving of the goalposts.<br /> <br /> I'd recommend dropping the matter and moving on. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","user":"Reasor","date":". 10-27-2019, 10:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T09:10:42-07:00","id":1344202,"title":"","content":"Being the game set in contemporary times I find being able to choose neutral gender in character creation actually a good thing. It is inclusive, encouraged to be used all around (at least in English speaking countries), and people have the right to be addressed that way. Kudos for WoD being progressive.<br /> <br /> A different matter is how would be used in-game. Do we know how the Prince of Detroit will be? Because taking Chicago as a reference, PKJ is not that old at all. Heck, he was a gang leader in the 80s... If the Prince is played as I play PKJ, he would have no problem using it regardless of what he thinks. He will screw you anyway with a friendly smile.<br /> <br /> Other elder vampires could have a problem though, but if the main story is not about gender discrimination I wouldn't stress it out too much. Maybe they will just ignore the request and use whatever pronoun they see fit, while the rest of NPCs use it properly. If the PC thinks they are being discriminated against by elders, well, they have another reason to go anarch.<br /> <br /> Depending on their age and cultural background, different elders would have different morals regarding sexual orientation and gender identity, which doesn't mean progressive ones. Those would usually be outdated and weird to us. Critias is gay and misogynistic. Romans wouldn't have much problem with gayness as long as the one they are addressing is not known for being passive. Also, any activity whose goal is not to get their own pleasure would be disregarded and mocked. I can imagine a lot of unsatisfied women in ancient Rome. And so on. About gender? I don't know how really grounded in reality it was, but I recently saw an episode on a tv series where a father castrated his son actually changing his (now her) gender against his will because he was gay. Trans-genderness was acceptable to his cultural background, homosexuality was not. So we don't really know how truly Elders would feel about this, some cultural backgrounds are too different to predict.<br /> <br /> How would they react - not feel - is a whole different question and would depend on how they approach the PC. Do they want to gain their favor or do they impose their will? Maybe they don't care about gender identity but are annoyed by the PC requesting anything at all.<br /> <br /> Then, with age, I've always assumed gender loses importance. Blood is important, everything else is subject to it.<br /> <br /> Regarding other anachronisms... that is why disadvantages such as anachronistic exist. Those elders would have the need to adapt, but adapting is harder with age. Toddlers absorb everything and have everything to learn. Teenagers learn fast. Adults feel more difficult to restructure the way they think. Also, time perception goes faster as they are surprised by fewer things. Now change decades by centuries. Sure, many of them adapt to a degree. But then again a common reason to embrace is to keep up with times by proxy.<br /> <br /> About language...<br /> <br /> There's a reason the crusader in Indiana Jones and the Holy Grail speaks modern English: we, the spectators, can understand him.<br /> <br /> Some anachronisms are not ignored by laziness, they are done in purpose to favor understandability. There is always a compromise between realism and plausibility. If you go for the first one, be aware that those elder characters will look alien in our eyes. If that is the desired effect, that is perfect. If that would rob protagonism to the story we are telling (and in a rpg games computer or not that is what we do) softening up is an option. Playability should come first.<br /> <br /> BTW, being a non-native speaker, Shakespeare in his original English is very difficult for me. After a couple of pages, with context growings thinner due to previous misunderstandings, nearly impossible. Lost in translation.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17974-strangelove","name":"Strangelove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17974_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T05:05:47-07:00","id":1344898,"title":"","content":"For those who are curious about the writing and such, here's a couple videos from people who got to see the first 20-30 minutes of the story during private interviews.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/s6iVe0qvG6A\" data-code=\"s6iVe0qvG6A\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/s6iVe0qvG6A/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/FVSHP9FNh3s\" data-code=\"FVSHP9FNh3s\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/FVSHP9FNh3s/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-31-2019, 09:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T05:31:23-07:00","id":1344906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1343870#post1343870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So when you say, &quot;oh a vampire from back in the day would kill young vampires for.... being young vampires used to modern norms,&quot; it's always going to feel weird; at best.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not weird at all, when you consider that the vast majority of modern day vampires have never been exposed to an aristocratic society, and have absolutely no desire to ever do so.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Welcome to existence as a vampire. Forget all that crap about presidents, elected officials, and terms of office. I would like to introduce you to this city's king, and who's office does not expire until he does!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;These are the Primogen, a council of elders who were all hand picked by the king himself. They'll be acting as your representative in matters of state. And these are the Sheriff and Scourge; if you do something the king doesn't like, they will kill you in your own home!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Now that we got that out of the way, please place any and all electronic communications devices into the shredder machine. These are now illegal contraband by order of the Camarilla!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1343930#post1343930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you even played the first game? For all your &quot;elders are out of date and don't use computers,&quot; you seem to have forgotten that the Prince in Bloodlines 1 emails you personally on multiple occasions, and you are never killed for talking back to him.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No... you just get Dominated into doing whatever he wants you to do...<br /> <br /> Also, the Prince is repeatedly trying to kill you since night one. In case you haven't noticed, the missions that he sends you on would be considered suicidal for a fresh faced neonate who's only half a year old by the end of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-31-2019, 08:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T06:02:45-07:00","id":1344914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orkar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1343960#post1343960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">snip</div> </div> </div> </div>Just let it go, dude. They've chosen to remain willfully ignorant of the situation, even if you present them with video evidence to back up your side of the argument.<br /> <br /> Just got off a ban for this shit. Let's get back to talking about Bloodlines 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-31-2019, 10:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T13:55:44-07:00","id":1345047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1344914#post1344914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just let it go, dude. They've chosen to remain willfully ignorant of the situation, even if you present them with video evidence to back up your side of the argument.<br /> <br /> Just got off a ban for this shit. Let's get back to talking about Bloodlines 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>You realize the irony here, right? Where the side you're calling &quot;willfully ignorant&quot; has posted numerous facts and statistics and the side you're defending has posted nothing but their own personal opinion with nothing to support it?<br /> <br /> Not to mention talking like you don't want to continue this discussion when you're trying to bring back an argument nobody has posted on for several days.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T14:02:12-07:00","id":1345049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1345047#post1345047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You realize the irony here, right? Where the side you're calling &quot;willfully ignorant&quot; has posted numerous facts and statistics and the side you're defending has posted nothing but their own personal opinion with nothing to support it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that's an outright lie. I posted not one, but 2 videos of people supporting Orkar's claims. The videos featured several news articles, pictures of on site lack of attendance, critics intentionally interfering with audience review scores, people who actually work within and alongside Disney talking about how bad the situation is, and Disney being investigated of lying about ticket sales in regards to their franchises.<br /> <br /> The people I tried to post these videos for not only didn't believe the mountains of evidence provided, but outright refused to even give them a look, just because they thought the people in the video were just there to shit talk the franchise / people working on it. That is the literal definition of being willfully ignorant. They ask for proof, we supply them with proof, and they toss it in the waste bin without even looking at it.<br /> <br /> <br /> And for the record, Orkar has the right of it. People aren't upset with inclusivity, they're upset with inclusivity being valued higher than immersion. It distracts from the story you're trying to tell the audience, and makes the characters come across like token inserts meant to increase sale revenue.<br /> <br /> Now, I personally don't give a shit about the whole pronoun thing in Bloodlines 2, just like I didn't give a shit when they were present in Battletech. It's such a minor feature as to be easily overlooked. I don't care if an NPC in the game is transgender, or whatever. What I do care about is if them being transgender is the entire focus of their character, and they have no greater depth beyond that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-31-2019, 05:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T14:25:05-07:00","id":1345060,"title":"","content":"Does the anachronism particularly apply in this game anyway? The Pioneers are probably of the late 19th century, with nostalgia for most of the 20th century too, while the local Camarilla are yuppies, even if they're actually hundreds of years old. Or could they be <i>more </i>annoyed by modern culture than some pre-Enlightenment aristocrat, because they've seen fewer trends come and go?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","user":"Spencer from The Hills","date":". 10-31-2019, 05:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T14:38:04-07:00","id":1345064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1345060#post1345060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the anachronism particularly apply in this game anyway? The Pioneers are probably of the late 19th century, with nostalgia for most of the 20th century too, while the local Camarilla are yuppies, even if they're actually hundreds of years old. Or could they be <i>more </i>annoyed by modern culture than some pre-Enlightenment aristocrat, because they've seen fewer trends come and go?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, since this version of the Camarilla has a hand in the technology industry, I'm almost positive that most of them keep in touch with social media, and would be aware of the changes going on. They might not be as sensitive about it, because of that.<br /> <br /> Pioneers, however, may be a lot more old fashioned and stubborn to accept these new world ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T15:03:41-07:00","id":1345070,"title":"","content":"Ferris Wheel Guy has a name now, it's Mr. Damp!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.bloodlines2.com/en/characters-cosplay-guides\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines 2 Cosplay Guides</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T15:28:31-07:00","id":1345078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1344906#post1344906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not weird at all, when you consider that the vast majority of modern day vampires have never been exposed to an aristocratic society, and have absolutely no desire to ever do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most modern day vampires have absolutely been exposed to an aristocratic society even if ones without officially recognized aristocrats. America, for example, was founded as an aristocracy that rigged the system in favor of rich white land owning men, and then put a coating of democracy on top of it to sate the masses the founding fathers absolutely didn't trust with real power in the system. And a lot of US history has been fighting over the desire to make the democracy side of things more of a reality.<br /> <br /> This is also completely twisting the point. The issue I'm bringing up is that older vampires <b>have to be used to young vampires being young</b>; they're not going to fly off the handle because a neonate acts like they expect neonates to be acting: young. Elders aren't so stupid that they expect newer vampires to magically become immersed in vampire culture and society... they know it's a learning process (one they're happy to exploit, but that's because vampires tend to be assholes). So the idea that they're going to kill neonates over such things is absurd. Put neonates &quot;in their place&quot; sure! Because that's &quot;helping&quot; them learn and also creating debts said neonates will owe them later. Outright killing them over culture clashes gets an Elder nothing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No... you just get Dominated into doing whatever he wants you to do... </div> </div> </div>Yeah... exactly. Elders have better tools to assert their power than death sentences.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T15:56:10-07:00","id":1345089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1345078#post1345078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Most modern day vampires have absolutely been exposed to an aristocratic society even if ones without officially recognized aristocrats. America, for example, was founded as an aristocracy that rigged the system in favor of rich white land owning men, and then put a coating of democracy on top of it to sate the masses the founding fathers absolutely didn't trust with real power in the system. And a lot of US history has been fighting over the desire to make the democracy side of things more of a reality.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Regardless of how the system mechanically functioned during its inception, the fact of the matter is that most people living under that system in the modern age have been brought up to believe that everybody is considered equal, and has the opportunity for advancement if they're willing to apply themselves. Leaders are elected by the people, and serve a defined period of office. And in the case of the highest office in the land, they're only allowed a maximum of 2 terms.<br /> <br /> A system which is starkly contrasted by vampire society, where your only hope for advancement is if the people above you (who have far more experience than you could ever dream of) screw up majorly, and end up getting taken out of the picture. Unfortunately for you, dear neonate, they've clawed their way into a position where the majority of your kind will be sacrificed as meat shields long before that ends up happening.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Yeah... exactly. Elders have better tools to assert their power than death sentences.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">He dominates you into going on suicide missions, like blowing up a Sabbat warehouse by yourself, taking out the Sabbat's headquarters in the city by yourself, going to retrieve Johanson from the Society of Leopold by yourself. Just because Lacroix can't put a gun to your head and pull the trigger in public, doesn't mean that he's willing to tolerate your continued existence. Sure, he may lavish you with praise upon your successful return, but only to save face. Before he sends you out on yet another suicide mission that any kindred in the city can easily see through.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T16:04:05-07:00","id":1345091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1345049#post1345049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except that's an outright lie. I posted not one, but 2 videos of people supporting Orkar's claims. The videos featured several news articles, pictures of on site lack of attendance, critics intentionally interfering with audience review scores, people who actually work within and alongside Disney talking about how bad the situation is, and Disney being investigated of lying about ticket sales in regards to their franchises.<br /> <br /> The people I tried to post these videos for not only didn't believe the mountains of evidence provided, but outright refused to even give them a look, just because they thought the people in the video were just there to shit talk the franchise / people working on it. That is the literal definition of being willfully ignorant. They ask for proof, we supply them with proof, and they toss it in the waste bin without even looking at it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Emh, actually no, again you are spreading fake news.<br /> <br /> <br /> You posted crap videos from youtube channels, while me and others posted Reuters data, Financial Times articles: your sources were not eminent.<br /> You posted fake news, like the one about &quot;femminist artist&quot; of Mass Effect Andromeda sabotaging the development of the game, debunked by Bioware itself.<br /> Most of the video you posted were not even related with the subject of the thread (I mean your fake news that &quot;Disney went woke and went broke&quot;). Some of those videos didn't said a thing about it, but were just subjective complaints about the quality of the writing, which is called &quot;shifting the goalpost&quot; or &quot;strawman&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, you have quite the immagination, and even more you are a troll spreading fake news to justify reactionary,misogynist and racist trash.<br /> And that's a fact.<br /> <br /> If anyone is interested in how things went: that's the link, that's how things happened.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game/page8?_=1563782979376\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1563782979376</a><br /> <br /> That's the story, everything else is, I am afraid, fake news.<br /> <br /> And that's why the mods kicked you, it was not because you were a paladin of free speech, but because you were throwing racist and homophobic shit in the fan.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1326814#post1326814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Hi there! Mod here.<br /> <br /> While I fully realize sexism was the topic of the thread from the get go, some posters may need to be reminded that misogynistic, homophobic leaning posts are not likely to be well received on the forums for a company that famously champions progressive issues</span>.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">So let's stop talking about how wokeness is ruining the industry. It isn't.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 10-31-2019, 07:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T16:28:50-07:00","id":1345098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1345091#post1345091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Emh, actually no, again you are spreading fake news.<br /> <br /> <br /> You posted crap videos from youtube channels, while me and others posted Reuters data, Financial Times articles: your sources were not eminent.<br /> You posted fake news, like the one about &quot;femminist artist&quot; of Mass Effect Andromeda sabotaging the development of the game, debunked by Bioware itself.<br /> Most of the video you posted were not even related with the subject of the thread (I mean your fake news that &quot;Disney went woke and went broke&quot;). Some of those videos didn't said a thing about it, but were just subjective complaints about the quality of the writing, which is called &quot;shifting the goalpost&quot; or &quot;strawman&quot;.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You seem to be talking about something completely different, from so long ago that I don't even remember it anymore.<br /> <br /> I was talking about the Movies thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-31-2019, 07:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T16:56:55-07:00","id":1345110,"title":"","content":"5 months ago is not that long ago. And no it was no different because the themes were just the same, even more you didn't take account of the informations you were given 5 months ago and repeated, as a machine does, the same lines (or lies) about Disney's financial situation and the profitability of Star Wars, merged with a series of NO TRUE SCOTSMAN arguments, answering with youtube channels of dubious authority, going as far as claiming that there is plot by Disney to upvote videos and trailers of the new star wars (very paranoid thinking by the way)... what can I say? One more proof of &quot;recidivity&quot;?<br /> <br /> <br /> And still you had to enter this topic and pushing with shit that already got you admonished by the Mods, and later got you banned. I would call it a &quot;relapse&quot;, but that would be a gentle description.<br /> <br /> By the way, with just a bit of checking one could also find that while you accuse people &quot;remaining willfully ignorant of the situation&quot;, that accusation comes from a man that REALLY, REALLY do not know what he is talking about, since, by his own admission he didn't even saw the film he is criticizing, and it's working on second hand sources, and youtube videos.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1235843#post1235843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>After watching The Force Awakens and realizing that I've already seen that story a dozen times over the last 20 years? No, I did not go see The Last Jedi. In fact, the very name of the movie infuriates me, because the entire point of the original trilogy was leading up to the RETURN of the Jedi. And then over the course of these last 2 movies, we switch back to the Jedi being driven to the brink of extinction. Fuck you Disney, fuck you!</b><br /> <br /> My only consolation is that Lucas is probably laughing his ass off right now as he watches the people who paid him billions of dollars for the franchise continue to drive it into the ground.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>But from what I've heard from reviewers and seen through online clips, it sounds like I made the right decision by not seeing the movie.</b><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>And here you are again, speaking of things you do not know, and accusing others of &quot;remaining willfully ignorant of the situation&quot;.<br /> <br /> Nihil novum sub sole","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 10-31-2019, 08:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T17:05:00-07:00","id":1345115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1345110#post1345110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5 months ago is not that long ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is for me, I can't even remember most things I've done from an hour ago, unless I wrote down a note, or specifically focused on the memory during that time.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T18:02:51-07:00","id":1345128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1345089#post1345089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regardless of how the system mechanically functioned during its inception, the fact of the matter is that most people living under that system in the modern age have been brought up to believe that everybody is considered equal, and has the opportunity for advancement if they're willing to apply themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>They might have been raised to believe it, but most of us figured out somewhere in our early adulthoods that this belief is an aspiration goal, not how reality really works. Our society doesn't treat everyone as equal, we don't have equal opportunity for advancement, and the failure of upwards mobility is not just people that aren't &quot;willing&quot; to apply themselves. Just like adults all know Santa Claus isn't real, even if there's secular value to general society to use the story as a way to influence norms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Leaders are elected by the people, and serve a defined period of office. And in the case of the highest office in the land, they're only allowed a maximum of 2 terms. </div> </div> </div>Leaders are nominally elected by the people, but again, as adults learn quickly enough, they're elected by a small portion of the population that they largely self-select (see: voter suppression, gerrymandering, refusal to expand the House or Representatives to be more proportional to population as it's supposed to be, etc.). And the Camarilla has it's own ways to put it's thumb on who the Prince of a city is if they decide they want to throw their weight around.<br /> <br /> Term limits on the POTUS is less then 70 years old (after FDR), and there's a lot of questions around the 22nd Amendment that haven't been tested (like, can Bill Clinton becomes a VP? If so wha if the President dies the first day in office... does Clinton get an effective 3rd term?). There's still a fairly big philosophic debate in political science over whether or not this was a good idea and should be applied to more positions, or a bad idea and be modified; after all having FDR in office for three terms was rather useful for continuity of leadership during WWII, and we're seeing some difficulties in swapping leadership around while we're still engaged militarily in Afghanistan, Iraq, and Syria. So modern sensibilities on this are actually mixed, and not exactly something that's going to be horribly foreign to a neonate.<br /> <br /> We also do have things like the SCOTUS which is a lifelong appointment and they only hope of advancement in the federal court systems are waiting for those above you to move up first, retire, or die. I mean, technically they could get impeached, but that's very rare.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying neonates are going to instantly adapt to Cam society, but none of these are strange and foreign concepts since a lot of them are in place one way or another in our lives.<br /> <br /> And! You're still making this about neonates instead of Elders... is there a reason you keep banging this drum instead of actually talking about by point at hand?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Just because Lacroix can't put a gun to your head and pull the trigger in public, doesn't mean that he's willing to tolerate your continued existence. Sure, he may lavish you with praise upon your successful return, but only to save face. Before he sends you out on yet another suicide mission that any kindred in the city can easily see through. </div> </div> </div>Yep. But it's actually Camarilla law that you be put down as an illegal Embrace, and he needs to convince the Camarilla that he's a strong prince that can enforce the law, while having a very Anarch heavy Domain to manage that doesn't want to tolerate it.<br /> <br /> LaxCroix also starts to value you if you play your cards right, and considers it a win-win of either you die with his hands clean enough, or he gets a useful pawn that surprises him with competence.<br /> <br /> Because again, the point is that <b>Elders aren't dumb.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T20:40:15-07:00","id":1345156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1345128#post1345128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Leaders are nominally elected by the people, but again, as adults learn quickly enough, they're elected by a small portion of the population that they largely self-select (see: voter suppression, gerrymandering, refusal to expand the House or Representatives to be more proportional to population as it's supposed to be, etc.). And the Camarilla has it's own ways to put it's thumb on who the Prince of a city is if they decide they want to throw their weight around.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sadly, no, we don't quickly learn this here in America. Because our public education system is <a href=\"https://youtu.be/8xe6nLVXEC0\" target=\"_blank\">a waste of tax payer money</a>, and I fully understand why the other countries of the world think we're a bunch of idiots. The first time I ever heard about the Electoral College was on an episode of Adam Ruins Everything, and that was several years after getting out of Highschool. I also never even knew what the difference between Democracy and Republic was, because the people I asked couldn't give me a proper answer beyond trash talking whichever party they didn't support.<br /> <br /> Gotta be honest, a lot of the terms your using (POTUS, SCOTUS, est), I have no idea what they mean. Not trying to insult you, we simply didn't cover any of this in school. Yes, I know, not teaching students how the friggin government works is shocking, but such is the way of the American education system...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T21:02:05-07:00","id":1345160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1345156#post1345156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sadly, no, we don't quickly learn this here in America. Because our public education system is <a href=\"https://youtu.be/8xe6nLVXEC0\" target=\"_blank\">a waste of tax payer money</a>, and I fully understand why the other countries of the world think we're a bunch of idiots. The first time I ever heard about the Electoral College was on an episode of Adam Ruins Everything, and that was several years after getting out of Highschool. I also never even knew what the difference between Democracy and Republic was, because the people I asked couldn't give me a proper answer beyond trash talking whichever party they didn't support.<br /> <br /> Gotta be honest, a lot of the terms your using (POTUS, SCOTUS, est), I have no idea what they mean. Not trying to insult you, we simply didn't cover any of this in school. Yes, I know, not teaching students how the friggin government works is shocking, but such is the way of the American education system...</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying this is the same situation you're in, but I will say that we learned about the Electoral College in my public high school - we spent a couple of weeks on it and stuff related to it. I'll also say that now, more than a decade out of school, I've seen several people that were <i>in my government class</i> talk about how they had no idea about these finer details until they became an adult. Mostly, it was the people who weren't paying much attention.<br /> <br /> I don't really understand why you're calling out not understanding the terms someone is using and blaming your education when you could literally spend less wordcount (read: energy) googling the terms. The fact that it's so easy to discover is probably why it was referenced as being learned 'quickly enough'.<br /> <br /> FWIW:<br /> POTUS = President of the United States<br /> SCOTUS = Supreme Court of the United States","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T21:23:27-07:00","id":1345163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1345160#post1345160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I don't really understand why you're calling out not understanding the terms someone is using and blaming your education when you could literally spend less wordcount (read: energy) googling the terms. The fact that it's so easy to discover is probably why it was referenced as being learned 'quickly enough'.<br /> <br /> FWIW:<br /> POTUS = President of the United States<br /> SCOTUS = Supreme Court of the United States</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if you've never heard of them before, you wouldn't have thought to google them. Also, I grew up in the 90's, a time when access to the internet was a luxury that most of us didn't understand how valuable it was. Heck, I believe there were even televised infomercials specifically dedicated to teaching people what the internet was. Because at the time, they thought it was just some passing fad among nerds.<br /> <br /> But yes, I've obviously heard of the President and the Supreme Court. I've just never seen those abbreviations used for them before, so my mind didn't connect the dots. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T23:54:00-07:00","id":1345174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1345163#post1345163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, if you've never heard of them before, you wouldn't have thought to google them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s\u2026 kinda the <i>opposite</i> of my process for using Google. And I also grew up in the 90\u2019s, so that\u2019s not to blame.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T01:13:20-07:00","id":1345178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1345156#post1345156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sadly, no, we don't quickly learn this here in America. Because our public education system is <a href=\"https://youtu.be/8xe6nLVXEC0\" target=\"_blank\">a waste of tax payer money</a>, and I fully understand why the other countries of the world think we're a bunch of idiots.</div> </div> </div> </div>You seem to be missing that I'm talking about adults, not high-school students.<br /> <br /> Though objectively speaking, however much we need to massively overhaul our public education system, it is not a waste of tax payer money. At no level of public education does the money invested fail to produce greater returns in economic productivity. So for every dollar we spend on education, we get more than a dollar back in taxes paid thanks to educated citizens performing trained work. And music videos aren't actually really convincing ways to prove a point here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The first time I ever heard about the Electoral College was on an episode of Adam Ruins Everything, and that was several years after getting out of Highschool. </div> </div> </div>So... my point exactly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Gotta be honest, a lot of the terms your using (POTUS, SCOTUS, est), I have no idea what they mean. Not trying to insult you, we simply didn't cover any of this in school. Yes, I know, not teaching students how the friggin government works is shocking, but such is the way of the American education system... </div> </div> </div>I have literally taught those terms to high-school students (as part of the education system even if not as a teacher proper).<br /> <br /> Those terms are also over 100 years old. They started with the telegraph because telegraph messages charged per character and thus created a huge number of now common American specific abbreviations.<br /> <br /> A lot of them did fall out of use during the hey day of radio and live broadcast TV, but the Internet has brought most of them back rather swiftly as Internet communication has always favored abbreviation heavy language (ex: Twitter character limits).<br /> <br /> But hey, I grew up in the late 80s early 90s... so I shouldn't know anything about these computer things, right?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T05:03:04-07:00","id":1345203,"title":"","content":"Heads up, the game's release is being delayed from the initially planned Q1 2020 date. The plan is still for a release sometime in 2020, but there's no specific date beyond that given. You can read the developers' statement <a href=\"https://www.bloodlines2.com/en/dev-blog-post\" target=\"_blank\">here<img src=\"https://static.tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pub/external_link.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a>.<br /> <br /> Since I'm already bumping the thread, I found the <a href=\"https://www.bloodlines2.com/en/dev-diary-6-environment-design\" target=\"_blank\">latest Dev Diary<img src=\"https://static.tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pub/external_link.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a> an interesting read. It talks a bit about environmental design, about them trying to make Seattle always 'drearily wet and misty' and them figuring out what a new vampire's living space would look like. The game apparently takes place during Christmas, incidentally. Hoping the game's tingled with festive spirit!<br /> <br /> The bigger news since this thread was last active, though, is that they revealed <a href=\"https://www.bloodlines2.com/en/the-pioneers\" target=\"_blank\">the factions<img src=\"https://static.tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pub/external_link.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a>.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T06:52:27-07:00","id":1345219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1345174#post1345174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That\u2019s\u2026 kinda the <i>opposite</i> of my process for using Google. And I also grew up in the 90\u2019s, so that\u2019s not to blame.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, I mean it's kind of difficult to google something before you know that it exists. Just out of the blue one day, decide <i>&quot;I think I'll type SCOTUS into the search bar and see what comes up.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> Yes, I kind of was posting updates to the thread when a new faction came out. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I don't mind the delay, especially if they're using it to improve the game's appearance. Let's be honest, the current pre-alpha game play footage could use some work with it's janky combat animations. I've got a lot of games on my wishlist already, Coteries of New York being one of them. So I should have enough to tide me over until Bloodlines 2 releases.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 11-01-2019, 09:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T07:01:36-07:00","id":1345221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1345178#post1345178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But hey, I grew up in the late 80s early 90s... so I shouldn't know anything about these computer things, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you frequently get ASL Dial Up CD's delivered to you in the mail? Only 1 computer to share between the whole house hold, and your internet connection cut out every single time the phone was used?<br /> <br /> edit: darn, meant to add this to the post above!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.