.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-15T17:54:42-08:00","id":1355094,"title":"","content":"Games often get pushed back a month if they're worried about competing with the release date of another game, or sometimes 3 or 4 months if there are some big problems with the game, but pushing it back close to a full year? I can't help but imagine that there must have been some deeply serious flaws that they felt required a lot of massive, time consuming work to get fixed before they could release the game in a playable state.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-15T18:58:59-08:00","id":1355103,"title":"","content":"Well, here's the article.<br /> <br /> It could be the opposite and they think the game has real potential to excite the masses when they intended something more modest initially.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/articles/2019-10-16-vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2-delayed-to-avoid-repeating-the-mistakes-of-the-first-game\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/-1571232913775.jpg?width=1200&amp;height=630&amp;fit=crop&amp;enable=upscale&amp;auto=webp\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/articles/2019-10-16-vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2-delayed-to-avoid-repeating-the-mistakes-of-the-first-game\" target=\"_blank\"> Vampire: The Masquerade - Bloodlines 2 delayed to avoid repeating the mistakes of the first game </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/articles/2019-10-16-vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2-delayed-to-avoid-repeating-the-mistakes-of-the-first-game\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.eurogamer.net/articles/2019-10-16-vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2-delayed-to-avoid-repeating-the-mistakes-of-the-first-game </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Vampire: The Masquerade - Bloodlines 2 has been delayed. The game was due out during the first quarter of 2020, but wil&hellip; </div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-15T23:33:45-08:00","id":1355134,"title":"","content":"Anything is possible, of course. It's just that in my experience, when a company pushes the release date back by almost a year it's usually because the product had major flaws and they believe it will take that long to get it to a point where they can release it, rather than the idea that they already have a playable game that could be released much, much sooner, but they want to keep it in development for another year in order to tweak it a bit.<br /> <br /> Or to put it another way, based on past experience with video games this isn't a terribly encouraging sign for the game, but there have been other games that had dates pushed back fairly significantly and ended up being pretty good so it's not like I'm trying to be Negative Nancy or anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T06:20:42-08:00","id":1355166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1355134#post1355134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anything is possible, of course. It's just that in my experience, when a company pushes the release date back by almost a year it's usually because the product had major flaws and they believe it will take that long to get it to a point where they can release it, rather than the idea that they already have a playable game that could be released much, much sooner, but they want to keep it in development for another year in order to tweak it a bit.<br /> <br /> Or to put it another way, based on past experience with video games this isn't a terribly encouraging sign for the game, but there have been other games that had dates pushed back fairly significantly and ended up being pretty good so it's not like I'm trying to be Negative Nancy or anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if it's pushed back an entire year, we haven't got a solid date beyond pushing it back past the 1st quarter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T08:05:57-08:00","id":1355186,"title":"","content":"Great move to push it back.The game was not even close to be ready for Q1 launch. Going by the released footage, the graphics were poor and the combat was atrocious. If they launched in Q1, it would have been a mediocre game only loved by hardcore vtm fans. Now it has a chance to be a good game. And yes i am sure Cyberpunk 2077 played a role in this decision. Comparing the two games side by side made bloodlines look like a joke. Now they have time to polish it and avoid the biggest game of the year.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T08:54:48-08:00","id":1355194,"title":"","content":"Bloodlines should not be compared to Cyberpunk. Cd projekt has an enormous budget and Is one of the most skilled studios out there. Bloodlines resources are far more limited.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 12-16-2019, 12:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T09:55:05-08:00","id":1355203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1355194#post1355194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bloodlines should not be compared to Cyberpunk. Cd projekt has an enormous budget and Is one of the most skilled studios out there. Bloodlines resources are far more limited.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't need every game to be a Triple A one. I liked Outer Worlds just fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T11:40:27-08:00","id":1355220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1355194#post1355194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bloodlines should not be compared to Cyberpunk. Cd projekt has an enormous budget and Is one of the most skilled studios out there. Bloodlines resources are far more limited.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It''s probably not a fair comparison. Regardless you can't tell me you were impressed with the graphics, animations or combat system. If you only liked the atmosphere and written dialogue then it's an average game at best. This may have been acceptable in 2004 but expectations are a bit higher in 2020. That's why i am glad they realized this and postponed the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T11:44:55-08:00","id":1355222,"title":"","content":"The atmosphere and the written dialogue were what made people love the first game. It certainly isn't considered &quot;an average game&quot; and most games are awful at both of those. Atmosphere and dialogue is all the sequel needs to nail.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T11:55:34-08:00","id":1355225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1355222#post1355222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The atmosphere and the written dialogue were what made people love the first game. It certainly isn't considered &quot;an average game&quot; and most games are awful at both of those. Atmosphere and dialogue is all the sequel needs to nail.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Right people loved the first game for the reasons you mentionend, but like i said that was 2004. Most people expect more from their games these days. I certainly do, you may feel differently. Dont get me wrong i am sure most vtm fans will like the game regardless but if you want to reach a larger audience you need to make a proper game on all levels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24527,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","user":"blackshade","date":". 12-16-2019, 02:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T11:57:09-08:00","id":1355227,"title":"","content":"Atmosphere and dialogue were the final nail in the coffin of a company that desperately needed a commercial success but Bloodlines 1 bombed. Atmosphere and dialogue were what gave the game cult status and has people playing till this day, but it wasn't enough to keep the people that made it in business.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T12:02:01-08:00","id":1355228,"title":"","content":"Somehow people seems to forget one important thing.<br /> <br /> Vampire the Masquerade Bloodlines was a commercial failure. A commercial failure that killed Troika Games.<br /> The game became a cult (which doesn't mean mass seller) much later, when the developers were already out of buisness.<br /> <br /> A game should choose wisely its scope and its target.<br /> <br /> If Bloodlines 2 is a game that has been made to play in the same arena of Cyberpunk, it will be a commercial failure.<br /> If Bloodlines is a game that has been made to be a great AA game, it could be quite the hit.<br /> <br /> So I do not pretend to be impressed by the graphic, neither by the animations. What I want is a product that fit is target niche. And the target niche of Bloodlines is a niche were good quest-design and writing are paramount, and surely way more important than shader and texture.<br /> <br /> The game that won most award at the Game Awards this year ( Best RPG, best Narrative, best Debut game, Best Indie) is a indie game called Disco Elysium, which is a complete masterpiece that, in the future, will be held in the same regard Planescape Torment was held once.<br /> <br /> <br /> Among other thing the game run against (in the categories where it won prize) against triple AAA titles like Death Stranding, Control, Outer Worlds and so on.<br /> <br /> The game looks like this.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://multiplayer.net-cdn.it/thumbs/images/2019/10/23/disco-elysium-07_jpg_1400x0_q85.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And it was also a commercial hit for its developers, since they are already planning a sequel.<br /> What matters, when you develop a game, it setting your target straight. Find your commercial niche, and fill it.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, it's a matter of scope.<br /> What do I expect from Bloodlines? Surely not what I expect from Cyberpunk.<br /> The important thing, is that when the game was made, and the budget was chosen, the developers had also this thing clear.<br /> <br /> If they are aiming at a game that can compete with AAA games, I expect another failure as Troika.<br /> If they are aiming at a game thatn can compete with AA games, Bloodlines can be a hit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 12-16-2019, 03:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T12:03:49-08:00","id":1355229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1355227#post1355227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Atmosphere and dialogue were the final nail in the coffin of a company that desperately needed a commercial success but Bloodlines 1 bombed. Atmosphere and dialogue were what gave the game cult status and has people playing till this day, but it wasn't enough to keep the people that made it in business.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Good point. If it wasnt enough back then it certainly isn't enough today. If they ever intend to release bloodlines 3 then they need to reach the larger rpg audience and not just people that like vtm. Cause let's face it, that's a niche market.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T12:08:22-08:00","id":1355230,"title":"","content":"Bloodlines was a commercial failure because of two things:<br /> <br /> 1. A thing called Half Life 2.<br /> <br /> 2. The bugginess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T12:32:31-08:00","id":1355235,"title":"","content":"Half-life 2 had no role in it.<br /> In the year Half-life 2 came out, many other games were a commercial and a critical success: Metal Gear 3, Halo 2,GTA San Andreas, Fable,Doom 3, Far Cry and so on.<br /> <br /> What killed Bloodlines was :<br /> <br /> <br /> 1) A lack of budget, at the end of the development the funds were gone.<br /> <br /> 2) The choice to use a (very powerful, complex, and expensive) game engine never relased before, which was not already tested and had several faults (faults you can fix if you are Valve and had a lot of money, not surely thing you could do if you were Troika).<br /> <br /> 3) Deadlines from Activision<br /> <br /> 3) Bugginess, mostly caused by point 1,2 and 3<br /> <br /> 4) High hardware requirements, which shrinked an already small market niche.<br /> <br /> ah, also important<br /> <br /> 5) Bad game design.<br /> Bloodlines was a good RPG, a terrible FPS, and an horrible TPS. Stealth was so so.<br /> If you choose to make an RPG that walks the hybrid path walked by Deus Ex and System Shock, you must balance all of its part.<br /> That's the reason CD Project dropped every hint of third person view in Cyberpunk 2077. Sometimes you must choose what you are doing. Trying to do a Jack of All Trades is a good way to botch the design.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 12-16-2019, 03:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T13:17:47-08:00","id":1355248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1355235#post1355235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Half-life 2 had no role in it.<br /> In the year Half-life 2 came out, many other games were a commercial and a critical success: Metal Gear 3, Halo 2,GTA San Andreas, Fable,Doom 3, Far Cry and so on.<br /> <br /> What killed Bloodlines was :<br /> <br /> <br /> 1) A lack of budget, at the end of the development the funds were gone.<br /> <br /> 2) The choice to use a (very powerful, complex, and expensive) game engine never relased before, which was not already tested and had several faults (faults you can fix if you are Valve and had a lot of money, not surely thing you could do if you were Troika).<br /> <br /> 3) Deadlines from Activision<br /> <br /> 3) Bugginess, mostly caused by point 1,2 and 3<br /> <br /> 4) High hardware requirements, which shrinked an already small market niche.<br /> <br /> ah, also important<br /> <br /> 5) Bad game design.<br /> Bloodlines was a good RPG, a terrible FPS, and an horrible TPS. Stealth was so so.<br /> If you choose to make an RPG that walks the hybrid path walked by Deus Ex and System Shock, you must balance all of its part.<br /> That's the reason CD Project dropped every hint of third person view in Cyberpunk 2077. Sometimes you must choose what you are doing. Trying to do a Jack of All Trades is a good way to botch the design.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was released the SAME WEEKEND.<br /> <br /> So, yes, I would say it played a role.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T13:31:55-08:00","id":1355250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1355248#post1355248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It was released the SAME WEEKEND.<br /> <br /> So, yes, I would say it played a role.</div> </div> </div> </div>No it didn't. They were not even games of the same genre, one was the sequel of linear First Person Shooter, the other one was a hybrid Rpg-Stealth-Action game made from the creators of Fallout. Apples and oranges.<br /> <br /> <br /> Vampire the Masquerade Bloodlines and Half-Life were relased 16 november<br /> <br /> Halo 2, Jak 3 were relased 7 days before, (9 November 2004)<br /> Metroid 2 and Need For Speed were both relased one day before (15 november)<br /> Dragon Ball Budokai 3 was relased the very same day (16 november) and it was a hit.<br /> Metal Gear Solid 3 was relased the day after (17 november 2004)<br /> San Andreas was relased less than a month before (26 october 2004)<br /> <br /> All of these game were commercial hit, and being relase in near Half-life didn't stopped them from becoming a commercial hit.<br /> <br /> Bloodlines was not a good title with bad luck. It was a bad title with a lot of reedeming features.<br /> <br /> <br /> At the time, the review didn't went well.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.metacritic.com/game/pc/vampire-the-masquerade---bloodlines\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.metacritic.com/game/pc/v...e---bloodlines</a><br /> <br /> Just check the Metacritic of the other games I quoted, and you will see the problem.<br /> And 8 doesn't mean what it means today. Today a game with metacritic 8 is good. At the time, when 9 and 10 were given almost for free 8 was not a good vote.<br /> <br /> You want to know what killed Bloodlines?<br /> The thing that killed Bloodlines was that it was a great RPG, and a bad unfinished videogame which could not even be played on some computers.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Gamespy<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#4B4B4B\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">In the end, though, the problems with mediocre combat wouldn't have stopped me from playing </span></span><i>Bloodlines</i><span style=\"color:#4B4B4B\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">; having gone through the game once, they won't stop me from replaying it, either, in order to experience the different endings. <b>How that will affect gamers in deciding whether to purchase the game depends very much on what kind of mind-set they go in with. If you go in with the idea that </b></span></span><b><i>Bloodlines</i></b><span style=\"color:#4B4B4B\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b> is a hybrid FPS / RPG, you're going to be dramatically disappointed.</b> On the other hand, if you're looking for one of the best role-playing game experiences of this year, then you should really look into </span></span><i><a href=\"http://pc.gamespy.com/pc/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines/index.html\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Masquerade - Bloodlines</a></i><span style=\"color:#4B4B4B\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">. <b>Congratulations, </b></span></span><b><a href=\"http://www.gamespy.com/company/027/027061.html\" target=\"_blank\">Troika</a><span style=\"color:#4B4B4B\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">, on producing a </span></span><i>Vampire</i></b><span style=\"color:#4B4B4B\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b> game that doesn't\u2026 um\u2026 suck</b>.</span></span> </div> </div> </div><br /> Eurogamer<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Gibson\">Easy to sum up: <b>Game isn't finished.</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Gibson\">At the opening, you forgive the array of bugs and glitches as it being &quot;rough around the edges&quot;, so joining the long line of games which stressed imagination above mere competence and polish: Sure, characters glide out of the room in the intro sequence... who cares? Look how amazing Santa Monica is...</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Gibson\"><b>Problem is, as you progress, they escalate. By the time you've reached the climax, they're become impossible to ignore and made all the worse by you not even particularly enjoying the game anymore. </b>Having animation flickers and textures going wrong is a different thing from - say - reloading and finding that simple action has broken some of the level's scripting or getting caught in a game-ending crash bug upon exiting a mandatory mission. It runs considerably worse than Half-Life, sharing the stutter-frame-rate problem of its mother engine, but generally worse. It eats up Virtual Memory like anything, with long sessions leading to increasingly lengthy load times and slower frame-rates (I'm not a programmer, but &quot;Memory Leak&quot; sounds like a likely explanation). It just crashes. Even surface level shows signs of being rushed to release amass, like the dialogue in Chinatown having so many typos that even I, with my rudimentary grasp of the English tongue, wince.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Gibson\"><b>While a determined player - especially a PC RPG player - will forgive much of this, and my selection of bugs are fairly extreme examples of what's going wrong, it's really not on.</b> Suffice to say, those stories about it being done ages ago and being stuck on a shelf until Half-Life 2 was finished are evidently a lie. Someone decided to throw this into the shops and then patch later.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><br /> GamerNode<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Now that I have told you about the positives of Bloodlines, mine is the painful task of talking about the many shortcomings. With all due respect to Troika, <b>do not under any circumstances play this game without patching it. I have heard many heart wrenching stories about bugs just eating this game alive to the point that it is unplayable. On top of the bugs, do not even bother buying this game if your computer does not feature a NVIDIA card. </b>At some points, even with my 9800 xt pro turbo, it was unplayable due to frames being dropped by the dozens. It pains me terribly when a game that is as great as Bloodlines, is released too early and is not as perfect as it should be.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Bloodlines contains one of the worst FPS aspects that I have ever come across.</b> Due to the fact that using weapons is point based, the FPS aspect of the game is governed by how many points you have in using ranged weapons. Unless you put all of your points in ranged combat, you have better chances of you enemies dying of a heart attack than you doing any damage to them with a gun. So my biggest tip when playing this game is to forget about guns and grab a melee weapon. In retrospect I recant saying that the FPS aspect is awful, since it is a skill point based RPG and not a run and gun shooter. Just remember that in Bloodlines guns don,t kill people, katanas do.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Overall I think that despite the bugs and at times choppy graphics, Bloodlines is one of my most favorable and memorable RPG adventure games ever. I<b>f you are a person who can,t stand long load times, bugs and choppy graphics then avoid this game like the plague. But on the flipside, if you are a person who doesn,t want to miss out on arguably one of the greatest RPGs to hit the market this year, then get out there and pick up a copy of the game.</b></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><br /> I still remember the game killing bug that hit me at the end of the Society of Leopold level, I had to use cheats to load the next level, because each time I escaped the game crashed down, no way to avoid it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 12-17-2019, 05:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T13:50:49-08:00","id":1355257,"title":"","content":"Uhmm....<br /> <br /> Here's where you're wrong.<br /> <br /> Dead wrong.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.gamespot.com/articles/bloodlines-bites-half-life-2s-release-date/1100-6112907/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.gamespot.com/articles/bl.../1100-6112907/</a> <i>Since last fall, the release date of Half-Life 2 was put on hold because its Source engine had been compromised by hackers. An oft-overlooked consequence of the attack was the delay of the other game to use the Valve-developed Source engine, Vampire: The Masquerade - Bloodlines. Even though the game dropped its multiplayer functionality, the Source code theft also caused enough concern to put it in ship-date limbo as well.</i><br /> <i>So it is more than a little ironic that the first two games to use the Source engine are going to be released on the same day. Activision and developer Troika have announced that Vampire: The Masquerade - Bloodlines will join Half-Life 2 on store shelves on November 16, alongside Metal Gear Solid 3: Snake Eater, Metroid Prime 2: Echoes, Need for Speed Underground 2, Call of Duty: Finest Hour, GoldenEye: Rogue Agent, and several others.</i><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T14:07:23-08:00","id":1355262,"title":"","content":"Bullshit.<br /> <br /> Eurogamer<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><i><span style=\"font-family:Gibson\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Easy to sum up: <b>Game isn't finished.</b></span></span></i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><i><span style=\"font-family:Gibson\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">...</span></span></i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><i><span style=\"font-family:Gibson\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><b>While a determined player - especially a PC RPG player - will forgive much of this, and my selection of bugs are fairly extreme examples of what's going wrong, it's really not on.</b> Suffice to say, <b>those stories about it being done ages ago and being stuck on a shelf until Half-Life 2 was finished are evidently a lie. Someone decided to throw this into the shops and then patch late</b></span></span></i></span></span> </div> </div> </div><br /> When the game came out, it wasn't finished yet.<br /> <br /> <br /> It was a fucking bugfest, with bad game desing. No way they would have been able to relase it before, simply because when the game came out it WASN'T FINISHED.<br /> <br /> <br /> From Wikipedia<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Activision introduced the game in May 2003,<sup><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vampire:_The_Masquerade_%E2%80%93_Bloodlines#cite_note-GamespotReveal-46\" target=\"_blank\">[46]</a></sup> but in October, Valve experienced a security breach in which hackers stole the source code for <i>Half-Life 2</i>. The breach required new security implementations for the engine, delaying both games; the release of <i>Bloodlines</i> was postponed until early 2005.<sup><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vampire:_The_Masquerade_%E2%80%93_Bloodlines#cite_note-CNNBReach-47\" target=\"_blank\">[47]</a></sup> Until May 2004, Troika and Activision said that the game would feature a multiplayer component and modes including a team of vampires against a team of vampire hunters, with the ability to upgrade characters between each round.<sup><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vampire:_The_Masquerade_%E2%80%93_Bloodlines#cite_note-GSPotMulti-48\" target=\"_blank\">[48]</a></sup> The team was left without a producer by Activision for over a year before <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/David_Mullich\" target=\"_blank\">David Mullich</a> was assigned to the project. With no producer oversight, Mullich found the game's design incomplete, game levels created and abandoned, and several technical issues, including problems with code for the proposed multiplayer option.<sup><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vampire:_The_Masquerade_%E2%80%93_Bloodlines#cite_note-MullichInterview-49\" target=\"_blank\">[49]</a></sup><sup><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vampire:_The_Masquerade_%E2%80%93_Bloodlines#cite_note-MullichInterviewGer-50\" target=\"_blank\">[50]</a></sup> The Source multiplayer code was in its infancy, increasing its development time, and the idea was abandoned.<sup><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vampire:_The_Masquerade_%E2%80%93_Bloodlines#cite_note-GameBansheeHistory-41\" target=\"_blank\">[41]</a></sup></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">In addition to problems with the Source engine, the designers found that the game's scope exceeded their resources. <i>Bloodlines</i> has several styles of gameplay, requiring different interfaces, animations and artificial intelligence for stealth and melee combat, and first- or third-person capability.<sup><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vampire:_The_Masquerade_%E2%80%93_Bloodlines#cite_note-EuroDevelopment-27\" target=\"_blank\">[27]</a></sup><sup><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vampire:_The_Masquerade_%E2%80%93_Bloodlines#cite_note-RPSDevelopment-32\" target=\"_blank\">[32]</a></sup> Compared to contemporary first-person shooters, with 10 to 20 animated character models, <i>Bloodlines</i> had over 150 characters with 3,000 unique animations, in addition to boss characters, with their own styles of movement.<sup><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vampire:_The_Masquerade_%E2%80%93_Bloodlines#cite_note-=GamespotDev4-42\" target=\"_blank\">[42]</a></sup> The designers underestimated the length of time required to develop and improve these systems. The game's scope suffered from content <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cruft\" target=\"_blank\">not being removed when necessary</a>; other components would be endlessly refined without being finalized, preventing the developers from focusing on other parts of the game system.<sup><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vampire:_The_Masquerade_%E2%80%93_Bloodlines#cite_note-EuroDevelopment-27\" target=\"_blank\">[27]</a></sup><sup><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vampire:_The_Masquerade_%E2%80%93_Bloodlines#cite_note-RPSDevelopment-32\" target=\"_blank\">[32]</a></sup> All content additionally required approval by White Wolf and Activision.<sup><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vampire:_The_Masquerade_%E2%80%93_Bloodlines#cite_note-EscapistTroikaPG3-36\" target=\"_blank\">[36]</a></sup></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>After three years in development, the game was progressing slowly, and it was unknown when it would be finished</b>.</span><sup><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vampire:_The_Masquerade_%E2%80%93_Bloodlines#cite_note-EuroDevelopment-27\" target=\"_blank\">[27]</a></sup> <b>Activision set a series of deadlines for the project's development to ensure Troika would have sufficient time to effectively test the game, though these milestones were repeatedly extended, and <i>Bloodlines</i> eventually ran over budget</b>.<sup><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vampire:_The_Masquerade_%E2%80%93_Bloodlines#cite_note-GameStakers-30\" target=\"_blank\">[30]</a></sup> In 2003 Activision intervened, ordering that the game be ready for release in the next few months, and even advancing more money to Troika to complete its work on <i><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Temple_of_Elemental_Evil_(video_game)\" target=\"_blank\">The Temple of Elemental Evil</a></i> for <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Atari\" target=\"_blank\">Atari</a>, freeing the Troika team to work on <i>Bloodlines</i> exclusively.<sup><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vampire:_The_Masquerade_%E2%80%93_Bloodlines#cite_note-Escapist1PG3-35\" target=\"_blank\">[35]</a></sup><sup><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vampire:_The_Masquerade_%E2%80%93_Bloodlines#cite_note-EscapistTroikaPG3-36\" target=\"_blank\">[36]</a></sup> Activision eventually issued an ultimatum that the project be finished within months, on September 15, 2004.<sup><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vampire:_The_Masquerade_%E2%80%93_Bloodlines#cite_note-EuroDevelopment-27\" target=\"_blank\">[27]</a></sup><sup><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vampire:_The_Masquerade_%E2%80%93_Bloodlines#cite_note-GameStakers-30\" target=\"_blank\">[30]</a></sup> Troika delivered a version of <i>Bloodlines</i> on the required date; due to its scale, the game underwent three weeks of testing. Activision decided that the game was suitable for release, but was contractually bound to withhold <i>Bloodlines</i> until after the debut of <i>Half-Life 2</i> in November 2004. Troika convinced Activision to use the delay to fund further development; the additional budget was not enough to pay all of Troika's staff, and some employees worked unpaid to complete the project. This version underwent another three weeks of testing to become the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Software_release_life_cycle#Release_to_manufacturing_.28RTM.29\" target=\"_blank\">final release code</a>;<sup><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vampire:_The_Masquerade_%E2%80%93_Bloodlines#cite_note-GameStakers-30\" target=\"_blank\">[30]</a></sup><span style=\"font-size:36px\"> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>the game was still unfinished when Activision forced its release.</b><sup><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vampire:_The_Masquerade_%E2%80%93_Bloodlines#cite_note-EuroDevelopment-27\" target=\"_blank\">[27]</a></sup> <b><i>Bloodlines</i>' creative director <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jason_Anderson_(artist)\" target=\"_blank\">Jason Anderson</a> blamed Activision, saying that the publisher took the game from Troika without providing enough time to test and polish it.<sup><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vampire:_The_Masquerade_%E2%80%93_Bloodlines#cite_note-Escapist1PG3-35\" target=\"_blank\">[35]</a></sup></b></span> C</span></span>onversely, Boyarsky defended Activision for supporting Troika as the project exceeded its budget and schedule.<sup><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vampire:_The_Masquerade_%E2%80%93_Bloodlines#cite_note-PCGamesN2017-51\" target=\"_blank\">[51]</a></sup> During the nearly four years of development, Anderson estimated that the team worked overtime for all but two months.</span></span> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><sup><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Half-Life code breach didn't matter because even if it would have they would never have been able to relase the game before 16 November because even <u>at 16 november they were not done.</u></span></sup></span></span><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.escapistmagazine.com/articles/view/video-games/issues/issue_244/7258-The-Last-Masquerade.3\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.escapistmagazine.com/arti...t-Masquerade.3</a><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\">But while the Los Angeles that Troika built may have been conceptually complex, its actual construction was a much simpler affair. Many of the buildings were crude things, with details and decorations relegated to textures on flat blocks, making much of the city look like a painted backdrop in a high school play. Troika tried to hide it where they thought you wouldn't notice - typically anything above the ground floor - but it was easy to spot, even by a casual observer. Moreover, Troika's efforts to populate the city fell just as flat. The small number of NPC models meant that you saw the same people, with very little variation, over and over again as they shuffled awkwardly and silently around the city. It wasn't uncommon to see half a dozen identical hobos roaming the streets, or two identical goths lined up to get into a club with a third walking past. And while this didn't actually spoil the atmosphere, it certainly didn't help.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\">So what actually went wrong?<span style=\"font-size:24px\"><b> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">How did a game so clearly unfinished ever see the light of day?</span></b></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\">All signs suggest Troika simply needed more time. </span></span><i>Bloodlines</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"> was made in a hurry, with the team working in almost constant crunch mode just to get the game out of the door. The developers used a prototype of Valve's Source engine that was still under construction, forcing Troika to write its own code to fill in the gaps. Because of this, </span></span><i>Bloodlines</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"> was riddled with bugs on release. Some were trivial, like animation and graphical glitches. Others were more severe, like bugs that dumped you out of the game or made it impossible to proceed. <b>When it was released, </b></span></span><b><i>Bloodlines</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"> was still very much a work in progress, and everything from the blocky level design to the wildly varying quality of character models to the plethora of bugs marked a game that simply was not yet ready for prime time.</span></span></b> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 12-17-2019, 05:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T01:54:14-08:00","id":1355348,"title":"","content":"I remember I bought VtM Bloodlines on release, started blowing through it, really enjoyed it and then got stuck at the werewolf. It's a scripted scene where an invincible werewolf chases you around for 5 minutes until the overhead countdown expires, at which point a cable car is supposed to arrive to let you escape. But when I played, the car never showed up. Even spending an extra 10 minutes running around from that stupid werewolf, the car never arrived. I reloaded saves from before the mission started, and the car still never showed up. I restarted the game, ran through it again and when I got to that point the car still never showed up. It was just impossible to go any further. I ended up making a few other characters and played up until that point, but it was a wall I couldn't pass. <br /> <br /> When my other friends, who were also into White Wolf games asked me if they should buy it my response was to tell them to hold off until the bugs got fixed because it just wasn't playable or complete-able. Eventually (maybe 3 weeks or a month later) Troika finally released a patch that allowed me to get past that bugged area and I was able to beat the game. <br /> <br /> If it hadn't been for game breaking bugs like that I would have recommended it to my friends and they would have undoubtedly ended up buying it, but as it was I couldn't do that in good conscious. In retrospect I probably should have recommended they buy it anyway, but I wasn't considering the possibility that Troika would go out of business because people were steering clear from the game for exactly those sorts of reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T02:13:46-08:00","id":1355349,"title":"","content":"Rabbit, I know you want to make your point, but 