> * The game is coming out around Christmas.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> When I first saw the trailer tonight, I was thinking WTF? It really didn't have me interested, but I've watched it more and saw your comment. I'm thinking sickko too. Or some major use of Dominate or Presence in the case of Elif. Those eyes! Who wouldn't want her?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18963-chris313allnight","name":"Chris313AllNight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T21:26:45-07:00","id":1386608,"title":"","content":"Is the dancing guy supposed to be the big bad?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris313AllNight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1386603#post1386603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those eyes! Who wouldn't want her?</div> </div> </div> </div>What are you talking about? She's bad at social distancing and not even wearing a mask.I bet she has the covid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T21:33:20-07:00","id":1386609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1386608#post1386608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the dancing guy supposed to be the big bad?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's Mr. Damp, a psychotic Malkavian.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://vtmb.fandom.com/wiki/Mr._Damp\" target=\"_blank\">https://vtmb.fandom.com/wiki/Mr._Damp</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T00:18:04-07:00","id":1386628,"title":"","content":"My small hopes shrink. It looks like they Looked at Farcry's nutty villains maybe Bioshock's twist and thought &quot;We should top that&quot; without actually having clever writers to pull it off. Is that dude using celerity a blood god or something? (I mean, I totally appreciate that they're using VTM celerity rather than V5 celerity, though it's not conclusive) <br /> <br /> It just feels like everyone's showing off and it's difficult to imagine in-character justification for it. Doesn't &quot;The Masquerade&quot; demand everyone be low-key vampires? Why is everyone doing their best to justify an inquisition? I get that the OG Bloodlines was pulpy nonsense at times, but this game looks like it wants to be serious art and yet is totally filled with BS.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T00:57:31-07:00","id":1386637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1386628#post1386628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My small hopes shrink. It looks like they Looked at Farcry's nutty villains maybe Bioshock's twist and thought &quot;We should top that&quot; without actually having clever writers to pull it off. Is that dude using celerity a blood god or something? (I mean, I totally appreciate that they're using VTM celerity rather than V5 celerity, though it's not conclusive)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's just meant to look cool and fun as well as give a sense of the area bosses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It just feels like everyone's showing off and it's difficult to imagine in-character justification for it. Doesn't &quot;The Masquerade&quot; demand everyone be low-key vampires? Why is everyone doing their best to justify an inquisition? I get that the OG Bloodlines was pulpy nonsense at times, but this game looks like it wants to be serious art and yet is totally filled with BS. </div> </div> </div>I have no sign this intends to be serious, or at least more serious than Bloodlines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T01:34:24-07:00","id":1386642,"title":"","content":"Fair points, I feel like I need to elaborate further. <br /> <br /> I don't like this attempt at being &quot;zany&quot;. From what I've seen of bloodlines so far, it looks tacky; Characters are trying way too hard. It looks unnatural, and it makes me feel like the characters are dorks who are totally new to power, rather than people who are used to it. Whilst the OG bloodlines could get away with a lot of characters trying too hard because of graphical limitations, B2 doesn't have that cushion. And I don't feel like B2 has really shown that they can deliver &quot;camp&quot; half as good as B1. B1's dialogue mostly felt good with the scene even if the animations were whack, whilst B2's dialogue feels very scripted. This new trailer hasn't improved my perceptions of the game; the dance is dumb. The malkavian family murder is tasteless and, though I can imagine some context where it'd work, it certainly doesn't look good without that context.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T10:05:32-07:00","id":1386731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1386628#post1386628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My small hopes shrink. It looks like they Looked at Farcry's nutty villains maybe Bioshock's twist and thought &quot;We should top that&quot; without actually having clever writers to pull it off. Is that dude using celerity a blood god or something? (I mean, I totally appreciate that they're using VTM celerity rather than V5 celerity, though it's not conclusive)<br /> <br /> It just feels like everyone's showing off and it's difficult to imagine in-character justification for it. Doesn't &quot;The Masquerade&quot; demand everyone be low-key vampires? Why is everyone doing their best to justify an inquisition? I get that the OG Bloodlines was pulpy nonsense at times, but this game looks like it wants to be serious art and yet is totally filled with BS.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As far as rules versus game mechanics, they did what the last Bloodlines game did: used mechanics and such that map to a video game, not directly 1 for 1 with the tabletop. That 'doiesn't mean 'oh look they're ignoring V5!' Otherwise, the devs on both sides have openly stated that they were developed in tandem (some powerrs were developed for BL2 first and ported to tabletop, and vice-versa), and that the material and plot and such will mesh with V5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T11:01:35-07:00","id":1386737,"title":"","content":"I will say this trailer fell pretty flat for me. I didn't dislike it, but it didn't show me anything that made me particularly excited about the game, other than the one moment when the guy those the axe at you and you catch it. That was kind of cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T17:35:11-07:00","id":1386835,"title":"","content":"The animations certainly look less janky to me than from last year, which is much appreciated. <br /> <br /> I certainly don't think the Mr. Damp scene is meant to be humorous. The intention is clearly to create a sense of foreboding and dread by juxtaposing his inhumanity with a light-hearted pop song. <br /> <br /> Personally- and people are welcome to disagree with me on this- Masquerade has always had an undercurrent of camp to it, as only something made in the early 90s could. There's horror and mystery, sure, but with a pulp sensibility that keeps things from getting too grim and self-important. So juxtaposing Damp's antics, the Prince(?) dancing in his office, and all the other stuff fits. The soul of the World of Horror is heavily rooted in a late 80s/early 90s aesthetic and sensibility, and nothing will ever change that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T17:37:49-07:00","id":1386836,"title":"","content":"The art reminds me a bit of Borderlands and the Outer Worlds.<br /> <br /> Stylized art compensates for a AA budget.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T04:45:16-07:00","id":1386950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1386731#post1386731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That 'doiesn't mean 'oh look they're ignoring V5!' Otherwise, the devs on both sides have openly stated that they were developed in tandem (some powerrs were developed for BL2 first and ported to tabletop, and vice-versa), and that the material and plot and such will mesh with V5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Physical disciplines in V5 are metaphysically different. Celerity, for example; In VTM, VTMB and VTMB2, celerity can be seen to work by essentially speeding up time, which is why you ignore velocity and don't uncontrolably fling yourself forward whenever you move at super speed, why you can still use all your dice to shoot someone even though you should be moving too fast for that much cognition, and why you don't do extra damage when you hit someone (Untill you get to elder levels where rules can be bent) or recieve extra damage when they hit you (Ok, it's simplified for gameplay reasons, but that's basically how it works) While in V5, Celerity is simply a big collection of speed powers. Potence and fortitude are easier arguments to make because they're very simple and all encompassing outside of V5 whilst in V5 each dot of potence/Fortitude carries a highly specific power... <br /> <br /> So, yeah, if VTMB2 treats celerity as just &quot;slow mo&quot;, Potence as just a &quot;super strength&quot; ability that can do all things at once (Super jump, super lift, super throw, extra damage) and fortitude as a very simple &quot;reduce all the damage&quot; then it'd be a step away from V5. The simpler the system, the better, and the less like V5 it is, which is also good. <br /> <br /> <br /> But, the trailer is too tacky. <br /> There's good camp, there's bad camp. I'm not a stranger to this. I feel this trailer just doesn't look good. A few short flashes of scenes look nice, but the stuff it puts a lot of time into doesn't look good. If it turns out the dead family are of plot importance, it might be a really good scene, if it's just whacky antics, it's tired and dumb. World of Darkness has some great camp stuff, it's a fucking <i>satire </i>after all, but a lot of recent writings have proven they're not all that adept with such material. I for one feel like a lot of vampires in these trailers are trying to show charisma and are failing at it, because I find them rather unlikeable, because they're just saying or doing dumb shit in an unappealing voice. Cocky and confident are different things after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T05:17:54-07:00","id":1386954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1386950#post1386950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Physical disciplines in V5 are metaphysically different. Celerity, for example; In VTM, VTMB and VTMB2, celerity can be seen to work by essentially speeding up time, which is why you ignore velocity and don't uncontrolably fling yourself forward whenever you move at super speed, why you can still use all your dice to shoot someone even though you should be moving too fast for that much cognition, and why you don't do extra damage when you hit someone (Untill you get to elder levels where rules can be bent) or recieve extra damage when they hit you (Ok, it's simplified for gameplay reasons, but that's basically how it works) While in V5, Celerity is simply a big collection of speed powers. Potence and fortitude are easier arguments to make because they're very simple and all encompassing outside of V5 whilst in V5 each dot of potence/Fortitude carries a highly specific power...<br /> <br /> So, yeah, if VTMB2 treats celerity as just &quot;slow mo&quot;, Potence as just a &quot;super strength&quot; ability that can do all things at once (Super jump, super lift, super throw, extra damage) and fortitude as a very simple &quot;reduce all the damage&quot; then it'd be a step away from V5. The simpler the system, the better, and the less like V5 it is, which is also good.</div> </div> </div> </div>The disciplines have already been described on the game's website. Every discipline, including the three physical ones, has two distinct powers (except for Thaumaturgy, which has three), which improve in some way as more dots in the discipline are invested. The Celerity that you're talking about is probably &quot;Accelerate&quot;, unlocked at Celerity 3.<br /> <br /> Apart from that, the diciplines have been interpreted loosely for the sake of gameplay, much like in VTMB1. So they're distinct from any pen and paper version of VtM, although they have more in common with what you'd call VTM disciplines: there are no choices within discipline progression, Dementation is a discipline rather than an amalgam and thinbloods have new disciplines (I think you pick one of three) rather than thinblood alchemy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T08:54:30-07:00","id":1386983,"title":"","content":"Even in a thread not about V5, MyWifeIsScary finds a way to shit it up and complain about V5","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26082-mulengro","name":"Mulengro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T09:13:12-07:00","id":1386985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1386950#post1386950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find them rather unlikeable, because they're just saying or doing dumb shit in an unappealing voice. Cocky and confident are different things after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you...have you played the original Bloodlines?<br /> <br /> Serious question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T11:46:02-07:00","id":1387027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1386950#post1386950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...I find them rather unlikeable, because they're just saying or doing dumb shit in an unappealing voice. Cocky and confident are different things after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lot's of people who think they are cocky and or confident are unlikeable to everyone else and sound dumb with an unappealing voice.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T13:49:49-07:00","id":1387069,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mulengro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1386983#post1386983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even in a thread not about V5, MyWifeIsScary finds a way to shit it up and complain about V5</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Just as a priest can turn every conversation to God. </span></span></span><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1387027#post1387027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lot's of people who think they are cocky and or confident are unlikeable to everyone else and sound dumb with an unappealing voice.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find it a litlle... eh.. unbelievable though. Like the dude knows he's playing a character, and knows he's not doing a good job of it; Whats his motivation for that? (I am primarily refering to the guy from the last trailer who asserts &quot;We only have one rule&quot;) <br /> <br /> Lots of Character-Characters. Few people-characters. That's what I see, and whilst VTMB had a handful of those, most characters could be seen as people, and the few that were character-characters were actually well done and were funny/intriguing for at least the first playthrough. I still find myself impersonating the lines of Fat Larry and the Taxi driver after all. The characters of VTMB2 look like they've come for a quota on quirk, rather than something organic that fits the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T15:46:18-07:00","id":1387102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mulengro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1386983#post1386983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even in a thread not about V5, MyWifeIsScary finds a way to shit it up and complain about V5</div> </div> </div> </div>Report complaints, please don't say them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7