08:00","id":1468169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1468125#post1468125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In my opinion, building up hype for the release of Bloodlines 2 may have been an error.</div> </div> </div> </div>With all due respect, the error wasn't in building up hype. Building hype is standard marking for pretty much everything. The error was in letting management bungle the game's development.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T12:42:04-08:00","id":1468170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1468169#post1468169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With all due respect, the error wasn't in building up hype. Building hype is standard marking for pretty much everything. The error was in letting management bungle the game's development.</div> </div> </div> </div>Chris Avellone basically said that out of nowhere the new manager decided she didn't want him or Brian Mitsoda involved and ordered their content thrown out.<br /> <br /> Apparently she didn't know or care that was ALL the sidequests.<br /> <br /> And they didn't have any new ones written.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T17:08:53-08:00","id":1468198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1468165#post1468165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Ye<span style=\"color:#494949\">ah th</span><span style=\"color:#494949\">at's the games and cra</span><span style=\"color:#494949\">cks </span><span style=\"color:#494949\">are begining to show </span><span style=\"color:#494949\">after recent g</span><span style=\"color:#494949\">affes</span><span style=\"color:#494949\">. I wonder when the shift occured from niche but enthusi</span><span style=\"color:#494949\">astic developers to </span><span style=\"color:#494949\">a proto E</span><span style=\"color:#494949\">a? the s</span><span style=\"color:#494949\">ad thing I w</span><span style=\"color:#494949\">as cautiously optimistic when they first got the brand from their works</span><span style=\"color:#494949\"> emph</span><span style=\"color:#494949\">asis on diversifying b</span><span style=\"color:#494949\">ased development. If they developed their g</span><span style=\"color:#494949\">a</span><span style=\"color:#494949\">mes like they h</span><span style=\"color:#494949\">ave v5 you'd only be </span><span style=\"color:#494949\">able to pl</span><span style=\"color:#494949\">ay C</span><span style=\"color:#494949\">atholics in crusader kings.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Except Paradox isn't the Devs on Bloodlines 2. They're the Producers. Hardsuit Labs were the Developers.<br /> <br /> If the issues that caused Hardsuit to loose Bloodlines 2 were on the development side, that's on them for the most part.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1468170#post1468170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Chris Avellone basically said that out of nowhere the new manager decided she didn't want him or Brian Mitsoda involved and ordered their content thrown out.<br /> <br /> Apparently she didn't know or care that was ALL the sidequests.<br /> <br /> And they didn't have any new ones written.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I can kind of get that with Avellone due to the allegations made against him the other year, it still puzzles me that Mitsoda was dropped. He was their front and center link to the cult classic original that face it is a big part of why people were so damn hyped for Bloodlines 2. Removing him without a good reason was a bad move as it pissed off a good chunk of the core fanbase for the game.<br /> <br /> Doubly so with dropped them and throwing out all of the content they made. That is just utterly bonkers to me.<br /> <br /> Either said manger was completely oblivious or there was something going on that we're still not privy to and may never know.<br /> <br /> Which honestly is the most frustrating part of this whole situation, that we may not find what exactly happened for years, if ever. Just as we will likely never find out about the original iteration of Bloodlines 2 with Avellone's and Mitsoda's content.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T20:05:17-08:00","id":1468216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1468169#post1468169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With all due respect, the error wasn't in building up hype. Building hype is standard marking for pretty much everything. The error was in letting management bungle the game's development.</div> </div> </div> </div>Building hype isn't a simple marketing tool that one should apply freely at every turn. As every marketing tool, it actually takes strategic decision, with aim to intensity, method and timing.<br /> <br /> In this case we have a game that is a sequel to an old classic, being made by a new developer company, in the midst of a complex IP gamble with several fronts.<br /> <br /> Every hype is a gamble. You attract early investors and increase the likely absorption of your product by the market, but you also intensifies the effect of any problem that comes. You also raise the bar for expectation, making it even harder for your product to be seen in a positive light.<br /> <br /> Here we have a situation where people have too high preset expectations and things can go bad royally. There is already a strong hype built in the entire process, the legacy of the name. A lot of people will totally buy it just because it is VtM Bloodlines. But there's also a lot of pressure and raised sensibilities to the dark history of bad legacies and vaporware.<br /> <br /> Let me clarify: I don't think they shouldn't build a hype at all. I think it was too soon and they're now reaping the consequences. They had other projects that could receive attention and be delivered in a reasonable span of time and less risk. Why do that at the time? To increase public interest? They could hold the release of the finalized game to have time to build hype. Was it to get more investing up front? This is gambling with your shares, extremely risky.<br /> <br /> Now they have the opposite effect. They will have to pull this on their own not to get an increase in their income and valuation, but simply to recover public and investment trust. A big loss that could have been easily avoided with a more conservative move on this side of their business.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T20:34:08-08:00","id":1468220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1468198#post1468198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which honestly is the most frustrating part of this whole situation, that we may not find what exactly happened for years, if ever. Just as we will likely never find out about the original iteration of Bloodlines 2 with Avellone's and Mitsoda's content.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am very curious if the new developer will be reintegrating Avellone's and Mitsoda's content, since it seems like that would be the easiest thing to do, assuming that the previous manager didn't have all of that permanently erased.<br /> <br /> For me, at least, whether Mitsoda's content ends up in the finished product is the chief and most important detail about whether I will end up purchasing Bloodlines 2 or not. Getting Mitsoda on as a major writer for the game was what got me interested in Bloodlines 2 in the first place and his removal killed any interest I had in buying it. If they want my money the only way that's happening is if what he wrote ends up being in the final product.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-18T01:39:28-08:00","id":1468245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1298479-bloodlines-2-announced?p=1468198#post1468198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I can kind of get that with Avellone due to the allegations made against him the other year, it still puzzles me that Mitsoda was dropped. He was their front and center link to the cult classic original that face it is a big part of why people were so damn hyped for Bloodlines 2. Removing him without a good reason was a bad move as it pissed off a good chunk of the core fanbase for the game.<br /> <br /> Doubly so with dropped them and throwing out all of the content they made. That is just utterly bonkers to me.<br /> <br /> Either said manger was completely oblivious or there was something going on that we're still not privy to and may never know.<br /> <br /> Which honestly is the most frustrating part of this whole situation, that we may not find what exactly happened for years, if ever. Just as we will likely never find out about the original iteration of Bloodlines 2 with Avellone's and Mitsoda's content.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Avellone stuff isn't even true. Avellone stopped working on Bloodlines 2 in 2018, when his contract with Hardsuit Labs ended. The allegations against him came out in 2020.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/FYRCwYV.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Why wasn't Avellone's writing used in the game? We don't know. Avellone doesn't know. Maybe it didn't fit the final vision. Maybe it was bad. Maybe Avellone was getting high and not delivering on time. Maybe the manager is an ass. No one can tell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}